\par }{\fs20\lang1024\langfe1024\noproof {\shp{\*\shpinst\shpleft1440\shptop2070\shpright10800\shpbottom2070\shpfhdr1\shpbxpage\shpbxignore\shpbypage\shpbyignore\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt0\shpz2\shplockanchor\shplid2049{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn fFlipH}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn fFlipV}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn shapePath}{\sv 4}}{\sp{\sn fFillOK}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn fFilled}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn fArrowheadsOK}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn posrelh}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn posrelv}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn fLayoutInCell}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn fLayoutInCell}{\sv 1}}}{\shprslt{\*\do\dobxpage\dobypage\dodhgt8194\dpline\dpptx0\dppty0\dpptx9920\dppty0\dpx1190\dpy2070\dpxsize9920\dpysize0\dplinew15\dplinecor0\dplinecog0\dplinecob0}}}}{\f0\fs16  \par }}{\footerf \pard\plain \s22\ql \b\f354\fs18  Page {\field{\*\fldinst PAGE}{\fldrslt 1}}{     }\'a9 2026 \uc2 Factiva, Inc.  All rights reserved.\par }{\footer \pard\plain \s22\ql \b\f354\fs18  Page {\field{\*\fldinst PAGE}{\fldrslt 1}} of {\field{\*\fldinst NUMPAGES}{\fldrslt 1}}{     }\'a9 2026 \uc2 Factiva, Inc.  All rights reserved.\par }\pard\plain \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\fs20 {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 Harris, Trump Spar Over Policies In Pivotal Debate; Hannity Live From The Spin Room In Philadelphia; Trump Confronts Harris Over Her Radical Record; \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  Provides No Clarification On Long List Of Flip Flops; Trump Joins Hannity Live In The Spin Room\b0\par\par\uc2 Sean Hannity \par \uc2 11,379 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 September 2024\par \uc2 Fox News: Hannity\par \uc2 SHAN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2024 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2024 ASC Services II Media, LLC.  All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 BRET BAIER, FOX NEWS CHIEF POLITICAL ANCHOR: And how much did it move this race? Because it's as tight a race as we have ever seen in this country.\par \par \uc2 MARTHA MACCALLUM, FOX NEWS ANCHOR: And last time we sat here, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  was running against President Trump. So, who knows what's going to happen next? Thank you all for tuning in tonight and joining us for the presidential debate.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: "HANNITY" is up right now.\par \par \uc2 SEAN HANNITY\uc2 , FOX NEWS CHANNEL HOST: All right. Thank you, Brett. Thank you, Martha. Welcome to HANNITY. We are live. We are in the spin room and we are in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, where the first and only scheduled debate between \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is officially now in the books. In just a moment, we're going to get reaction from Senator \uc2 Marco Rubio\uc2 , Senator Ted Cruz, Trump's running mate, J.D. Vance and Robert Kennedy, Jr.\par \par \uc2 But first, in case you missed it, here's how it all went out.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 DONALD TRUMP\uc2  (R) PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE: I don't say her, because she has no policy. Everything that she believed three years ago and four years ago is out the window. She's going to my philosophy now. In fact, I was going to send her a MAGA hat. She's gone to my philosophy. But if she ever got elected, she'd change it, and it will be the end of our country. She's a Marxist. Everybody knows she's a Marxist.\par \par \uc2 Will she allow abortion in the eighth month? Ninth month? Seventh month?\par \par \uc2 KAMALA HARRIS\uc2  (D) UNITED STATES DEMOCRATIC PRESIDENTIAL NOMINEE: Come on.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : OK. Would you do that? Why don't you ask me that question?\par \par \uc2 HARRIS: Why don't you answer the question?\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : That's the problem.\par \par \uc2 HARRIS: Would you veto -- answer the question.\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : You could do abortions in the seventh month, the eighth month, the ninth month.\par \par \uc2 HARRIS: That's not --\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : They allowed criminals, many, many millions of criminals. They allowed terrorists. They allowed common street criminals. They allowed people to come in, drug dealers to come into our country, and then, now in the United States, fracking? She's been against it for 12 years. Defund the police. She's been against that forever. She gave all that stuff up, very wrongly, very horribly and everybody is laughing at it. OK?\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. What you didn't hear tonight was any substance from \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  about pretty much anything. She delivered a lot of pre- rehearsed, memorized platitudes, lines, plenty of attacks. This was, I hate Trump. I hate Trump. I hate Trump, and I hate Trump more. Anyway, with lots kind of weird faces and expressions. We still don't have answers where she stands on defunding the police, electric vehicle mandates, mandatory gun confiscation which he lied about, Medicare for All, the $93 trillion Green New Deal she cosponsored in the \uc2 U.S. Senate\uc2  with \uc2 Bernie Sanders\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Banning plastic straws, reducing red meat consumption up to a 70 or 80 percent income tax rate. Bidenomics. We call it Bidenomics and we're proud of it. Offshore drilling, fracking, decriminalizing illegal immigration, free housing, healthcare, education, college education, and now sex change surgery provided by taxpayers. We didn't hear about the border wall that she was against, that now she's for.\par \par \uc2 And we didn't hear about illegal immigrants and returning home, late-term abortion. She didn't answer the question about restrictions, about months seven, eight and nine, and the list goes on and on. Left-wing moderators, the biggest loser of the night, ABC, \uc2 Disney\uc2 , \uc2 Bob Iger\uc2 's network. It was a disgrace. They barely asked her about important issues. We've got 56 days until an election.\par \par \uc2 Early voting starts in this commonwealth in seven days. You know, in between, so-called fact-checking and clapbacks only against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  because Kamala didn't offer any details on her own, as predicted, tonight's debate was three on one. Anyway. Joining us now from the spin room, Florida Senator, my senator, free state of Florida, \uc2 Marco Rubio\uc2 . Senator, how are you?\par \par \uc2 SEN. MARCO RUBIO (R-FL): Thank you.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: He's doing a big gaggle before I walked over. Tapping around the back. He's my senator.\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 RUBIO: They're impressed. The reporters were impressed.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: The biggest, I think, failure for the country tonight was ABC.\par \par \uc2 RUBIO: Yes. It's an embarrassment. That's an embarrassment to journalism. I mean, it's an -- I mean, there -- literally, there was times where they would say, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , why did you do or say this horrible thing? And then the question to \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is, what do you think about the horrible thing that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  did? There was no -- listen, they didn't ask her. Grocery bills are up 50 percent from 2020. 50 percent.\par \par \uc2 What do you say about that, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , how are you going to deal with that? They didn't ask her about the Afghan, they let her get away with this lie that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  didn't withdraw us from Afghanistan. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  was run out of Afghanistan in humiliating fashion. Even the fact-checkers were wrong where she said there's no state in the country with this -- there are multiple states in this country including \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 's Minnesota where if a baby is born in a botched abortion, they allow the baby to die.\par \par \uc2 OK? And then they let her get away with not answering what restrictions she would be supportive of.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: See? This is a frustrating thing, is when you have three on one and you have a fact like you just laid out about \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  and his position on late-term abortion and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was 100 percent right. He's talking about Governor Northam, well, first the baby will be born and will make the baby comfortable, and then the doctor will talk to the mother, but that's not the point.\par \par \uc2 Months seventh, eighth and ninth, even at people I know that a pro-choice that would be infanticide.\par \par \uc2 RUBIO: Of course. But here's the bottom line, Americans know \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . He was their president. He's been campaigning out since 2016. They know his positions. They know very little about \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 . Tonight, for the first time, despite the best efforts of these moderators, Americans began to learn that this was someone who was raising money to bail rioters out of jail.\par \par \uc2 This was someone who said she wanted to defund ICE. This was someone who basically said that we should be paying for the sex change operations of illegal migrants in detention. This was someone who accused the border patrol of whipping Haitian migrants at the border. And this is someone that has been in the White House for four years talking about all these things she's going to do. They've done none of them.\par \par \uc2 She talks about immigration and this bill, they have the power in the law right now to enforce our immigration laws. She has no campaign plan. She just unveiled her policy plan. It was literally, I'm not saying this New Republic, a liberal left-wing magazine is saying it. She literally cut and pasted from the \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 RUBIO: And so think about it, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and worse, because of what she stood for in 2019 --\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Just bear with me. The list. No restrictions on abortion from him and for her and her running mate. Mandatory gun buyback. She lied about that at the end of the debate. No border wall, decriminalizing illegal immigration, free housing, healthcare, education, free college in Minnesota, legal driver's licenses. We've had murder, we've had rape, we've had violent crime, and now we're going to offer what taxpayer-funded sex change operations.\par \par \uc2 She supports reparations, the $93 trillion Green New Deal which would be the end of capitalism. She cosponsored it. Government healthcare for all, the elimination of private health insurance. How does ABC not bring that up?\par \par \uc2 RUBIO: Not a single one of those things was asked.\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Did they not bring up well --\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: -- say radical Islamic terrorism or illegal alien.\par \par \uc2 RUBIO: But President Trump did a good job of injecting that in there. And in the end of the debate, he said the most important thing, and that is, she's been there for four years, all these things she's promising, they haven't done. And frankly, she wouldn't answer the most important question she was asked all night. Are Americans -- she was asked this. Are Americans better off today than they were four years ago? She didn't even answer.\par \par \uc2 She went on to talk about how she was born to a middle-class family, raised in Canada for part of that time and what apparently is not a middle-class neighborhood. But nonetheless, she went into her biography and I think she was exposed tonight. The talking heads, you know, they analyze this because they all -- they all want to pretend like \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  was born on July 24th of this year.\par \par \uc2 She has a record. She has a record as a senator, and she has a record as vice president. And Americans tonight, got a glimpse of who she -- what she really believes, what she really stands for, and what direction she'll actually take our country. And I think that was a big win, a big win.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Does this move the needle in your view?\par \par \uc2 RUBIO: I think it does, because there's a lot of vote -- remember, voters in the real world don't analyze this like the people that talk on cable news. They're viewing it and their mindset, OK? Who's this lady? And they start hearing these things. Hold on second. She helped bail out rioters? Hold on a second. She wouldn't answer the question about, at what point should an abortion not be allowed? You know, the day before the due date.\par \par \uc2 She wouldn't answer that question. They pick up on these things. And for her to brag about Afghanistan, she bragged about Afghanistan. She said \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Unbelievable. 13 Americans.\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 RUBIO: He didn't get -- he was run out of there. And not only did, he was run out of there, we lost $90 billion worth of American equipment that they're parading down the street. There are a lot of real people in the real world who are not political junkies, who are going to vote and decide this election, who watched tonight, they saw the man that was president, and they remember their lives were better when he was president.\par \par \uc2 They were safer, they were more prosperous. We were more respected in the world. And then they saw this person, they didn't know a lot about her and now they're beginning to learn facts about her that I think will be decisive.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Senator, great to see you.\par \par \uc2 RUBIO: Thank you.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Thank you. Appreciate it. All right. Now, according to \uc2 The Washington Post\uc2 , the Harris campaign is now saying they want a second debate. What does that tell us? Joining us with more reaction to tonight's debate, Texas Senator Ted Cruz is with us. Senator, how do you interpret that and your overall thoughts on the debate tonight?\par \par \uc2 SEN. TED CRUZ (R-TX): Well, listen, I'm skeptical that Kamala's team will have her do a second debate. I think they