rything that you want to say. And the bottom line is fundamental, I hate Trump.\par \par \uc2 VANCE: That's exactly right. And also, look, both of them have records. That's what's different about this election. Almost any other election in my lifetime. You have two people with a record. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is proud of his record. \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is running away from her record because her record is higher grocery prices, homes that are unaffordable, a wide-open southern border, rising fentanyl deaths.\par \par \uc2 This is happening because of her failed leadership. And all we need to remind the American people of. And I think \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  did a great job of this tonight is the reason why these problems happen is because \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  failed to do her job.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You know, the thing is, she's 50 days, and prior to tonight, she does one interview, no press conferences. You're out there every day. Between you and President Trump, you're nearing what 50 combined and it's still a mystery. It's like the candidate Protection Program and the media keeps her in there. You know, I have all of these files, the Kamala files, the Walz files, them in their own words.\par \par \uc2 This was all available to ABC tonight. You said this about fracking. You said this about drilling. You said this about sex change operations that taxpayers pay for for criminals and for illegal immigrants, free housing, healthcare, education for illegal immigrants, the elimination of private health care. All of these positions that she's taken, you know, and it's amazing that we're this far -- that we're this close to an election we don't have these answers.\par \par \uc2 VANCE: That's exactly right. Well, she's running a campaign based on vibes, and she's running --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Vibes. What the hell is a vibe? Are we in the 60s?\par \par \uc2 VANCE: It feels like it sometimes. I feel like watching \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , like I've taken some psychedelics. But look, she is a total disaster, Sean. And she runs away from a record. This is the most striking thing is, if you're the vice president, you've been in power for 3-1/2 years, is she running by saying, look what we did to lower your grocery prices. Look what we did to make the world more secure.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: She can't.\par \par \uc2 VANCE: She can't because her record is one of failure. And we just have to remind the American people of this, Sean. I mean, look, I think if you watch the debate, you're sitting at home, you're an undecided voter. What you saw as a person who repeats slogans instead of respecting you enough to treat you like an adult. You know, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , and he gets criticized by this -- by the left of this, by the way.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  actually answers the questions because he respects the American people enough to treat them like citizens. That's why he does everyday debate. That's why he goes out there and talks to people, because he thinks he ought to try to win the people's vote, not just have it given to you.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: She also told a lot of lies about Project 2025. Project 2025 is her radical agenda for her. A national abortion ban. That wasn't true. She lied about her saying, in 2000, no, I didn't say I'm for fracking. Mandatory gun buyback, she said at the end of the debate, oh no, I never said that.\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Yes.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I'm a gun owner. I'm like, that is exactly what you said. Yes, you did. It's on tape. We have it. We played it.\par \par \uc2 VANCE: That's right. Well, that's the entire trick here, right? Is the media is helping \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  run away from a record. But we have her on tape saying all these things, Sean. And by the way, when she said that she supported a ban on fracking, then she changed her view in 2020, that's another complete fabrication. She has never once changed her view that she wanted to ban fracking and you're an American sitting at home.\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: -- she became the presumptive nominee.\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Well, that's right. She trades your mind in 2024 but not in 2020. So, another complete fabrication. But think about this, if you're a Pennsylvania energy worker or you're an American suffering from high utility and energy bills, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is telling you she wants to make you pay more and she wants to put these energy workers out of a job. It's a disgrace, but it's what she said in her own words. And we've got a record of success to run on. We just have to keep on doing it.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Let me ask you this, because I think this is very important. So, with 56 days, but we have early voting. We're one week away where early voting starts here in Pennsylvania. You spend -- you're spending a lot of time in Wisconsin, Michigan, Pennsylvania and one has to wonder, you know, to what extent has her past statements radical positions penetrated the consciousness of the American people?\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Look, I think they penetrated a little bit. And it's our job. Over the remaining 56 days of the campaign, you're right. Early voting starts in just a couple of weeks. It's our job to make it --\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Starts in a week.\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Sean, we have to do this every single day. We have to remind the American people of what she said. But this is not complicated. We just have to tell the truth. \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  wanted to ban fracking. She wanted to defund the police. She said it all on video. We just have to remind people of what she said. By the way, Sean, it's not just reminding people what she said. It's reminding what \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  did and has plans to do again.\par \par \uc2 We had prosperity, we had peace, we had the American Dream that started to feel alive again thanks to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's leadership. Sean, you know, I believe this. I think we've got the best workers, the best history and cultural traditions in the world. We've got the best natural resources in the most beautiful country. We've got failed leadership that is ruining our great inheritance as a country. We just need better leadership. It's that simple.\par \par \uc2 Good to see you, man.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Senator, good to see you. Appreciate it. We'll see out on the campaign trail. All right. One issue that did get a lot of attention from ABC's far left moderators was the weaponization of our Department of Justice. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  still made it a point of emphasis. Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : Every one of those cases was started by them against their political opponent, and I'm winning most of them and I will win the rest on appeal. And you saw that with the decision that came down just recently from the Supreme Court. I'm winning most of them, but those are cases, it's called weaponization. Never happened in this country. They weaponized the Justice Department.\par \par \uc2 Every one of those cases was involved with the DOJ from Atlanta and \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2  to the Attorney General of New York and the D.A. of New York. Every one of those cases, and then they say, oh, he was -- he's a criminal. They're the ones that made them go after me, it's weaponization, and they used it, and it's never happened in this country. They used it to try and win an election and fake cases.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Joining us now, someone who knows firsthand about the weaponization of justice. Live from the spin room, Robert F. Kennedy, Jr. Great to see you.\par \par \uc2 ROBERT F. KENNEDY, JR., FORMER INDEPENDENT 2024 PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE: Good to see you, Sean.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You left your party. A party that was near and dear to your father, to your uncle, I think it has no resemblance to the Democratic Party today. And this is the frustrating part abou