ddle- class family which I'm sure is nice but that doesn't answer why you have been in power for three and a half years and Americans are worse off. They did not pin her down and ask follow-up questions on all her flip-flop.\par \par \uc2 She acts like she's always been a big supporter of fracking, never addressed her open borders past. And so, yes, it was a three-on-one debate. It was disappointing that she didn't have her feet held to the fire by the moderators. They went out of their way to try to do that to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . But I think people that take away from this debate even with all that, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is the candidate that's going to change things, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is the candidate that as President Trump said in his closing statement, she's been there three and a half years, why hasn't she fixed any of these problems during that time. She does not have an answer to that question.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You know, it doesn't. But you know, at some point isn't it really the moderators? Isn't that their job? I mean, if you say you want a $93 trillion Green New Deal and you're going to eliminate the filibuster to pass it, shouldn't we ask that? If you want to mandate, you know, government health care and eliminate private insurance, shouldn't that have come up in this debate? If you want sex change operations paid for by taxpayers for convicted criminals and illegal immigrants, don't you think that would come up in a debate?\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS: Yes. Well, it was all about looking at all this stuff through a left-of-center prism. So, they were hitting Trump on of course January 6. They were hitting Trump on some of his statements about holding people accountable. All these different things that's right out of what a left-of- center person would do. They never hit her from the right.\par \par \uc2 She took more liberal positions when she ran for president than \uc2 Bernie Sanders\uc2  did on a wide variety of issues. And yet they acted