thing out. She went to wind and went to all this other stuff that doesn't work from an economic standpoint and even a visual standpoint. I don't get the wind. You take these gorgeous plains and deserts and all this stuff. They put these windmills up. They go up like a 30-story building in some cases. They destroy everything. They cut out all. And the environmentalist say aren't they wonderful. But it's the most expensive form of energy and it's never going to do for our country.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: So, if we look at the issues on the economy, on immigration, on law and order, on energy, and America's role in the world --\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : Yes. It's all covered.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Is there anything you could point to that you would say they have been successful on?\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: No, they have been unsuccessful at everything. And even the economy, I said as part of the economy, you've let 21 million people, more than that I think with all the gotaways, that's killing our economy.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: By the way, there are known terrorists, and we do have the murders and the rapes and the violent crimes.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: Oh, and you haven't seen anything yet. Wait till you see it in the months to come.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You know what scares me and I've said this on the air is by having open borders, unvetted illegal immigrants, that I don't think it's a matter of if, I think it's a matter of when that this country is going to be attacked.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : If you look at Springfield, Ohio. Look at what's happening there. You look at \uc2 Aurora\uc2  in Colorado. These beautiful little towns and little cities, small city, they're being taken over by illegal migrants. I mean, there are people that poured in and they have weapons like our military doesn't have. You know, they have AK-47s. They have weapons like our military doesn't have.\par \par \uc2 And you know, some sheriff in one of these towns where he's got two deputies and they -- they're not into this. There's no way they can protect the people from this. But look at what's going on in Springfield today, it's -- nobody's ever seen anything like it.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: We really appreciate it. I know your people are calling for you to roll. What made you come to the spin room?\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : I just felt I wanted to. I was very happy with the result. It's a very unfair situation. They've weaponized our government politically, so I mean, that's unfair. And I just felt we had a great night. And I'd come over here, actually gave a little bit of a news conference. We were swarmed.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: By the way, I could hear it.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: No, no --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You were interrupting my show by the way, just for the record.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : But I had to come over and do yours. I would hate like heck to leave here and I didn't do Sean.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: No, I would be mad.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : I would have been --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I would take that as a personal offense, there's no doubt.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : I would have been in a big trouble.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right, so no answer on their offer for a second debate?\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: Again, the reason you do a second debate is if you lose and they lost. And we looked at one poll. It was 92 to seven.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Yes.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : We looked at another one, 86 to three. I mean, we have all of these results coming in. But I'll think about it, yes. You know, very quick.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Mr. President, thank you for taking time.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : Thank you very much.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: We really appreciate it. Thank you, sir.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : I appreciate it. Thank you.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right, by the way, tomorrow you -- by the way, you're going to be on "FOX AND FRIENDS" tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: I am indeed, 6:45 in the morning.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Oh, boy.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : And then I'm going down to --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You're going to get a lot of sleep tonight.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: Then I'm going down to the World Trade Center to honor the people that died September 11th.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You know what scares me? We have known terrorists in the country.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : Yes.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And we don't know where they are and then -- and that's -- and we don't even know about the gotaways.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : More than we've ever had before times 10.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Scary.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : Yes, scary.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right, President Trump will be on "FOX AND FRIENDS" tomorrow morning. We'll have with more reaction to the debate from tonight. Be sure to tune in as we continue. We're live. We're in Philadelphia. We're in the spin room. One week from today, early voting in Pennsylvania, the Commonwealth, as we continue.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Joining us now with more on tonight's debate -- wow, we have two senators from South Carolina, Senator Tim Scott, \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2 , former 2024 Presidential Candidate, \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2 . By the way, you all had more time scheduled, but \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  stole it. What are you going to do?\par \par \uc2 Lindsey, we making your stand -- we're making you stand, so we're going to put you up first.\par \par \uc2 SEN. \uc2 LINDSEY GRAHAM\uc2  (R-SC): Well, this is the only time I'll ever be tall. I'm still not taller than him and he's sitting down. Terribly moderated debate, three against one.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Oh, it's awful.\par \par \uc2 GRAHAM: The best closing in presidential debate history. If you could have done it, why didn't you do it. One thing I wish we have done a little bit better is I gave you the most secure border in four years. When I left, mortgage rates were below three percent, gas was $1.87. We're energy independent. We're getting the Arabs and the Israelis making peace and you screwed it all up. And you're never going to fix it.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: It's amazing how we don't -- how much we don't know about her radical positions --\par \par \uc2 SEN. TIM SCOTT (R-SC): Absolutely not.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: -- after this debate because ABC sucked that bad.\par \par \uc2 VIVEK RAMASWAMY\uc2 , FORMER PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE: Yes.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: They really did.\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: And every position she's ever had, it's like a jailhouse Jesus conversion. What she believed before, she doesn't believe again. I look at it as a Kamala of the B.C. Before the convention, she was absolutely opposed to fracking. The energy industry has been decimated under this administration. Think about the border.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Why would she said she changed the position in 2000?\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: Yes, 100 percent. It was -- it wasn't just that though. The border, she now wants a wall. They've allowed the greatest invasion in the history of our country to pour across our Southern Border.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: The people in South Carolina I am sure have no problem with free housing, health care, education, and sex change operations for illegal aliens and convicted felons. I mean, how do you not ask that question?\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: 100 percent.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: How do not ask that?\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: We need moderators that are not an extension of the \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  for president campaign.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: That's true.\par \par \uc2 RAMASWAMY: So, you know, I'm always going to give it to you straight. So, a few things I would say is did she exceed the very low expectations that were set for her? Yes, she did. That being said, if you were going to fact- check one candidate, you can't not -- or perceived to fact-check. Some of those weren't even real fact-checks. You have to apply the same standard to the other candidate. They absolutely failed to do that tonight.\par \par \uc2 I do think the strongest moment for either candidate that'll matter three weeks from now is actually \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  being crystal clear on his position on abortion. \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and their campaign have consistently been stating outright as though it's a fact that he would sign a federal abortion ban. He did a good job tonight saying that this is an issue for the states. It's issue where different Republicans may even differ. But he got a chance to make his position known on one of the issues where Democrats were trying to hang Republicans out to dry. And I thought he excelled at that. It's the most underappreciated part of tonight.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I actually think you're right on the money here because I think the reason we didn't have the red wave in 2022 was because of that issue. And it was demagogued to death and lied about. And what do you think some of the best moments were?\par \par \uc2 GRAHAM: His closing.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: What?\par \par \uc2 GRAHAM: His closing.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Yes.\par \par \uc2 GRAHAM: Everything he say you're going to do to make our country better, you've had three and a half years. Where have you been?\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Why don't you go back to Washington tonight?\par \par \uc2 GRAHAM: So -- and why don't you go do something while you're still in power. We're nation in decline. He made the case we're going in the wrong direction. And he nailed at the end by saying you're all talk. You're not going to pass a bill to restore Roe v Wade. You're not -- you're all talk.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: That was a good moment too.\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: He's already done it. You know the numbers as well as anybody. You're brilliant. The lowest unemployment rate for demographic groups all across the country under his four years. The poorest Americans had their wages growing faster than the richest Americans. We saw funding for HBCUs hit a record number under \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Here's a president that created more than seven million jobs, two-thirds going to women and minorities. But beyond that, a nine percent raise for our military. The president of the United States is a strong commander-in- chief. No ground wars in Europe. No force invasion in Israel. We need four more years of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I look at the situation on the border. Free housing, healthcare, education, and sex change operations, but more importantly, we have all these dead Americans. It's not just Laken Riley, and Rachel Morin, and Jocelyn Nungaray. It is dozens and dozens of murdered Americans, raped Americans, violent crimes against Americans, the cost to Americans. And we have known terrorists in the country.\par \par \uc2 Now, Lindsey, I bring this up to you and I see your face go wide every time. It is how is every American not like wanting that border secure?\par \par \uc2 RAMASWAMY: So, I thought actually -- I thought on the substance Trump nailed it on the abortion question, but my favorite moment of the debate was actually on this question.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: What?\par \par \uc2 RAMASWAMY: The essence of this debate was \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 ' words versus her action. Action speak louder than words. And where I think \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  nailed it was that moment in the debate where he looked at her and said, why don't we just end this now? You go back to Washington, D.C. and you and your boss either sign a bill or sign an executive action closing the border now. Is that more important than any legislation --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: They don't need legislation.\par \par \uc2 RAMASWAMY: They don't need legislation. And I think the way he highlighted that, that almost gets to the philosophical core of tonight's debate. It's all talk. You have the chance to go with action to actually solve that problem and you're not. For me I thought that was the single most powerful moment where he landed on the single most important issue in this election which is mass illegal migration into the country.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: That would be the economy. And we didn't even get to her high taxes, unrealized capital gains. There's so much on the table.\par \par \uc2 GRAHAM: Tomorrow is 9/11 in about 30-something seconds. I've never been more worried about another 9/11 for two reasons, our withdrawal from Afghanistan put as every terrorism on steroids and a broken border.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right, guys, good to see you all. I appreciate it. That's all the time we have left this evening. Back at our normal time, 9:00 Eastern tomorrow. Stay with the Fox News Channel continuing coverage of tonight's presidential debate. Trace Gallagher takes it from here.\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2024 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2024 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document SHAN000020240911ek9a00001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 Fox News Democracy '24: Presidential Debate; Harris And Trump Face Off In High-Stakes Debate\b0\par\par\uc2 12,380 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 September 2024\par \uc2 Fox News: Live Event\par \uc2 FXLV\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2024 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2024 ASC Services II Media, LLC.  All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR, ABC NEWS HOST: Good evening. I'm David Muir. And thank you for joining us for tonight's ABC News presidential debate. We want to welcome viewers watching on ABC and around the world tonight.\par \par \uc2 Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  are just moments away from taking the stage in this unprecedented race for president.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS, ABC NEWS HOST: And I'm Linsey Davis.\par \par \uc2 Tonight's meeting could be the most consequential event of their campaigns, with Election Day now less than two months away.\par \par \uc2 For Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , this is her first debate since President Biden withdrew from the race on July 21. Of course, that decision followed his debate against President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in June. Since then, this race has taken on an entirely new dynamic.\par \par \uc2 MUIR: And that brings us to the rules of tonight's debate, 90 minutes with two commercial breaks. No topics or questions have been shared with the campaigns.\par \par \uc2 The candidates will have two minutes to answer questions. And this is the clock. That's what they will be seeing, two minutes for rebuttals and one minute for follow-ups, clarifications or responses.\par \par \uc2 Their microphones will only be turned on when it's their turn to speak, no prewritten notes allowed. There is no audience here tonight in this hall at the \uc2 National Constitution Center\uc2 . This is an intimate setting for two candidates who have never met.\par \par \uc2 DAVIS: President Trump won the coin toss. He chose to deliver the final closing statement of the evening.\par \par \uc2 Vice President Harris selected the podium to the right.\par \par \uc2 MUIR: So let's now welcome the candidates to the stage, Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 KAMALA HARRIS\uc2  (D), VICE PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES, CURRENT PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE: \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 . Let's have a good debate.\par \par \uc2 DONALD TRUMP\uc2  (R), FORMER PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES, CURRENT PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE: Nice to see you. Have fun.\par \par \uc2 HARRIS: Thank you.\par \par \uc2 MUIR: Welcome to you both. It's wonderful to have you. It's an honor to have you both here tonight.\par \par \uc2 DAVIS: Good evening. We are looking forward to a spirited and thoughtful debate.\par \par \uc2 MUIR: So let's get started.\par \par \uc2 I want to begin tonight with the issue that voters repeatedly say is their number one issue. And that is the economy and the cost of living in this country.\par \par \uc2 Vice President Harris, you and President Trump were elected four years ago, and your opponent on the stage here tonight often asks his supporters, are you better off than you were four years ago? When it comes to the economy, do you believe Americans are better off than they were four years ago?\par \par \uc2 HARRIS: So, I was raised as a middle-class kid. And I am actually the only person on this stage who has a plan that is about lifting up the middle class and working people of America.\par \par \uc2 I believe in the ambition, the aspirations, the dreams of the American people. And that is why I imagine and have actually a plan to build what I call an opportunity economy, because here's the thing. We know that we have a shortage of homes and housing. And the cost of housing is too expensive for far too many people.\par \par \uc2 We know that young families need support to raise their children. And I intend on extending a tax cut for those families of $6,000, which is the largest child tax credit that we have given in a long time, so that those young families can afford to buy a crib, buy a car seat, buy clothes for their children.\par \par \uc2 My passion, one of them, is small businesses. I was actually -- my mother raised my sister and me, but there was a woman who helped raise us. We call her our second mother. She was a small business owner. I love our small businesses.\par \par \uc2 My plan is to give a $50,000 tax deduction to start-up small businesses, knowing they are part of the backbone of America's economy.\par \par \uc2 My opponent, on the other hand, his plan is to do what he has done before, which is to provide a tax cut for billionaires and big corporations, which will result in $5 trillion to America's deficit.\par \par \uc2 HARRIS: My opponent has a plan that I call the Trump sales tax, which would be a 20 percent tax on everyday goods that you rely on to get through the month.\par \par \uc2 Economists have said that that Trump sales tax would actually result for middle-class families in about $4,000 more a year because of his policies and his ideas about what should be the backs of middle-class people paying for tax cuts for billionaires.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR, ABC NEWS MODERATOR: President Trump, I'll give you two minutes.\par \par \uc2 DONALD TRUMP\uc2  (R), PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE: First of all, I have no sales tax. That's an incorrect statement. She knows that. We're doing tariffs on other countries. Other countries are going to finally, after 75 years, pay us back for all that we've done for the world. And the tariff will be substantial in some cases.\par \par \uc2 I took in billions and billions of dollars, as you know, from China. In fact, they never took the tariff off because it was so much money they can't. It would totally destroy everything that they've set out to do. They've taken in billions of dollars from China and other places. They've left the tariffs on. When I had it, I had tariffs and yet I had no inflation.\par \par \uc2 Look, we've had a terrible economy because inflation has -- which is really known as a country buster. It breaks up countries. We have inflation like very few people have ever seen before. Probably the worst in our nation's history. We were at 21 percent. But that's being generous because many things are 50 percent, 60 percent, 70 percent, and 80 percent higher than they were just a few years ago.\par \par \uc2 This has been a disaster for people, for the middle class but for every class. On top of that we have millions of people pouring into our country from prisons and jails, from mental institutions and insane asylums. And they're coming in and they're taking jobs that are occupied right now by African-Americans and Hispanics and also unions. Unions are going to be affected very soon. And you see what's happening.\par \par \uc2 You see what's happening with towns throughout the United States. You look at Springfield, Ohio. You look at \uc2 Aurora\uc2  in Colorado. They are taking over the towns. They're taking over buildings. They're going in violently. These are the people that she and Biden let into our country. And they're destroying our country. They're dangerous. They're at the highest level of criminality. And we have to get them out. We have to get them out fast.\par \par \uc2 I created one of the greatest economies in the history of our country. I'll do it again and even better.\par \par \uc2 MUIR: We are going to get to immigration and border security during this debate. But I would like to let Vice President Harris respond on the economy here.\par \par \uc2 HARRIS: Well, I would love to. Let's talk about what \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  left us. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  left us the worst unemployment since the Great Depression. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  left us the worst public health epidemic in a century. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  left us the worst attack on our democracy since the Civil War. And what we have done is clean up \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's mess. What we have done and what I intend to do is build on what we know are the aspirations and the hopes of the American people.\par \par \uc2 But I'm going to tell you all in this debate tonight you're going to hear from the same old tired playbook, a bunch of lies, grievances and name- calling. What you're going to hear tonight is a detailed and dangerous plan called Project 2025 that the former president intends on implementing if he were elected again.\par \par \uc2 I believe very strongly that the American people want a president who understands the importance of bringing us together knowing we have so much more in common than what separates us. And I pledge to you to be a president for all Americans.\par \par \uc2 MUIR: President Trump, I'll give you a minute here to respond.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: Number one, I have nothing to do, as you know and as she knows better than anyone, I have nothing to do with Project 2025. That's out there. I haven't read it. I don't want to read it purposely. I'm not going to read it. This was a group of people that got together, they came up with some ideas. I guess some good, some bad. But it makes no difference. I have nothing to do.\par \par \uc2 Everybody knows I'm an open book. Everybody knows what I'm going to do. Cut taxes very substantially and create a great economy like I did before. We had the greatest economy. We got hit with a pandemic. And the pandemic was not since 1917 where 100 million people died has there been anything like it. We did a phenomenal job with the pandemic.\par \par \uc2 We handed them over a country where the economy and where the stock market was higher than it was before the pandemic came in. Nobody has ever seen anything like it. We made ventilators for the entire world. We got gowns. We got masks. We did things that nobody thought possible. And people give me credit for rebuilding the military. They give me credit for a lot of things. But not enough credit for the great job we did with the pandemic.\par \par \uc2 But the only jobs they got were bounce-back jobs. These were jobs, bounce- back. And it bounced back and it went to their benefit. But I was the one that created them. They know it and so does everybody else.\par \par \uc2 MUIR: Vice President Harris, I'll let you respond.\par \par \uc2 HARRIS: So \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has no plan for you. And when you look at his economic plan, it's all about tax breaks for the richest people. I am offering what I've described as an opportunity economy.\par \par \uc2 HARRIS: And the best economists in our country, if not the world, have reviewed our relative plans for the future of America. What \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  has said is that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's plan would make the economy worse. Mine would strengthen the economy.\par \par \uc2 What the \uc2 Wharton School\uc2  has said is \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's plan would actually explode the deficit. Sixteen Nobel laureates have described his economic plan as something that would increase inflation and by the middle of next year would invite a recession.\par \par \uc2 You just have to look at where we are and where we stand on the issues. And I'd invite you to know that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  actually has no plan for you because he is more interested in defending himself than he is in looking out for you.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : That's just a sound bite. They gave her that to say. Look, I went to the Wharton School of Finance and many of those professors, the top professors, think my plan is a brilliant plan. It's a great plan. It's a plan that's going to bring up our worth, our value as a country. It's going to make people want to be able to go and work and create jobs and create a lot of good, solid money for our company -- for our country.\par \par \uc2 And just to finish off, she doesn't have a plan. She copied Biden's plan and it's like four sentences, like run, spot, run, four sentences that are just, oh, we'll try and lower taxes. She doesn't have a plan. Take a look at her plan. She doesn't have a plan.\par \par \uc2 MUIR: Mr. President, I do want to drill down on something you both brought up. The Vice President brought up your tariffs. You responded. And let's drill down on this because your plan is what she calls is essentially a national sales tax. Your proposal calls for tariffs, as you pointed out here, on foreign imports across the board. You recently said that you might double your plan, imposing tariffs up to 20% on goods coming into this country.\par \par \uc2 As you know, many economists say that with tariffs at that level, costs are then passed on to the consumer. Vice President Harris has argued it'll mean higher prices on gas, food, clothing, medication, arguing it costs the typical family nearly $4,000 a year. Do you believe Americans can afford higher prices because of tariffs?\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : They're not going to have higher prices. What's going to have and who's going to have higher prices is China and all of the countries that have been ripping us off for years. I charge -- I was the only president ever. China was paying us hundreds of billions of dollars. And so were other countries. And, you know, if she doesn't like them, they should have gone out and they should have immediately cut the tariffs. But those tariffs are there three and a half years now under their administration.\par \par \uc2 We are going to take in billions of dollars, hundreds of billions of dollars. I had no inflation, virtually no inflation. They had the highest inflation, perhaps in the history of our country, because I've never seen a worse period of time. People can't go out and buy cereal or bacon or eggs or anything else. These -- the people of our country are absolutely dying with what they've done. They've destroyed the economy.\par \par \uc2 And all you have to do is look at a poll. The polls say 80 and 85 and even 90% that the Trump economy was great, that their economy was terrible.\par \par \uc2 MUIR: Vice President Harris, I do want to ask for your response. And you heard what the president said there because the Biden administration did keep a number of the Trump tariffs in place. So how do you respond?\par \par \uc2 HARRIS: Well, let's be clear that the Trump administration resulted in a trade deficit, one of the highest we've ever seen in the history of America. He invited trade wars. You want to talk about his deal with China. What he ended up doing is under \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's presidency, he ended up selling American chips to China to help them improve and modernize their military, basically sold us out when a policy about China should be in making sure the United States of America wins the competition for the 21st century, which means focusing on the details of what that requires, focusing on relationships with our allies, focusing on investing in American based technology so that we win the race on A.I. on quantum computing, focusing on what we need to do to support America's workforce so that we don't end up having -- on the short end of the stick in terms of workers' rights.\par \par \uc2 But what \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  did -- let's talk about this with COVID, is he actually thanked President Xi for what he did during COVID. Look at his tweet. Thank you, President Xi. Exclamation point. When we know that Xi was responsible for lacking and not giving us transparency about the origins of COVID.\par \par \uc2 MUIR: President Trump, I'll let you respond.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: First of all, they bought their chips from Taiwan. We hardly make chips anymore because of philosophies like they have and policies like they have. I don't say her because she has no policy. Everything that she believed three years ago and four years ago is out the window. She's going to my philosophy now.\par \par \uc2 In fact, I was going to send her a MAGA hat. She's gone to my philosophy. But if she ever got elected, she'd change it, and it will be the end of our country.\par \par \uc2 She's a Marxist. Everybody knows she's a Marxist. Her father's a Marxist professor in economics, and he taught her well. But when you look at what she's done to our country, and when you look at these millions and millions of people that are pouring into our country monthly, where it's, I believe, 21 million people, not the 15 that people say, and I think it's a lot higher than the 21, that's bigger than New York state pouring in.\par \par \uc2 And just look at what they're doing to our country. They're criminals. Many of these people coming in are criminals. And that's bad for our economy, too. You know, you mentioned before, we'll talk about immigration later. Well, bad immigration is the worst thing that can happen to our economy. They have and she has destroyed our country with policy that's insane, almost policy that you'd say they have to hate our country.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR, ABC NEWS REPORTER: President Trump, thank you. Linsey?\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS, ABC NEWS REPORTER: I want to turn to the issue of abortion. President Trump, you've often touted that you were able to kill Roe v. Wade last year. You said that you were proud to be the most pro life president in American history. Then last month, you said that your administration would be great for women and their reproductive rights.\par \par \uc2 In your home state of Florida, you surprised many with regard to your six week abortion ban because you initially had said that it was too short. And you said, quote, I'm going to be voting that we need more than six weeks. But then the very next day, you reversed course and said you would vote to support the six week ban.\par \par \uc2 Vice President Harris says that women shouldn't trust you on the issue of abortion because you've changed your position so many times. Therefore, why should they trust you?\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: Well, the reason I'm doing that vote is because the plan is, as you know, the vote is they have abortion in the ninth month. They even have, and you can look at the Governor of West Virginia, the previous Governor of West Virginia, not the current Governor, who's doing an excellent job, but the Governor before, he said, the baby will be born and we will decide what to do with the baby. In other words, we'll execute the baby.\par \par \uc2 And that's why I did that, because that predominates, because they're radical. The Democrats are radical in that. And her Vice Presidential pick, which I think is a horrible pick, by the way, for our country, because he is really out of it. But her Vice Presidential pick says abortion in the ninth month is absolutely fine. He also says execution after birth. It's execution.\par \par \uc2 No longer abortion because the baby is born is OK. And that's not OK with me. Hence the vote. But what I did is something, for 52 years, they've been trying to get Roe v. Wade into the states. And through the genius and heart and strength of six Supreme Court Justices, we were able to do that.\par \par \uc2 Now, I believe in the exceptions for rape, incest, and life of the mother. I believe strongly in it. \uc2 Ronald Reagan\uc2  did also. 85% of Republicans do. Exceptions, very important. But we were able to get it. And now, states are voting on it. And for the first time, you're going to see, look, this is an issue that's torn our country apart for 52 years.\par \par \uc2 Every legal scholar, every Democrat, every Republican, liberal, conservative, they all wanted this issue to be brought back to the states where the people could vote. And that's what happened. Now, Ohio, the vote was somewhat liberal. Kansas, the vote was somewhat liberal, much more liberal than people would have thought.\par \par \uc2 But each individual state is voting. It's the vote of the people now. It's not tied up in the federal government. I did a great service in doing it. It took courage to do it, and the Supreme Court had great courage in doing it. And I give tremendous credit to those six justices.\par \par \uc2 DAVIS: There is no state in this country where it's legal to kill a baby after it's born. Madam Vice President, I want to get your response to President Trump.\par \par \uc2 KAMALA HARRIS\uc2 , VICE PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES AND 2024 PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE: Well, as I said, you're going to hear a bunch of lies, and that's not actually a surprising fact. Let's understand how we got here. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  hand selected three members of the \uc2 United States Supreme Court\uc2  with the intention that they would undo the protections of Roe v. Wade.\par \par \uc2 And they did exactly as he intended. And now, in over 20 states, there are Trump abortion bans, which make it criminal for a doctor or nurse to provide healthcare. In one state, it provides prison for life. Trump abortion bans that make no exception, even for rape and incest, which understand what that means. A survivor of a crime of violation to their body does not have the right to make a decision about what happens to their body next.\par \par \uc2 HARRIS: That is immoral. And one does not have to abandon their faith or deeply held beliefs to agree the government and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  certainly should not be telling a woman what to do with her body. I have talked with women around around our country. You want to talk about this is what people wanted, pregnant women who want to carry a pregnancy to term suffering from a miscarriage being denied care in an emergency room because the healthcare providers are afraid they might go to jail and she's bleeding out in a car in the parking lot? She didn't want that. Her husband didn't want that.\par \par \uc2 A 12 or 13-year-old survivor of incest being forced to carry a pregnancy to term. They don't want that.\par \par \uc2 And I pledge to you, when Congress passes a bill to put back in place the protections of Roe v. Wade, as president of the United States, I will proudly sign it into law.\par \par \uc2 But understand, if \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  were to be re-elected, he will sign a national abortion ban.\par \par \uc2 Understand in his Project 2025, there would be a national abortion -- a monitor that would be monitoring your pregnancies, your miscarriages.\par \par \uc2 I think the American people believe that certain freedoms, in particular the freedom to make decisions about one's own body, should not be made by the government.\par \par \uc2 DAVIS: Thank you, Vice President Harris.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: Well, there she goes again. It's a lie. I'm not signing a ban. And there's no reason to sign a ban because we've gotten what everybody wanted.\par \par \uc2 Democrats, Republicans and everybody else, at every legal scholar, wanted it to be brought back into the States. And the States are voting. And it may take a little time.\par \par \uc2 But for 52 years, this issue has torn our country apart. And they've wanted it back in the States. And I did something that nobody thought was possible. The States are now voting.\par \par \uc2 What she says is an absolute lie. And as far as the abortion ban, no, I'm not in favor of abortion ban, but it doesn't matter, because this issue has now been taken over by the states.\par \par \uc2 DAVIS: Would you veto a national abortion ban if you could?\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: Well, I won't have to because again, two things. Number one, she said she'll go back to Congress. She'll never get the vote. It's impossible for her to get the vote, especially now with the 50/50 and essentially 50/50 in both Senate and the House. She's not going to get the vote. She can't get the vote. She won't even come close to it. So it's just talk.\par \par \uc2 You know what it reminds me of when they said they're going to get student loans terminated and it ended up being a total catastrophe. The student loans.\par \par \uc2 And then her, I think probably her boss, if you call him a boss, he spends all his time on the beach.\par \par \uc2 But look, her boss went out and said, we'll do it again. We'll do it a different way. He went out, got rejected again by the Supreme Court. So all these students got taunted with this whole thing about this whole idea.\par \par \uc2 And how unfair that would have been part of the reason they lost to the millions and millions of people that had to pay off their student loans. They didn