 Vice President Harris, in your last run for president you said you wanted to ban fracking. Now you don't. You wanted mandatory government buyback programs for assault weapons. Now your campaign says you don't. You supported decriminalizing border crossings. Now you're taking a harder line. I know you say that your values have not changed. So then why have so many of your policy positions changed?\par \par \uc2 HARRIS: So my values have not changed. And I'm going to discuss every one - - at least every point that you've made. But in particular let's talk about fracking because we're here in Pennsylvania. I made that very clear in 2020. I will not ban fracking. I have not banned fracking as vice president of the United States. And in fact, I was the tie-breaking vote on the Inflation Reduction Act, which opened new leases for fracking.\par \par \uc2 My position is that we have got to invest in diverse sources of energy so we reduce our reliance on foreign oil. We have had the largest increase in domestic oil production in history because of an approach that recognizes that we cannot over-rely on foreign oil.\par \par \uc2 As it relates to my values, let me tell you, I grew up a middle class kid, raised by a hardworking mother who worked and saved and was able to buy our first home when I was a teenager.\par \par \uc2 The values I bring to the importance of home ownership knowing not everybody got handed $400 million on a silver platter and then filed bankruptcy six times is a value that I bring to my work to say we are going to work with the private sector and home builders, to increase 3 million homes, increase by 3 million homes by the end of my first term.\par \par \uc2 My work that is related to having a friend when I was in high school who was sexually assaulted by her stepfather. And my focus then on protecting women and children from violent crime is based on a value that is deeply grounded in the importance of standing up for those who are most vulnerable.\par \par \uc2 My work that is about protecting Social Security and Medicare is based on longstanding work that I have done, protecting seniors from scams.\par \par \uc2 My values have not changed, and what is important is that there is a president who actually brings values and a perspective that is about lifting people up and not beating people down, and name-calling.\par \par \uc2 The true measure of the leader is the leader who actually understands the strength is not in beating people down. It's in lifting people pull up.\par \par \uc2 I intend to be that president.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS, ABC NEWSW MODERATOR: President Trump, your response?\par \par \uc2 DONALD TRUMP\uc2 , FORMER U.S. PRESIDENT & 2024 PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE: Well, first of all, I wasn't given $400 million. I wish I was.\par \par \uc2 My father was a Brooklyn builder, Brooklyn, Queens, and a great father. And I learned a lot from him.\par \par \uc2 But I was given a fraction of that, a tiny fraction, and I've built it into many, many billions of dollars, many, many billions. And when people see it, they are even surprised. So we don't have to talk about that.\par \par \uc2 Fracking? She's been against it for 12 years. Defund the police, she's been against that forever.\par \par \uc2 She gave all that stuff up very wrongly, very horribly, and everybody's laughing at it, okay? They're all laughing at it.\par \par \uc2 She gave up at least 12 and probably 14 or 15 different policies like she was big on defund the police. In Minnesota, she went out -- wait a minute, I'm talking now if you don't mind, please? Does that sound familiar?\par \par \uc2 HARRIS: (INAUDIBLE)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : She went out -- she went out in Minnesota and wanted to let criminals that killed people, that burned down Minneapolis, she went out and raised money to get them out of jail. She did things that nobody would ever think of.\par \par \uc2 Now, she wants to do transgender operations on illegal aliens that are in prison. This is a radical left liberal that would do this. She wants to confiscate your guns and she will never allow fracking in Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 If she won the election, fracking in Pennsylvania will end on day one.\par \par \uc2 Just to finish one thing so important in my opinion. So I got the oil business going like nobody has ever done before. They took -- when they took over, they got rid of it, started getting rid of it, and the prices were going up the roof. They immediately let these guys go to where they were.\par \par \uc2 I would have been five times, four times, five times higher because you're talking about three and a half years ago. They got it up to where I was because they had no choice because the prices of energy would were quadrupling and doubling. You saw what happened to gasoline. So they said, let's go back to Trump.\par \par \uc2 But if she won the election, the day after that election, they'll go back to destroying our country. And oil will be dead. Fossil fuel will be dead. We'll go back to windmills and we'll go back to solar where they need a whole desert to get some energy to come out.\par \par \uc2 You ever see a solar plant? By the way, I'm a big fan of solar, but they take 400, 500 acres of desert soil. These are not good things for the environment that she understands.\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 DAVIS: President Trump, we have a lot of issues that we have to get to. We're out of time. Thank you.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR, ABC NEWS MODERATOR: Linsey, thank you.\par \par \uc2 We have an election in just 56 days, and -- and I want to talk about the peaceful transfer of power which, of course, we all know is a cornerstone of our democracy and the role of a president in a moment of crisis.\par \par \uc2 Mr. President, on January 6th, you told your supporters to march to the Capitol. You said you would be right there with them. The country and the world saw what played out of the Capitol that day, the officers coming under attack.\par \par \uc2 Aides in the West Wings say you watched it unfold on television off the Oval Office. You did send out tweets but it was more than two hours before you sent out that video message, telling your supporters to go home.\par \par \uc2 Is there anything you regret about what you did on that day?\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : You just said a thing that isn't covered.\par \par \uc2 Peacefully and patriotically, I said during my speech, not later on, peacefully and patriotically. And nobody on the other side was killed. Ashli Babbitt was shot by an out-of-control police officer that should have never, ever shot her. It's a disgrace.\par \par \uc2 But we didn't do -- this group of people that have been treated so badly. I ask, what about all the people that are pouring into our country and killing people that she allowed to pour in? She was the border czar. Remember that. She was the border czar.\par \par \uc2 She doesn't want to be called the border czar because she's embarrassed by the border. In fact, she said at the beginning: Well, I'm surprised you're not talking about the border yet.\par \par \uc2 That's because she knows what a bad job they have done. What about those people? What's -- when are they going to be prosecuted? When are these people from countries all over the world, not just South America -- they're coming in from all over the world, David, all over the world.\par \par \uc2 And crime rates are down all over the world because of it.\par \par \uc2 MUIR: But let me just ask you.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : But one those -- David, when are those people going to be prosecuted? When are the people that burned down Minneapolis going to be prosecuted or in Seattle? They went into Seattle. They took over a big percentage of the city of Seattle.\par \par \uc2 When are those people going to be prosecuted?\par \par \uc2 MUIR: But let me just ask you.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : You might ask her that question.\par \par \uc2 MUIR: You were the president. You were watching it unfold on television. It's a very simple question as we move forward toward another election.\par \par \uc2 Is there anything you regret about what you did on that day, yes or no?\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : I had nothing to do with that, other than they asked me to make a speech. I showed up for a speech. I said, I think it's going to be big.\par \par \uc2 I went to \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  and the mayor of Washington, D.C., and the mayor put it back in writing, as you know. I said, you know, this is going to be a very big rally or whatever you want to call it. And, again, it wasn't done by me. It was done by others.\par \par \uc2 I said, I'd like to give you 10,000 National Guard or soldiers. They rejected me. \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  rejected me. It was just two weeks ago, her daughter has a tape of her saying she is fully responsible for what happened.\par \par \uc2 They want to get rid of that tape. It would have never happened if \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  and the mayor of Washington did their jobs. I wasn't responsible for security. \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  was responsible. She didn't do her job.\par \par \uc2 MUIR: The question was about you as president, not about former Speaker Pelosi.\par \par \uc2 But I do want Vice President Harris to respond here.\par \par \uc2 HARRIS: I was at the Capitol on January 1. I was the vice president-elect. I was also an acting senator. I was there.\par \par \uc2 And on that day, the president of the United States incited a violent mob to attack our nation's Capitol, to desecrate our nation's Capitol. On that day, 140 law enforcement officers were injured, and some died.\par \par \uc2 And, understand, the former president has been indicted and impeached for exactly that reason.\par \par \uc2 But this is not an isolated situation. Let's remember Charlottesville, where there was a mob of people carrying tiki torches spewing antisemitic hate. And what did the president then at the time say? There were fine people on each side.\par \par \uc2 Let's remember that, when it came to the Proud Boys, a militia, the president said, the former president said, "Stand back and stand by."\par \par \uc2 So, for everyone watching who remembers what January 6 was, I say, we don't have to go back. Let's not go back. We're not going back. It's time to turn the page.\par \par \uc2 And if that was a bridge too far for you, well, there is a place in our campaign for you to stand for country, to stand for our democracy, to stand for rule of law, and to end the chaos, and to end the approach that is about attacking the foundations of our democracy because you don't like the outcome.\par \par \uc2 And be clear. On that point, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  the candidate has said in this election, there will be a bloodbath if this and the outcome of this election is not to his liking.\par \par \uc2 Let's turn the page on this. Let's not go back. Let's chart a course for the future and not go backwards to the past.\par \par \uc2 MUIR: Let me just follow up here.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: (OFF-MIKE) bloodbath, it was a different term, and it was a term that related to energy, because they have destroyed our energy business. That was where bloodbath was.\par \par \uc2 Also, on Charlottesville, that story has been, as you would say, debunked. Laura Ingraham, \uc2 Sean Hannity\uc2 , Jesse, all of these people, they covered it. If they go an extra sentence, they will see it was perfect. It was debunked in almost every newspaper. But they still bring it up, just like they bring 2025 up. They bring all of this stuff up.\par \par \uc2 I ask you this. You talk about the Capitol. Why are we allowing these millions of people to come through on the southern border? How come she's not doing anything. And I'll tell you what I would do, and I would be very proud to do it. I would say we would both leave this debate right now. I'd like to see her go down to Washington, D.C. during this debate because we're wasting a lot of time. Go down to -- because she's been so bad, it's so ridiculous.\par \par \uc2 Go down to Washington, D.C. and let her sign a bill to close up the border because they have the right to do it. They don't need bills. They have the right to do it. The president of the United States, you'll get him out of bed. You'll wake him up at 4:00 in the afternoon.\par \par \uc2 MUIR: All right.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : You'll say come on, come on down to the office, let's sign a bill. If he signs a bill that the border is closed, all he has to do is say it to the Border Patrol, who are phenomenal. If they do that the border is closed.\par \par \uc2 MUIR: Mr. President --\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : Those people are killing many people unlike J-6.\par \par \uc2 MUIR: I want to -- we talked immigration here tonight. I do want to focus on this next issue to both of you because it really brings us -- this into focus. Truth in these times that we're living in.\par \par \uc2 Mr. President, for three and a half years after you lost the 2020 election you repeatedly falsely claimed that you won, many times saying you won in a landslide. In the past couple of weeks leading up to this debate you have said, quote, "You lost by a whisker," that you, quote, "didn't quite make it," that you came up a little bit short. Are you --\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : I said that?\par \par \uc2 MUIR: Are you now acknowledging that you lost in 2020?\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: No, I don't acknowledge that at all.\par \par \uc2 MUIR: But you did say it.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : I said that sarcastically. You know that. It was said, oh, we lost by a whisker. That was said sarcastically.\par \par \uc2 Look, there's so much proof. All you have to do is look at it. And they should have sent it back to the legislatures for approval. I got almost 75 million votes. The most votes any sitting president has ever gotten. I was told if I got 63, which was what I got in 2016, you can't be beaten.\par \par \uc2 The election, people should never be thinking about an election as fraudulent. We need two things. We need walls. We need -- and we have to have it. We have to have borders. And we have to have good elections. Our elections are bad. And a lot of these illegal immigrants coming in, they're trying to get them to vote.\par \par \uc2 They can't even speak English. They don't even know what country they're in practically. And these people are trying to get them to vote. And that's why they're allowing them to come into our country.\par \par \uc2 MUIR: I did watch all of these pieces of video. I didn't detect the sarcasm, lost by a whisker, we didn't quite make it. And we should just point out here as clarification, and you know this, you and your allies, 60 cases in front of many judges. Many of them Republicans --\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: No judge looked at it.\par \par \uc2 MUIR: -- and said there was no widespread fraud.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : They said we didn't have standing. That's the other thing. They said we didn't have standing. A technicality. Can you imagine a system where a person in an election doesn't have standing? The president of the United States doesn't have standing? That's how we lost.\par \par \uc2 If you look at the facts, and I'd love to have you -- you do a special on you. I'll show you Georgia and I'll show you Wisconsin and I'll show you Pennsylvania and I'll show you -- we have so many facts and statistics. But you know what? That doesn't matter. Because we have to solve the problem that we have right now. That's old news. And the problem that we have right now is we have a nation in decline and they have put it into decline.\par \par \uc2 We have a nation that is dying, David.\par \par \uc2 MUIR: Mr. President, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Vice President Harris, you heard the president there tonight. He said he didn't say that he lost by a whisker. So he still believes he did not lose the election that was won by President Biden and yourself.\par \par \uc2 But I do want to ask you about something that's come up in the last couple of days. This was a post from President Trump about this upcoming election just weeks away. He said, "When I win, those people who cheated," and then he lists donors, voters, election officials, he says will be prosecuted to the fullest extent of the law, which will include long-term prison sentences.\par \par \uc2 One of your campaign's top lawyers responded saying, "We won't let \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  intimidate us. We won't let him suppress the vote." Is that what you believe he's trying to do here?\par \par \uc2 HARRIS: \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was fired by 81 million people. So let's be clear about that. And clearly he is having a very difficult time processing that. But we cannot afford to have a president of the United States who attempts as he did in the past to upend the will of the voters in a free and fair election.\par \par \uc2 And I'm going to tell you that I have traveled the world as vice president of the United States. And world leaders are laughing at \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . I have talked with military leaders, some of whom worked with you. And they say you're a disgrace.\par \par \uc2 And when you then talk in this way in a presidential debate and deny what over and over again are court cases you have lost, because you did in fact lose that election, it leads one to believe that perhaps we do not have in the candidate to my right the temperament or the ability to not be confused about fact. That's deeply troubling. And the American people deserve better.\par \par \uc2 MUIR: I'll give you one minute to respond, Mr. President.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : Let me just say about world leaders, \uc2 Viktor Orban\uc2 , one of the most respected men -- they call him a strong man. He's a -- he's a tough person, smart Prime Minister of Hungary. They said why is the whole world blowing up? Three years ago, it wasn't. Why is it blowing up? He said because you need Trump back as president. They were afraid of him. China was afraid and I don't like to use the word afraid, but I'm just quoting him. China was afraid of him. North Korea was afraid of him. Look at what's going on with North Korea, by the way, he said Russia was afraid of him.\par \par \uc2 I ended the \uc2 Nord Stream 2\uc2  pipeline and Biden put it back on day one. But he ended the XL pipeline. The XL pipeline in our country, he ended that. But he let the Russians build a pipeline going all over Europe and heading into Germany, the biggest pipeline in the world.\par \par \uc2 Look \uc2 Viktor Orban\uc2  said it. He said the most respected most feared person is \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . We had no problems when Trump was president. But when this weak, pathetic man, that you saw at a debate just a few months ago that if he weren't in that debate, he'd be running instead of her. She got no votes. He got 14 million votes. What you did, you talk about a threat to democracy? He got 14 million votes and they threw him out of office.\par \par \uc2 And you know what? I'll give you a little secret. He hates her. He can't stand her.\par \par \uc2 MUIR: Mr. President --\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : But he got 14 million votes. They threw him out. She got zero votes and when she ran, she was the first one to leave because she failed and now she's running. I don't understand it --\par \par \uc2 MUIR: Mr. President --\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : -- but I'm OK with it because --\par \par \uc2 MUIR: Mr. President, your time is up. Thank you.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : I think we're going to do very well.\par \par \uc2 MUIR: We've got a lot more to get to. Yes.\par \par \uc2 DAVIS: Turning now to the Israel-\uc2 Hamas\uc2  war and the hostages who are still being held, Americans among them. Vice President Harris, in December, you said, quote, "Israel has a right to defend itself." But you added, quote, "It matters how," saying international humanitarian law must be respected, Israel must do more to protect innocent civilians. You said that nine months ago now an estimated 40,000 Palestinians are dead, nearly 100 hostages remain.\par \par \uc2 Just last week Prime Minister \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  said, there's not a deal in the making. President Biden has not been able to break through the stalemate. How would you do it?\par \par \uc2 HARRIS: Well, let's understand how we got here on October 7 \uc2 Hamas\uc2 , a terrorist organization slaughtered 1,200 Israelis, many of them young people who are simply attending a concert. Women were horribly raped. And so absolutely, I said then, I say now. Israel has a right to defend itself. We would. And how it does so matters because it is also true far too many innocent Palestinians have been killed, children, mothers.\par \par \uc2 What we know is that this war must end. It must win and immediately and the way it will end is we need a ceasefire deal and we need the hostages out. And so we will continue to work around the clock on that, work around the clock. Also understanding that we must chart a course for a two-state solution. And in that solution there must be security for the Israeli people and Israel and in equal measure for the Palestinians.\par \par \uc2 But the one thing I will assure you always, I will always give Israel the ability to defend itself in particular as it rates to -- as it relates to Iran and any threat that Iran and its proxies posed to Israel. But we must have a two-state solution where we can rebuild Gaza, where the Palestinians have security, self-determination and the dignity they so rightly deserve.\par \par \uc2 DAVIS: President Trump, how would you negotiate with Netanyahu and also \uc2 Hamas\uc2  in order to get the hostages out and prevent the killing of more innocent civilians in Gaza?\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : If I were president it would have never started. If I were president Russia would have never ever -- I know Putin very well, he would have never -- and there was no threat of it either by the way for four years, have gone into Ukraine and killed millions of people when you add it up far worse than people understand what's going on over there.\par \par \uc2 But when she mentions about Israel all of a sudden she hates Israel. She wouldn't even meet with Netanyahu when he went to Congress to make a very important speech. She refused to be there because she was at a sorority party of hers. She wanted to go to the sorority party. She hates Israel. If she's president I believe that Israel will not exist within two years from now. And I've been pretty good at predictions. And I hope I'm wrong about that one.\par \par \uc2 She hates Israel. At the same time in her own way, she hates the Arab population because the whole place is going to get blown up, Arabs, Jewish people, Israel -- Israel will be gone. It would have never happened. Iran was broke under \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2024 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2024 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document FXLV000020240911ek9a0002t\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  And \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  Prepare For Crucial Debate Tomorrow; \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  And \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  Ties Up After Vice President's Summer Honeymoon; Afghanistan Exist Disaster: House GOP: Admin Lied, Misled Americans Over Withdrawal; Food For Thought: Media Focuses On Kamala's Cooking, Ignores Her Policies; Brilliant: Elton John Loves Trump's Little Rocket Man Nickname\b0\par\par\uc2 Jeanine Pirro, Jessica Tarlov, Jesse Watters, Dana Perino, Greg  Gutfeld \par \uc2 7,891 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 September 2024\par \uc2 Fox News: The Five\par \uc2 FOXFIV\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2024 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2024 ASC Services II Media, LLC.  All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 SANDRA SMITH, FOX NEWS CHANNEL HOST: -- celebrated icon on screen and off. James Earl Jones was 93 years old, passed away today.\par \par \uc2 All right, that -- OK, that does it for us.\par \par \uc2 JEANINE PIRRO, FOX NEWS CHANNEL LEGAL ANALYST: Hello everyone. I'm Judge Jeanine Pirro along with Jessica Tarlov, Jesse Watters Dana Perino and Greg Gutfeld. It's 5:00 in New York City, and this is THE FIVE.\par \par \uc2 Bernie Sanders dropping a bombshell on comrade Kamala right before the debate, the vice president is gearing up for her big showdown with former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  tomorrow night, and she's turning to method acting to prepare.\par \par \uc2 According to \uc2 The New York Times\uc2 , Harris has been holed up for five days in a Pittsburgh hotel doing highly choreographed debate practice sessions with an advisor who is dressed up like \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . "There's a stage and replica T.V. lighting and an advisor in full Lee Strasberg method acting mode, not just playing \uc2 Donald J. Trump\uc2 , but inhabiting him, wearing a boxy suit and a long tie."\par \par \uc2 And while Harris will be super careful to pretend that she's a moderate at the debate, socialist Bernie Sanders just blew her cover.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 KRISTEN WELKER, NBC NEWS ANCHOR: Do you think that she is abandoning her progressive ideals?\par \par \uc2 SEN. BERNIE SANDERS (I-VT): No, I don't think she is abandoning her ideals. I think she is trying to be pragmatic and doing what she thinks is right in order to win the election.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Harris giving this preview of how she plans to attack Trump.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 KAMALA HARRIS\uc2  (D), U.S. PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE: He tends to fight for himself, not for the American people, and I think that's going to come out during the course of the debate.\par \par \uc2 But you know, I expect that he's going to -- he's going to -- you know, I think he's going to lie. And you know, he has a playbook that he has used in the past, be it, you know, his attacks on President Obama or \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2 , so we should expect that some of that might come out.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: OK, Jesse, before I get into this specific since three years and nine months in the White House, 50 days without a real presser other than the one she did with the coach, associate coach, and five days on lockdown. What is Kamala so worried about, she is the Vice President?\par \par \uc2 JESSE WATTERS, FOX NEWS CHANNEL HOST: Well, she's worried about people getting to know Kamala, and she's insecure about who she is, and the hiding hasn't worked, it's backfired, and now we're going to talk about the polls. She's now tied, which means she's about to lose.\par \par \uc2 These aren't flip flops, what Bernie said, these are just lies. Trump should just say, she's not flip-flopping, she's a fraud. She's just saying whatever she needs to say to win. And she doesn't care if you lose, all she cares about is winning. She doesn't want to do the job. She just wants to get the job. That's what I would hammer.\par \par \uc2 And then I would just make sure everybody knows that she was for reparations, defunding the police, bailing out BLMers and abolishing ice, and keep it on policy, be steady. Be statesman-like, don't get baited, because that's what she's trying to do.\par \par \uc2 Her entire strategy is dependent on him snapping. So, as long as he doesn't snap, he'll just be fine. She's been very secretive. I would use that word secretive. And she's very dependent on handlers, and you don't want anybody in charge who's not dependent.\par \par \uc2 She's had good moments, though, Judge. We look back at some of her debates even as far back as going against D.A.s in 2003 she had two guys where she was running against. She comes out after they said the Willie Brown thing. She goes, they caught you in a massage parlor, and you're a deadbeat dad. Whoa.\par \par \uc2 So, she's had good moments like that. She had him against Kavanaugh. She's had him against Jeff Sessions, and she remembers she had it against Biden.\par \par \uc2 So, apparently, she's nervous, and the team is nervous because she keeps on trying to get in the weeds about policy. She's not going to win on policy. If she stays on policy, she's going to lose.\par \par \uc2 She's been over-preparing for these gotcha moments that she thinks is going to be able to make her win. If she has won, the media is going to say she won, but we'll see how Trump does. I think he's in a good position.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: You know, Jessica, what is it? 28 percent I think, is the number that don't know what her policies are, that really don't know what she stands for. And yet, when Bernie Sanders is asked if she's dropping her far-left policies. He says, "In order to win the election." He says, "She's trying to be pragmatic and do what she thinks is right in order to win the election." How Machiavellian is she?\par \par \uc2 JESSICA TARLOV, FOX NEWS CHANNEL CONTRIBUTOR: I'm sorry, does anyone who is running for elected office want to lose or feel OK about losing? I'm sure that Bernie Sanders sometimes in his darkest moments when he's sitting there with Jane (ph), says, if I had moderated a little bit, I was doing pretty well.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: So, she'll sell her leftist agenda?\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: No, she's -- it's not --\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: To win?\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: Oh, you mean, like, sell it out? She hasn't parroted any of these open border stuff, Medicare for all, defund the police, any of it since 2019 and I know that there's this debate about how much should she hew towards President Biden and what happened during the last four years, or three years, nine months, that is her record, for better or for worse, but that isn't a far-left record. That's a record that Bernie Sanders became the most vocal advocate and defender of anyone. He was going all the Sunday shows when it looked like Biden was going to be pushed out, he was like, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  needs to stay in. This man is accomplishing things that are good for America and that he had never even dreamed of having someone who was so good on climate action, for instance.\par \par \uc2 So, Bernie Sanders, it's not a gotcha moment in what he was saying, you said 28 percent don't know about where she stands. What I found to be one of the more interesting points of the New York Times Sienna poll, and we're going to talk about it a lot more later in the show, is how much room she has to grow with. 53 percent of young people, 43 percent of Latinos, 41 percent of Black voters, who all say that they want to know more about her.\par \par \uc2 Now, the issue has always been with Trump, has he hit his ceiling? It's clear from these numbers that Kamala, she may lose the election, but she still does have room to grow, and so she's got to tell these people, this is who I am, and this is how I'm going to govern for the next eight years.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: You know, Greg, the Harris campaign is already downplaying her performance before it even happens. What is that about?\par \par \uc2 GREG GUTFELD, FOX NEWS CHANNEL HOST: Well, I think that's a good strategy, because you can't lose if people you know, underestimate you. She'll always -- oh, she wasn't that bad. She wasn't that b