t do we know about Biden? He basically was like, no, I'm going forward. And what do we know about Harris? She made sure that everybody knew that she wrote on the history book of the Afghanistan withdrawal. Harris was here. She made it -- she wanted everybody to know she was the last person in the room to talk to.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Yes.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: So, then what -- you fast forward to the campaign. She knows this anniversary is coming up. She knows the report is coming up. What do they do? They try -- they trot this thing out again to say oh, it's all Trump's fault. But there's cameras everywhere. She could step out and make a statement. She could also have one of her people on background say Biden had no idea what he was doing or the Vice President makes no decisions on foreign policy. But she can't do that because she wrote the Harris was here on her book.\par \par \uc2 They also tried this with one other issue and that's with the job losses from COVID and the shutdown. They act and actually they'll say, it's unbelievable, that Biden would not have had any job losses because economy would not have shut down because they would have handled COVID much differently if they were in power. And it's just so unbelievable and that they're trying to rewrite this history. And obviously, it's not working either.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Yes. You know, Judge, Kamala blames Trump, but if it had actually gone right, she -- would she have credited Trump?\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: I think history has already given us an answer to that one. And obviously, if she wants to claim credit, she's got to take responsibility. And the truth is that a New York times poll shows that 50 percent blame Kamala a lot for the withdrawal. So -- and I think that feeds into the 44 percent, you know, who believe that she's this leftist Progressive.\par \par \uc2 But you know, I mean, there's so much that we can talk about. You know, Biden didn't listen to his generals. He didn't listen to the Pentagon. And according -- I think on page 26 of the -- of the report, the chief of staff of operations said President Biden had decided that we were going to leave and he was not listening to anybody.\par \par \uc2 And I will never forget -- for me, it's like when America crossed the \uc2 Rubicon\uc2  when the Biden Administration said, you know what, we're leaving. And yes, there'll be some Americans left behind. I -- you know, in my life as an American, you always believe that the cavalry is coming for you. And this was the first time in my life that I suddenly realized that they were politicians who didn't believe in that concept.\par \par \uc2 And in the end, what you had was, you know, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  who for whatever reason, I mean, whether or not it's -- you know, this callous foreign policy withdrawal that he had or the fact that he's been wrong on every foreign policy issue he's ever been involved in, according to \uc2 Bob Gates\uc2 . You know, you look at everything that's gone wrong. He comes in and he's funding Iran. Now there's terrorism all over the place right after Afghanistan. Russia invades Ukraine. I mean, the -- it's like the world fell apart when the world looked at what he did.\par \par \uc2 And then we had to have this Pineapple Express mission where we had to have people like Cory Mills and people in the military who had their own mission to get Americans and Afghans who helped us in the war in Afghanistan. I mean, these is -- this is a disgusting disgrace.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: You know, Jessica, you could argue that the Republicans are exploiting this catastrophe for political means, but the Dems were exploiting this whole exercise for political optics. They rushed the thing for a political reason. They wanted it out. They -- it was supposed to be timed when they shouldn't have. So, where do you stand on this absolute catastrophe that your party is responsible for?\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: I stand nowhere near that vantage point on this, a