e as nine of those injured are in the hospital, some with serious gun wounds. The shooter, 14 years old. He gave himself up immediately to school resource officers. It's not clear what his motivation was in this shooting, but authorities have already said, he will be charged with murder and tried as an adult. The sheriff here said what happened today was an act of pure evil.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: I never imagined that I would be speaking to the media in my career over something that happened today, the pure evil that happened today. My heart hurts for our community, but I want to make it very clear that hate will not prevail in this county. I want that to be very clear and known, love will prevail over what happened today. I assure you that.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HARRIGAN: The shooter got off roughly 10 shots before surrendering, laying down on the ground floor. Students were initially moved to the football field, and then, over the course of several hours, reunited with their parents. Laura, back to you.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: All right, Steve. Thank you so much. And just ahead, Kamala and Biden make a major policy change after something the Angle pointed out last night, find out what it is, next.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Now, as we told you last night, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  was trying to have it both ways on the impending sale of that iconic American company, \uc2 U.S. Steel\uc2  to a foreign interest, Japan's \uc2 Nippon Steel\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HARRIS: \uc2 U.S. Steel\uc2  should remain American owned and American operated, and I will always have the back of America's steelworkers.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well, that was a nice try, but the truth was that the Biden administration had been dragging its feet on the transaction for months, clearly trying to run the clock out until the election. They un