congressman, always want to find a way to downplay this and also tie it back to Trump. Check this out.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: Speaker Mike Johnson pandering to former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  as we get close to election day, trying to attach what Democrats are calling this poison pill, the SAVE Act, to any sort of continuing resolution. This is sort of a fear tactic, as Democrats are calling it, to try to scaremonger ahead of the November election.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Congressman, your reaction to that?\par \par \uc2 ROY: Yeah, scaremonger. This is all the talking points, rather than the normal playbook. Look, the fact is the American people by 85 percent, Laura, 85 percent of the American people support requiring the only citizens vote in American elections. Democrats are on the wrong side of the issue. They're scared to death that President Trump gets it. He's about to call their bluff. Mike Johnson and House Republicans want to rally behind President Trump to stand up for that simple concept.\par \par \uc2 And here's my question for \uc2 Mark Kelly\uc2 , all these Democrats, and the woman that was just on the screen. If there's no problem, if you say that there are no non-citizens voting, then what are you worried about? You know what they're worried about. Their worry will actually stop it.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well, Republicans have had ample time to get this entire situation cleaned up. I'm glad they're doing something now. But, man, we had the last three and a half years to do something. But Congressman, we appreciate your leadership on this. Thank you.\par \par \uc2 All right, coming up, Biden gets downsized and we dive into the Walz family feud, and Kamala prepares for her big night. Raymond Arroyo has it all. Seen and Unseen is next.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: It's time for Seen and Unseen, where we reveal the stories behind the headlines. For that,