m if he was pandering to women because he's not doing as well with the female vote. He denied he was pandering. And then he said this about his plan to give IVF to women nationwide. Listen.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 LLENAS: You had a huge announcement yesterday on IVF. What is your message to pro-lifers who are concerned about the federal government providing this service to women for free?\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: I think, when the -- when we look at IVF -- and I have been an early proponent of IVF very early on -- and we're going to -- government's going to pay for IVF when people need the treatment, when they want the treatment, when they want to go in with the fertilization.\par \par \uc2 Government's going to get totally involved, and they're going to help people. We want to have babies. We want to have lots of beautiful babies in this country, and we're going to do it. And that was received very, very well yesterday, very well.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 LLENAS: I asked him whether or not same-sex couples would be able to receive IVF treatment under his plan. He said that those details will be released this week.\par \par \uc2 I also asked if there were going to be any guardrails put in place under his plan. He also said those details will come. And then I talked to him about the interview yesterday. This was his response to Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 ' interview on the other network last night.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 LLENAS: You have had a chance now to digest that interview last night by Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 . What are your top-line thoughts about how she did?\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: Well, I think it was not exactly a great performance. It was a low- energy performance.\par \par \uc2 To take all of that time and get ready for that kind of an interview, it was a softball interview. There were 100 percent on the radical left side. It was CNN. I was surprised a little bit. I thought that Dana would be a little bit stronger.\par \par \uc2 But I really think that probably, if you look at it, was not considered a big success. If you go by the reviews, it was considered much less than a success.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 LLENAS: Last night, Neil, Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  said that she would appoint a Republican to her Cabinet. I asked former President Trump if he would appoint a Democrat.\par \par \uc2 And he said -- quote -- "If I found somebody that had the right views and was very talented. I'd have no problem with it" -- Neil.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: I was curious his reaction to Dana Bash. What's he saying that she was nicer to him than she was to \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  or the reverse?\par \par \uc2 Because it just seemed pretty straightforward to me.\par \par \uc2 LLENAS: Yes, he was saying that the interview was easy. And then I pushed him on what else he thought about the interview and what he would tell Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  when he finally sees her in person.\par \par \uc2 And he says he's -- he would ask her why she's a flip-flopper.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: Right.\par \par \uc2 LLENAS: So he didn't want to get into too much detail on that. But that was his go-to line on last night's interview.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: Oh, OK. I just wanted to get a sense of his perspective.\par \par \uc2 You mentioned -- \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's idea to pay for IVF. This is on top of a no tax on tips and no tax on Social Security, yet he has pointed out that it's the Democratic ticket that's doing all these giveaways with $25,000 home credits to those for purchasing their first home, with $6,000 for children. But what's -- what's the difference when you're handing out tax gifts to people?\par \par \uc2 LLENAS: Yes, it's a good question.\par \par \uc2 And I asked him about essentially that, about IVF and what are the guardrails and all that. And when you talk about the cost of IVF, Neil, it's about $40,000 