re information about that in the book coming out October 1st.\par \par \uc2 Shannon.\par \par \uc2 BREAM: Can't wait. Got mine on order.\par \par \uc2 Trey Yingst, thank you very much.\par \par \uc2 And just a quick note, my podcast "Livin' the Bream" drops today. This week I had the privilege of talking with one my heroes, speaker, author and disability advocate Joni Eareckson Tada. We talked what her new book, "The Practice of the Presence of Jesus: Daily Meditations on the Nearness of our Savior." Get it anywhere you like to get your books. And check out the podcast, where you like to get your podcast.\par \par \uc2 That's it for today. Thank you for joining us. I'm Shannon Bream. Have a great week. We'll see you next FOX NEWS SUNDAY.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2024 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2024 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document FOXN000020240825ek8p00001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 Final Night Of The DNC Underway In Chicago\b0\par\par\uc2 Sean Hannity, Newt Gingrich, Mike Tobin, Marie Harf, Kellyanne  Conway, Charlie Hurt, Tomi Lahren \par \uc2 9,906 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 August 2024\par \uc2 Fox News: Hannity\par \uc2 SHAN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2024 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2024 ASC Services II Media, LLC.  All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 SEAN HANNITY\uc2 , FOX NEWS HOST: And welcome to "Hannity".\par \par \uc2 And tonight, we are once again broadcasting, we are live, it is the final night of the DNC in Chicago, let not your heart be troubled, it's almost over.\par \par \uc2 Anyway coming up, we're going to have full coverage of the far-left demonstrations. Things are getting a little crazy outside. We'll tell you all about it. We'll have full coverage.\par \par \uc2 And also all of the rage coming from inside this venue. I have a nice monologue I want to share with you tonight. A live performance from the far-left band formerly known as the Dixie Chicks. They will do our national anthem. That I think is worth listening at any time.\par \par \uc2 But, first, before I get to my monologue, before we get to the national anthem, for a quick synopsis of this convention and where we are is FOX News contributor, former speaker of the House, Newt Gingrich.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Speaker, you're missed here. I know you're beloved in this building. We appreciate it.\par \par \uc2 You know, as I -- as I watched night after night after night, one thing has become apparently clear, and I'll go into more detail of my monologue is that there's a lot of -- there's not a lot of joy here. I mean, there's joy and people smiling and they're playing music, but a lot of rage on that stage, not a lot about how they're going to fix America's problems inflation, the border, energy, America's place in the world, law and order, I don't hear a lot about that at all.\par \par \uc2 NEWT GINGRICH, FOX NEWS CONTRIBUTOR: Well, look, I mean, there two big facts about this convention. First is it's the anti-Trump convention. That's the one thing that brings all the Democrats together. They're against Trump.\par \par \uc2 The second is that in fact uh all of their core values are so far away from the American people, they can't talk about them. So what you end up with is a lot of personality talk, a lot of babble, but none of it relates to the real world.\par \par \uc2 And if they actually explained what they wanted to do, they would be defeated so decisively, that just as a practical matter they can't do it. So they want to run a personality based campaign, things like, you know, Coach Walz, even though he was never actually a coach. These kind of things are going to be the heart of what they're doing. And they want you to be distracted with Oprah or Beyonce or anybody except serious political conversation.\par \par \uc2 The other thing I'd say, Sean, is it really struck me that the Democrats have continued to be who they are. So you get Pelosi. You get -- you get \uc2 Bill Clinton\uc2 , \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2 , the Obamas.\par \par \uc2 The Republican convention which Callista and I are at, was exactly the opposite. This is a new Republican Party. It's a populist, working or party of people who go out every day and work for a living, it is a profound change from the traditional Republican Party.\par \par \uc2 And I think in that sense, the difference in the two conventions tells you a lot about what's happening in America.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I'm going to get into these specifics and ask you about the dramatic, the largest tax increase in the history of the country in the world that Kamala's campaign has put out here. But, first we're going to turn to the national anthem.\par \par \uc2 (THE CHICKS PERFORM "THE STAR-SPANGLED BANNER")\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. That was the national anthem. Dixie Chicks, I think they have a new name. I forget what it is.\par \par \uc2 Anyway, we go back to Newt Gingrich.\par \par \uc2 And so, Kamala's campaign again it's no interviews, no gaggles no press conferences at all and apparently after the price gauging as she calls it, or price gouging speech, she's now backing off that. But they did announce "\uc2 New York Times\uc2 ", I guess we'll get more of the details, they want to raise the corporate rate. They want to raise $5 trillion in new taxes, and I'll go into the specifics later.\par \par \uc2 The corporate tax, 21 to 28, quadruple the tax on stock buybacks, double the global minimum tax from 10 to 20 percent. That would take away America's competitiveness, raise the top income tax rate, raise the corporate minimum tax from 15 to 21, raise the capital gains tax -- get this -- capital gains, 24 to 43.5 percent and the first ever tax on unrealized capital gains at 25 percent.\par \par \uc2 Now, that would be -- that would make America the least attractive investment country in the entire world. It would be a destruction of our capitalist system. Are they serious about this? Because I can't believe they put it in writing.\par \par \uc2 GINGRICH: Look, I was surprised. I thought the Harris strategy was to be all personality, no policy, try to get through to the election without admitting how radical they were. That speech last week in Raleigh where she outlined her economic plan, that was crazy. I mean that was so far to the left of \uc2 Bernie Sanders\uc2  that, you know, Gorbachev in Russia would have thought it was a radical speech.\par \par \uc2 And let me just say to our audience, you need to understand a 25 percent increase in unrealized capital gains means, theoretically at least, if your house goes up in price in value, the government can step in and say give me the money. If you don't have the money the government can step in and say give me the House.\par \par \uc2 I mean this would be the most, most crazy tax structure we have ever seen. It makes Venezuela looks normal. It makes Russia look normal.\par \par \uc2 And I can't -- I really wonder -- I'm going to write about this in the near future, who was sitting in the room I mean how did they cut -- I mean, unless they were really doing a lot of drugs, how did they come up with this, because it is so crazy, it's so unsustainable. No serious adult could have come up with this program.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Well, maybe it's incrementalism of what she really wants, which is what she co-sponsored the green new deal, $93 trillion, cradle to grave, womb to the tomb, Medicare for all, no private health insurance, again, the media, state-run media mob has ignored all of this, and maybe this is their first step. No?\par \par \uc2 GINGRICH: Well, look, you know, I don't care what "The \uc2 New York Times\uc2 " and "The \uc2 Washington Post\uc2 " coverage. If you threaten people with a 25 percent tax on any game, does it count for furniture, does it count for your car, does it count for your house, your family farm? I mean -- and that's annually. So are -- first of all, how are they going to detect it?\par \par \uc2 Are you going to fill out a form is every American in the country going to fill out a form? Are they going to reach in then and say, give me the money or you're going to seize your property? I mean, this is truly -- you know, every once in a while the mask comes off and you realize you're dealing with somebody who's crazy and, of course, you have with Walz, the most radical governor in the country, far to the left of \uc2 Bernie Sanders\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 And you have with Harris, a San Francisco radical and now we're beginning to see what that really means.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Former Speaker of the House, Newt Gingrich, it's great to have you as always.\par \par \uc2 We also tonight turn to a disturbing story, this one out of Arizona, where a man is now in custody after threatening to assassinate \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in Arizona. He was down at the border today.\par \par \uc2 Joining us now with the full report is our very own Kevin Corke.\par \par \uc2 Wow, these are scary times, Kevin.\par \par \uc2 KEVIN CORKE, FOX NEWS CORRESPONDENT: No question about that, my friend. Good evening to you.\par \par \uc2 Sixty-six-year-old Ronald Syvrud is behind bars tonight, Sean, after he allegedly threatened to kill former President Trump on social media. Now, Syvrud was taking into custody in Cochise County, without incident today. That according to a spokeswoman for the sheriff's office there.\par \par \uc2 The 66-year-old has several outstanding warrants on separate charges, including for a DUI, and for failing to appear in court in Wisconsin.\par \par \uc2 He's also wanted for failing to register as a sex offender, as well as a hit and run in the state of Arizona. Clearly, he's got issues.\par \par \uc2 Now, the threat comes just weeks after former President Trump's survived an assassination attempt in Butler, Pennsylvania. Syvrud's wrap sheet also includes over a dozen aliases, 17 by my count, and multiple felonies. In case, you're wondering, no, no bond has been set as of this hour.\par \par \uc2 You mentioned it, Sean, the former president was in the great state of Arizona at the border today. We have also learned tonight from the Trump campaign that an unnamed special guest is expected to join him at a rally Thursday -- or make that Friday afternoon at the Desert Diamond Arena in Glendale. That announcement comes amid speculation that independent presidential candidate \uc2 Robert F. Kennedy Jr.\uc2  may endorse him.\par \par \uc2 Of course, we'll be there for all the details. But for now, Sean, back to you.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Kevin, as always. Thank you.\par \par \uc2 Now, anti-Israel protesters they have gathered in pretty big numbers tonight again in the streets of Chicago. Our very own Mike Tobin once again live on the ground.\par \par \uc2 Mike, as I was coming in tonight, I saw a bigger crowd than what I had seen on previous nights. I'm not sure what you're see seeing where you are. Tell us.\par \par \uc2 MIKE TOBIN, FOX NEWS CORRESPONDENT: It certainly is a sizable crowd. It's always tough to give you an accurate number from inside the ranks of the demonstrators because you're looking at ground view. But certainly within the thousands, the train's going overhead right now, and that gives you an idea where we are.\par \par \uc2 We're on Lake Street, underneath the L tracks, and they're back here, coming in this direction again in the thousands. They marched along the pre-plan route. They went to their closest point to the United Center there, and that's park 5, 7, 8.\par \par \uc2 Stopped for a while, they chanted, they banged drums, they made noise, and then kept on marching. We've got some reports of skirmishes with the police, things like bottle throwing, that came and went. That's not confirmed by the police.\par \par \uc2 But what we've seen for the last couple of nights is they're sticking to the root and they're marching. They're just trying to get their -- get their point out there and they do believe they've been successful referencing that quote from \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , that they've got a point they believe they've reached all the way up to the president. They believe they are indeed putting pressure on the leadership inside of the DNC.\par \par \uc2 One of the things -- in fact, let me show you one of the placards they're handing out. It says "abandon Harris in `24". So they're -- they're definitely trying to put some pressure on the politicians in there. The interesting thing though is they say abandoned Harris for '24, they're not pro-Trump. Some people have shown up here with Trump signs. They get, you know, shown the bird. They get treated to some kind of flowery language.\par \par \uc2 As far as whether this will melt down into violence on the last night, really it's anybody's guess. We've seen some pack of the kids -- packs of the kids with the black clad, the hoodies, the keffiyehs on their heads, the typical uniform that you've come to recognize at this point. And frankly, the owner -- the organizers, the spokespeople, they just call that escalation and they think that gets their point heard.\par \par \uc2 They say if people are still dying in Gaza, there won't be any business as usual. So they're not going to shy away from things like vandalism, disruption escalation as they call it. So we're watching it through the night, but they do believe that they've made the point and put some pressure on the politicians to this point -- Sean.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Mike, we'll be checking in throughout the evening. Thank you.\par \par \uc2 Now back to the -- well, convention still ongoing behind me and there's going to be a lot happening. \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  speaking later.\par \par \uc2 Despite a promise of happiness and joy, the theme in this building all week has frankly been nothing but hatred and loathing, Democrats hoping that you hate \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  as much as they do, and that has been and remains the theme every single night and it will be so tonight.\par \par \uc2 They want you to hate \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  so much, you will even vote against what is in your own best interest, policies that'll improve the economy, secure our borders, bring back law and order and safety and security to your town and city, and bring you lower energy prices and, of course, reestablish America's role in the world.\par \par \uc2 They hope that your hatred of Trump will blind you to the Harris-Biden border crisis, you know, people with known terror ties in this country, confirm, people from countries with terror ties.\par \par \uc2 Our top geopolitical foes, Iran, Syria, Russia, China, Egypt, Afghanistan, they hope that you ignore that Kamala would like to decriminalize illegal immigration, give free housing, health care, education to illegal immigrants.\par \par \uc2 They hope you're not going to notice a running mate is allowing illegals to get legal driver's licenses and offering in Minnesota free college education, courtesy of the taxpayers.\par \par \uc2 And, of course, they both support sanctuary cities, states -- and states, and they both want amnesty, or what they call a pathway to citizenship which would be amnesty. They want you to hate \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  so much that you ignore all the crime in small towns, big cities. They want you to ignore all of the unvetted Harris-Biden illegals that we know have been involved in raping and murdering and other violent crimes against Americans.\par \par \uc2 Thirteen-year-old girl, Queens, New York, park, broad daylight, raped. Of course, Laken Riley, Jocelyn Nungaray, 12-year-old girl tortured for two hours and murdered. She fought back with all of her might, or maybe Rachel Morin, mother of five, and the list we scroll it so often of the names you've never heard of before, unvetted Harris-Biden illegals, that, you know, they're hoping you hate Trump more than wanting to solve that problem.\par \par \uc2 They hate that you -- you know, they want you to hate them so much that you're going to forget about the wars raging overseas happening in large part because of their weakness on the world stage, and they' love that your focus only be on the rage you they have for Trump projected on to you, more than you would say hate what you see when you go into your local grocery store, paying more for everything you buy.\par \par \uc2 Every store you go to, costs higher, Harris-Biden inflation, Bidenomics is great, Kamala was telling us, now she's complaining about the high cost of things like bread and eggs et cetera, or what about for example the high gas prices, electricity prices, energy prices. It's just killing American families, two-thirds of Americans now saying they're gulping water financially.\par \par \uc2 And, of course, they're really hoping that you hate \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  so much that you want more of your hard-earned money, you know, to go for their cradle to grave, womb to the tomb green new deal because Kamala co- sponsored that bill and Medicare for all with no private health insurance. And, you know, obviously showing herself to be the radical and revealing her true self.\par \par \uc2 For example, look at this headline, this is from tonight. According to "\uc2 The New York Times\uc2 ", \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is poised to enact what would be, pay attention, the biggest tax hike by far in the history of America. In terms of sheer dollars, the biggest tax hike she is proposing in the entire world. I can't even believe that they have put this forward.\par \par \uc2 Pay attention to the details, it will impact in spite of what they claim, anybody that has a 401k or an IRA or retirement, whatever you have, and it's -- you know, it includes $5 trillion, they want in new taxes, previously rejected by Congress, but that's even when Democrats control both chambers.\par \par \uc2 The difference is this is a new, radicalized, you know, socialist/communist Democratic Party. Kamala wants to raise the corporate tax rate from 21 to 28 percent. And, by the way, remember corporations, small businesses, they don't pay taxes. They pass those higher costs on to all of you, so you will cover that bill, every time you go to a store to buy anything you'll be paying yet more again, she's proposing a hike on income taxes and small business taxes.\par \par \uc2 That includes an initial raise on Americans making they say over $400,000 a year, but it includes anybody. And then in 2025, she plans on letting the Trump tax cuts expire. That'll cause taxes to go up for almost all Americans, including families making under $100,000 a year.\par \par \uc2 And that's not all. Kamala also wants to raise the Medicare surtax. She's also planning to raise the capital gains tax, look at this, from 15 percent to 20 percent to as much as 39 percent. That will destroy investment in America, might crash the stock market, too.\par \par \uc2 And the housing market on top of it. She's endorsing a tax hike on stock buybacks. She wants something called a global minimum tax. She wants it to go from 10 percent to 20 percent.\par \par \uc2 Why are we paying for global anything? That's where the U.S. and Europe, they kind of get together and they collude and they conspire, and they together come up with the same corporate tax rate to prevent competition among countries for businesses and investment? Why? To ensure a high tax rate and perpetuity.\par \par \uc2 Again, this tax gets passed on to all of you in the form of higher prices, and so much by the way for making America a tax safe haven for people around the globe to invest here because this is the best place to invest. That would take away our competitive advantage.\par \par \uc2 Now, Kamala has also invented a brand new tax on something called unrealized gains. Okay, slow down, Newt spoke to this earlier. If you have a 401k, or you own a house, okay, or you have business or some stocks, which most Americans have in any retirement account, the values of those assets, let's say they go up on paper, oh my stocks went up 15 percent, you'd have to pay an annual tax on that even though you didn't get a penny, you didn't realize the gain, and when you sell it, what if you -- what if the stock had gone down in the interim, you're going to get a refund? I tend to doubt it.\par \par \uc2 And you'll have to cut a big check every year on unrealized profits from any asset you have if you bought a house for say 200 grand in the '90s and the house is now worth a million dollars. Oh, get ready to come up with some cold hard cash if Kamala gets her way, and God help you if you're a farmer or a rancher, you're entire life will be destroyed if you bought into a mutual fund prepare for your portfolio, it'll drop in value, while your investment company is forced to sell off stocks in order to pay for that massive tax bill.\par \par \uc2 You have a 401k that you paid into your entire life, and you're still getting money and the value of it is going up, and you want the value to go up so you can retire and have some financial piece of mind, okay, as that value continues to go up and you get ready to cash it in, every year you're going to be paying an annual tax. The big lie that they're 