ntly for a long time, we cannot afford another four years of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and I think, you know, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  would be even worse.\par \par \uc2 So we need to send \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  back to the White House. We need to retake the Senate. We need to hold the House. We need to hold our legislative majorities that we have in the great state of Georgia.\par \par \uc2 And it takes hard work. That's what we've been doing. We've been in the -- in the field since after the Fourth of July knocking doors, really working in swing districts where we have vulnerable legislators, but also making sure that we're turning out the base for the whole ticket, so that we win from top to bottom.\par \par \uc2 And I just want to urge everybody out there -- we cannot take this for granted. We have got to get the vote out. We got to stay focused. We got to stay focused on the future.\par \par \uc2 We need to do like you just did and like \uc2 Stephen Moore\uc2  just did, continue to hammer \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 's record and the record of, you know, really, the \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  and \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  and the other people that have been really for 12 -- like Scott Jennings said, Sean, for 12 of the last 16 years punishing the American people.\par \par \uc2 And I was thinking earlier when you were on with \uc2 Stephen Moore\uc2 , I feel the -- you know, I know the Democrats have been talking about joy at the convention all week, and I feel like the joy is subsiding.\par \par \uc2 And when the sugar high of the convention subsides, people are going to really start thinking, it's not so joyful when I look at my bank account. It's not joyful when I can't make my car payment or my rent payment, or I have to decide whether I'm going to buy gas or buy groceries.\par \par \uc2 And I know former President Trump was at the border today. People have not forgotten the disaster at the border, and the millions and millions of illegal people that are in our country that are getting better benefits than some of our hardworking Georgians and hardworking Americans out there.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Governor, are you as surprised as I am at the tax plan for example that was announced today or the whole idea, you know, for example, price gouging when grocery margins -- the profit margins are 1.6 percent historically, in line where they've always been?\par \par \uc2 Are you surprised when you hear Kamala talk about decriminalizing illegal immigrants, free housing, healthcare, education? The fact that she tweeted out the bail fund, wants to get rid of ICE, defund, dismantle, no bail laws on crime which is -- it's happening in your state, it's happening around the country. Or no fracking, no drilling, we'd economically, unilaterally disarm that. This scares me.\par \par \uc2 Your reaction?\par \par \uc2 KEMP: Well, I mean, they're move -- they're moving back to who they really are, Sean. I mean, we saw that the day they took office when they changed the policies at the border that we're working, we know that firsthand. I told somebody the other day, when \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was in office, we were working with his administration, sending our National Guard troops to secure the border.\par \par \uc2 Now, we're having to do that with Governor Greg Abbott in Texas, because this administration doesn't want to secure the border. You know, they had complete power in Washington, D.C., the Democrats did. The White House, the House and the Senate did nothing about the border, did nothing but really ramp up spending, create these bad policies that created 40-year high inflation.\par \par \uc2 Now, they're take -- trying to take credit for driving inflation down. They created it to start with. So we don't need to let them forget about that.\par \par \uc2 They're trying to move away from some of those things and flip-flop on their positions and I think when the -- when the convention is over with and the 