FOX News over this century, and no one has been more relevant and survived more longer than you have. So, hats off to you.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: No, I -- look, I appreciate it.\par \par \uc2 CARVILLE: Proceed with the questions.\par \par \uc2 HANNIT Y: But we -- but we've also -- we've also had fun but we don't agree, we just don't and -- but I will say this, you know, for example. I'm going to play a clip. Bill and \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2 , okay, and this is them talking about abortion, and I won't play it but they also -- you know, \uc2 Bill Clinton\uc2  famously said the era of big government is over, the end of welfare as we know it.\par \par \uc2 But here's Bill and Hillary on abortion and as I ask it keep in mind that neither \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  or \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  want any restrictions on abortion at all, none whatsoever, that in the -- in the case of Walz, I mean he wants gender affirming care provided to children without parental consent, and he wanted to put feminine prod -- hygiene products in boys bathrooms, in schools. Listen -- but here's Bill and Hillary.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BILL CLINTON\uc2 , FORMER U.S. PRESIDENT: Our vision -- our vision should be of an America where abortion is safe and legal but rare.\par \par \uc2 HILLARY CLINTON\uc2 , FORMER SECRETARY OF STATE: I have worked for, for many years, is to make abortion safe, legal and rare.\par \par \uc2 B. CLINTON: Our people have genuine and deeply felt differences on the subject of abortion, even if abortion is safe, legal and rare.\par \par \uc2 H. CLINTON: Well, I believe abortion should be safe, legal and rare.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: So we've known each other all this time. I don't see James Carville as a radical \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , \uc2 Bernie Sanders\uc2  left-wing, you know, lunatic, and you kind of said as much yourself. I mean, if the country knows who they really are, can they win?\par \par \uc2 CARVILLE: Well, certainly, they can win and I agree with everything that President and Mrs. Clinton said. I think abortion should be safe, legal and hopefully, it'll be rare, and if we have aggressive contraception and aggressive availability, we can do that.\par \par \uc2 You know, the actually abortion rate -- number of abortions gone up since this idiotic Dobbs decision, and I think that Roe v. Wade is right. It takes in account certain rights in the first trimester , certain rights in the second, certain rights third trimester and I will disagree with you vehemently and friendly on one thing. I think offering tampons to students is one of the best ideas I've ever heard.\par \par \uc2 You know, Utah --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: To boys -- to boys in the bathrooms -- to boy's bathrooms?\par \par \uc2 CARVILLE: It had nothing to do with the boys in the bathroom. That's something that's made up.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: James, they changed the language, they changed the language.\par \par \uc2 CARVILLE: You know, what it doesn't matter, there should be young people who are going through embarrassing enough to be a young girl to have to go through this. I am wholeheartedly for that. I don't care if they put it in the library, but wherever they put it.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You want to know the library?\par \par \uc2 CARVILLE: That argument, I'm -- I'm really -- I'm really for it. Yes, I don't care where it is.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You're -- but wait, but you and Mary are good parents. You love your kids. Would you want gender affirming care without you being consulted?\par \par \uc2 CARVILLE: I don't -- I would -- I -- we'll make those decisions, I don't think really think about that very often. I think that Governor Walz is a patriot. I think he's a soldier. I think he's a football coach. He's a hunter. He's done some tremendous things.\par \par \uc2 And if we're going to sit here and nitpick every little thing he did --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Nitpick?\par \par \uc2 CARVILLE: -- and this and that, and I'm very -- I'm very comfortable with tampons being offered free to students in school. I'm totally 100 percent.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. So let's not belabor the point, you're okay with it in boy bathrooms, have no problem with it gender affirming care --\par \par \uc2 CARVILLE: Put it in the cafeteria for all I care.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Okay, let me ask you this. We've got to have the courage to stop using the term radical Islamic terrorism and illegal alien, let me play it for you.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 KAMALA HARRIS\uc2 , VICE PRSIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES & 2024 PRESIDENTIAL CANDDIATE: We must have the courage to object when they use that term radical Islamic terrorism which ignores how Muslims have overwhelmingly been the greatest victims of terror.\par \par \uc2 And we must also have the courage to reject that term illegal alien. I have seen some of the worst of criminal behavior, I have seen the worst of crime, an undocumented immigrant is not a criminal.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Do you -- do you think that's a little out of the mainstream to not say radical Islamic terrorism or illegal aliens? Who attacked us on 9/11? Who's entering our country illegally?\par \par \uc2 CARVILLE: Well, let me -- let me -- well, okay, let's back up. In the last shootings in Buffalo when Margaret Douglas (ph), the people -- the guy that shot at President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , all of these shootings have something in common. They're all by white males who could get an assault weapon.\par \par \uc2 I'd rather use the term radical terrorist. I would prefer to leave the term Islamic out of it because there's so many, many good people who follow the religion of Islam, and I wouldn't want to do anything that would bring any -- any --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: But the word radical delineates.\par \par \uc2 CARVILLE: The quotes in the term --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: The word radical delineates between Muslims and radical Islamists, that's very clear.\par \par \uc2 CARVILLE: I would -- I would just say radical terrorist, but that's something I prefer.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. That's you.\par \par \uc2 CARVILLE: Rather I would call someone -- I don't think -- I don't think any human being is an illegal. But I do think you should -- you should have border laws, I wouldn't mind saying that they're undocumented. But I just wouldn't call another human being an alien.\par \par \uc2 That -- that's just maybe -- that's the Catholic in me. I don't know. But I don't like the term "alien" applied to another human being.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: By the way, the term "illegal alien" happens to be a government term, the one that they put in all their government documents. Anyway, James is a character. More my interview with James Carville tomorrow night.\par \par \uc2 But first, joining us now, FOX News contributor Charlie Hurt, alongside with the host of "Tomi Lahren is Fearless" on Outkick.\par \par \uc2 Tomi, you know, I don't know how you ducked and you dodged and you weaved your way out of this, but I don't think we didn't notice as Charlie and I sit here, but we noticed.\par \par \uc2 TOMI LAHREN, OUTKICK HOST: Well, listen, Sean, I'm very excited to hear Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  speak tonight. I know she's been preparing this for quite some time. I hope that the teleprompter holds strong because, Sean, if that teleprompter does not hold strong tonight, I think we're about to be unburdened by what has been in the passage of time. It's going to be quite rough for the current vice president.\par \par \uc2 So I hope they don't have any technical difficulties or we might see the real \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  come out once again, 2019 \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  might make a reappearance.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Yeah, but you know, Tomi raises a good point. Do you know over fake news CNN, I think it was Erin Burnett said, well, maybe she -- they claim they're journalist -- maybe they should stick with the strategy of not doing an interview or answering a question.\par \par \uc2 You know, I give James Carville, although I don't understand putting feminine hygiene products in a cafeteria.\par \par \uc2 CHARLIE HURT, FOX NEWS CONTRIBUTOR: Cafeteria.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: That kind of, you know, really?\par \par \uc2 HURT: You think we could at least draw the line there. But maybe --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Wait until part two tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 HURT: Right.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: But in all seriousness, they have been hiding, they have been ducking, dodging. The media's complicit, compliant, they are an extension of their press office. So far, they've gotten away with it. Whatever we're going to see tonight is all written you know, perfected by others.\par \par \uc2 She did release an economic plan, the highest tax increase in America and world history. That says a lot.\par \par \uc2 HURT: Yeah, and what's so extraordinary about that is that -- it's that CNN does claim to be a news operation. You would think at the very least a CNN would be clamoring to get a real unscripted stuff from her. But of course, they're not because they're running her -- helping her run her campaign.\par \par \uc2 But from her perspective, I don't blame her. It's working for her. Why would she expose herself to embarrassing herself like that when she can do these scripted events and rely on CNN to do --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I don't blame her, but it's not fair to the country.\par \par \uc2 HURT: It's terrible for the voters.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And they're also not showing her and what she has said sponsoring the green new deal in the Senate, Medicare for all, no private health care, decriminalized illegal immigrants, free healthcare, housing, education, no fracking, no drill -- I mean, the list is exhausted.\par \par \uc2 HURT: Yeah, and this line of attack that we're hearing from Democrats she's only been the nominee for 30 days, give her a second. It's like, well, first of all, that's your fault, that's not our fault.\par \par \uc2 And the second thing is the people who are -- as you point out, the people who are hurt by this are the American people, the voters who want -- who need to be informed in order to cast their ballots in November.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And I think this is the big challenge, I -- I would argue, Tomi, for the Trump campaign and that is that you have what is frankly a treasure trove of material radicalism on tape from both Kamala and \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , that if the American people see, I am convinced beyond any, any doubt in my heart and mind they would never vote for this.\par \par \uc2 LAHREN: Right. I think that's why it's so important to not only get out the vote but also be spending money on these ad buys and just show Kamala in her own words. That's really all the Trump campaign has to do is put Kamala in her own words.\par \par \uc2 And it's not unfair because she hasn't given us any of her current or up- to-date policy positions. When you go to KamalaHarris.com, you get a place to donate, you get a place to see puff pieces on her and \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , but you don't see any policies.\par \par \uc2 I don't expect many policies tonight. This is essentially a concert series we been experiencing all week long. It might have been fun at first on Monday night, maybe Tuesday, but when it comes to Thursday, it's insulting to the American people.\par \par \uc2 What is Beyonce going to do to lower the price of your gas, your food, your groceries, your housing? Absolutely nothing. What's Kamala going to do with the speech that she's prepared for, for two days? Absolutely nothing to help average Americans.\par \par \uc2 And I hope average Americans are paying attention to the lack of substance we've been given all week long.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Well said. Last word, Charlie.\par \par \uc2 HURT: Yeah and I think the event that President Trump did at the border today is a perfect event. He was talking about things people care about. He stayed on the message and it was a very powerful event.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And the victims of unvetted Harris Biden illegals were there.\par \par \uc2 HURT: The Biden-Harris victims were there and they need to highlight those victims. They're direct victims directly of these policies.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: That's -- and you know what? They have blood on their hands. I've said it before, America needs to hear from them. All of that would have been preventable.\par \par \uc2 All right. Thank you, Charlie. Tomi, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Unfortunately, that is all the time we have left this evening. Please stay with the FOX News Channel for continuing coverage of the DNC. Don't forget to set your DVR so you never ever, ever, ever miss an episode of "Hannity". For news anytime, every time all the time FOXNews.com, go to hannity.com.\par \par \uc2 And in the meantime, go to Chicago. Bye, Chicago. The hot dogs are great.\par \par \uc2 Let not your heart be troubled, Bret Baier, Martha MacCallum, they take it from here. Have a great night.\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2024 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2024 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document SHAN000020240823ek8m00001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 Now: Final Night Of DNC Underway In Chicago; Now: MI Gov Whitmer Speaks On Night 4 Of DNC; Soon: VP Harris Takes Center Stage At DNC Night 4; Soon: VP Harris Headlines Final Day Of DNC; Now: VP Harris' Sister Maya Speaks At DNC; Soon: VP Harris Addresses DNC On Final Night; Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  Accepts Democratic Party's Presidential Nomination During Speech at Democratic National Convention; \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  Criticizes President Trump for His Comments and Policy on Abortion.\b0\par\par\uc2 Sean Hannity, Bret Baier, Martha MacCallum, Peter Doocy, Brit  Hume, Harold Ford, Bill Hemmer \par \uc2 5,551 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 August 2024\par \uc2 Fox News: Live Event\par \uc2 FXLV\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2024 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2024 ASC Services II Media, LLC.  All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 SEAN HANNITY\uc2 , FOX NEWS HOST: Do not forget to set your DVR, so you never, ever, ever, ever miss an episode of Hannity. For news anytime, every time, all the time, foxnews.com, or hannity.com. And in the meantime, from Chicago, by Chicago, hot dogs are great. Let not your heart be troubled. Bret Baier and Martha MacCallum will take it from here. Have a great night.\par \par \uc2 MARTHA MACCALLUM, FOX NEWS HOST: History in the making here in Chicago, Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  set to deliver a speech, she not planned on doing just a few short weeks ago. Big night here in Chicago. Good evening, everybody. I'm Martha McCallum.\par \par \uc2 BRET BAIER, FOX NEWS HOST: And I'm Bret Baier. Welcome to Democracy '24 coverage of the final night of the Democratic National Convention live from the United Center in Chicago. Right now, we have Michigan Governor, \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2 , another up and comer in the Democratic Party. Let's listen in to the floor\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 GRETCHEN WHITMER\uc2 , GOVERNOR OF MICHIGAN: White women across America, we just GSD, get stuff done. At 29, I joined the sandwiched generation, sandwiched between working and raising my newborn, and caring for my mom, who was dying from brain cancer. It was hard, but not extraordinary. It's life. Those nights reminded me who I was fighting for, people just trying to make it.\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  knows who she's fighting for too. She took care of her mom, who also battled cancer. As President, she'll fight to lower the cost of healthcare and eldercare for every family. She has lived a life like ours. She knows us. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  doesn't know you, at all. You think he understands that when your car breaks down, you can't get to work.\par \par \uc2 No, his first word was probably chauffeur. You think he's ever had to take items out of the cart before checking out? Hell, you think he's ever been to a grocery store? That's what the chauffeur is for. But \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , she gets us. She sees us. She is us.\par \par \uc2 Look, we've all lived through a lot of history over the past few years, floods and fires, an attempted coup, a plot and a pandemic, it's exhausting. We don't know what the next four years will bring, but what we do know is this, through it all, your life won't stop. You're going to have to get to work, pick up the kids, and pay your bills.\par \par \uc2 And then, one day, when you're just trying to get everyone out the door, a news alert goes off. Something happened. Something hit the fan. You'll ask, is my family going to be OK? And then you'll ask, who the hell is in charge? What if it's him? What -- what if it's that man from Mar-a-Lago?\par \par \uc2 I know in a crisis, we need someone strong enough to come up with a plan, to tell the truth, and to bring people together. Right now, before the crisis, is when we get to choose. Why wouldn't we choose the leader who is tough, tested, and a total badass. I know who I want as our Commander in Chief. America, let's choose \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Michigan Governor, \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2 , again, a star in the Democratic Party, pointedly, making some remarks against the former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . Welcome back. We are just getting started on this final night of the convention, and to do that, Peter Doocy is live on the convention floor with a little flavor. Peter?\par \par \uc2 PETER DOOCY, FOX NEWS CORRESPONDENT: And Bret, it makes sense. But this is, by far, the most crowded the, floor has been of the four nights. It is like we are -- would you say it's like we're standing in a crowded subway car?\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Yes.\par \par \uc2 DOOCY: It is at rush hour, right? And we can pan around just to see there are a lot more passes handed out to come to the floor, it would seem, than there are chairs. So far, everybody has seemed like they are very engaged, very excited. There are a lot of whispers about people trying to figure out who the celebrity surprises? Have you guys heard there might be a surprise tonight?\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: -- in the building.\par \par \uc2 DOOCY: Yancy is in the building. OK, that's a single source. Do we have a second source on that? OK, all right. Here, they think that Beyonce is in the building. The Rhode Island section, if there's a problem with Beyonce, visit Rhode Island, right.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Peter, we got to get that confirmed. The whole sign thing was really threw us off.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: Two sources, buddy.\par \par \uc2 DOOCY: We will get a second source on that tonight. Don't you worry. All right.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: We want you to go find Beyonce and ask her personally.\par \par \uc2 DOOCY: There you go.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: You take care of that. All right. Let's bring in our panel, Brit Hume, Dana Perino, and Harold Ford Jr., great to have all of you with us tonight. We have been here all week watching this unfold. Brit, you have seen a lot of candidates come out on this big night. It's a life-changing moment for them, one way or the other.\par \par \uc2 BRIT HUME, CHIEF POLITICAL ANALYST, FOX NEWS: And unusually big for her, because she's been such a relatively invisible figure throughout most of her vice presidency, and certainly not the kind of -- the kind of figure that you'd want to be in terms of how the public regarded him. They didn't see much of her. A lot of what they saw was, was statements that were denounced as word salad and so on.\par \par \uc2 I can't help, but think also, Martha, that you know, for all the excitement here tonight, could this not possibly be the last of these? I mean, there was a time when the -- when the nominees were chosen at the convention with a vote on the floor, uncertainty would have bound up until the moment when the vote was taken.\par \par \uc2 Then, after -- even then, when that subsided, after the primaries began to dominate the choices, you had fights over seeding some delegate against -- delegation against another, when there were controversies about that, there were fights over planks in the party platform. There's none of that anymore.\par \par \uc2 Everything of any consequence has been decided and acted upon before we get here. So, what we get is a four-night show to promote the candidates, and it's true in both parties.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: Right, absolutely.\par \par \uc2 HUME: And there's one reason why all these people are here now, and it's not because she's speaking, and it's not because she's the nominee, it's because we are here. We, in the media, whose ring this -- this -- this tier of this -- of this convention hall. And what I would say about it is, if we stop coming, they wouldn't have this. They could -- it wouldn't be worth it. So, the question I have is --\par \par \uc2 BAIER: So, what are you trying to tell us? You're done?\par \par \uc2 HUME: Yeah. I'm going to retire myself, retire in tradition. But, as long as we keep coming, they'll keep having it. But remember, we're being used as a -- as an outlet for a four-day commercial for a political party. Both parties do this.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: That's pretty amazing. We just want to confirm we're going to take all of a number of different species and obviously focus on Vice President Harris' speech and all the balloon dropping and ceremonies around that. But we've just confirmed that former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will be joining us on the phone to react real-time after that moment of the balloon drop in the celebration right here on Fox.\par \par \uc2 So, we'll have an interview with the former President immediately after. Dana, interesting, the campaign, obviously, putting him out there. He also has a press conference in Arizona tomorrow, and there's a lot of speculation that \uc2 Robert F. Kennedy Jr.\uc2  may get out and maybe endorse him there.\par \par \uc2 DANA PERINO, HOST OF AMERICA'S NEWSROOM AND THE FIVE: I thought it was smart of the campaign to have J.D. Vance join us last night right afterwards, especially when \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , the vice presidential nominee on the Democratic side, really tried to demean him, and insult him for going to Yale, of all things, even though he went there on the merits, and didn't grow up in a wealthy household and neither did \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Tonight, I'm feeling like we are a long way from Monday night. So, just three nights ago, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  made everybody stay here very late. Maybe it wasn't his fault that it was late, but he gave an hour-long speech that was a lot of yelling. It was interrupted by applause lines, because I think everybody here was like, we are almost done with this part.\par \par \uc2 They wanted to thank him. They do feel grateful. They talk a lot about joy in here. It's not just joy, it's relief, because if \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  were the one giving the speech tonight, this room would be about a quarter full, I think, and there would not be any of this enthusiasm.\par \par \uc2 And what \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has been able to do in 32 days is a lockdown, not just the nomination, but to raise up the enthusiasm and the fundraising. She could not have had a better setup. But as I said before, everything gets harder for her after tonight.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: Yeah, Harold, I remember you saying in Milwaukee that you felt like it was one of the best convention you would have ever seen. And so, you have this enormous enthusiasm in Milwaukee, and now you've got it again here in Chicago. So what is that? How does that feed the process from here? Because there have been a lot of sleepy conventions that they tried to juice up. These are both real, real movement, sort of energy on both sides.\par \par \uc2 HAROLD FORD, FOX NEWS CONTRIBUTOR: The unity in Milwaukee was really amazing to me. They -- remember that, we can't even really recall, because so many events have taken place. President Trump was shot that Saturday and Monday he comes into that hall in the unity in the Republican Party. I remarked that week was as good as I've ever seen at a convention.\par \par \uc2 I've been blessed to go to a dozen or more, not as many as my great pal across the -- across the desk. But, a couple things that struck me, the number of American flags, the number of Go USA signs, and the patriotism in the room, the number of veterans who've been on the stage speaking, and the number of veterans, military veterans, in the audience, I think, is something that's good for America.\par \par \uc2 After 9/11, so many young men and women Americans decided to go in to go serve their country in the military. Now, so many have come back and are serving in government, which I think is a good thing too. We've seen that second the bench for the Democrats, Beshear, Whitmer, Cooper, Shapiro, my friend Wes Moore, this is a good thing for the Democratic Party.\par \par \uc2 And I think it's a good thing for politics, because you have young people in it. But, let's be clear, we came here to see the Taylor Swift of the night, the Beyonce of the night, the Stones. I wish he was still alive, for instance, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 ' show tonight. If she does well tonight, this will have been a smashing success of a convention. And then, we get on to the issues, and that's where I think this campaign will be joined.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: You know, notably, one of the big luminaries that wasn't on the stage to speak was California Governor, \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 FORD: And he's one of our stars. Let me be clear about that.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: And I asked him about that on special report, he said he did all that he was asked to do. So how about that? Let's go to Bill Hemmer down on the floor. Hey, Bill.\par \par \uc2 BILL HEMMER, CO-ANCHOR, AMERICA'S NEWSROOM: Hi, guys. Good evening to you. \uc2 Adam Kinzinger\uc2  from Illinois had a lot of choice things to say about \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  over the past couple of years, and he's on the stage here tonight. This is my Fifth Democratic Convention. I have never seen such an obvious display of patriotism, of red, white and blue, and any of the five conventions I have been to on the Democratic side until tonight.\par \par \uc2 The flag waving, the music, the signs that say USA, and there's a clear objective to try and get that middle part of America to convince them that they are just as patriotic as a lot of people watching at home tonight. \uc2 CBS\uc2  did a poll recently. They found more than a third of Americans did not know what \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  stands for.\par \par \uc2 In a matter of minutes, she's going to have that opportunity. She will say, in part, after seeing some of these excerpts, she will call \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  an unserious man. She will say, consider the power after the Supreme Court just gave him immunity from criminal prosecution, imagine the power he would have if he were back in the White House.\par \par \uc2 She'll talk about the personal effect of her when a friend came to her and talked about a sexual abuse at the hands of a family member, and that is what drove her into the legal field and drove her into the world of law. Climate change is making a comeback tonight, guys, I know I've talked about this a lot over the past couple of nights, but clean air, clean water was kind of the line that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  had eight years ago.\par \par \uc2 We've heard a lot of that tonight, for the first time, really, in the four nights here. What we have not heard is the word fracking, all week, and you have to think that's a nod to Pennsylvania trying to make sure that does not stay -- does not come into the headlines. We were given word a short time ago that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , on that vacation, in California, after he left here about midnight and Monday night, called \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  earlier tonight, along with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , and wished her good luck in her speech.\par \par \uc2 Last point, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was on Fox & Friends earlier today, way before the sun came up here in Chicago, and he said, I was mentioned 271 times last night, being sarcastic. I'll tell you, based on the speakers we've heard so far tonight, we may have passed that 271 thus far. One bit of good news for the planners, they figured it out. It took them four nights, but \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will speak and the 10 PM, the coveted 10 PM Eastern Time slot for the Finale here in Chicago. Bret, Martha, back to you.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Anybody down there saying, Beyonce, I mean, do we have the second source?\par \par \uc2 HEMMER: No, we do not. We've heard the rumors. But listen, four hours ago, it was Taylor Swift, and I don't know if that's going to happen either.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: All right, Bill, we'll wait patiently. By the way, the former President, we said, he's going to join us on the phone. He's been active on Truth Social, just in the past few minutes, he said, thank you, \uc2 Brian Kemp\uc2  of Georgia, the Governor of Georgia, for all of your help and support, where a win is so important. As you remember, there's a little tiff between the Governor of Georgia and the former President. Looks like that is getting mended quickly, at least over Truth Social.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: Yeah, seems like a good idea. George is a very important state, and they're both on the same side politically, so we'll talk to the former President and the current GOP candidate for the next presidency just a little bit later tonight, but let's bring in Kellyanne Conway, and Jessica Tarlov with a look at ahead for tonight.\par \par \uc2 Jessica, let me start with you. You know your thoughts about what we're going to hear tonight. You know, we've heard about a lot of joy. We haven't heard a lot of, and I know you've heard this, a lot of specifics on policy. What do you think is the most important thing for her to get across tonight? She stands on the stage on her own steam as the Vice President who wants to be President tonight.\par \par \uc2 JESSICA TARLOV, FOX NEWS CONTRIBUTOR AND POLITICAL CONSULTANT: I think that she has to seem like a serious person. I think that's still a conception about her from the 2019 primary heading into the vice presidency, where people, even some Democrats, didn't think that she was necessarily up to the job, and then, the fact that she hasn't been as front and center during the Biden Administration, and I don't know whose decision that was, but she had been kind of held behind closed doors until the Dobbs decision.\par \par \uc2 The folks don't know her for more than the clips, necessarily, right? Talking about the passage of time, and I think that she's going to stand up there on her own, she's going to deliver her remarks. It's supposed to be 30 to 40 minutes. We're going to hear more about her back story, but I think also what her values are, what was important to her, about what she accomplished during the vice presidency, and then, about her vision for the future.\par \par \uc2 I'm not saying, it's going to be heavy on policy, saying, this is exactly how I'm going to do it, but she is going to cast that forward-looking vision.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Let's listen in to Maya Harris. This is \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 ' sister.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 MAYA HARRIS, SISTER OF VICE PRESIDENT KAMALA HARRIS: but she stayed here to build a life. Her name was Dr. Shyamala Gopalan Harris. But, we called her mommy. Mommy was so many things to so many people, a civil rights activist, a scientist, a devoted mother to her two little girls, but most of all, mommy was a trailblazer, who defied the odds and defined herself. And when it came to Kamala and me, mommy had great expectations for us, but she had even greater expectations of us.\par \par \uc2 She -- she raised us to believe that we could be and do anything, and we believed her. You see, mommy understood the power and the possibility that come with knowing and showing who you truly are. She knew we could be the authors of our own stories, just as she'd been the author of her own. Mommy's journey and the opportunity that she wanted for Kamala and me, that's a distinctly American story.\par \par \uc2 We may all have different histories, different struggles or different perspectives, but what binds us together is the fervent desire to be free to fulfil our God-given potential. Kamala's entire life has been about fighting for each of us to have that freedom. And like so many Americans, Kamala knows what it's like to be underestimated, and be counted out.\par \par \uc2 She knows what it's like to be the underdog, and yet, still beat the odds. And now, she has created so much electricity, so much optimism, so much joy throughout the nation, and it is why we need her leadership in this historic moment. We are living in a time when some are trying to divide us, to separate us in ways that make it difficult for us to come together.\par \par \uc2 Well, look, my sister rejects that view. Where others push darkness, Kamala sees promise, where others feel detachment, Kamala fosters connection, where others want to drag us back to the past, my sister says, hold up now, we are not going back. Because, Kamala understands, we have so much more in common than what separates us.\par \par \uc2 She knows the measure of our success isn't just winning an election, it's about who we bring along, and lift up in the process. And so, as I look out at all of you today, and take in this incredible moment, I so wish that Mommy could be here tonight. I can just see her smiling, saying, how proud she is of Kamala. And then, without missing a beat, she said, that's enough. You got work to do.\par \par \uc2 She would tell all of us to roll up our sleeves and get to work to elect a leader who sees the potential in each of us, a leader who cares for all of us, a leader who fights for every one of us, our Democratic nominee, my big sister, the next President of the United States, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Younger sister, Maya Harris, delivering a speech on behalf of her sister, the big night, obviously, for that family,\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: Yeah, they're very politically involved in all of this. She's married to Tony West, her husband, and they are very much a part of the campaign in her workings. Let's bring in Kellyanne Conway for some thoughts on moving up to this moment. Obviously, you're filling in a lot of the pieces of the family story. She talked a lot about her mother, who raised Kamala and her sister, Maya.\par \par \uc2 KELLYANNE CONWAY, FORMER COUNSELOR TO THE PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: It's a beautiful moving tribute. We've heard lots of people speaking before and about \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  throughout the week. I think that's wonderful. I will say that we all have two lobes of the brain. On the one hand, we can say, well, this is an impressive woman of academic and professional accomplishments, and an amazing American Dream story for her parents.\par \par \uc2 And on the other side of the brain say, I don't think she's ready to be Commander in Chief, or I'm a little unsteady about her new tax plan or this price gouging nonsense. And that really is what the voter does. The voter tries to reconcile her two lobes to the brain to make a choice. I want to say something else. \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  risks tonight being the 10th or 14th most persuasive, compelling and memorable speaker of her own convention.\par \par \uc2 We've had some pretty big, heavyweight speeches here, Yvette, Oprah and the Obamas, and the others. And I just want to remind everybody in -- on November 5, 2016, Jay-Z and Beyonce did a concert in Ohio for Hillary. She lost to stay by 8 points three days later. It's difficult to transfer even this kind of energy and enthusiasm, and your own popularity to someone else. Vibes are not votes, and they certainly don't put food on the table, and pay the mortgage and the rent.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: OK. Kellyanne, with vibes are not votes. We'll write that one down. Could be a bumper sticker. Our panel's back. Brit, Dana, Harold Ford Jr., what about that? Vibes are not votes, Harold.\par \par \uc2 FORD: They are not. Kellyanne and I have a difference of opinion, maybe about the candidates in this race, but she's smart about these things. This is -- this is our pageantry here, and we've had a good one. I talked about some of the speakers, we've had a lot of cops and sheriffs and law enforcement on the stage, trying to counter a narrative that will be talked about -- that will be trying to be advanced during the campaign.\par \par \uc2 And we're soft when things are weak on things. I think people are going to look tonight. We may not get the substance that Kellyanne is speaking about this evening that will come, but we're going to get a chance to hear that bio again, see her temperament, because a lot of the country doesn't know her.\par \par \uc2 We have to remember she serves at the pleasure of the President, and she's now the nominee, so even some of the criticism leveled at her because of her affiliation with this administration, I think some of that is going to begin to whittle away, even this evening, and if she's able to answer the tough questions that Dana and my friends on The Five, we raise often, this will be a very different race as we head into the fall.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Let me say one thing about what we're not seeing. We are not seeing these protests that were forecast to overtake this -- this convention. And in part, in part, the reason that happened is because of the \uc2 Chicago Police Department\uc2 , the superintendent Snelling, the federal authorities, working with the \uc2 Chicago Police\uc2 , they did a fantastic job, and that is not a story here, even though, we thought it might be coming into fruition.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: Yeah. They talked about tens of thousands of protesters that would potentially be coming. Also, the weather has been amazing. It's a great -- it's great weather for protesting, if that's what you're committed to. So, it raises questions about how committed these uncommitted voters really are. There were about 5,000 people out there, a handful of arrests, really not a big event.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: And if the change of the ticket, Brit, changed the passion on that issue, you know, if taking President Biden off the top of the ticket, changed the anti-Israel protest fire?\par \par \uc2 HUME: No, it's just to the extent to which some people, at least, are not going to hold her accountable for the foreign policy or perhaps other policies of administration that they do not like because of the main issue of Israel versus the Palestinians in Gaza. So, she gets a break on that, at least from these people, which is fortunate, because a disrupted convention would have been an embarrassment to the party and a symbol of disunity, which is the one thing they're trying very hard not to project. And so far, successfully.\par \par \uc2 FORD: And Bret, we haven't seen it in the arena either, you've not seen Palestinian flags, or even (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Yeah, couple of small types, but not big.\par \par \uc2 FORD: Not many at all. Yeah.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: I'll tell you what I have seen, buttons that say I am a for Israel Democrat, and we've heard no one, Harold, talk about Israel on this stage, talk about any of the issues that are going on in the world.\par \par \uc2 FORD: Josh Shapiro mentioned Edward, one or two others, but to your point, we've not heard an elaboration on any of this, but I think we'll get a lot of it here, a little bit of it tonight, but when the race gets joined, we're going to hear a lot about the next few weeks.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: We're going to tune into this video. It is said to be a biographical video. Vice President, Harris.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE (voice-over): We're up and tighten with the neighborhood. It was the kind of place where your neighbor would look after you in school, let out, where your first grade teacher would show up at your law school graduation. It's where \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  learned what it means to be in the middle-class, making every paycheck count.\par \par \uc2 She was raised by a working mom who taught her about standing up for what's right and protecting the people you love.\par \par \uc2 M. HARRIS (voice-over): Kamala carries the lessons of our mother, the fighting spirit of our mother, the compassion. She was all five-feet tall. If you met her, you would have thought she was seven feet tall.\par \par \uc2 And our mother, if I'd ever come home complaining about anything, she wouldn't have it. The first thing she'd say is, well, just stop the complainant. Just tell me what you're going to do about it.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE (voice-over): And since she was a young girl, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has been fighting for families like the one she grew up with.\par \par \uc2 M. Harris: That is Kamala, she can't help herself from standing up for people and standing up for what she thinks is right. She has been that way our whole lives. Being a protector is what led her to become a prosecutor. Looking back now, I could say it was her calling.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE (voice-over): As a courtroom prosecutor, she went after predators who targeted women and children, and fraudsters who ripped off working families, and she put dangerous gang members and human traffickers behind bars.\par \par \uc2 TORI VERBER SALAZAR, FORMER DISTRICT ATTORNEY: We didn't have partnerships with DOJ or \uc2 FBI\uc2  or DEA or any of those law enforcement agencies. Now, we all work collaboratively. She was the person who built the foundation in how we do criminal justice in America.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE (voice-over): As Attorney General of California, she held the big Wall Street banks accountable for fraud, winning $20 billion for California families, she took on one of the largest for-profit colleges that were scamming students, and in the Senate, she fought for her constituents with the determination of the prosecutor, standing up for reproductive freedom.\par \par \uc2 KAMALA HARRIS\uc2 , VICE PRESIDENT OF THE U.S., (D) PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE: Can you think of any laws that give the government the power to make decisions about the male body?\par \par \uc2 JUDGE BRETT KAVANAUGH, SUPREME COURT: I'm not -- I'm not thinking of any right now, Senator.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE (voice-over): She fought to keep our children safe from the terror of gun violence.\par \par \uc2 K. HARRIS: How many of you guys had to have a drill where you learned about how you need to hide in a closet or crouch in a corner in the event that there was a mass shooter? Look at that. Look at that.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE (voice-over): On the Intelligence Committee, she defended our nation against foreign adversaries, and in 2020, she made history as the first woman to be elected Vice President of the United States. She cast the tie-breaking vote to deliver urgent relief to the American people during the pandemic.\par \par \uc2 She beat Big Pharma to lower prescription drug costs and capped the cost of insulin and led the fight to restore reproductive rights after Roe v. Wade was overturned.\par \par \uc2 K. HARRIS: We have worked too hard and fought too long to see our daughters grow up in a world with fewer rights than our mothers.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE (voice-over): Because she's never been afraid to stand up to powerful interests.\par \par \uc2 K. HARRIS: Sometimes people will open the door for you and leave it open. Sometimes they won't. And then you need to kick that (BEEP) door down. Excuse my language.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE (voice-over): Now she's running for President, still fighting for families like the one she grew up with.\par \par \uc2 K. HARRIS: Our campaign is about saying, we trust the people. We're saying we just want fairness. We want dignity for all people, and we are a work- in-progress. We haven't yet quite reached all of those ideals, but we will die trying because we love our country, we believe in our country.\par \par \uc2 We're not falling for these folks who are trying to divide us, trying to pull us apart. We know what we stand for, and we stand for the people. And we stand for the dignity of work, and we stand for freedom. We stand for justice.\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2024 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2024 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document FXLV000020240823ek8m00001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 Man Who Threatened To Kill Trump In Custody; DNC Day 4: Kamala's Big Night; Exposing The Harris-Walz "Freedom" Lie; Kamala's Elites And Fake Populism; Senator Warren Speaks At DNC; DNC Day 4, Kamala's Big Night; Democrats Replace Joy With Division At DNC; Democrats Desperate To Reinvent Kamala; Kamala's All Vibes, No Substance; Angel Moms Join Trump At Border; Kamala Set To Reintroduce Herself At DNC.\b0\par\par\uc2 Bret Baier, Laura Ingraham, Alicia Acuna, Peter Doocy, Dana  Perino, Jessica Tarlov, Ben Domenech, Katie Pavlich, Bill Hemmer, Jesse  Watters \par \uc2 10,355 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 August 2024\par \uc2 Fox News: The Ingraham Angle\par \uc2 INGANG\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2024 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2024 ASC Services II Media, LLC. All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 BRET BAIER, FOX NEWS HOST: Tomorrow, Former President Trump and \uc2 Robert Kennedy Jr.\uc2  are both in Arizona amid rumors of a possible alliance, we'll watch that. Plus, join Martha MacCallum and me tonight, 10:00 p.m. Eastern for special coverage of the Convention. This is going to wrap it up. Big night for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 . That's it for this Special Report. Fair, balanced, and still unafraid. Here's Laura.\par \par \uc2 LAURA INGRAHAM, FOX NEWS HOST: Good evening, everyone. I'm Laura Ingraham. This is The Ingraham Angle from the fourth and final night of the Democratic National Convention here in Chicago.\par \par \uc2 Tonight, after playing some of their gold and oldies, the Democrats will introduce the woman they hope will be their new star. But before we get into that, we have a Fox News alert. The manhunt is finally over. Police have arrested the man who threatened to kill former President Trump ahead of today's Arizona border event. Fox News Senior Correspondent Alicia Acuna is live from Cochise County with all the details. Alicia.\par \par \uc2 ALICIA ACUNA, FOX NEWS SENIOR CORRESPONDENT: Hi, Laura, yes, and we can give you a look here. That man is 66-year-old Ronald Lee Syrvud. That's according to law enforcement. He is also wanted on warrants in both Wisconsin and Arizona for crimes ranging from DUI to failing to register as a sex offender. In a statement, the local sheriff says the subject has been taken into custody without incident in Cochise County. We appreciate all of the information received and the incredible collaborative efforts of all of our public safety partners.\par \par \uc2 News of the manhunt broke this afternoon as the former President was just arriving here in Cochise County to tour the border and speak on the issue here. I talked to the former President shortly after.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 ACUNA: As you know, a manhunt is currently underway in Cochise County, where we are standing, and it's for a man who the Sheriff's Department says was threatening to kill you. Does that make you want to change the way you do events or anything? How do you respond to that?\par \par \uc2 DONALD TRUMP\uc2  (R), FORMER U.S. PRESIDENT AND 2024 PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE: No, it makes me want to get away from this interview, because you and I are standing out here, and I was told, do you think you could do it someplace else? But I said, I can't keep you waiting. You are Fox after all. But no, I've heard about that, but I have to do my job. It's a job. It's a dangerous job, but I have to do my job. This is so sad, and you've seen the whole thing today, and I hope you're going to report on it fairly.\par \par \uc2 But this border is so dangerous, it's so bad, and so horrible to people. They're losing children, wives, and husbands, and it's just a horrible thing, and we can stop it. And Kamala is a disaster. She's a radical Left, Marxist, and she wants an open border. She wants all the people, the man you're talking about. She wants him to just flow right through. No, we can't do that.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 ACUNA: And Laura, Trump has a very busy day tomorrow. He'll be in Las Vegas, and then he comes back to Arizona for an event here. Laura.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Alicia, thank you very much. Now, let's go live to the Convention floor where Fox News Senior White House Correspondent Peter Doocy is having a lot of fun. He's standing-by, making a lot of friends there tonight.\par \par \uc2 PETER DOOCY, FOX NEWS WHITE HOUSE CORRESPONDENT: Yes, we hope to, Laura. And the headliner, of course, on the fourth day of the Democratic Convention has to be the Democratic nominee, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 . But there's so much speculation about these big celebrities who are going to come. Front row of South Carolina, do you guys have any idea who the celebrities are that are coming tonight?\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Beyonce.\par \par \uc2 DOOCY: And how do you get seats in the front row?\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: You be good, and you sit in the back all week. So, you sit here on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 DOOCY: Is that right, OK? What do you guys want to hear from the Vice President tonight? The last night.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Oh my God, everything, literally just everything. I'm just so excited. It's just been a great week. I just want to hear what her plan is going to be for our future, and just how we're going to get out there and vote for her and make sure that she's elected.\par \par \uc2 DOOCY: This is the South Carolina delegation. You guys saved -- you guys saved \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in 2020. Is it hard to see Biden out the way that he went?\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: No, he didn't go.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Well --\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: I think he went out taking the (inaudible) --\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: And therefore --\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: I think --\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: He's done us well, and we support him. But right now, the move is gone. He passed the torch on --\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Nobly, he went out very nobly, and I think history will judge him very favorably and kindly for showing that type of leadership.\par \par \uc2 DOOCY: And beyond the front row, does anybody know about any of the celebrities that are going to be coming? She said, Beyonce. What'd you say right here?\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: If it's Taylor Swift, I'll freak out. That's all I'll say.\par \par \uc2 DOOCY: So, just be alerted, convention staff, there might be a freak out in the second row in South Carolina, if it is Taylor Swift. Laura, back to you.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: All right, Peter, my daughter Maria would be pretty happy about that as well. Thanks so much. All right. The Democrats have building up to this moment for the last month. It's the national debut of the new \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 . Now, with the help of a lot of high paid consultants, she's been repackaged into someone that they hope seems more likable, more experienced and more intelligent than the old \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Remember, it was just months ago that she was widely recognized as an annoying problem for Biden, not a capable substitute for him. So, to overcome her talent deficit, did she and her advisors unveil policies to address the economic problems facing American families? Or she maybe, maybe reconsidering her administration's budget busting climate change policies, that would be a no. But they want you to know that she's really happy.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BILL CLINTON (D) 42ND U.S. PRESIDENT: We need \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , the President of Joy.\par \par \uc2 OPRAH WINFREY\uc2 , TV PERSONALITY: Let us choose joy.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Thoughtful, loving, compassionate.\par \par \uc2 GOV. TIM WALZ (D-MN), VICE PRESIDENTIAL NOMINEE: Thank you for bringing the joy to this fight.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Now this could be the lamest attempt at a political rebranding I've ever seen in my entire career, because it requires America to live in an alternate reality where they deny their own lived experience, their own finances and what they see with their own eyes, illegals pouring into the country, into their children's schools, into gangs terrorizing urban America not too far from here. And we also have to pretend that the past three and a half years did not exist as well.\par \par \uc2 Right now, 65 percent of Americans think the country is on the wrong track. Where in the heck is the joy in that? Now, since the one policy she's articulated since Biden dropped out, price controls, was roundly panned, no one should expect a lot of substance in her address tonight, talking solutions is, after all, too dangerous, because when she does, we remember the real \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , a radical, unimpressive San Francisco extremist.\par \par \uc2 But imagine the cabinet should pick, or someone would pick for her. It'd be kind of a lot like the old cabinet. Big on the DEI factor, small on the brain factor.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Do you potentially think that this new numbers could be a liability for this campaign?\par \par \uc2 GINA RAIMONDO\uc2 , SECRETARY OF COMMERCE: No, when I hear that, first of all, I don't believe it, because I have never heard \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  say anything truthful.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: It is, though, from the Bureau of Labor.\par \par \uc2 RAIMONDO: I don't -- I'm not familiar with that.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\pa