t every transgender inmate in the prison system would have access to the medical care that they desired and need. At its core, it's a civil rights issue, it's a justice issue, and it's an issue of humanity.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: It's humanity. God shed a tear for the transgender prisoners. Is this joyful? Well, I guess you're going to have to be the judge, and a Harris administration wouldn't be either, except for the elites, like the ones we'll hear from tonight, who from the comfort of their private jets, fly over the chaos and suffering their own policies create on their way to their vacation homes surrounded by fences, walls, and private security.\par \par \uc2 Harris had three and a half years to show America, she had some common sense. Instead, she was a bumbling number two to a bumbling number one.\par \par \uc2 Joining us now is \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2 , former GOP Presidential Candidate, Vivek, just in, the Supreme Court has just ruled in a 5-4 decision giving partial victory to Republicans trying to enforce proof of citizenship when voting in Arizona looks like they did not grant a stay, and that law is going to go into effect. Thoughts tonight.\par \par \uc2 VIVEK RAMASWAMY\uc2  (R) FORMER U.S. PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE: Well, I think that's an obvious development, but the fact that that was controversial tells you where we are. It was 5-4. The fact that four liberal justices went the other way show that you have a Supreme Court that even still looks at the end and works backwards. But I think this is a good development, especially in a battleground state like Arizona, citizens should vote, and non-citizens shouldn't. It's that clear. This shouldn't be a controversy.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: So, the joy, are you feeling it tonight? You kind of look joyful. You're wearing blue. I like that. You're reaching out to the other side.\par \par \uc2 RAMASWAMY: Yes, for national unity (ph).\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: So, joy is what they're selling. And I think they're trying to draw this contrast or comparison to Trump, who they've caricatured as unhappy and grumpy, and Kamala, who's really fun, and you got \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  always doing this weird thing --\par \par \uc2 RAMASWAMY: Yes.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: -- and always bowing to people, too much time in China, I think. But so that's fun, and everything else is not fun. But how fun is this economy for most people?\par \par \uc2 RAMASWAMY: Well, you pointed out the real distinction there. By pointing to joy, this is a vibe. They're trying to run this entire campaign on style over substance. She had a Pavlovian experience. She was trained and when you put your hand in the policy cookie jar, when it bit back, she said that she doesn't want to touch policy anymore.\par \par \uc2 So, the reality is, can she get through this election naturally for 80 more days without touching policy? I think it's possible that she can, which has our work cut out for us. That's why I was here earlier today for a press conference, press \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  on the actual policies she stood for.\par \par \uc2 In 2020, she stood for single payer health care system. She stands for a tax on unrealized capital gains. Think about what that means --\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: What will that do? You're a big, big investor --\par \par \uc2 RAMASWAMY: Yes.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: -- big entrepreneur. What would that and explain it very simply, very simply --\par \par \uc2 RAMASWAMY: Yes. So that would trigger a market crash and here's why. It means that if you own a business or own land, you have to pay a tax to the government in cash with cash that you don't have. So, what does that mean? You have to sell assets to do it. But when you sell those assets, the asset price goes down, and then the next person has to do the same thing, that drives the asset price down further, so the person after has to do the next thing.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: This is a nightmare.\par \par \uc2 