ton's can do, what Kamala can do. I mean, this is an unbelievable ticket.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: He actually has a point. This is an unbelievably dangerous ticket for the entire country, though. Soviet style price controls, insanely high cost of living, bans on your gas-powered cars and stoves, radically transforming American cities and towns with millions more migrants. That's just for starters.\par \par \uc2 But what's particularly insidious about this agenda is how they couch it in terms of freedom.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 WALZ: This is a big part about what this election is about. Freedom. When we Democrats talk about freedom, we mean the freedom to make a better life for yourself and the people that you love.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Someone get him some Pepto, because Walz is suffering from a terrible disease. It's awful diarrhea of the mouth. Freedom from the governor who established a COVID snitch line. And if he knows how to give people a better life, why are so many Minnesotans leaving the state to escape the high taxes and the high crime in the Twin Cities?\par \par \uc2 The only freedom they care about in the end, when you really listen to this convention this week, the freedom to abort, the free -- up until birth. The freedom for biological men to use women's bathrooms and be on their teams, and the freedom, maybe to smoke weed, whenever and wherever, and of course, the freedom to harass, surveil, and even prosecute anyone standing in their way. This is a dark vision of America. This is what they sell as joyful, their freedom agenda, which requires their surrogates to sell their big con by trying to flip the script.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 PETE BUTTIGIEG (D), SECRETARY OF TRANSPORTATION: They are doubling down on negativity and grievance, committing to a concept of campaigning best summed up in one word, darkness. Darkness is what they are selling