ust had a vigorous debate. Just get on stage and debate him. That hurt them.\par \par \uc2 ROVE: Well, and also, I think he's got a lot of antagonism with the Democrats because they've gone in and actively tried to keep him off of ballots.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: The democracy crowd.\par \par \uc2 ROVE: Yeah, democracy crowd. We want to have free and open elections, but we're going to try and keep Robert Kennedy from getting on the ballot.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Bad choice. Guys, great to see you both. Harris and Karl --\par \par \uc2 FAULKNER: Thank you, Laura.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: -- thank you so much. Oh, look who just wondered onto the set.\par \par \uc2 JESSE WATTERS, FOX NEWS HOST: Hi, Laura. How you doing?\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: This is becoming a habit now.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: I think we should make it a duo. Just Laura and Watters.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: How are you.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Can you believe the Democrats like country music this much?\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: No, they don't.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: I think they like camouflage, football, dads. What happened to the Democrats?\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Common was bigger yesterday. Kind of a low in the crowd now.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: And then we have Stevie Wonder later, we're hearing. And a special guest we're not allowed to talk about.\par \par \uc2 INGARHAM: All right.\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2024 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2024 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document INGANG0020240822ek8l00001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 Kamala Harris Skips Obamas DNC Speech To Avoid Hurting \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 ; U.S. Jobs Report Revised Down By 818,000 Overall; RPT: RFK Jr. To Drop Out, Endorse Trump; DNC Chair On Walz: Uncle You Want To Hang With; DNC Night Three: Kamala's VP Pick Walz Takes The Stage; Dems Hope To Charm Country Music Fans At DNC\b0\par\par\uc2 Jeanine Pirro, Jessica Tarlov, Jesse Watters, Dana Perino, Greg  Gutfeld \par \uc2 7,531 \uc2 words\par \uc2 21 August 2024\par \uc2 Fox News: The Five\par \uc2 FOXFIV\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2024 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2024 ASC Services II Media, LLC.  All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 DON PEEBLES, FORMER BARACK OBAMA FUNDRAISER: So, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  doesn't beat \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , then it's going to be a tough race for Vice President Harris.\par \par \uc2 NEIL CAVUTO, FOX NEWS CHANNEL HOST: Got it. All right, Don, thank you very much. Good catching up with you. Don Peebles, big Obama fundraiser. Worried about Democrats, a little less so Republicans.\par \par \uc2 Here's THE FIVE.\par \par \uc2 JEANINE PIRRO, FOX NEWS CHANNEL HOST: Hello everyone. I'm Judge Jeanine Pirro, along with Jessica Tarlov, Jesse Watters, Dana Perino and Greg Gutfeld. It's 5:00 in New York City and 4:00 in Chicago, and even though this is THE FIVE, it really is 4-1/2.\par \par \uc2 Some ugly backstabbing drama playing out at the DNC as former President \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  and First Lady \uc2 Michelle Obama\uc2  took the stage in what turned out to be a Trump bash fest.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BARACK OBAMA\uc2 , FORMER PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: It has been a constant stream of gripes and grievances that's actually been getting worse now that he's afraid of losing to Kamala.\par \par \uc2 There's the childish nicknames, the crazy conspiracy theories, this weird obsession with crowd sizes.\par \par \uc2 MICHELLE OBAMA\uc2 , FORMER FIRST LADY OF THE UNITED STATES: Who's going to tell him that the job he's currently seeking might just be one of those Black jobs?\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: The Obamas getting snuggled by the woman that they crowned, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  skipping their speeches altogether. She was 90 miles away in Milwaukee, holding her own counter rally.\par \par \uc2 Fox's Jacqui Heinrich reports that her choice was made out of sensitivity and respect to President Biden, who Obama helped push out.\par \par \uc2 One source familiar with the situation told Fox that the Obamas are still not on the White House's good side, but Barack did his best to kiss up to the big guy.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 B. OBAMA: Joe and I come from different backgrounds when we became brothers. History will remember \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  as an outstanding president. I am proud to call him my president, but I am even prouder to call him my friend.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: But \uc2 Michelle Obama\uc2  just couldn't help herself. She opened her speech with a brutal jab at the Biden era.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 M. OBAMA: Something wonderfully magical is in the air, isn't it? We love a familiar feeling that's been buried too deep for far too long.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: All right, Jesse, I'll start with you. I mean, how do you navigate the rocky terrain between Biden and Obama clearly evidenced by the fact that \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  was 90 miles away and that, you know, Biden was the first one out at the convention and then exiled to California, and she wasn't even there for the Obamas.\par \par \uc2 JESSE WATTERS, FOX NEWS CHANNEL HOST: You just keep everybody apart. That's what it looks like. If you put them all in the room together and lock the door, only one person comes out, and it's probably Michelle.\par \par \uc2 My mother texted me after the speeches last night, and she said, are you a Democrat yet? This is what I'm dealing with. The Obamas can fool a lot of people, but they can't fool me. Yes, it was a persuasive speech. Yes, it was very powerful. Of course, it was well crafted.\par \par \uc2 But in order to buy what they're selling, you have to be completely oblivious to political reality. My grandmother, Judge Jeanine, used to tell me, beware of those who use their virtue as a cudgel. And this is what the Obamas do. They say, decency, dignity, charity, generosity. They have a monopoly on that. And if you would disagree with them, then you're just an evil ghoul.\par \par \uc2 I always say, don't listen to what people say. Watch what they do. They've lost 300,000 kids. They poured migrants into Black neighborhoods. They have ruined women's sports. They've made life more dangerous and expensive for Americans. Those aren't virtuous actions. That's incredibly dishonorable.\par \par \uc2 Then, the Obamas say, the Republicans aren't generous. Have you ever seen \uc2 Sean Hannity\uc2  tipped? They say Republicans don't sacrifice. Let's take a poll of the army. Let's see who they're voting for. They say Republicans avoid taxes while \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  is on trial for tax evasion. And then they go and say, oh, you know, Republicans want to poison rivers and fire people, but this country is too polarized, we need to come together. What?\par \par \uc2 Come on, guys, the whole thing about Trump complaining too much, this is like someone who stabs you, and then when you're crying, they call you a whiner. They fined this guy. They have arrested him. They've raided his house, and he can't talk about it? Give me a break.\par \par \uc2 Hope is not a plan, and we still have never heard a plan.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: And Jessica, you know, I think that most people would agree that \uc2 Michelle Obama\uc2  gave a great speech, but she acted as if the last 3-1/2 years weren't about hope and change, that's the Biden administration, or that the last 12 of the 16 years weren't about the Democrats.\par \par \uc2 JESSICA TARLOV, FOX NEWS CHANNEL CONTRIBUTOR: Well, I think that she was definitely focused on giving Kamala the biggest boost she possibly could. She knows how popular she is, she knows what an incredible and persuasive speaker she is, and she wanted to shine a light on Kamala, giving the most personal account of her back story, drawing the parallels between their experiences as smart women, lawyers, highly accomplished and also Black.\par \par \uc2 I thought that that was one of her best lines, where she said that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  just couldn't stand that her and Barack, people who had achieved so much, were raising to the highest heights, who happened to be Black, and then she went on to obviously make the Black job jab.\par \par \uc2 I don't think that anyone who is trying to pick apart these speeches is going to be taken seriously. No offense, Jesse.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: You're looking right at me.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: I'm not, I'm actually looking in the camera. I can feel the heat from the side here. But those were compelling, well delivered speeches that were exactly what Kamala needed.\par \par \uc2 And people complaining about the tone or the tenor of it obviously didn't watch the \uc2 RNC\uc2 , which was all about demonizing \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and have forgotten, I guess, that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was an O.G. birther, \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  and \uc2 Michelle Obama\uc2  need never be kind about that man for saying what he did about them.\par \par \uc2 I also wanted to say, just as a general emphasis on loving marriages and holding women up, from daughters to mothers to grandmothers, with such a compelling theme of this, I think Doug Emhoff, you know, hey, it's Doug. It's 8:30 in the morning, why am I calling you now? The whole thing about their love story was something that people can really connect to and they are going hard for that female vote. They know 53 percent of white women voted for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in 2016, got enough back in 2020 for Biden to win. And we need to keep holding on to that, to the -- to the emphasis on keeping women up in the spotlight and honoring them.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: You know, Greg, \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  made a big thing about the fact that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was a whiner, and even talked about since he came down the escalator. I mean, you know the guy was, he was impeached, he was indicted, he was convicted. They tried to kill him. I mean, he's a Russian asset, and Obama's whining about one thing, and that's his birth certificate and he hasn't stopped since 2011 on that.\par \par \uc2 GREG GUTFELD, FOX NEWS CHANNEL HOST: The Barack Obama going after Trump, and actually, I thought it was a fairly innocuous number of things about nicknames and about crowd sizes, because that's all he had. There was no Trump policy. There was no Trump economy. He couldn't say -- he couldn't point his finger at anything, because the last four years have been a disaster under the Democrats.\par \par \uc2 So, if you're going to run again on the metaphorical or allegorical mean tweet strategy, have at it, because everybody's used to Trump now. They're used to the nicknames.\par \par \uc2 If the best thing Michelle said last night, according to Jessica, was that Trump didn't like them because they were Black, maybe you should rethink the party you belong to if you're going to keep race-baiting and accusing people of being racist. I think America is tired of that. There are a lot of other things you could go for, other than calling people racist, and also that relies on mind reading, which no Democrat is capable of, because they can't even read their own mind.\par \par \uc2 Having said that, this is their time, it's not for us. I agree with Jessica on that. I don't want to be like a weirdo who hate watches THE FIVE and then tweets about it.\par \par \uc2 You know -- you know, if you're choosing to watch something that's not intended for you and you don't like it, that's kind of on you. So, I'm like, I sit here and I feel like, you know what? I'm not going to be like the guy at a bar who is over listening to a conversation that a family is having. It's none of my business.\par \par \uc2 And now to my last point, business and minding your own business. Obama made a side about generational wealth being basically affirmative action, whether you know it was for Trump or rich white people, who knows?\par \par \uc2 So, because your fa -- your parents did all right, it's not fair to other people. Fair enough you can say that, but mind your own damn business. You have no business getting to somebody's family's hard work. You keep your side of the street clean. We'll do ours.\par \par \uc2 Since when is somebody's family's wealth your business? Envy for what a person's family did is really sad and sick.\par \par \uc2 You know, generational wealth, for many people, is a myth. Ultimately wealth, when you accrue it is transferred down to your kids. It split and then it split again, and then it split again.\par \par \uc2 Generational wealth only lasts for most people one generation, it divides instead of -- instead of growing.\par \par \uc2 Unlike Obama, so he made his wealth through government, public service. Good for him. Corporations flock to him because of the star power that he got being in government, he has made millions, perhaps hundreds of millions, without ever creating one job, without ever creating one job in the private sector. All of that money goes to him and to his lovely children, the generational wealth that he has accrued, he is obviously going to pass to them, and they're going to pass to their kids.\par \par \uc2 But you know what they're not going to do? They're not going to stop working. Rich people don't stop working because they're rich, because they want to remain rich, and they know you can't live that way.\par \par \uc2 So, let's be done with this myth of how rich people somehow don't work because they have generational wealth. You know, he wasn't born with a silver spoon in his mouth, but right now, he can buy truckloads of silver spoons.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: All right. Dana, last question to you. I mean, one of the issues that Greg brought up is the fact that neither Michelle nor Barack talked about policy. You know, they talked about the chaos that would be -- that would be created, when the chaos was pretty much about the left reacting to Trump, but nothing about world peace, nothing about any of the good stuff in the policy.\par \par \uc2 DANA PERINO, FOX NEWS CHANNEL HOST: In the last two days, what I've noticed is that the convention is acting as if the Biden-Harris administration never existed. They're acting as if Trump is the incumbent.\par \par \uc2 One of the things \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  said last night was he goes like, we just can't afford another sequel. We can't afford any more of this chaos and the bumbling around.\par \par \uc2 And I was thinking somewhere Trump is watching this, going, yes, I agree. That's exactly what I've been trying to say.\par \par \uc2 I also want to add one thing, Jacqui Heinrich reported this morning that, I guess about the riff, I don't doubt that someone told her that. I actually wondered, though, when I saw it, if we were being punked.\par \par \uc2 Typically, the candidate isn't here all four nights. Also, what \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  did last night, she went to a swing state. They filled another arena, the same one that President Trump was in, just -- and we all were in a month ago. And the thing that's quite incredible is that, why would they do that?\par \par \uc2 Well, one of the reasons is because David Plouffe is now running this campaign, and he had run the Obama campaigns. He knows exactly how to get new voter's phone numbers and their names, and I bet that all of them were contacted today to said, will you vote? Can we count on you to vote? Can you give us $20.00?\par \par \uc2 They just raised $500 million in the last month, and 62 percent of the people that donated are people who never even gave a dime to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . So, I think that was also probably the strategic reason to have her there in a swing state, trying to get more press.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: All right. Up next, is the Biden-Kamala jobs boom all just one big fat lie? You won't believe shocking new numbers on how they've been cooking the books.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Kamalanomics dealt its first major blow after a stunning revision in the jobs market this morning. Almost a million jobs just vanishing into thin air. The \uc2 Bureau of Labor Statistics\uc2  is downgrading the total number of jobs created between April 2023 through March of this year by 818,000. I'm glad to go back to elementary school to figure out how to say that, making it the largest downward employment revision in 15 years. And it's not a headline that Vice President Harris wants as she campaigns and takes credit for the good parts of the economy.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 KAMALA HARRIS\uc2  (D), U.S. PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE: By virtually every measure, our economy is the strongest in the world. We have created 16 million new jobs.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 PERINO: And \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  wasting no time to hammer Harris over the revised numbers.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 DONALD TRUMP\uc2  (R), U.S. PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE: Harris-Biden administration has been caught fraudulently manipulating job statistics to hide the true extent of the economic ruin that they've inflicted on America.\par \par \uc2 With an extra -- listen to this one, 818,000 jobs that don't exist. So, they said they existed, and they never did exist. They built them up so that they could say what a wonderful job they're doing.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Greg, I think one of the most -- the least persuasive things I've heard on the economy lately has, and they've said it for a while, but increasingly this week, is that, well, the American economy is better than those around -- than the rest of the world, so everyone, you should just be happy. It doesn't seem to me to be working persuading people.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: It's basically saying, like, too bad. What are you going to do, leave, right? You're stuck here.\par \par \uc2 I think you know, for the Democrats, ignorance isn't just bliss, it's votes. You know, hence the tax on unrealized gains, which Kamala is pushing under the assumption that nobody knows what an unrealized gain means.\par \par \uc2 So, this is time for Greg's economic corner. I want everybody to grab their kids, pull them around the T.V. Gains occur when an asset rises. Let's say you have a prized collection of baseball cards, and they go up in price. A loss is when the price goes down since you paid, an unrealized gain is the value of the investment before you sell it.\par \par \uc2 So, a tax on unrealized gains is taxing money you don't have, and it goes right to the government.\par \par \uc2 So, to sell a corrupt, immoral idea, you got to call it something else. So, you call it instead of theft, it's unrealized gains. It's like saying an illegal is a newcomer.\par \par \uc2 So, an unrealized gain is the house that your parents live in, you know, the one that they hoped would gain in value. Well, if it does gain in value, 25 to 50 percent of that increase goes to the \uc2 IRS\uc2  every year, and they don't even sell the house, which means the money actually comes out of their pocket. How is that not theft?\par \par \uc2 And they're going to say, but we're only to do this to really rich people. But as you know, sooner or later, we run out of really rich people. Then it's rich people, then it's not too rich people, that it's poor people. Then you have, as \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  said, really bad shoes.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Yes, he did. Jesse, I think another unpersuasive thing is when the Biden-Harris team -- well, now, sorry, Harris-Walz team is now saying, but Biden created all these jobs, and when you point out that the jobs were starting to come back under Trump, the jobs were shut down because of COVID. They actually are trying to suggest that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  wouldn't have shut down the economy and that none of the jobs would have been lost. And I find that just really hard to believe.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Now, the border, the jobs, the crime numbers, they're all mirage. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  came in third quarter, GDP was at 35 percent, that's a record, fourth quarter GDP 2020 4.2 percent. He handed \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  a growing economy.\par \par \uc2 All of the Biden jobs are bounce back jobs from COVID, and then 40 percent of the jobs under \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  have been from foreign-born workers, AKA illegals.\par \par \uc2 Now, Greg is right. What they want to do is they want to tax wealth, it's a wealth tax. This is what Liz Warren wants. Kamala is like Liz Warren, but she's actually Indian. OK, the people say it's this is like a conspiracy that the government would like somehow juice the jobs numbers in an election year to help the Democrat.\par \par \uc2 OK, so when Trump wins and he investigates it, they're going to call that a revenge tour. This is what's happening here. You now need to make $120,000 a year to live a $ 100,000-a-year lifestyle.\par \par \uc2 $20,000 in purchasing power is gone because of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , medium household income under \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , 78 grand. Under Biden-Harris, $76,000 it's gone. They're just taking the money away. Now she wants to raise taxes and spend $3 trillion and cap prices like a communist, but don't call her comrade, that's mean. You don't want to call people names.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Jessica, the economy is the issue, aside from abortion, which I think that's if you're voting on abortion, you're voting on abortion, but the economy is the one that can move voters either way. And this is not great timing for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , who is trying to do this rollout.\par \par \uc2 She'll have a great speech tomorrow night, no doubt. But Friday, everything gets harder.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: Yes, it's going to get harder, and we'll have to see what kind of candidate she's going to be after this initial period, get through the convention. She's going to do long-form interviews. We're going to have a debate, hopefully we'll have multiple debates, and one on our network, which I think would be fantastic.\par \par \uc2 But this is not the headline that you want on day three of your convention that has been going really well. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  immediately jumping to conspiracy theories about how this happened, though, is a little rich.\par \par \uc2 In August of 2019, the height of COVID, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's own administration got an extra 501,000 jobs, magically out of thin air that had to be revised down.\par \par \uc2 So, if you think that what Kamala or what \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  did was fraudulent, then you think what \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  did was fraudulent.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: How much were they revised down?\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: Oh, you're going with that?\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: No, how much were they revised down?\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: But they were fake jobs. Sorry, he's sitting next to me.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Can I go?\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: They don't exist. One thing, though, that could be a silver lining for all of this, for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , is that this is going to signal that there is going to be a rate cut coming, and our impressions of the economy are pretty much baked in. She's cut into Trump's lead a little bit, but people are probably, on Election Day going to think that he's still better for the economy. We know that. If there is a rate cut, people will experience that, and they may associate that then with the Biden-Harris administration, and then hopefully for Harris-Walz on November 5th.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Judge, the way things are going, I imagine that you could even have Harris say that she's going to extend the Trump tax cuts in 2017 in order to help the economy.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Well, sure, but let's be clear about something, there are 818,000 jobs that vanished, that Biden-Harris said they had added to the economy. And let's be clear about it, that is the largest revision to a job report in 15 years. It's never been -- there's never been a claim like that.\par \par \uc2 But it seems that, you know, the Democrats are OK if they -- if they change the facts, because nobody fact-checks them. It's just like two nights ago when \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is repeating all the lies of the fine people hoax and the bloodbath and praising the Palestinian people and the idea of injecting bleach to people who had COVID. All of that has been debunked, but nobody says anything about it. The media doesn't hold the Democrats for the lies, for the straight-out lies and the misinformation.\par \par \uc2 But let's be clear, the impact on the market is very clear, because companies rely on these numbers in order to hire and in order to decide what they have to make for the consumer. And you know, it just doesn't fit.\par \par \uc2 And the lack of policy that these Democrats are promoting and stating is shocking. And I heard Dana on your show today on "AMERICA'S NEWSROOM", Governor Polis from -- is it Polis from Colorado? He says, you know, they've got all of these policies about the economy and this and that. And Bill Hemmer says, well, where did you get that from? We haven't seen it. And Polis pretty much doesn't tell the truth, and says, oh, it's on her website. And Bill Hemmer says, I've been on the website. I didn't see it.\par \par \uc2 But here's the thing, what has changed in this country is this, 20 years ago, if you were 19 points ahead on the border, six on the economy, seven on foreign policy, and five on crime. That's the end of it.\par \par \uc2 But today, it is a different, there is a -- there is a different paradigm. You got to feel unity and joy. They don't care if there's a policy or if you lie straight up. All they care about is feeling good, and that's what scares me about this whole thing.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: All right, good talk everybody. Ahead, a bombshell new report claims that RFK Jr. is ready to drop out and endorse \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: This could be the game changer that tips the scale in November. ABC News reporting that RFK Jr. plans to drop out of the presidential race and endorse \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . Kennedy himself says he'll address the nation on Friday in Phoenix. And wouldn't you know it, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  also in Phoenix that day. The former President seems open to rewarding him if he drops out.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : I like him a lot. I respect him a lot. I probably would if something like that would happen. He's very different kind of a guy, very smart guy. And yes, I would be honored by that endorsement.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Dana P., how big of a factor would this be?\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Well, he's weaker than he was before. So, before Biden got out of the race, he was around getting nine percent in some places. Now, he's getting around four percent. But I talked to a friend last week who works in Republican politics and said that in the Battleground states where RFK Jr. had a presence or was on the ballot, he was still taking about four points -- three to four points away from the other two candidates in the race, and that they do believe that these additional RFK Junior votes, if they can -- if Trump can get a few of them, it could -- it could certainly help. And as we all know, those states are razor thin so it could help a little bit but I don't think it's a huge deal.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Jeanine, how do you think the negotiation is between these two campaigns about a possible cabinet position?\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: You know, I can't -- obviously, I don't know what's going on there, but what I do know is this. Is you know the Democrats have been talking about how unity and joy and hope and all that. They pretty much trashed this guy. They did everything but cannibalize him. I mean, they tried to get him off the ballot. They sued him. They literally threw him out of the party. His whole family threw him out.\par \par \uc2 And in the end, they wouldn't even give him Secret Service protection. His father was assassinated. His uncle was assassinated. I mean, they treated this guy like a dog. So, you know I think that a lot of people -- and they've said historically -- and people like Dana and Jessica might know more than I do on these particular poll numbers, but that you know, his poll numbers -- or his numbers would take away from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . I don't know if that's true or they take away from Biden, but I think that in the end he really is saying to the Democrat Party, you know what, go screw yourselves. You did so much to me and to my effort -- and I wasn't even -- you could have beat me just by beating me, but you didn't do that. You had to destroy me. And he was sick and tired, he said, of the tribalism of the Democrat Party.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Jessica, we talked about this on my show last night. Even if it's just 10, 15, 20,000 voters in a Philly or a Phoenix, that's big.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: Yes. I mean, it probably won't be out of Philly but it'll be in some rural county in Pennsylvania where this is happening. Absolutely. I mean, look at the damage Jill Stein was able to do against \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2 , and it was smaller margins than that. So, it's obviously something that's on Democrats radar. We talked about this a few months ago when the DNC hired Liz Smith who was the person -- the consultant who brought us \uc2 Pete Buttigieg\uc2 , a real incredible communications professional. And they hired her just to focus on RFK Jr. and the threat that he poses to the party.\par \par \uc2 So, you know, all eyes on Phoenix on Friday for this. My expectation is that they will probably make the deal. Maybe RFK can finally become Health Secretary and we can all never get a vaccine again or something awesome like that. But it's a real risk and it's obviously top of mind for Democrats.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: I'm sure Harold Ford Jr. can get his seven COVID shots even if he's still at \uc2 HHS\uc2 . What's up Greg?\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: It would be hilarious if RFK Jr. decides who the next president is. I mean, what if he -- what if he was able to see who he's helping more in the race and then he goes to the other person and says hey, if I stay in, you lose, let's make a deal. If he did that, he's a genius. It's a great ploy. Love him or hate him, RFK is not woke. He's an independent thinker with a curious mind which no longer resonates in the hive mentality of identity politics in the Democrat world.\par \par \uc2 RFK knows that every person -- this is why people like him, Liberals, and Conservatives, and Libertarians. He sees people -- persons with unique problems but no problem is more special than the other. So, that's why the identity politics thing doesn't work. He reflects a true equality where you know he accepts that everybody's unique but nobody is special. The Democratic Party demands that you accept the supremacy of one group over another in relation to their problems. And that's B.S.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: All right. Well, if we do find a dead bear somewhere in the Trump White House, we know who did it.\par \par \uc2 Ahead, weird \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  has some wacky moves. We'll talk about it ahead. Big DNC speech tonight.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Weird \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  set to take the stage for DNC night three. Kamala's running mate, who walks around like he's got ants in his pants, just got busted lying for the millionth time. But who's counting? But Dems say it's just your crazy old uncle.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JAIME HARRISON\uc2 , CHAIR, DNC: \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  is just a good and decent man. In many ways what we saw and what we loved with Doug Emhoff on the stage is what we're going to see similarly with \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 . I mean, he's that uncle that you just want to hang out with and just -- you know, he's always there. And whenever he comes over to the house, you just get so excited because you're like, what's next?\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Yes, he's the uncle who comes over to the house and you get really excited, Jesse. All the kids are like, oh, the uncle is here. We're going to go play outside.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Yes, let's go jump on his lap and tickle me and tell me a story. I don't know, Greg. He looks like the next contestant on The Price is Right. You're like come on down. He's like whoa, whoa. This is a guy you can't trust. Greg, you know better than anybody, men need to be composed. Men who make wild gesticulations cannot be trusted.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: True.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: You have to keep yourself together and hold yourself with a little dignity and stature or else people think you're suspicious.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: I bet he has ice cream in public.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: And uses a straw.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Oh, he's a straw guy for sure.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: By the way, there is an exception to Jesse's rule and it's Rip Taylor, RIP. Dana, what do you think he's going to talk about tonight?\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Well, Rich Lowry a couple of weeks ago when he was announced said this is an MSNBC's pundit's idea of what a normal person looks like.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: True.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: And so, to be honest, I don't know. We were glad to have him on "AMERICA'S NEWSROOM" and -- a couple of times. And one of the times he came on was the morning after the disastrous Biden debate. So, I think he's a very loyal Democrat. He's willing to come on the shows which we appreciate. And he's got a lot of introduction to do.\par \par \uc2 I am very much looking forward to all of the debates, but in particular, the one that Walz and Vance will do on October 1st.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: That is going to be fun. Jessica, I'll give you two choices. What will Walz address tonight, lying about his military service or lying about the DUI coverup?\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: I'm going to go with none of the above. Is that C?\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: No, there was no C. I didn't have room to put in a C.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: OK.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: All of the above though would have worked.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: None -- that's what I said first. I led with none of the above.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: I said all.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: Yes. So, all of the attacks, everything that people have been throwing at him, is just not working. His favorability keeps climbing. So, he's at plus 11 now nationally and J.D. Vance is at negative 17. And they're going to have someone who served with him speaking tonight. I think that's going to be incredibly powerful.\par \par \uc2 But the latest round of attacks about whether he had IVF or IUI are some of the grossest that I've seen -- I'm sure \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will be talking about that plenty as the most fertile man on the planet or whatever he would call himself. But when you look at the historic gender gap that we are already in that is poised to get even larger and that Independents, Democratic, and Republican women alike all do not want abortion to be a state-level issue. They want federal protections.\par \par \uc2 Going down this route is dangerous. It's ugly. And \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  will be able to talk about the power of reproductive treatments to be able to have his daughter Hope. That's why she is called Hope. And Republicans are --\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Oh.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: Oh -- you know, keep doing it. Again, I said this on Monday, just bringing in all those women.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: No. Hey, you can have -- you know what?\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: What? I can have all the women?\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: You can have abortions. Have them all you want. I don't care. It's not my business. I just -- you know what? It interests me though. Why isn't Planned Parenthood care that much about fertility treatments? I mean, if that's what you're talking. You brought it up. I didn't.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: They do.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: No, they don't. Judge --\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: Oh, OK.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: What do you think?\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Can I -- first of all, I don't want to get into the abortion thing, but I mean let --\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: She brought it up.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: I mean, really. And she always does. But I mean, you know, what's wrong with the people deciding in their particular state? I mean, isn't that the democracy that you're always so worried about? That's democracy. Let them vote for it.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: A six-week -- a six-week abortion ban is deciding yourself?\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: But let me -- let me tell you that as far as I'm concerned, this guy is a congenital liar. I mean, this guy not only lied when he got -- and I got to talk about this because I was a prosecutor. He lied on his DWI, right? He says someone was chasing me. I didn't know it was a cop. But he doesn't explain who was chasing him before and why he was speeding before the cops started chasing him.\par \par \uc2 And then he says after the fact -- get this. He says after the fact, he published that he really wasn't drunk when he plead guilty to drunk driving.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: That's the -- that's the big thing.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: That's when he ran for Congress. He freaking lied and said I wasn't guilty and I didn't plead guilty. Anyone who lies that easily should be a Democrat. I guess it works. That's why they love him.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: But that doesn't matter, Judge, because he loves abortion.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: Greg --\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Yes, he loves abortion and he's joyful and he dances like, you know --\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: All right, Dems think camo hats will have them two stepping into country fans hearts.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: Are Democrats taking back country music from Republicans? \uc2 Rolling Stone\uc2  making that case that my party is attempting to reclaim the rural and Southern identity that it's long ignored by embracing camo hats and DNC performers by familiar Nashville faces like Jason Isbell and Mickey Guyton. Watch this.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: Dana, as our country music expert, are we stealing your peeps?\par \par \uc2 PERINO: No. But country music is continuing to evolve. And instead of breaking itself up into a hundred different type of genres, it's just saying like country music is the big tent of music. And so, now you have a lot of collaboration like with Post Malone and others. Morgan Wallen doing a lot of those as well. So, it evolves and it grows and I have not seen a single camo hat since I've been here.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: Yes. Jesse, has Johnny found a camo hat yet?\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Nope, but he did find the vasectomy van and he is going to get snipped momentarily.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Oh, no.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: He isn't.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: It's an order from Jesse Watters.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: Reproductive health care should be accessible to everybody.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Exactly, even Johnny. This is like when Jesse Jr. puts a sheet over his head and tells me he's a ghost. OK, you're in a costume. Go to bed. This is what the Democrats do. They wear costumes. \uc2 John Kerry\uc2  goes hunting. Hillary has her hot sauce on radio.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Dukakis in a tank.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Remember with the helmet? Come on. Greg has touched on this like all week. You know, they're getting into country music, they're all into dads now, they're into hunting and camo. Come on, they're not fooling anybody.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: OK. Greg.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Well, you know, it scares me. Once Democrats realize I something exists, they infuse it with messages. They ruin Star Wars: The Acolyte, effectively destroying the Star Wars brand. I mean, what are they going to do to the country music? What do -- how will the songs change? Will we start hearing mama don't let your abortions grow up to be cowboys?\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: You couldn't see me --\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Abortion! Abortion! A whole album of abortion classics. You replace the word baby with abortion. It's going to sell.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: That was really gross. OK --\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: I didn't know you had such great abortion material, Greg.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: I just wrote it in the break.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: Judge.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: OK.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: It's really smart. Judge?\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: One camo -- so one camo hat and all the Democrats are going to be, you know, happy that the Republicans are now buying into socialism. Look, country music is All American. It's about people who love the flag, who love this country, and don't want their liberties infringed upon including the right to carry a gun.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: They also like beer and dogs.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Big bear.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: And trucks.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Guns.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Trucks and big wheels.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: And abortions. OK, "ONE MORE THING" is up next.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: It's time now for "ONE MORE THING." Jesse?\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Would you like to lend a hand identifying this crazy woman for us? Please, America, we need to know who this woman is. She jumps the fence at a tiger enclosure at a zoo in Bridgeton, New Jersey. Almost gets called, just inches away from this ferocious jungle cat, and just casually walks away.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Wow.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: We just want to know if she's OK. And if she is, we'd like to have her on "JESSE WATTERS PRIMETIME." Tonight --\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Wait a minute. If she can jump the fence, so can the tiger.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: That is true. God, Jeanine, you are so smart.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Oh, shut up.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: We got Sanders, and Ramaswamy, and Miss Perino.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Oh.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: Oh.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: All right, Greg.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: All right, tonight, we got a great show. God knows when it will air. Will these people shut up? We got the great Walter Kirn, the delightful Emily Compagno, the brilliant Kat Timpf, and the genius Tyrus.\par \par \uc2 Let's do this. Greg's \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  News. Where is he? What's he doing? Well, apparently, he's in California just walking around. Here's \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  just strolling along the galleria. You know, they got him in a padded jacket in case he falls, but his gate is recognized everywhere as he walks and stumbles and walks. But you know what? With this new outfit, he can't fall down.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: You know what? They said they were going to keep Saran wrap for the --\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Yes.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: -- if he ran again.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Exactly.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: All right, my turn. It's time for --\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Oh, I love this.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: All right, so she steals $850 worth of \uc2 Lululemon\uc2  and Sephora products, very close to the $950 California misdemeanor limit, no doubt intentional. And instead of fleeing the scene, the woman decides to jump into the trunk of her \uc2 Tesla\uc2  in a failed bid to hide from the cops. When they open the trunk, peekaboo, to jail you go. But I'm sure they let her out immediately.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Talk about junk in the trunk, Judge.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Oh.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Oh, nice.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Jessica.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: OK. So, this U.K. food truck really thinking about their patrons. They're now offering insurance to customers to protect against hungry thieving seagulls. Hawkins Barbecue took notice that their patrons were being routinely victimized by the birds swooping on their meals, so they introduced an insurance policy guaranteeing a full meal replacement for only $130. I can't do the conversion to pounds, right? The second -- seagulls are protected animals in the U.K. and all proceeds from the insurance policies are going to be donated to the Manx Wildlife Trust.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: I think that's one pound.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: Is it just one pound?\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Yes.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: I think it's one pound. All right, one pound.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Dana, go.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: Oh, good.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: OK. Mine is pretty quick actually. I just -- you know, there's a lot of hats here. There's no camo hats. But check out these hats here at the DNC convention. You have cheese heads from Wisconsin. And then you've got the corn cob head in Iowa, of course.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Nice.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: And everybody is here to represent a little bit and I see that. I think Washington State has the cowboy hat. And yes, there's hats.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: We got Texas hats too. And we probably got lays from Hawaii.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Did you wear one, Dana?\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: Oh, yes, the big hats.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Where's what?\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: We got lays.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Oh, stop talking, Jesse, right now.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: You know nothing about ethnic culture.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: That's it for us. Have a great night tonight, everybody.\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2024 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2024 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document FOXFIV0020240822ek8l00001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 Night Two Of The DNC Underway In Chicago\b0\par\par\uc2 Sean Hannity, Mike Tobin, Paul Mauro, Jeanine Pirro \par \uc2 9,810 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 August 2024\par \uc2 Fox News: Hannity\par \uc2 SHAN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2024 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2024 ASC Services II Media, LLC.  All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 SEAN HANNITY\uc2 , FOX NEWS HOST: It is officially night two of the Democratic National Convention. We are in Chicago. We're in Illinois.\par \par \uc2 Roll call is underway but outside, violence erupting a group of protesters have gathered. We're going to take you live in the ground in just a moment.\par \par \uc2 First, in case you missed it, a quick recap. Biden actually kicked off today's events after midnight this morning. Now, just a few short weeks after getting kicked to the curb by \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 , \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 , and other Democratic elites, and, of course, disenfranchising their own voters, party leaders also bumped the president out of prime time