w, whether or not they came with intentions or not, it -- we'll get back to Mike Tobin in a minute.\par \par \uc2 Let's dip in one more minute, \uc2 Bernie Sanders\uc2 /AOC really have emerged as the big powerhouse. All the -- all the undercurrent reports of my sources saying that he was the one that was pushing very, very hard for \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  over Josh Shapiro.\par \par \uc2 SANDERS: And, my friends, at the very top of that to-do list is the need to get big money out of our political process.\par \par \uc2 (CHEERING)\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 SANDERS: Billionaires in both parties should not be able to buy elections, including primary elections.\par \par \uc2 (CHEERING)\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 SANDERS: For the sake of our democracy, we must overturn the disastrous Citizens United Supreme Court decision --\par \par \uc2 (CHEERING)\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 SANDERS: -- and move toward public funding of elections.\par \par \uc2 (CHEERING)\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 SANDERS: And let me tell you what else we must do. We need to join the rest of the industrialized world and guarantee healthcare to all people as a human right, not a privilege.\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 SANDERS: We need to raise the minimum wage to a living wage.\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 SANDERS: We need to pass the PRO Act, so that workers can organize in unions --\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 (CHEERING)\par \par \uc2 SANDERS: -- and gain the decent pay and benefits they deserve. We need to strengthen public education --\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 SANDERS: -- raise teachers' salaries --\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 SANDERS: -- and make sure that every American, regardless of income, receives the higher education he or she needs.\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 (CHEERING)\par \par \uc2 SANDERS: We need to take on Big Pharma --\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 SANDERS: -- and cut our prescription drug costs in half so that we no longer pay any more than other countries.\par \par \uc2 Joe and Kamala made sure that no senior in America pays over $35 a month for insulin. We need to make sure that reality is true for every American.\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 SANDERS: I look forward to working with Kamala and Tim to pass this agenda. And let us be very clear, this is not a radical agenda. But let me tell you what a radical agenda is. And that is Trump's Project 2025.\par \par \uc2 (BOOING)\par \par \uc2 SANDERS: At a time of massive income and wealth inequality, giving more tax breaks to billionaires is radical.\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 SANDERS: Putting forth budgets that cut Social Security, Medicare and Medicaid is radical.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. \uc2 Bernie Sanders\uc2 , really what's amazing is how the Democratic Party now has evolved into \uc2 Bernie Sanders\uc2 . You almost heard the real \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  that they've been trying to hide, you know, sort of channeled through what \uc2 Bernie Sanders\uc2  was saying in so many different ways.\par \par \uc2 By the way we continue to monitor the violence that has taken place on the streets. We do have videotape from earlier that we will be showing you, and as soon as we have that available. But there was a what Mike Tobin called a -- it's actually up right now. Let's look at it.\par \par \uc2 Now, this is from earlier if you look at that side of your screen and a live shot on the on what would be your right side of your screen but Mike Tobin describing it as a -- you know, contrived planned confrontation with the police by these protesters. You know, you can call it the -- you know, in some aspects many pro-\uc2 Hamas\uc2  which calls for the destruction of Israel and all of that happening.\par \par \uc2 But this is an amazing kind of historic moment watching how \uc2 Bernie Sanders\uc2  is articulating a position that has was even rejected by Democrats but now advocated by \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  although we don't know for sure because they're not answering questions and they're not doing press conferences and they've not been confronted.\par \par \uc2 For example, do you still against fracking and drilling? For example, do you still support defund, dismantle, no bail laws? Do you still support defunding ICE?\par \par \uc2 Do you still believe you should decriminalize illegal immigration, and offer free healthcare, housing, education and driver's licenses to illegals? Do you still support the radical green new deal that that \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  introduced in the \uc2 U.S. Senate\uc2  with \uc2 Bernie Sanders\uc2  or Medicare for all, universal health care, no private health insurance for any American?\par \par \uc2 Again, it'd be nice to get answers to a lot of these questions but we haven't -- we haven't gotten them so far.\par \par \uc2 We go back to Mike Tobin, he's been on the streets of Chicago. Mike we just did see and carry -- \uc2 Bernie Sanders\uc2  wrapping up, but let's go back.\par \par \uc2 Mike, we did see somebody just get arrested live but we also showed part of that confrontation earlier tonight that you happen to witness, we'll rerack that and show our audience again you felt it was contrived, seemingly planned. What is the status of things now as the protesters have been told to go home?\par \par \uc2 TOBIN: Well, I'll tell you. As far as that arrest you saw, what you didn't see on camera is that guy tagged one of the police vehicles. He put a big black A for anarchy on the hood of one of the police vehicles and that's why the -- why the police nabbed him.\par \par \uc2 What you're looking at right now, this is kind of repeating itself. This is an unplanned march. The demonstrators just took off marching around the streets of Chicago. We're kind of in the west loop area.\par \par \uc2 And what we're seeing with the police is they're blocking traffic to make sure these kids don't get run over. We're at of point now where you've got the cops who have lined up and they're saying you're not going to go any further. They've done that a couple of times, the protesters start to chant "let us through, let us through", and thus far we've seen the police let them through.\par \par \uc2 We got to this particular intersection at Clinton and Adam Street, and right now, they're not moving. The police have lined up. They're stopping.\par \par \uc2 It looks like there's a white shirt in there, talking with who's ever at the front of the pack. There does seem to be a few leaders within this protest group and right now, they're talking with them. Obviously, though, you can see the hands waving, they're demanding to get through, the police have pushed us back to this point.\par \par \uc2 So I can't really listen into what is happening, but again, this is very contrived. They had a deliberate confrontation with the police earlier, shortly after they formed up their demonstration that they called make it great like '68, throwback to the riots of 1968.\par \par \uc2 Every indication that they wanted a confrontation with police, and they're doing everything they can to get it, including just marching randomly around on the streets and having all of these small confrontations, Sean.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. We really appreciate it. Mike Tobin, he's been out there reporting for us all night, right in the middle of these protests.\par \par \uc2 Paul Mauro, our friend, happens to be on the ground, former \uc2 NYPD\uc2  detective himself and apparently he's on FaceTime with us and he's been watching this unfold.\par \par \uc2 Paul, what are you seeing there?\par \par \uc2 PAULA MAURO, FOX NEWS CONTRIBUTOR: So this thing seems to be dying down a little bit, Sean. I am right now at the back of it. As you can see behind me, there's a lot of police in riot here. But as Mike Tobin said, a lot of this has been very performative. It was a relatively small group of protesters and they did everything they could to provoke.\par \par \uc2 Ultimately, the Chicago PD decided that it was time to ask them to disperse because they were blocking an intersection and they've just started walking around this area looking for a confrontation, trying to play it up to the media. But, really, aside from a couple of arrests and a few flare ups, it's really just been a lot of marching, a lot of chanting, a lot of it is very, very vitriolic, a lot of it very profane, very anti-American, obviously very anti-Israel.\par \par \uc2 But so far, we haven't seen any serious injury and only a handful of arrests.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Paul, we really appreciate it. Thank you so much.\par \par \uc2 Joining us now is the co-host of the hit show "The Five", our good friend, Judge Jeanine Pirro.\par \par \uc2 You know, Judge, I'm watching a couple of things unfold here. I want your thoughts on everything. We've -- we've been seeing more protests tonight. We had a confrontation earlier with police.\par \par \uc2 Okay, that's one side of the Democratic Party. But then we had this moment tonight to me which is a little bit surreal and there's a reason I wanted to cover \uc2 Bernie Sanders\uc2  because what was unheard of for the Democratic Party even going back a few years ago has now become the mainstream of that party as represented by the stated positions of \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 And I don't know if it's ironic, I don't know -- I mean, we don't really know if she -- if Kamala is going to at least publicly stand by it, but we know that's where her heart is. That's the fascinating thing to me.\par \par \uc2 JEANINE PIRRO, CO-HOST OF "THE FIVE": Yeah.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: That the parties become radicalized in my view. Your reaction?\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Well, you know, it's very easy for them to run the convention this way because when you have a candidate who is not willing to sit down with