e no idea who this woman is. She's a blank slate. She is everything that you want her to.\par \par \uc2 And so you can't really blame the Democrats for saying, why should we change all this? America loves this, this smiling face about whom they know nothing. They don't seem to connect her to Biden. She's done everything she can to separate herself from Biden, literally throwing him under the bus after primetime at 11:30 at night, where half of America can't even hear from him.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I could barely -- by the way, I got to give Joe credit, he was jacked up again. We saw the return of jacked up Joe. I never thought we would see that again.\par \par \uc2 And there he was. He had his \uc2 Red Bull\uc2 , his Monster Energy Drinks, his caffeine or whatever.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: But, Sean, you know they had to do that. It was past as bedtime. He sounded exactly the way he sounded during the debate, they had to jack him up.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: It was screaming though. I don't know what all the screaming was last night, everyone giving a speech, is like, oh, man, I'm getting a headache.\par \par \uc2 We always appreciate having you. Thank you so much, Judge Jeanine Pirro. Don't miss her hit show "Five", every weekday here on FOX, 5:00 Eastern.\par \par \uc2 All right. Live protest continue outside the DNC. All right. We'll get back to that and former DNC Chairman \uc2 Terry McAuliffe\uc2  will join us. And tomorrow night, I'll give you a preview of my interview with the one and only James Carville. That's all coming as we come back to Chicago.\par \par \uc2 Quick break. Right back. We'll continue.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. This a FOX New alert. We're monitoring live pictures outside the DNC as anti-Israel protesters clashing with police throughout earlier tonight and we're still watching the ongoing protesting.\par \par \uc2 All right. Joining us now, old friend of the show, former DNC chair, former Virginia Governor \uc2 Terry McAuliffe\uc2  is with us.\par \par \uc2 How are you, sir? Good to see you.\par \par \uc2 TERRY MCAULIFFE\uc2 , FORMER DNC CHAIR: Sean, great to be back with you, man.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Come on.\par \par \uc2 MCAULIFFE: Like old days.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. So I have Carville tomorrow. I got you tonight.\par \par \uc2 MCAULIFFE: Yeah.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And here we go, it's like old home week.\par \par \uc2 MCAULIFFE: I would just say this, when I was chairman of the \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2  --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Yeah.\par \par \uc2 MCAULIFFE: -- you let me come on the show once a week.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I did.\par \par \uc2 MCAULIFFE: And I came on, we had a thing. Listen, we're friends, we may disagree on politics. Nothing wrong with it.\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: We don't have to agree, and I want our audience at home to understand.\par \par \uc2 MCAULIFFE: Right.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: But it's fine.\par \par \uc2 You know, and I talked to James earlier today and when you go back to \uc2 Bill Clinton\uc2 , I mean, that's where we really got to know each other, right?\par \par \uc2 MCAULIFFE: Yeah.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Okay, \uc2 Bill Clinton\uc2 , abortion, legal and rare, and he emphasized rare. There's no restrictions from \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 . You're going to have an abortion up until the moment of birth.\par \par \uc2 I know you. There's no way you support that.\par \par \uc2 MCAULIFFE: \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  doesn't support that.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Yes, she does.\par \par \uc2 MCCULLOUIGH: She doesn't. \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  doesn't support it.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Yes, he does.\par \par \uc2 MCAULIFFE: Listen, this is going to be a big issue in the election, abortion.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Right.\par \par \uc2 MCAULIFFE: Because of Trump and his Supreme Court, they've taken away a woman's right to choose. We, the Democrats, I mean -- Sean, we haven't lost an election since Roe v. Wade was overturned. I mean, we've done -- look at Kansas, look at Ohio.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You're going to demagogue it, but here's the question --\par \par \uc2 MCAULIFFE: We're not demagoguing.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: But here's the -- but here's the thing.\par \par \uc2 MCAULIFFE: Yeah.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I had \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  debate \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 MCAULIFFE: Yeah.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Did you watch the debate?\par \par \uc2 MCAULIFFE: Yeah.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Okay. I had to press him, do you support any restrictions months seven, eight, nine, and he wouldn't answer. I went back in, fourth time I got an answer, it's between a doctor, her patient and their conscience. That means no restrictions.\par \par \uc2 Kamala is there and \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  is there. Now, they've been reversing every other position but at that point, isn't that infanticide? Is that really what you think -- is that where you want this party to be?\par \par \uc2 MCAULIFFE: And that's not our party, but the bigger broader issue is, let's take Florida, a bunch of states have just put a six-week abortion ban.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Every state gets to decide, different states.\par \par \uc2 MCAULIFFE: OK, I'm just telling, many women don't even know they're pregnant in six weeks. And you've seen speakers up there --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I support Dobbs 15 weeks, figured out by that.\par \par \uc2 MCAULIFFE: Yeah, there you go.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And I'm pro-life by the way.\par \par \uc2 MCAULIFFE: And you had a girl yesterday who was raped by her father, 12 years old. Under the new law in --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: So we're talking about but --\par \par \uc2 MCAULIFFE: I don't want to spend the whole day --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I don't want to talk about.\par \par \uc2 MCAULIFFE: Yeah, yeah.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. But then another social issues, then we'll get to the economy and immigratio