ut this week, Insider Advantage had him up in Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 MCAULIFFE: Sean, I love you.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I love you back.\par \par \uc2 MCAULIFFE: You're getting your ass kicked in these states today.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: We'll see. You know that's --\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 MCAULIFFE: I'm just telling you though that message is working. We're running against a convicted criminal, who's got extreme agenda.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: This is the problem. We don't know what message there is, because you have Kamala that that co-sponsored Medicare for all, no -- universal health care, no private insurance with \uc2 Bernie Sanders\uc2 . You have \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  that's co-sponsored with Bernie, the green new deal $93 trillion, and now her campaign says, oh, never mind, but we don't hear from her.\par \par \uc2 For a month, she can't talk to the press. She can't do an interview. She can't do a gaggle. Come on.\par \par \uc2 MCAULIFFE: She's been in this race 27 days. I think once we get out --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: It's time to hear from her?\par \par \uc2 MCAULIFFE: I think --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Except the off prompter for once?\par \par \uc2 MCAULIFFE: She's doing -- she's doing events all over the country. When she walks off the press --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: How about an interview?\par \par \uc2 MCAULIFFE: But let's just -- yeah, she should, absolutely.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: How about right here?\par \par \uc2 MCAULIFFE: Well, let -- well, here's what I'd say, let's get -- let's get the convention --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Let's not push it.\par \par \uc2 MCAULIFFE: Let's get the convention out of the way, okay? Then you're going to see --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You need a month to give an interview. Walked in off the street and I'd put you on.\par \par \uc2 MCAULIFFE: Well, I always do that. I mean, what the heck? You know, we got an own relationship. But you know, listen, we're doing great today, she's going to build