o fix inflation on day one and fix the border problem on day one?\par \par \uc2 She's been vice president for three and a half years. Why didn't she fix it now?\par \par \uc2 MCAULIFFE: And she's been vice president. Yes, thank you. You had --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Oh, she had no say, the last person --\par \par \uc2 MCAULIFFE: You had -- \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  as president, we lost millions of jobs, look what happened to our economy --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Only during COVID.\par \par \uc2 MCAULIFFE: And he was president though.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Oh, did he cause the pandemic?\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 MCAULIFFE: He tells Putin can invade \uc2 NATO\uc2  countries.\par \par \uc2 And I'll tell you one thing that drives me crazy, I was governor of Virginia, so much military. I have a son, he was a cap -- \uc2 United States Marine Corps\uc2 , very proud of him.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  saying those who wore in the cloth of the country were losers and suckers who lost their lives.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: That was one aid that said it. There's no confirmation by anybody else.\par \par \uc2 MCAULIFFE: The \uc2 VFW\uc2  just came out the other day and attacked him for saying the presidential freedom --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: OK, I have never heard it verified except for one person who made the allegation.\par \par \uc2 MCAULIFFE: Okay, but the \uc2 VFW\uc2  the other day just came out and attacked him when he said the presidential medal of freedom is better than congressional medal freedom. You talked to one military person.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: One more question.\par \par \uc2 MCAULIFFE: Yeah, okay, let's go.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. So green new deal, Medicare for all, okay, we're just going to forget all that.\par \par \uc2 MCAULIFFE: Yeah.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I'll ban fracking and drilling. That would you -- would we not then unilaterally disarm our economy? It's the lifeblood of the world's economy.\par \par \uc2 MCAULIFFE: Well, I'm going to let her speak to her energy policy.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Well, she already said, I will ban fracking and drilling.\par \par \uc2 MCAULIFFE: I was a pro-energy. Today, we're producing more energy than we've ever produced.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: She said it. How did she back off that?\par \par \uc2 MCAULIFFE: I'll let you come in and ask when she comes, but today --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Is she going to come --\par \par \uc2 MCAULIFFE: I would hope --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Will you broker that?\par \par \uc2 MCAULIFFE: A hundred percent.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I know you try.\par \par \uc2 MCAULIFFE: Why not?\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: The hell would freeze over before she had the courage that you do.\par \par \uc2 MCAULIFFE: Under Biden and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , we are now producing more energy than any time in the history of our country.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I'm going to have to admit, I admit you're one of the great ducking, dodging debaters I've ever met but it's great to have you.\par \par \uc2 MCAULIFFE: Well, you're one of the great cherry pickers on things, but I love you, buddy.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Oh, cherry pickers.\par \par \uc2 MCAULIFFE: Sean, fair and balanced.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: That's all the time we have left. Set your DVR so you never, ever, ever miss an episode of "Hannity".\par \par \uc2 Bret Baer and Martha are next. Let not your heart be troubled. See you tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2024 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2024 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document SHAN000020240821ek8k00001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 Michelle And \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  To Address DNC Tonight; DNC's Real Themes: Hatred And Retribution; Democrats ignore the will of their own voters; Democrats denigrate democracy with Biden coup; DNC night 2, the Obamas take the stage; Trump surging with black voters; DNC roll call vote underway\b0\par\par\uc2 Laura Ingraham, Peter Doocy, Mary Katharine Ham, Maria Bartiromo,  Bill Hemmer, Marc Thiessen, Jesse Watters \par \uc2 9,420 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 August 2024\par \uc2 Fox News: The Ingraham Angle\par \uc2 INGANG\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2024 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2024 ASC Services II Media, LLC. All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 BRET BAIER, FOX NEWS ANCHOR: We will hear from the Obama's and all of the primetime speeches and always, thanks for having us into your home tonight. We'll keep it fair, balanced, and still unafraid. The Ingraham Angle starts right now.\par \par \uc2 LAURA INGRAHAM, FOX NEWS HOST: Hey everybody. I'm Laura Ingraham, and this is The Ingraham Angle from day two of the Democratic National Convention here in Chicago. They're playing "tell me something good", one of my favorite songs, but Biden's out and Kamala's in. The torch has officially been passed, and tonight's theme is a bold vision for America's future, not to be confused with Thursday's theme of, for our future. What's the difference?\par \par \uc2 Tonight's big draw, the return of \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 . Now let's go live to the convention floor where Peter Doocy, Fox News Chief White House Correspondent is standing-by. Peter, what can we expect to see tonight in the Globama that's going to be lighting up the place.\par \par \uc2 PETER DOOCY, FOX NEWS WHITE HOUSE CORRESPONDENT: Well, we're told, Laura, that we can expect a show that's going to run a little bit closer to on time, as we all know, because we were here last night watching. They say it was because there was too much applause. I guess they weren't planning on people clapping for the first night of a convention, but they pushed the President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  past primetime. They're going to try to avoid that with \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 . They want him speaking in the prime slot when everybody is watching.\par \par \uc2 So, we're told they're making some real-time changes to the program. And what's happening all around us right now. You can see people are being seated for the roll call vote. These are Washington, D.C. delegates. More excited for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  a month ago or \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  now.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: I'm excited for both of them. Democrats are going to do well in this country.\par \par \uc2 DOOCY: How old are you guys?\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: I'm 20 years old.\par \par \uc2 DOOCY: 20, so you guys have not seen \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  in a situation like this, right?\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: What do you mean?\par \par \uc2 DOOCY: Like you haven't been to a big Obama speech probably?\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: No.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Doocy, who are you more excited for?\par \par \uc2 DOOCY: Pardon me?\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Who are you more excited for?\par \par \uc2 DOOCY: I'm excited to talk to you guys. I could be up backstage right now. I'm talking to you. So, those are Washington, D.C. delegates, as we continue to make our way, something that we've noticed with 15,000 credentialed members of the media, a lot of what is happening on the convention floor is you're just standing in a line to try to get different places. And so, Laura, we are going to see \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  and \uc2 Michelle Obama\uc2 . \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , not here. She will pop up for a couple minutes in Milwaukee. That is where she is choosing to be tonight. Back to you.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: All right. Thank you, Peter. There are a lot of fun means out there. You've seen them, Comrade Kamala and the Angle's original Kama- Chameleon, but now a new one. How about Kamala, the Killjoy. Americans with eyes and ears and a little bit of common sense see that the slick, joyful branding for what it is, it's a cover for something that is far more sinister. I like to call it socialism with a smile. It's a seething disdain for tens of millions of Americans who still support \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his policies.\par \par \uc2 Now, they tell us that the DNC was a celebration of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  last night and a joyful turning of the page, but it's all lies. First, they were ready to go scorched earth, remember against \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  just one month ago. And second, beyond the Obama nostalgia tonight, and boys, they're going to be on overload. There's not much joy in this convention hall, certainly not compared to what we saw at the \uc2 RNC\uc2 , because what really gets the crowd pumped up it's not love and it's not optimism, it's hatred and retribution.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Flag on the American conscience.\par \par \uc2 REP. ALEXANDRIA OCASIO-CORTEZ (D-NY): \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  would sell this country for $1 if it meant lining his own pockets and greasing the palms of his Wall Street friends.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Trump hasn't spent much time in New York lately, except that is to get convicted of 34 felonies, and that's just fine with us.\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2  (D), PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: He'll be a dictator on day one. We saved democracy in 2020 and now we must save it again in 2024.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Yes, right after the coup that kicked him out. So, welcome to the DNC, everyone. Have a great time. It's part freak show, part revenge play. They don't get this mad, I don't think at the terrorists in Gaza. They don't get this upset about China for committing genocide in Tibet. Certainly not that mad at Russia, crushing Ukrainian forces. But listen to Kentucky Governor \uc2 Andy Beshear\uc2  saying the most horrific things about J.D. Vance and his family.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 GOV. \uc2 ANDY BESHEAR\uc2  (D-KY): And J.D. Vance calls pregnancy resulting from rape, inconvenient. Inconvenience is traffic. I mean, it is -- make him go through this.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: He was given the chance to clean up that disgusting comment after J.D. Vance called him out, but Beshear did not.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BESHEAR: It's ridiculous, but it's also deflection. As a man, J.D. Vance will never have to face any of this personally, but it's sad that he lacks the empathy to be able to put himself in a different position.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Yes, he was implying that J.D. Vance's family should have to undergo a rape to really understand this. Nice guy. Now, I understand that people aren't always the most eloquent, but when he said it, he meant it, and he wants you to know that he's not backing down. So, is this what Kentucky elected him to do? Is that part of the joy campaign, be a vicious, hateful national spokesman for abortion.\par \par \uc2 So, I had this funny idea that they elected someone like a Beshear, by the way, he wants to be in the Senate to run the Commonwealth. But the diehards here at the DNC, they don't really care about raising our standard of living. They don't care about lowering energy costs for working families. They don't care about our declining military recruitment. You're not going to hear anything about that here. They're not going to care about how many migrants flood urban America, not too far from where we're broadcasting tonight.\par \par \uc2 But what they are really committed to doing is to punishing \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and all of his followers. So, how are they passing the torch when they're stuck in a bitter time warp laced with lies?\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: Extremists coming out of the woods, carrying torches, their veins bulging so emboldened by a president then in the White House that they saw as an ally, this will be the first presidential election since January 6th, on that day, we almost lost everything about who we are as a country. And that threat, this is not hyperbole. That threat is still very much alive.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: By the way, any time a politician says that's not hyperbole, it is hyperbole. And he's tried this for how long in order to get him, he's in Santa Ynez, California, I think right now, for a couple weeks. David Plouffe, a top advisor to \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 ' presidential campaign told Axios today that the democracy theme, what you just heard Biden say last night, it's going to be hit hard all week. But Biden has tried this argument for years. It didn't work.\par \par \uc2 So, again tonight, I say, what happened to joy? What happened to the vibes? Are they already running out of ideas? I mean, beyond the free vasectomies and abortion that is, it sure seems like it.\par \par \uc2 Now, I remember the locker up chance, they made a big deal of that at the Trump rallies in 2016 and whatever you think, it seemed to me that they were kind of chanted all in good fun. But these people, these people are serious.\par \par \uc2 (VIDEO PLAYING)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Look at her nodding. Now they aren't here to work with Republicans. They want to crush Republicans and all traditionally minded Americans. Now we know the Democrats' freedom agenda. You'll hear a lot about that, but it's a crock. Their idea of fundamental freedoms. They're not the constitutional ones. Second Amendment. First Amendment, no, it's about ensuring more abortions, even late term ones, more pot, more porn, more DEI giveaways. How inspiring.\par \par \uc2 And Kamala doesn't for a second think that she's going to be the president of all the people and the little bone they're going to throw to the little man, \uc2 Adam Kinzinger\uc2 , this week, it means nothing. It's a cheap nod to fake bipartisanship, because he's not a Republican at all. He's just an angry, diminutive chap who needs friends. By contrast, when Trump talks about working with the Democrats to rebuild American cities, he actually means it, because he's worked with Democrats for most of his life, long before politics. Again, this is all about the policies as he's told us back in February, his success will be the best revenge.\par \par \uc2 Joining us now. Mary Katherine Ham, Fox News Contributor and Kaylee McGhee White, Blankley Fellow at the Steamboat Institute. Mary Katherine, where's all the joy. Last night, this was like a back to the dark Brandon moments. What's going on?\par \par \uc2 MARY KATHARINE HAM, FOX NEWS CONTRIBUTOR: I'm actually a little bit surprised, because I know they're doing fan service for the room, right? It's not necessarily, it should partly be for swing voters out there watching, but I'm not sure it is. I think the only smart thing maybe the \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  campaign has done in this shift is to shift off the democracy is in trouble. The Republic is going to go down in flames messaging, because it wasn't working for vote --\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 HAM: -- all week. I don't think it's a good idea. I think the campaign about nothing, where she gets asked no questions, was better than the one about democracy dying.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well, Kaylee, this is an odd moment, because, again, Biden tried this, it wasn't successful, and he's actually a better speaker than she is.\par \par \uc2 KAYLEE MCGHEE WHITE, STEAMBOAT INSTITUTE BLANKLEY FELLOW: This is how they feel, though, and I think the best representation of where the Democratic Party's mind is at, was actually a few blocks away yesterday at the anti- Israel protests. And I got the feeling, I went there, I spoke with many of the young adults my age who were out there protesting, and I realized something, that the same ideology underpinning those anti-Israel protests, leading them to call Kamala, Killer Kamala is the exact same ideology that the Democratic Party has been running on for years.\par \par \uc2 These kids didn't get terms like settler colonialism or oppression or genocide from nowhere. They got them from Democratic controlled institutions, from universities, from corporations, and that's why \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  got up on that stage last night and could not condemn them because he actually shares their ideology. And it's vindictive, it's angry, and that is why, no matter how hard they try to push the joyful front, they can't do it.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: One thing that I found hysterically funny last night, of all the funny things happening here was when Hillary Clinton got up. Again, this was the old nostalgia tour with Hillary, but listen to how angry this sounds.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HILLARY CLINTON\uc2  (D), FORMER PRESIDENTIAL NOMINEE: I see freedom. I see the freedom to make our own decisions about our health, to speak our minds freely and honestly. I see freedom from fear and intimidation, from violence and injustice, from chaos and corruption.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: I mean we just had the pro-Palestinian protesters basically shut down Washington a couple of weeks ago, ripping down statues, defacing statues, and she's talking about, you know, we're going to keep it all calm.\par \par \uc2 HAM: No, it's wild. I don't know if they're trying to break my brain, but like I lived through the last four years, I lived through COVID. They're talking about freedom to make medical decision --\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: You can't say anything.\par \par \uc2 HAM: I lived through all of this. They want to be kind to your neighbor. We're about joy in letting you mind your business. You started a snitch line, \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , for people to call the police on their neighbors for having cookouts with too many people. But this is like a recurring theme. They're trying to recast as something different. But you see the tone, and you see what they actually believe when you hear these speeches. And you know, Biden's going to the well of the find people on both sides, and then he does his own find people on both sides about the pro-\uc2 Hamas\uc2  protesters outside, and then he hits the blood bath thing.\par \par \uc2 They're just -- they're addicted to this type of messaging, and I don't know if they're going to get out of it this week or in the next couple of months.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Now, by the way, Michigan Senator Gary Peters is out on the stage. Now, just yesterday, he said that Kamala needs to be clear that her views on the war in Gaza are different from Biden's. Translation. You need to appeal to the antisemites and their party. But there's another reason why Peters' remarks are significant tonight. He's the Chair of the Democrat Senate Campaign Committee and a handful of his most vulnerable candidates, Kaylee, \uc2 Jon Tester\uc2 , \uc2 Sherrod Brown\uc2 , \uc2 Jacky Rosen\uc2 , they're otherwise occupied.\par \par \uc2 They didn't make it to the DNC. Now, if it's all about joy, all about love, all about optimism, all about we love each other. Why aren't they here, Kaylee?\par \par \uc2 WHITE: Because they know that it's a risk to their campaign. It's kind of the ironic factor. And you know, being here for the past couple of days, you get the sense that these people are perpetually stuck in 2016. They can't move on.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: 2020.\par \par \uc2 WHITE: Well, and 2020, but you know, Trump's campaign tweeted this out earlier that yesterday during the speeches on that stage, they mentioned \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's name 134 times. They mentioned immigration about eight times, they mentioned the economy even less. They don't want to talk about the issues. They don't want to move forward. They want this to be about \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Do you think it's unfair of me to conclude that this really seems like a revenge play out there, when you saw their faces, when you saw those chants, they were most excited when Trump's face went on the stage and it was, get him, get him behind bars.\par \par \uc2 HAM: I think anti-Trumpism is what animates the Democratic Party, and they can't leave that part of them behind, right? They have to use that to get the base together and to get them excited, because they were not excited a month ago, and now here they are.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Now, the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  are walking out on stage with Gary -- with -- is that with Gary Peters? Yes, with Gary Peters, they're all walking on stage. So, they're making a big play of this. But Kaylee, the \uc2 UAW\uc2 , for instance, the union head out there speaking for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 . What's going to happen to the auto industry with these EV mandates? They're going to lose their jobs. This industry is going to be killed. But I'm glad the union leader, he's going to have his invite to the White House.\par \par \uc2 WHITE: Listen, I'm from Detroit. My parents are great friends with a lot of people who work in the auto industry. All of my neighbors growing up, their dads all worked for Ford or GM or \uc2 Stellantis\uc2 . These people are not voting for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 . They're very frustrated with the past four years, specifically with the green energy agenda, because they know their jobs are on the line.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Don't you agree Mary Katherine that the rank and file union workers, the ones like Trump visited with in New York, people he was with the other day, those are hardcore conservatives, most of these people.\par \par \uc2 HAM: There's clearly a split between the more well off upper crust of the union leadership and rank and file, that's just something that's been happening for years, and they've been separating, and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has been able to message to them.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well, he said that and when he met with them, he said, look, it's not about the next two weeks. This is about the survival of your industry, but they're going to make a big show of it, because they have to. But there's no substance that's going to be discussed in press interviews by \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , do you agree that those press interviews aren't going to happen?\par \par \uc2 WHITE: No, because the one that she did on the tarmac a couple days ago went so poorly for her that she's going to run and hide.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Wait a second, Kaylee McGhee White, there was a big return on investment in those comments as she made --\par \par \uc2 WHITE: Big return, big return.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Four time, five times. Mary Katherine, Kaylee, thank you both very much.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: We care about public safety; we need to prevent gun violence. It makes me ashamed when I travel the world, which I do, more children in America are killed by a gunshot than any other cause in the United States, more die from a bullet than cancer, accidents or anything else in the United States of America. My God, that's why Kamala and I are proud, we beat the \uc2 NRA\uc2  when we passed the first major bipartisan gun safety on 30 years.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Biden made his proud announcement on the same day, eight people were shot, three of them killed in Chicago. So, the truth is, Democrats really aren't focused on making your lives better, where policies are going to make you richer, safer, happier. We didn't hear any of that last night or today, and I suspect tonight there's going to be a lot of cliches and a lot of bromides and a lot of nostalgia for the Obama's, but the DNC is really driving home the message that the biggest thing they care about is not the American people but defeating Trump.\par \par \uc2 Just look at what they talked about yesterday. Trump's name was brought up, as Kaylee said about 160 times, the economy, number one issue in the country mentioned 28 times. The border, eight times. Crime, just six.\par \par \uc2 Joining us now is Chicago City Council Alderman, Raymond Lopez. Alderman Lopez, great to see you. Democrats winning any new voters at this convention?\par \par \uc2 RAYMOND LOPEZ (D), CHICAGO CITY COUNCIL ALDERMAN: I highly doubt it. I think this is all playing to their own base, not trying to recruit new people. Because clearly the Democratic Party, my party, is not interested in talking about what matters. How are you going to keep people safe? How are you going to secure the border? And how are you going to deal with the 8 million undocumented individuals that they let in under \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 ' lead?\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: A bunch of folks came up to me, I went for a little exercise today, walking, walking all around and walking out (inaudible) and people who lived in Chicago, and man, they love this city, and they are really mad, still mad, and it's not even political. It's not a political response. This is just a common sense desire for a better life. And I'm not hearing any policies about how to recruit, one of them said we were down what a 1000 law enforcement officers in Chicago, I believe, is that a correct number.\par \par \uc2 LOPEZ: Almost 2000.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Almost 2000, I'm off by -- I'm like the \uc2 Bureau of Labor Statistics\uc2 . I'm off by, you know, 100 percent. So that -- that -- that's a problem. And why aren't we discussing things like that?\par \par \uc2 LOPEZ: Because right now we're like in this beauty pageant of hypocrisy going on right now, where --\par \par \uc2 INGRAHA