is a real scandal. And there needs to be like an investigation into how this could happen, because to regular people, this just looks like putting a finger on the scale to make \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  look better, and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  look better going into an election cycle.\par \par \uc2 To regular people, maybe that's not what happened, but to regular people that's what it looks like.\par \par \uc2 BARTIROMO: Of course, because you're saying, oh, we thought that it was 242,000 jobs every month for the last year. And in fact, the Philadelphia Federal Reserve is saying that it's more like 130,000 jobs every month. How do you have such a wide disparity in exactly how many jobs there were and how many jobs you reported there were.\par \par \uc2 So, this is -- we'll see how this is perceived tomorrow by markets. I think this is going to raise the expectation that we're going to go into a recession in the coming months. Here's a report from \uc2 Evercore\uc2  saying that the likelihood of a recession within roughly six months is actually heightened now given this question about job creation.\par \par \uc2 So, you know, we're probably going to see an impact on Wall Street in terms of the markets, and we're certainly going to see people questioning what the Labor Department tells us every month in terms of job creation.\par \par \uc2 I think the bigger -- yeah.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: No, I'm sorry, Maria. But I think every American watching tonight has to realize that this was the shining glory of their economic bragging, OK? This is what their bragging point was, jobs created. The media reported, all the press poodles, Biden, Harris. Waltz, all of them. \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 , over and over again.\par \par \uc2 And we find out in the middle of the Democratic convention that it was a fraud, that number was fraudulent, it was wrong, and I think it was fraudulent. And so, what are they going to do? Tell the Fed to lower interest rates to help them again in an election cycle?\par \par \uc2 BARTIROMO: Well, that's going to be the betting tomorrow. If, in fact, we learn that the economy is so much weaker than everybody thought, then you're going to have more bets that the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  is going to lower interest rates in September.\par \par \uc2 But don't forget, the Fed is facing this tsunami of spending. I mean, it's so disingenuous to come out and say that the reason we have inflation where it is, up 20 percent on \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 ' watch, is because of price gouging.\par \par \uc2 I mean, it's so disingenuous to talk about price gouging and not mention $7 trillion in spending. Of course, it was obviously too many dollars chasing too few goods from the Democrats in all their spending.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Yeah, Economics 101. Maria, always great to see you. Thank you so much. All right, the DNC's big pate, the celebratory roll call votes just began. But Kamala is already the Democrats' official nominee, so I don't know what the --.\par \par \uc2 Joining me now, Bill Hemmer, co-host of America's Newsroom. Bill, what's going on down there? The pomp and the circumstance and all the fun.\par \par \uc2 BILL HEMMER, CO-HOST, AMERICA'S NEWSROOM: I hit a bit of a wall a moment ago here, Laura. Good evening to you. We're getting ready for this virtual roll call. It's a roll call rather. It's rather perfunctory because we know that \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 ' name is the only one in there. So, we'll get that going here in a couple of minutes as you hear the delegates roar here.\par \par \uc2 Laura, what we've been watching for the last hour or so are videos here in the arena from Republicans who say they will not vote for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . We've seen videos from women who have talked about abortion. And remember, the female vote is a significant part of this convention for all four nights here.\par \par \uc2 What we haven't heard is who \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is, what she's done in her life, what she's done as vice president, what she would do as president. And we've heard nothing about \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 . I think you'd be challenged to find a lot of delegates who really know his resume very well here, thus far, going into night two.\par \par \uc2 Now the job for that goes to her husband, the first gentleman who will speak on her behalf, and it goes to \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 , whose hometown is here in Chicago.\par \par \uc2 Jim Messina was on with Cavuto a bit earlier today, and he called \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  the explainer in chief. He's going to come out here and make this bridge for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  away from \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  into Harris and explain where the party is, why it is where it is and where it's headed. So, that's the big job.\par \par \uc2 Now, if you thought that last night was expected to be a classy sendoff for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , I think you could make a pretty good case that well after midnight or 12:30 on the East Coast, it was not the classy sendoff that perhaps a lot of people here in Chicago with the DNC had expected.\par \par \uc2 Having said that, Laura, I just looked at the schedule. Central Times listed, \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  is expected to come out, according to this schedule now, at 10 o'clock local time, which would hit him well into the 11 o'clock East Coast hour as well.\par \par \uc2 So, I don't know if we're up against it, again, like we were last night, or if they're going to cut out a lot of things in this program. But right now, that's how it reads. And we'll see how it goes momentarily when the roll call vote gets underway.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: All right, Bill. All right. Thanks so much. Kills me to hear Leonard Skinner playing in Sweet Home Alabama. That's OK. Alabama gets its say.\par \par \uc2 Joining me now, Marc Thiessen, former speechwriter to President Bush and Fox News contributor. Marc, great to see you. I mean, we had hiding Biden.\par \par \uc2 MARC THIESSEN, FOX NEWS CONTRIBUTOR: Yep.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Now we have duck and cover Kamala. Hiding and sliding Biden. And now we have duck and cover Kamala. She will try to get through this election cycle without giving a major interview to a real journalist.\par \par \uc2 THIESSEN: Oh, 100 percent. I mean, look, she's rising in the polls right now, but it's a sugar high. Because all it is that she's not an octogenarian who has dementia. That's why people are excited about her. She is the least examined major party nominee, probably in American history.\par \par \uc2 She didn't make it through the primaries. She didn't make it to Iowa in the first time around. She didn't go through a primary this time around, which means she didn't have a debate where Democrats attacked her record. She hasn't done a single town hall with voters, taking questions from voters, hasn't done a single major interview, hasn't done a press conference, and she's only going to do one debate.\par \par \uc2 Now, we all know that one debate can ruin a presidential campaign, so there's a great opportunity there for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Has that happened before in modern politics where they've only done one presidential debate?\par \par \uc2 THIESSEN: I think \uc2 Ronald Reagan\uc2  only had one debate with \uc2 Jimmy Carter\uc2 , but most of the time it's three debates at least, and they agreed to two. So, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  took one of the debates. Did she get a pass because the former nominee got to have, took one of her debates?\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Oh, OK.\par \par \uc2 THIESSEN: I think she ought to do -- they agreed to two debates. They should do at least two. But one debate can end a presidential campaign. We just saw that with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . So --\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Don't you agree that the meme campaign and the joyful stuff, that's all going to kind of fall away in the debate and it's going to be bait \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . To me, that's what they're going to prep her to do, to bait him January 6th or Charlottesville or go back to, oh, you don't like the way I look, or, you know, it's going to be that kind of thing.\par \par \uc2 THIESSEN: They're going to try and get him off his game. Look, if he goes into that debate the way he went into the debate with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and focuses on the record, and lays the traps and lets her fall into them, she is just as inarticulate as \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  without the excuse of age.\par \par \uc2 So, you just need to give her a chance to get her off the teleprompter and let her fall on her own face. She will do it. She hasn't given anything without a teleprompter yet. So, I think he's just got to be incredibly disciplined because this may be his one chance. This may be the one time we get her clean for an unscripted moment.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well, there's American Samoa just gave the roll call. We got the DJ up there and, yeah, Cassidy the DJ. So, hopefully that will get everyone jazzed up.\par \par \uc2 Marc, you wrote a great piece about the two factors that are most important in understanding the support that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has and that Kamala's vulnerabilities. Really quickly, what those are.\par \par \uc2 THIESSEN: So, the two statistics you need to understand and why all this - - what Biden was saying yesterday didn't fell flat, is on Biden and Harris's watch, Americans have gone from the highest personal savings ever recorded to the highest personal debt ever recorded.\par \par \uc2 All the savings were spent down. They now got record credit card debt, record personal debt, and record interest rates, which means they can't get out of that debt, and it's compounding every month.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: That's real life. By the way, RFK has now -- apparently, they're trying to figure out whether they're going to join forces with Trump.\par \par \uc2 THIESSEN: Wow.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: That would make a huge difference, yes?\par \par \uc2 THIESSEN: That would indeed. I agree 100 percent, yes.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: He's either deciding whether he's going to drought or he's going to join forces with Trump to beat the party that refused to allow him to have a real debate within the party.\par \par \uc2 THIESSEN: That would be quite a thing to have the son of Robert Kennedy endorsing the Republican candidate.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: In the end, will it have been a mistake for them to have shunned him aside as they did?\par \par \uc2 THIESSEN: I think very much so, yes.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: All right, we appreciate it. Thank you so much, Marc.\par \par \uc2 THIESSEN: Thank you.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Fabulous column. Oh, look who just showed up. Oh, wait.\par \par \uc2 JESSE WATTERS, FOX NEWS HOST: Hey, what's up, Laura?\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Where is he?\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: How you doing?\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Great.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: It's great to see you.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: So, we got the DJ. Killed me to hear a Sweet Home Alabama play, you know.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Can you believe they played Sweet Home Alabama at the DNC?\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: No.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: When they showed the Alabama flag up there, I thought a lot of people were going to lose it.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Wait, you can't have that.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: No, no, no Alabama flag at the DNC.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: So, a lot of love, a lot of joy. It sounded like a lot of hate last night. They get like that bulging, bulging vein.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Hating Trump gives them joy. That's what brings joy to the Democrats.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Is it hard for them when Obama gets on stage, Michelle, \uc2 Bernie Sanders\uc2 , and their electric personalities, is that a hard comparison for Kamala to --\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: I definitely wouldn't want to have to speak after these people. It's a big night. And Bernie, I'm really looking forward to \uc2 Bernie Sanders\uc2 , because when Bernie endorses Kamala that's not the endorsement you want.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Whoops. Jesse, take it away my friend.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: All right. Thank you so much, Laura. I really appreciate it.\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2024 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2024 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document INGANG0020240821ek8k00001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's DNC Speech Pushed Out Of Primetime; Obamas To Crown \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  On 2nd Night Of DNC; Kamala Crime Wave: Trump Blasts Harris Over Increase In Violent Crime; That's Scary: Van Jones Stunned Kamala Hasn't Pulled Away From Trump; Who's The Weird One? DNC Has Gender Neutral Prayer Room, Trash Police\b0\par\par\uc2 Jesse Watters, Judge Jeanine Pirro, Harold Ford Jr., Dana Perino,  Greg Gutfeld \par \uc2 7,470 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 August 2024\par \uc2 Fox News: The Five\par \uc2 FOXFIV\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2024 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2024 ASC Services II Media, LLC.  All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 NEIL CAVUTO, FOX NEWS CHANNEL HOST: OK. \uc2 Marianne Williamson\uc2 , very good catching up with you again. The former presidential candidate \uc2 Marianne Williamson\uc2 , we don't know what the future holds for her. She ran a very respectable and thoughtful campaign, a good many do, but that campaign at least for Democrats is done.\par \par \uc2 THE FIVE is now.\par \par \uc2 JESSE WATTERS, FOX NEWS CHANNEL HOST: Hello everybody. I'm Jesse Watters along with Judge Jeanine Pirro, Harold Ford Jr., Dana Perino and Greg Gutfeld. It's 5:00 in New York City and 4:00 in Chicago, and this is THE FIVE.\par \par \uc2 It's officially Kamala's party on the second night of the DNC, the Dems ditching \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , but making sure he suffered one last humiliation. Old yeller getting pushed out of his coveted primetime spot, speaking closer to midnight, and team Joe isn't happy about it.\par \par \uc2 One longtime aide saying, "This is awful. He literally set up a campaign and handed it over to them. Do they have to cut him out of primetime?" Dems letting other speakers before him drone on and on with really long applause lines, making the big guy 40 minutes late for his legacy-defining speech.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 , PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: Are you ready to elect \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 ? And because of you, we've had one of those extraordinary four years of progress ever, period. When I say we, I mean Kamala and me. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  said, and I quote, there are very fine people on both sides. My god, that's what he said.\par \par \uc2 Women are now without electrical, wilnado (ph) -- not allowed, because there's not without electric -- electoral.\par \par \uc2 We need to preserve our democracy. We need you to beat \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Crazy Nancy looking like a mob boss. She watched \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's speech. She was clutching a we love Joe sign and acting like she didn't just single-handedly snuff out the man's presidency. Pelosi says she has no regrets on cold capping him, listen.\par \par \uc2 REP. \uc2 NANCY PELOSI\uc2  (D-CA): I have to do what I have to do. He made the decision for the country. My concern was not about the president, it was about his campaign.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Judge Jeanine Pirro was up all night watching \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . Definitely did not record it and watch it in the morning. What was it like experiencing that?\par \par \uc2 JEANINE PIRRO, FOX NEWS CHANNEL LEGAL ANALYST: Well, I'll tell you, even my dogs fell asleep, Jesse. Look, half of America didn't see \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's speech because it came on at 11:30 and the truth is that a lot of the swing states didn't hear that speech either. And I think it's part of the plan to keep \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  away from the public as much as they can, which is clear with the juxtaposition of when Joe was speaking versus when Kamala is speaking.\par \par \uc2 But you know, in addition to that, I mean, they could have brought him on earlier, really. I mean, they torched this guy, they threw him over a cliff, and then they hit his final -- you know, his final eulogy.\par \par \uc2 And in that eulogy, I mean, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  was classic \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , he lied in this convention where all they talk about is joy and love and we're so joyful, and it's so wonderful.\par \par \uc2 And they could have bumped some of the other speakers. They could have bumped the abortion speakers, but they didn't want to do this. So, what does it tell you? They wanted him as far away from the public as they could.\par \par \uc2 And you know, here's the difference between Republicans and Democrats. The Republicans stick with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , through Russian collusion, through impeachments, indictments, convictions and his attempted assassination, and with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and the Democrats. Hey, as soon as it doesn't look like the guy is going to win, the hell with democracy. Forget the fact that Kamala hasn't gotten one vote. We're going to have her run for president.\par \par \uc2 I mean, it is the antithesis of democracy. And as Biden yells about, you know, all of those things that have been debunked, the fine people hoax. And, you know, he talks about the protesters, the \uc2 Hamas\uc2  people actually have a point. He's never criticized the anti-Semitism.\par \par \uc2 I mean, this is a guy who clearly is part of the left wing progressives, and Kamala is more the same, but in the end, it was simply about the fact that they're getting rid of him as quickly as they can.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Harold Ford, how relieved are you that you'll never hear from \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  again?\par \par \uc2 HAROLD FORD JR., FOX NEWS CHANNEL CONTRIBUTOR: Well, it's good to be back around the table. It's good to see my friend, the Judge and Greg.\par \par \uc2 I think last night, Democrats let the president down. President Biden down a little bit on the stage by not getting him out soon. I would agree with the Judge on that, but I thought he gave a recitation of some of the things that he's accomplished. A lot of the things he's accomplished, there's clearly an animosity and a competitiveness between President Trump and President Biden that showed -- that shows all the time when President Trump speaks about President Biden, and it showed last night with Mr. Biden speaking about Mr. Trump.\par \par \uc2 Some of us wanted a more cheery speech, but this is what these guys have done over the last six, seven, fice, or six years against one another.\par \par \uc2 I think the larger issue here for the campaign is and President Trump, I think, realizes this, and I think Vice President Harris is going to have to come to this with some more substance and specificity. Is who can address the concerns and aspirations and meet voters where they are in the country, in the middle class.\par \par \uc2 It's clear that Senator Vance understands that, his speech in Milwaukee talk a lot about Main Street versus Wall Street. I'm going to be curious as I listen to President \uc2 Obama\uc2 , and I don't know if we're going to talk about that, but I'll be curious to hear Governor Walz and even Vice President Harris, how she talks about making housing and health care more affordable, and the kinds of things she's going to do in a concrete and specific way to reduce prices.\par \par \uc2 But I think the Judge is on to something. I don't -- I don't agree fully. I don't agree with you, there was a ne -- a terrible speech, but I do agree that there are a lot of Democrats who were happy to hear him talk last night, but are relieved that Vice President Harris is the nominee of the party because she's a more competitive candidate and a likelier candidate to win in November.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Dana, do you feel the relief in the building? Yesterday was kind of a weird vibe. What does it feel like to you today now that he's gone?\par \par \uc2 PERINO: I feel like they've turned the page, and I don't know if they -- I don't believe that they were intentionally insulting to him. I think that they had a terrible scheduling problem, and they did not handle it well.\par \par \uc2 And I did note this, though, that nobody left. They all stuck around until the very last minute, and it was late to the point that my phone was like, hey, you're supposed to be in bed. I said, I know.\par \par \uc2 I also believe that you remember like having a good -- well, I don't have children, but if I had a recital or a play, and my parents had to come and you had to stay through the end, because you just have to stay through the end. And that's just the way that it is. I felt like that's what it was last night. I do not think that President Biden gave a good speech. I thought it was the speech from the State of the Union, with a few lines of \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is great, sprinkled in.\par \par \uc2 I remember in particular he said, she cast the tie-breaking vote for the Inflation Reduction Act, and very few people clapped, and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  absolutely sat on her hands, because that's one of the sticking points that she's going to have to deal with when she meets \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  at the debate stage September 10th.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Well, I'm definitely not one of those parents that leaves after my child has finished their recital performance. I always stay to the end. Don't listen to what you heard.\par \par \uc2 Greg, you definitely had a late night, and I'm glad I wasn't there to experience any of your emotions.\par \par \uc2 GREG GUTFELD, FOX NEWS CHANNEL HOST: It was long, it was painful. It was like last night Joe's speech reminded me of the worst part of every action movie, the death scene that keeps going, you know?\par \par \uc2 I think of Mr. Orange from "Reservoir Dogs". It's like, oh, he's about to die. Oh, no. He's still going. Oh, I think he stopped breathing. No, he's talking again. There were so many fake endings in that speech, and I do believe that was payback on Joe's part. He was just going to throw it all out there, because what they did to Joe last night is exactly what I do to the weird stuff in my house when I have company, I shove it under the bed, and I hope nobody looks and he didn't like to be shoved under the bed.\par \par \uc2 But this is -- this is the Democrats' week to present their party in the most appealing light possible. It's their coming out party for millions of people who don't pay attention to politics, right? The irony, though, is that in order for them to be appealing, they have to hide their true identity and embrace the traits that they usually mock when there's no election, suddenly they're about joy. They're about joy after four years of apocalyptic fervor about Trump ending democracy, climate change, ending the earth and racial division, being an eternal stain in our country, and that unless you employ in a full-scale radical change, our country is doomed.\par \par \uc2 And all of a sudden, happy, joy, hugs and kisses, they're like -- the Democratic Party is like someone on a dating profile stealing their photo from a J. Crew catalog when they really look like \uc2 Jerry Nadler\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But I want to touch on the speech. It's fair to say every politician lies. It's called spin. But there are harmless lies. There are deadly lies. Harmless lie, crowd size, golf game, a deadly lie is creating and perpetuating a hoax saying a leader defended Nazis and that hoax provides an umbrella for four years of sanctioned hate, you know, and then what do the fact-checkers do? They don't fact-check that because they'd have to fact-check themselves. That's why Daniel Dale at CNN is such a fraud. He'd rather fact-check a joke than something that put people's lives in danger and might have directly contributed to an attempted assassination of Trump.\par \par \uc2 Biden entered the living rooms of America and took a giant angry crap after feeding on a putrid buffet of hoaxes which were created to demonize not just the president, but half the country who supports him. He took the Jussie Smollett model and he made it to scale. He's actually worse than Smollett, because he created 70 to 80 million suspects, not just a few white guys in MAGA hats.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Can you please say reservoir again?\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Reservoir.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Reservoir.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Reservoir.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Reservoir.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Reservoir. Pinot noir.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Putting a little French on it. I like it.\par \par \uc2 All right, coming up, backstabbing Barack takes the stage. It's the \uc2 Obama\uc2 's turn to twist the knife into \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and crown Kamala.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: The Barack stabber is back after tossing Biden out like moldy cheese. The Os are set to take the DNC stage tonight to crown Kamala as the queen of the Dems. Harris is hoping to capture some of Barry O's 2008 campaign magic.\par \par \uc2 The artist behind the iconic Hope \uc2 Obama\uc2  poster creating similar artwork for her presidential bid. Look at that. Kamala has also been rocking an \uc2 Obama\uc2 's tan suit, delightful. And the media is getting a thrill up their leg.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: The people in this room had a great time last night.\par \par \uc2 JOY REID, MSNBC HOST: Exuberance, joy. I have not seen so many Democrats laugh, smile, sing.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: This was a legitimate moment of catharsis and love.\par \par \uc2 REV. AL SHARPTON, MSNBC HOST: All of us saying, we can really do this. We are coming out of this darkness that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has put us in.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: I think back to the Republican convention and just how much there was a lot of spiking the football.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Into Republican candidates, they're always looking for retribution there. They're looking for people to blame.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Everything here is relief and excitement.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: You know, Dana, I listen to that, and I think, how horrible it must be those people that their -- that their -- the joy in their life, or the horror in their life is based on how they feel about other people.\par \par \uc2 You know, Joe and Mika, they have been miserable for months, and now they're happy, and it's all based on some kind of external stimulus known as Trump or Kamala. Is that kind of sad?\par \par \uc2 PERINO: No, but it's almost as if there was a splinter in the foot of the Democratic Party. And every time they took a step during Biden's presidency, thinking that he was going to be their nominee, and having spent 14 million votes on it, that they were like, oh, this is so annoying. And honestly, if \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  was the nominee and gave that speech last night, I think the room would have been half empty.\par \par \uc2 So, when \uc2 Al Sharpton\uc2  says that this is -- they took us out of the darkness that Trump put us in. Like, no, the darkness was that the problem for the Democrats was that their nominee was the President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  who could not -- it became clear to everybody, apparently, including to at least \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 , and then maybe to himself, that he was not able to serve for another four years, and they were not willing to sacrifice the party.\par \par \uc2 So, the reason that all these people feel joyful is because they got rid of the one guy that eight weeks ago they told you was perfectly fine and capable to be president for the next four years.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: All right, Harold, good to see you. You're looking good as always. Isn't this strategy here what you would call star power transference, bring the star power into the room through the Obamas, and hope there's some tangential star power for Harris? I would do the same thing. They often use me like that here at THE FIVE.\par \par \uc2 FORD JR.: I mean, that's what the -- when Jamie Harrison, the chair of the party called and asked for an analogy about this. I used this analogy with you in THE FIVE.\par \par \uc2 I said, you said something at the outset of the last segment about how a vast majority of Americans are being introduced to the Democrats speaking here, and even the notion and the reality of \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  as our candidate nominee. I think you're right, and the reason tonight is so critical is really because of that frame, Greg, because America knows \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 , they know \uc2 Michelle Obama\uc2 . Many people believe that \uc2 Michelle Obama\uc2  would be as viable a candidate for Democrats to run -- to run for president as anyone.\par \par \uc2 So, for her and the president to stand before this convention hall. And Dana said it well a few minutes ago, the convention hall last night, no one left. People listened, they clapped, they responded at the right time.\par \par \uc2 So, when you have the -- really, the proverbial leader of our party, President \uc2