de, reminding people what it was like when he and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  took office in January of 2021 and how far this country has come.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: The president and the vice president have worked together very hard these four years. Made a lot of progress, but there's a lot of work left to do.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 PERINO: And we just heard from the president moments ago. Watch here.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Mr. President, are you ready to pass the torch, sir? Are you ready to pass the torch?\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 , PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: Yes.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 PERINO: OK, Jessica, this is as Jesse said when we walked in, this is your convention. I want to turn it over to you. I've read a few things today that President Biden, who will speak very late tonight. It's going to be 10:50 p.m. Eastern, he apparently is not going to spend a lot of time on his legacy. Apparently wants to look to the future, and he will give a full endorsement to \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 JESSICA TARLOV, FOX NEWS CHANNEL CONTRIBUTOR: Yes, that is the expectation. And I do think that what Senator Klobuchar was saying is absolutely correct. You will see tears. You did see tears even when \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  did a -- their first joint rally together since he passed the torch to her last week, and the crowd spontaneously started chanting, thank you, Joe, especially as they were discussing lowering prescription drug prices, which are one of the marquee achievements for the Biden-Harris administration.\par \par \uc2 I think it's really great that he will be focused on the future. I'm sure that lamenting too much about the past might be too sad for him, since we all know that he did want to be there tonight as the top -- at the top of the ticket, but I think that he is excited by the prospect of continuing his legacy through \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , he did pick her as his V.P. for a reason, and I think it's going to be a really nice unifying evening for Democrats.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Greg, it was not too long ago that there were Democratic donors even wondering if Biden and Harris should be the ticket at all, but they have apparently come out in full force, and even after her economic speech got pretty widely panned, including by some left-wing column economists, excuse me, they still I guess right now tonight, they're just going to say, we are all on board that train.\par \par \uc2 GREG GUTFELD, FOX NEWS CHANNEL HOST: But it doesn't matter who the person is, it's the machine, they just slotted out the old guy and put in the second wife. That's how it works.\par \par \uc2 So far, I've heard passing the torch four or five times just in this show all day. I've heard passing the torch, not the best analogy when you're dealing with a party that let multiple cities burn to the ground. Do you think maybe we should use something else, like maybe pass the baton because, or maybe it is the right one, because this is the party that nearly burned this country to the ground, at least economically for example.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , the only thing he passed was gas. Might be a good thing he let that torch go. You had to wrestle this job away from him like it was car keys from a drunk. And I don't think he's the one that's resentful. It's Dr. Jill, let's be honest, his life isn't going to change that much. You can tell him he's president. He won't know any better.\par \par \uc2 Paint his -- paint his house white, it will be fine in Wilmington, but she's not getting another four years, right? No more Hamptons galas, no more expensive designer dresses, no more glowing profiles and glossy magazines. She doesn't want to go to Delaware and have to shop at Wilmington outlets. All they have is Anne Klein, Dana. Anne Klein, she's too important for Anne Klein.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: I'm going to pass the