ny of these police officers are white men. Right there, there are two racist dog whistles, you know, right-wing elements that they're again exploiting for their personal behalf. It's kind of disgusting.\par \par \uc2 But you're right, it is infuriating that basic things people need for their own safety and security is denied them, but for them, they get it whenever they want.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Killer Kamala. Judge Jeanine, how much of an impact do you think that will be in this movement will have at this election?\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Well, you know, it appears that they're not separating Kamala from Biden. And according to -- there is an organization, the chair of the organization called The U.S. Palestinian Community Network. "We all come to a consensus", and there are many organizations, the pro-Palestine organizations, we come to the consensus that it won't make a difference if Harris represents this administration, they see it as \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and Biden.\par \par \uc2 So, this is -- she is responsible. She can't say or do anything that will convince them that she is different or will be different than Biden. They want to promise that no arms will go there. And, you know, try as they might, the Democrats sent \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2  to Israel, to the Middle East. I think he's in Tel Aviv yesterday, and he comes out today, and he talks about the fact that Israel has accepted a proposal, as if anybody cares right now, because \uc2 Hamas\uc2  hasn't accepted anything. \uc2 Hamas\uc2  doesn't even show up.\par \par \uc2 I mean, again, it's the smoke and mirrors. And, you know, make -- they made it clear, I think when the woman took over the mic at the DNC welcome party, she said, welcome to hell week. I think we all know what that means for them. They are angry, they're upset about the proposal of the -- of the Democrats, and the fact that they think that the United States is supporting genocide. It's that simple.\par \par \uc2 And they may be ready 