cluding ending the Trump tax cuts. One of the largest tax cuts ever in our country's history. And working with families, a gigantic capital gains tax hikes.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BREAM: Well, Vice President Harris and President Trump attacking each other's economic plans for the country this week.\par \par \uc2 It's time now to break it down with our Sunday group. Former Bush White House advisor and Fox News contributor Karl Rove. Democratic strategist, co-host of The Five and Fox News contributor, Jessica Tarlov. Juan Williams, Fox News senior political analyst, and Brit Hume, Fox News chief political analyst. Welcome to Chicago, everyone.\par \par \uc2 You made it downtown (ph).\par \par \uc2 JESSICA TARLOV, FOX NEWS CONTRIBUTOR: Yes.\par \par \uc2 BREAM: OK. So you'll heard me talking with Senator Vance there about where they are in the polls. He says they've got the message. They're going to win.\par \par \uc2 Here's another Fox News poll we have out this week. How do you feel about how things are going in the country? Sixty-five percent say they're dissatisfied.\par \par \uc2 So, Brit, knowing that and knowing in this setup, Trump is the challenger. Why is he not doing better, polling-wise?\par \par \uc2 BRIT HUME, FOX NEWS CHIEF POLITICAL ANALYST: Because he's Trump. I mean, the truth of the matter is --\par \par \uc2 BREAM: And the show was over. Yes, Brit has dropped the mic.\par \par \uc2 HUME: I think you have to get down to it. The past 8 to 10 years have been about \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . Everything has been about \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . I don't think that the Democrats would have let \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  get as far as he did if it wasn't -- if the party hadn't been confident that the -- that the Republicans are going to nominate \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  again, which the Republicans did.\par \par \uc2 The fact that Biden was doing even as well as he did, until the very, end is testament to the fact that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , he has 