 \par \uc2 And \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  was given a chance to push back on the protesters, and she took it. Remember last week when she was speaking and she gave that - that stare right at them and she said, stop, because she had also met with them beforehand. And I think that's the balance that she's been able to strike with this where they know that she is willing to listen to them, she will sit down with them, but she's not going to have you disrupting them like that. And I don't foresee it happening because of the police presence as well.\par \par \uc2 But also, this is a diminished movements within the party. I was on the Jewish Women for Kamala call. There was a lot of talk about this. I mean majority of people are on the side of the Biden-Harris administration, that they want a cease-fire. They want to see the hostages come home first before any of that and are strong supporters of Israel. And I think that she's going to be a great standard bearer for that balance.\par \par \uc2 BREAM: Well, and, Brit, that's caused her a little bit of trouble because, you know, one group comes forward and says, we were given indications that she might be willing to have an arms embargo on Israel. Then we get, you know, a statement from her campaign, no, she's not for that. It's a tricky one in some respects.\par \par \uc2 HUME: Yes, and I think police departments nationwide, and other security services, have gotten a lot more skilled at dealing with the kind of situation that developed in Chicago in 1968. We've come a long way since then. And it's probably a good bet that the police and other authorities here will do a good job of keeping this tamped down.\par \par \uc2 It will, however, be kind of a bad look to have people in the streets opposed - who would normally be considered Democrat or Democrat types opposing this administration and therefore \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 ' policies. We'll see.\par \par \uc2 BREAM: We will. We have estimates, 30,000 to 40,000, maybe 100,000. But I think, as you said, Monday may be the big night. So, we'll all be here for it and we will keep you covered.\par \par \uc2 Panel, thank you. We'll see you next Sunday.\par \par \uc2 So, we're going to take you behind the scenes here at the United Center and our Fox workspace as well, when we come back.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 BREAM: We are live at the United Center here in Chicago. It takes a lot to put together these conventions. And we wanted you to see how it's all getting done.\par \par \uc2 So, I'm taking you behind the scenes in this week's "Sunday Special."\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 BREAM: Welcome to the United Center. We'll give you a little behind the scenes look. This is where you're watching FOX NEWS SUNDAY right now and our main set that you will have coverage every single night of the DNC. It takes a cast of dozens and dozens, dare I say hundreds of people, to get this thing done. One of our team members has been here since August 5th.\par \par \uc2 Also, we can take you behind the scenes of the convention. We'll take you down to the floor, next.\par \par \uc2 Normally the 20,000 seats here in the United Center are full of fans cheering for the Bulls or the \uc2 Blackhawks\uc2 . But this week, it's going to be more than 4,600 delegates from all 50 states, seven U.S. territories, here to celebrate their official ticket. This is the 11th time that Democrats have held their convention in Chicago dating all the way back to the first time in 1864. You're going to hear from President Biden, former President \uc2 Obama\uc2  and Clinton. And then finally, Thursday night, Vice President Harris takes that stage.\par \par \uc2 And here is our home away from home. Sort of a Fox News village that's been transported by three to four semi truckloads of stuff from the \uc2 RNC\uc2  in Milwaukee to here. We've got engineering. We've got IT. We've got hair and makeup. And we've got catering, which just put out lunch, so I'm going to head over there and see you later.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 BREAM: You've got to have catering.\par \par \uc2 OK, a reminder, the Fox News Channel will have extensive prime time coverage every night of the Democratic National Convention starting 10:00 p.m. Eastern, including Wednesday and Thursday nights. You'll hear from Governor Walz and then Vice President Harris giving their acceptance speeches.\par \par \uc2 I'll bring you coverage around key speeches on many Fox affiliates at 10:00 p.m. Eastern Monday, Wednesday and Thursday. You can find us all over your channels.\par \par \uc2 That's it from Chicago today. Thank you for joining us. I'm Shannon Bream. Have a wonderful week. We'll see you a bunch this week and then on next FOX NEWS SUNDAY.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2024 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2024 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document FOXN000020240818ek8i00001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 's Fake Evolution Is Underway; J.D. Vance On \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  Accepting VP Debate Invitation; Joe Biden Bitter After Being Dumped By Democrats; Kamala's Campaign Is Deeply Worried; Democrats Hiding From The Press; \uc2 New York Times\uc2  Reports That 3.3 Million New Naturalized Citizens Under Biden; Democrats Hoping New Citizens Will Mean New Democrat Voters; Walz Locked Up Grandma For Defying COVID Lockdown; Harris-Walz Continues Divisive Zoom Campaign; Harris Trying To Frame Herself As Pro-Faith; Biden Is On The Hunt For A New Job\b0\par\par\uc2 Laura Ingraham, Ari Fleischer, Jason Chaffetz, Raymond Arroyo \par \uc2 7,767 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 August 2024\par \uc2 Fox News: The Ingraham Angle\par \uc2 INGANG\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2024 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2024 ASC Services II Media, LLC. All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 JASON RILEY, OPINION COLUMNIST, THE WALL STREET JOURNAL: So that is again something she would have to answer for --\par \par \uc2 BRET BAIER, FOX NEWS ANCHOR: And that's one thing we're going to talk about --\par \par \uc2 RILEY: -- if she ever sits down for an interview.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Yes, tomorrow on Special Report, President Biden and Vice President Harris will talk about trying to lower costs. We'll cover it all. Fair, balanced, and unafraid. Panel, thanks. The Ingraham Angle --\par \par \uc2 LAURA INGRAHAM, FOX NEWS HOST: Good evening, everyone. I'm Laura Ingraham here in Texas. This is The Ingraham Angle. Thank you very much for being with us tonight. \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  just accepted the first vice presidential debate on October 1st. Will J.D. Vance be there? Well, I'll ask him in moments. But first, Kama-Chameleon is trapped. That's the focus of tonight's Angle.\par \par \uc2 All right, everyone ready? Get ready for Kamala's phony transformation.\par \par \uc2 (VIDEO PLAYING)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Her Obamafied campaign team has obviously come to the conclusion that she can't win with her radical views or her record, no way, and they gave the story of her fake evolution on the issues to Axios to prepare the narrative for the week. Now, a big part of the Harris plan they write is to unapologetically change some of her more liberal positions and claim her White House experience help change her mind. She's also a fine plucking popular Trump ideas, notably, no tax on tips for service and hospitality workers, popular in Nevada, one of the biggest swing states.\par \par \uc2 Now, the Obama team, everyone has to remember, they never really respected Biden's record or performance, and at the same time, they know that a Bernie Sanders's \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  type Harris campaign cannot and will not beat Trump. Therefore, her big economic speech in Raleigh this Friday will feature a big magic act.\par \par \uc2 Tonight, ladies and gentlemen, behold the spectacle with astounding skill. \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will make her entire radical record, and her views disappear. Well, look, of course, they're correct, right, that Biden was a disaster, and his economic record, it's simply indefensible.\par \par \uc2 But the problem is, the political cure they're giving her is worse than the disease. The entire strategy makes her look like a lightweight who was just playing wrong on major issues for years, and while VP that -- while the VP was sitting around helping organize social events, well, what did she actually accomplish?\par \par \uc2 She's going to try to run away from all of her old positions in this effort to reinvent Kamala at age 60. Tonight, I'm telling you, it's not going to work. First, she doesn't have the political skill to do this. It takes skill to do it. It would require huge talent to explain what you believed a month ago or four years ago, you now reject. But she's just not competent enough to methodically distance herself from her old, detailed record. Now, \uc2 Bill Clinton\uc2 , \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 , maybe they could, but she cannot. Second, we have her on tape on all the issues.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 KAMALA HARRIS\uc2 , VICE PRESIDENT OF THE U.S., (D) PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE: I am prepared to get rid of the filibuster to pass a Green New Deal. There's no question, I'm in favor of banning fracking.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: For people out there who like their insurance, they don't get to keep it.\par \par \uc2 HARRIS: Let's eliminate all of that. Let's move on. We can't treat people like criminals when they're crossing the border.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: She's flip flopped on all of those issues. She's now opposed to banning fracking. She's not going to rip away your private health insurance, and suddenly \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is tough on the border. Why shouldn't we believe her? Of course, we shouldn't. She has a credibility problem because she was defending Biden's mental competence literally just six weeks ago.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HARRIS: The person I see in the Oval Office who is meeting with heads of the military and the intelligence community and in the Situation Room ensuring the safety of America, I've been watching the last three and a half years of performance. So, that's the \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  I know.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Third, third, third, when she did have her own say as the nominee, she skipped over more moderate people for VP, like \uc2 Mark Kelly\uc2  and Josh Shapiro, and she chose \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , one of the most hard Left people around. Now, his views are now by association her views, bad.\par \par \uc2 Fourth, by doing the cynical fake pivot away from the Biden-Harris failed record, she's conceding that they've been wrong for three and a half years on huge issues, after literally just saying a few weeks ago how historic Biden was and one of the greatest presidents ever.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HARRIS: A few words about our incredible President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . Joe's legacy of accomplishment over the past three and a half years is unmatched in modern history.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: If she believes Biden's record is so fantastic, why does she feel the need to come up with her own new ideas for her speech on Friday?\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 ADRIENNE ELROD, HARRIS-WALZ CAMPAIGN SENIOR SPOKESPERSON: She and President Biden have gotten a lot done, but she's also going to lay it out her own vision for the economy, how she's going to continue to lower costs for families, how she's going to continue to put consumers first and corporations last.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: This is all part of her plan to distance herself from Biden. And Axios is saying that she wants to break with Biden on issues on which she's unpopular. First up, rising prices. Well, someone better let the White House know that Kamala wants nothing to do with them.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 KARINE JEAN-PIERRE\uc2 , WHITE HOUSE PRESS SECRETARY: What I can speak to is the last three and a half years, and how much the Vice President was a critical partner in getting a lot of the big pieces, historic pieces done, the heavy lifting. She was part of that, whether it's the Inflation Reduction Act, the first piece of policy, which is the American Rescue Plan.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Those policies on which Kamala did the heavy lifting are directly responsible for the inflationary crisis that we're in today. Brand new data reveals that wages still are not keeping up with rising prices. Even Axios thinks that she'll have to pull off a very delicate dance to distance herself from Biden. Of course, Kamala knows that she will have the full support of most people in the press behind her when she does this, but in the end, I'm telling you guys, it's not going to work, because it just gives more credence to Vance's view and the Angle's moniker of two weeks ago that she's a Kama-Chameleon.\par \par \uc2 This is a desperate move at a time when the regime media is trying to convince voters that the GOP is desperate and disunited, but that's just bunk. Republicans are united and proud of their record. We don't need to restate our views or rebrand or rethink our views on everything from taxes to the border to energy production. For the past two weeks, the other side has tried to cement the narrative that somehow, they're on a glide path to victory, but all this rigmarole just shows that they're in real trouble.\par \par \uc2 The more voters focus on their pocketbooks, on crime, the migrant nightmare, the more serious they're going to get about choosing a candidate who has a record of success and one who, of course, can make America great again.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 DONALD TRUMP\uc2  (R), FORMER U.S. PRESIDENT AND 2024 PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE: I will terminate \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 's green new scam and rescind all of the unspent funds, give all of the unspent funds back to building roads, bridges, and give it back to the government and we will. To further reduce consumer prices, I will immediately eliminate every single costly job killing regulation the Biden-Harris administration has created to get to economic relief to workers and families. We will make additional tax cuts.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: The choice is Trump's economic success versus Harris's record of failure, and you just can't escape that. She is now and always will be the same smarmy Leftist who empathize with the Floyd rioters and welcome illegals and destroy California. And that's the Angle.\par \par \uc2 Joining me now, Ohio Senator J.D. Vance, the 2024 Republican Vice Presidential Candidate, a running mate of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . Senator, it's great to see you. When you look back on this. They destroyed Biden's career. They pushed him out of the race. They used the media to whip up the propaganda to try to demoralize Trump supporters. And at the end of all this, Senator, your campaign is up one point nationally in the Fox News poll that was just released. \uc2 Pew\uc2  has you down by one point. But what does this tell you about all the good vibes of the Harris-Walz ticket tonight?\par \par \uc2 SEN. J.D. VANCE (R-OH), 2024 VICE PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE: Well, I think it's good vibes generated by the media, Laura, but nobody actually believes it, because everybody can look at their checking account. Everybody can look at the price of groceries, the price of rent, and they recognize that \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 's policies, certainly on the economy, but on the border as well have completely failed.\par \par \uc2 The American people are actually smart, and the media and the Democrats give them no credit for this, but they think that they can somehow run a campaign purely on vibes. \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  says in her rallies, Laura, that she's going to reduce inflation starting on day one.\par \par \uc2 Well, day one, Laura, was three and a half years ago, her policies are what caused the inflation crisis, and the American people, I think, are just too smart to buy this garbage. It's why we continue to win this race. And look, we're going to run through the finish line, Laura, we're going to need every single vote that we can get, but I'm as confident today as when I joined the ticket that we're going to win this race.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Now. Senator, tonight, Walz agreed to a Vice Presidential debate on \uc2 CBS\uc2 , and he wrote on X, see you on October 1st, J.D. Senator, are you in?\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Look, Laura, we're certainly going to debate \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 . We just heard about this thing three hours ago, so we're going to talk to them and figure out when we can debate. I actually think we should do more than one debate. So, hopefully, we're going to see him on October 1st, but hopefully we're going to see him either before or after that, because I think it's important for the American people to actually see us discuss our views.\par \par \uc2 If you look at the way that we've run this campaign, Laura, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and I are giving every media interview. We're talking to every audience that we can get in front of, because our vision is so clear, we don't think that Americans who work hard and play by the rules should struggle to afford groceries.\par \par \uc2 We don't think our children should be killed by fentanyl. And we have a vision for how to implement public policies that are going to secure that border, cut down on the drugs, and bring the cost of everything from groceries to housing down to reasonable levels, because we have that vision. We're going to go anywhere and talk to anybody. It's a shame that the \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  campaign seems to run not just from the media, but from voters. And I think again, the American people see right through it.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well, Senator, is there any doubt that you will not be there on October 1st to debate Walz?\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Look, Laura, we want to actually look at the debates, look at the moderators, talk about the rules a little bit. \uc2 CBS\uc2  reached out to us about this literally three hours ago, I was landing from a rally and a press conference in Michigan. I strongly suspect we're going to be there on October the 1st, but we're not going to do one of these fake debates, Laura, where they don't actually have an audience there, where they don't actually set the parameters in a right way, where you can have a good exchange of ideas.\par \par \uc2 In other words, we're not going to run in -- walk into a fake news media garbage debate. We're going to do a real debate and if \uc2 CBS\uc2  agrees to it, then certainly we'll do it.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: What's it like to work with President Trump, because we're hearing from all the usual suspects that he's in a bad mood. He's snapping at everyone. He's this and that. But tonight, I want to give you the chance to just tell everyone now that you've had some time to work with President Trump, what's it been like?\par \par \uc2 VANCE: It's so weird, Laura, to hear the media reports and to see what they say about him and actually talk to him every day, sometimes, multiple times per day. He's in a great mood. I mean, he gets -- he just got shot a month ago, of course, and you wouldn't know it seeing or talking to the guy. But I think he feels extremely confident about how we're doing in the election. I think he's very excited about getting to work and solving the problems for the American people, but he's just having a good time.\par \par \uc2 He's laughing, he's telling jokes. He calls people and just wants to shoot the breeze and understand what's happening in the country, because he knows that's an important part of becoming a good leader and doing a good job for the American people. He's in a great mindset, and it's such a dishonest piece of garbage that the media says that he's somehow frustrated or upset.\par \par \uc2 He knows he's going to win this race, Laura, but most importantly, he knows he's going to be able to be a very good president for the American people one more time.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Now, this story about the manipulation of headlines via \uc2 Google\uc2  from the Harris campaign. People say, well, it's technically not disallowed. There's no real problem. I mean, it's been done before, but it's injecting pro-Harris spin into a lot of these ads. Senator, I think that seems like an effort to obviously help her. They're worried about -- they're obviously worried about their internal polls. That's obvious to me tonight.\par \par \uc2 But this is a sign of, to me, not strength, but real desperation on their part, that this is what they have to do?\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Well, that's exactly right, Laura. And by the way, I talked to a number of people behind the scenes, I don't think the \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  campaign is especially excited about where they are, nowhere near the optimism that we have on the Trump campaign. But look, \uc2 Google\uc2  is doing election interference, and it's not just \uc2 Google\uc2 , by the way, Laura.\par \par \uc2 If you go on X or any of the social media platforms, you'll see \uc2 The Washington Post\uc2  paying for advertisements for stories that attack me and attack \uc2 Donald J. Trump\uc2 . That's not the activity of a media organization. That's the activity of a Super PAC, and I hope the \uc2 FEC\uc2  looks into it.\par \par \uc2 Same thing with \uc2 Google\uc2  and all these Big Tech companies. Laura, we know that we are playing in a broken, fundamentally unfair game, but we also know that we're doing this for the American people. So, they're going to throw everything at us. We're not going to complain about it. We're going to plow ahead, do our job, and remind people. \uc2 Donald J. Trump\uc2  delivered peace across the world. He delivered prosperity and rising wages here at home. Give him another chance, he's going to do the exact same thing one more time.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Now, Team Kamala, Senator, is still refusing to commit her to doing any press conferences. Check this out.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Would it kill you guys to have a press conference? Why isn't she had a press conference?\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL TYLER, COMMUNICATIONS DIRECTOR, HARRIS-WALZ CAMPAIGN: Listen, the Vice President and Governor Walz have been busy cris-crossing this country. She said last week, we're going to be having a sit down interview here before the end of the month.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Senator, that's weeks away, weeks away.\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Look, Laura, and if she can't face a media that's fundamentally biased and friendly to her, how is she ever going to sit in a room with \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  or Xi Jinping or any of the world leaders that you have to deal with as United States President? I think it's very revealing, Laura, of her character, that she's terrified of the media. She's terrified of taking tough questions. And people say, Laura, you know, the critics say, well, it's because she's not that smart. And I actually disagree with that. I think it's because she knows that if her real views come out, the American people are never going to support a dangerous radical who opened the American southern border.\par \par \uc2 And they don't want somebody who is a prosecutor did to San Francisco. They don't want that to happen to the entire country. So, I think \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is hiding from the media because she's hiding the truth from the American people that she is a San Francisco radical, and if we give her a promotion of President of the United States, she'll just take the policies that turn San Francisco into a disaster nationwide. We're not going to let her and as much as she hides from the media, she cannot hide from the American people on Election Day.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Senator, I want you to respond to this Axios piece that, again, I think, bespoke real concern on the part of the Harris campaign about her radical views and the Biden record, that they're going to pivot away from Biden's record and key aspects and also these old positions, old, four years ago, positions she had when she ran for president. What does this tell you and is this going to work? The big pivot?\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Well, it tells you, Laura, that they have actually ran the poll numbers, and they know that this is a complete disaster. The American people don't want to ban fracking. \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  endorsed that. They don't want to bankrupt Medicare by giving it to illegal immigrants. \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  endorsed that. They don't want to eliminate private insurance or have an open border. \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  endorsed all these things and campaigned for them aggressively.\par \par \uc2 They know that if the American people see their candidate, she's going to lose, Laura. So, it's our job to remind people again of the contrast that \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  was a disaster. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  delivered peace and prosperity, as much as they try to hide her away and run her out of a basement, the American people are smart. They're going to know the truth, and they're going to not reward \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  when it comes to the election in November.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: J.D., one of my -- Senator, excuse me, I still call you, J.D. Senator, one of my dear friends tonight said to me --\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Please.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: -- well, all these suburban women, all these suburban women, all they care about is abortion, and they don't understand that decision is with the states now. It's not banned nationally, even if people, some people want to be banned nationally, it's with the states. What do you say to suburban women out there who are marinating in this propaganda.\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Well, first of all, I don't buy that, Laura. I think most suburban women care about the normal things that most Americans care about, right? They care about inflation, they care about the price of groceries, they care about public safety in the streets where their kids play.\par \par \uc2 Look, as \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has said he wants the American people at the state level to decide abortion policy, and you compare that to the Democrats who want to do nationalized taxpayer funded abortion up to the moment of birth. I think \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is actually trying to identify the reasonable compromise where he lets California figure out its abortion policy, Alabama and Ohio figure out their abortion policy. That is actually the common sense approach, and it's the approach that's most respectful of the American people.\par \par \uc2 The Democrats are obsessed with late term abortion and making sure taxpayers fund it. Obviously, Republicans disagree with that, but I think that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has charted a very reasonable course for the American people. Let the American people decide this, the federal government, we're going to focus on securing that border and bringing down the cost of groceries and housing.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Now, you went to Yale Law School. You know how to make an argument. You got a one minute pitch in a break room, you're a worker somewhere. You like Trump and Vance, and you got someone in California, someone from Massachusetts, and they're like, I don't like these guys. What's the one minute pitch to those people who are kind of independent but still somewhat skeptical.\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Yes. Laura, I think the one minute pitch is, first of all, don't believe the media lies about \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . Believe your own remembrance of the record and believe what actually happened when \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was President. We're not running in a vacuum here. Laura, this is not just campaign promises. This is about a proven record of leadership that \uc2 Donald J. Trump\uc2  delivered on. We had the fastest rising wages in the country in 40 years.\par \par \uc2 We had a world that was at relative peace and calm. We had manufacturing that was coming back into our country as opposed to leaving our country. And we had an energy policy that both punished the bad guys overseas, but also rewarded American energy workers right here at home.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's policies worked, and if you give him an opportunity to do it again, he's going to do even better the second time around. I think that pitch is what we have to take to the American people. Your life was better when \uc2 Donald J. Trump\uc2  was President. Give him another chance, and he'll deliver it again.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Senator Vance, it's great to see you. Thank you so much for spending so much time with us tonight. Up next, Biden is so mad, they got kicked off his own ticket. Well, he's throwing a bit of a temper tantrum. Why does it matter though? That's next.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2  (D), PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: I've been around a long time, and it's never been this bad before, I'm don't mean the press. I mean, the way we treat each other in politics, and it is literally getting incredibly difficult to count the number of lies people hear.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: What is it, lies, like these lies.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: MAGA forces are determined to take this country backwards. They promote authoritarian leaders, and they fan the flames of political violence that are a threat to our personal rights, to the pursuit of justice, to the rule of law.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Now that was a vicious, dark, and deeply defamatory view of the American people, and more recently, the guy who was forced out by his own party he's trying to brag.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Has the U.S. beat inflation, Mr. President?\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: Yes, yes, yes, yes. I've told you we're going to have a soft landing. We're going to have a soft landing. My policies are working. Start writing that way, OK,\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: More lies. This President was forced out again by the people who were closest to him politically in the middle of a campaign after one debate. And the administration has done such harm to family's finances that now the Harris camp is worried and trying to distance itself.\par \par \uc2 Now their internals, as J.D. Vance and I were just discussing -- discussing must show that she is actually in real trouble that she has to step back from Biden at his own party's convention. We learned that they're slotting \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  into speak on Monday night, not later in the week, and he's leaving immediately after the speech. I could hear the conversation.\par \par \uc2 Hey Hunter. Jim, Valerie, find some other place to get free food and drinks. You're out. They're all being forced out now. Joining us now, \uc2 Ari Fleischer\uc2 , former White House Press Secretary, and Jason Chaffetz, former Utah Congressman, both Fox News Contributors.\par \par \uc2 Ari, we hear that Biden is mad at how things turned out, but maybe to some extent, he kind of has a point given how short this Kamala honeymoon was.\par \par \uc2 ARI FLEISCHER\uc2 , FORMER WHITE HOUSE PRESS SECRETARY: Well, first, Laura to hear \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  complain about how bad things are, don't forget, he is the man when \uc2 Mitt Romney\uc2  was running for President. He said that Republicans under \uc2 Mitt Romney\uc2  want to put African Americans back in chains, so he has no grounds to complain against anybody.\par \par \uc2 Now, as for him getting forced out, you know, yes, he is bitter. He should be bitter. He has been forced out. He did not quit. He didn't -- I mean, he did not step down. He was driven out of the party by \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 , \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , and \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But his bitterness doesn't matter, because it's all about \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 . And as for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , yes, she's doing better than \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  was doing a month ago. Any Democrat would be doing better than \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  a month ago, but \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is doing worse than \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  was four years ago, and she is doing worse than \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  was eight years ago.\par \par \uc2 So, this race is still a race that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , if he does everything right, can win the race. The fundamentals are still there for Trump to turn this around on Harris. Biden is increasingly going to be a non-factor. The only issue for Biden is how fast can Kamala distance herself from him.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Jason, I want to get to that point. We talked about it a little bit with J.D. Vance, but this idea that \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , her staff goes to Axios and says, OK, this is what we're going to do on Friday. We're going to try to step away from Biden and her old positions because we think they're deeply unpopular, and then we're going to get all wound up around the axle about Biden feeling slighted.\par \par \uc2 The story tonight is the \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  campaign is deeply worried and one point up in the Fox poll, that's extremely significant, along with that Pew poll that came out today, it's way too close to be good news for the Democrats and Trump is up one in Fox.\par \par \uc2 JASON CHAFFETZ, FOX NEWS CONTRIBUTOR: Yes. The problem is that \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , she has no principles, she has no driving imperative. She is simultaneously trying to wrap herself around the Biden agenda, calling a great success. She was the last person in the room on Afghanistan, on all these issues. We have video tape of her talking about all these issues.\par \par \uc2 And then she has to say, well, no, I'm actually this person, and I'm going to fight inflation on day one, and as J.D. Vance just told us, she's been in office for three and a half years. So, which one is it? And when you aren't built on principle, you have no driving policy that's behind you, you get a Hollywood type and it just blows with the wind, and people see right through it.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: And Ari, they have a presidential candidate in Harris who can't speak to the press. Now they have a vice presidential, her running mate who also can't give a wide-ranging interview, because he's going to get nailed on all his omissions and misstatements and misrepresentations on stolen valor stuff. So, they're left with this. just mushy vibes campaign.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, you got Vance out there who torches the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  today off the cuff on inflation because now it's below three percent. Watch this, Ari.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 SEN. J.D. VANCE (R-OH), U.S. VICE PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE: When they say that inflation is down, they mean from a baseline where groceries are already 30 percent more expensive than they were when \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was president.\par \par \uc2 And they're not saying it's coming down. They're just saying it's not going up as fast as it was three years ago. That is not a reputation or a record to brag on. That's a record to be ashamed of.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Ari, this idea that they're worried about J.D. Vance. J.D. Vance is a dangerous pick. Meanwhile, \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  literally cannot give an interview. And this guy is just -- he's -- I mean, he's just on the Angle. But the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  thing today was amazing.\par \par \uc2 ARI FLEISCHER\uc2 , FOX NEWS CONTRIBUTOR: Anybody who saw Senator Vance on CNN over the weekend, taking it to the Democrats, taking it to CNN, taking it to \uc2 Jonathan Karl\uc2  on ABC. Senator Vance is an articulate, sharp man, and he's a great candidate in this race.\par \par \uc2 And, you know, it does tell you something when the Democratic presidential candidate and vice-presidential candidate are incapable of addressing their own base, the media. The mainstream media is their heart and soul, Laura. This is what's propped them up. It's what's given them the free ride. And they are afraid to take the free ride.\par \par \uc2 And when they do, when they do start to ask questions, I will predict you they're going to all be lollipops and softballs. There'll be horse race, silly questions. The press is going to fail to do its job fundamentally. They did in 2020 when they let Biden get away with the basement campaign.\par \par \uc2 And Republicans everywhere have got to realize that. Do not count on the media asking them a single hard question when they do come out of their shell. They will. They'll pick Rachel Maddow or somebody else to give them a softball interview, and they'll say, look, I answered questions.\par \par \uc2 Republicans have got to win this race on their own, doing it the old- fashioned way with advertising and being the tough guys on the block because the Democrats will never hold them to account. I mean, the press will never hold the Democrats to account.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Yeah, no joy in Mudville. I think there's no joy in the K-Hive tonight after these polls. Ari and Jason, great to see you both.\par \par \uc2 All right, come up just in time for the election. Biden is adding millions of immigrants to the voter rolls. Now, how is that happening? We'll expose it next.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: The \uc2 New York Times\uc2  is reporting that under \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , American citizenship is being granted to immigrants at a much faster clip than during the Trump years. The figure is around 3.3 million new naturalized citizens and counting. Now, it's obviously, to most of us, why this is happening and how it's happening.\par \par \uc2 Democrats are banking that they're going to get repaid by the newly naturalized citizens. For this entire process, they'll end up voting Democrat. According to Zhao Wang, whose business helps immigrants through the process, it's all about electoral outcomes.\par \par \uc2 He said the surge in naturalization efficiency isn't just about clear backlogs. It's potentially reshaping the electorate merely months before a pivotal election. Every citizenship application could be a vote that decides Senate seats or even the presidency.\par \par \uc2 Joining me now, \uc2 Stephen Miller\uc2 , former senior advisor to President Trump and founder of America First Legal. Now, Stephen, we obviously support people emigrating here the right way, but this process is being sped up by Biden. What is the real objective here?\par \par \uc2 STEPHEN MILLER\uc2 , FOUNDER, AMERICA FIRST LEGAL: The objective is simple, Laura. Maximum migration with maximum speed. Their hope is that having a massive amount of unvetted migration into this country, it will tilt the scales to the left.\par \par \uc2 Think about how much money is spent trying to move 1,000 votes in Michigan, 2,000 votes in Pennsylvania, maybe 500 votes in North Carolina. Whereas for nothing, the government can just mit hundreds of thousands if not millions of new citizens.\par \par \uc2 Under the Trump administration, a premium was placed on vetting, on ensuring that those who are granted the awesome privilege of citizenship have an attachment to the principles and constitution of the United States, to make sure that they would be economically self-sufficient, that they would pay their own way, that they would not rely on taxpayer dollars, and they would not commit crimes or threaten national security.\par \par \uc2 All of those vetting and screening mechanisms were thrown out by the Biden administration. There are no rules. There are no guardrails. It's get them in as fast as you can and make them citizens as fast as you can.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well, of course, Stephen, Kamala just keeps using the same line in her speeches. We don't have to play it, but she says, well, I'm for earned, an earned pathway to citizenship. She's repeated that over and over.\par \par \uc2 What does that really mean? Earned.\par \par \uc2 MILLER: Earned means the sellout scammer politicians in Washington really, really, really want to give amnesty as much as they possibly can, as fast as they possibly can.\par \par \uc2 Look, we've heard this nonsense phrase earned path to citizenship to describe mass amnesty going back to the 2013 mass amnesty bill. Every proposal just keeps getting worse. The one that Biden and Harris sent to Congress has no restrictions on even criminal aliens being able to get waivers for amnesty.\par \par \uc2 In other words, the same administration that is rubber stamping asylum applications for people who have no right to be here can also rubber stamp citizenship for criminal illegal aliens. They want illegal aliens to vote.\par \par \uc2 They want them on welfare and they want them to enjoy chain migration, so they can bring in their 30 million relatives and friends from all across the globe. Make no mistake. This is about getting as many illegal citizenships as fast as they can.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Stephen, great to see you. Thank you so much. And up next, \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  threw a grandma behind bars because she opened her business during COVID. She's here with a warning for America, next.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 GOV. TIM WALZ (D-MN): Some of us are old enough to remember when it was Republicans who were talking about freedom. It turns out now what they meant was the government should be free to invade your doctor's office.\par \par \uc2 In Minnesota, we respect our neighbors and their personal choices that they make. Even if we wouldn't make the same choice for ourselves, there's a golden rule. Mind your own damn business.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Mind your own business, really? Pot kettle black, Timmy. Consider his record during COVID, which included setting up snitch lines so neighbors could turn in neighbors.\par \par \uc2 And now let me tell you about Lisa Hanson. She's a mother of eight, a grandmother of 18. She owned a wine and coffee bistro 90 miles south of Minneapolis, and she wanted to mind her own business.\par \par \uc2 So, when Governor Walz issued a shutdown order during COVID, she tried to comply. But of course, the shutdown orders kept coming, and it soon became clear that she may not have a business if she follows that order.\par \par \uc2 So, between December 2020 and January 2021, she reopened her business on six different occasions. No one died. No one was hurt. She was just trying to take care of her family. For disobeying Governor Walz, she was fined $1,000 and sentenced to 90 days in jail. That's how Governor Walz feels about minding your own business.\par \par \uc2 Lisa Hanson joins me now. Lisa, great to see you. I know you ended up serving about 60 days, but what's your message to everyone watching tonight about the type of leader \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  really is?\par \par \uc2 LISA HANSON, JAILED FOR DEFYING WALZ'S LOCKDOWN: Thank you, Laura, for having me on. We know, us Minnesotans know the type of leader that \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  is. I know personally the type of leader that he is. He is an evil man, and we have seen him orchestrate this evil.\par \par \uc2 We have great concern that his evil, orchestrated with Harris's evil, will destroy our country, just like Walz destroyed Minnesota, has destroyed Minnesota and so many businesses.\par \par \uc2 My business is gone. My business was destroyed by Walz and Attorney General Keith Ellison. And he is not the cute, cuddly leader that people are making him out to be, that some of the MSMs are making him out to be. \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  is truly a radical tyrant.\par \par \uc2 And we -- this is not a country of tyranny. This is supposed to be a republic. If we get \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  as vice president and Harris as president, the republic is done.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well, Lisa, I know you've moved out of Minnesota, and I've got to say, I've spent so much time in Minnesota over the years. I love Minnesota. I love Minnesotans.\par \par \uc2 But for the life of me, I can't believe what's happened, especially under his leadership. Minneapolis was a great place. I know you're from outside of mini, but great town, great city, great people. I don't even recognize it anymore.\par \par \uc2 And that's what Americans want? That's what voters want for the country? Again, you left. Why did you leave, ultimately? It wasn't just going to jail. Why did you leave?\par \par \uc2 HANSON: Correct. Well, I mean, look at all the things that Walz has put in place over this last year, over this last session. Horrific bills that they have passed at the Capitol. You know, you can't even protect yourself anymore without fear of going to jail, going to prison for a very long time.\par \par \uc2 You know, we're the sanctuary state. If you want to have abortion right up until moment of birth, come on into Minnesota. We'll do that for you. If you want to genetically alter surgery for your children, come on into Minnesota. We'll do it for you. It is the things that this man has done to our state --\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Lisa, slap on high taxes on top of it. High taxes, unbelievable environmental regulation. It's a disaster. Minnesota has to save itself, and the country can't go down that road. Lisa, I'm glad you got out. It's sad what's happened to the state. But thank you for setting the record straight about \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  tonight. We appreciate it.\par \par \uc2 Seen and Unseen with Raymond Arroyo is next.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: It's time for Seen and Unseen, where we reveal the stories behind the headlines. For that, we turn to Fox News contributor Raymond Arroyo. All right, Raymond, the Harris campaign has taken identity politics to really an art form with all these Zoom meetings.\par \par \uc2 RAYMOND ARROYO, FOX NEWS CONTRIBUTOR: Yeah, Laura, every day there's a new one. Hispanics for Harris, white women for Harris. Just the other day, it was Christians for Kamala. At least it was called Christians for Kamala.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: She obtained her bachelors of arts from \uc2 Georgetown University\uc2  and served in the army from 2005 to 2012, achieving rank of corporal.\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: I just want to point out, I never did make corporal. I was just a lowly specialist. I pronounce our, she, her. Trust us when we say that we want to build community with you.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: That would have been more properly built as trans Christians for Harris. But I digress. The granularity is really important, though, to the campaign, Laura.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Now, Raymond, the Harris campaign, they're very worried about religious voters. And tonight, there's an evangelicals for Harris event plan. What are the -- three people there?\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Yeah. But even that is courted controversy. It's being hosted by an activist theologian named Ekemini Yuan. Expect inspiring, unitive messages like this one.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: We have to understand something. Whiteness is wicked. It is wicked. It always means it's rooted in violence. It's rooted in theft. It's rooted in plunder. It's rooted in power and privilege.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: I miss that gospel, Laura. But, look, 40,000, 40,000 progressive Christians turned up for this -- for this zoom call the other day. OK. And there's a Catholics for Kamala event later this week.\par \par \uc2 So, look, the Trump has no corollary at this moment, but perhaps they should be planning one. I think it's also a hard pitch, Laura, to sell the faithful when \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is the only vice president to not only visit an abortion clinic, but to endorse abortion with no limitations.\par \par \uc2 Still, that didn't stop the Irish for Kamala from assembling. They had \uc2 Terry McAuliffe\uc2  there and Linda Carter and the Lucky Charms leprechaun. But it appears their next zoom will have to be hobbits for Harris.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: Here I am in downtown Chicago at the corner of East Grand and West Grand. I just decided that I need to get out and start campaigning for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  for president.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: I don't even know who that was. Who is that? Oh, Sean Astin. Oh, that's what it is.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Yeah, Sean Astin.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Are there any actors not appearing on social media to support Harris at this point? I mean, it's lonely at this point. They got to do something.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: The Democrats, they're taking no chances, OK? Their PACs have been paying social media influences -- influencers to push democratic policies. And today, the president invited 100 influencers to the White House for a creator's economic summit, also known as a federal suck up session.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 , PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES OF AMERICA: More people want to go into your business than any other these days. What do you think? When I retire, where do you think I'm going?\par \par \uc2 I think you're going to change the entire dynamic of the way in which we communicate. And that's why I invited you to the White House, because I'm looking for a job.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Laura, this is a determined strategy. And this whole influencer summit, they gave them special access to the White House. They're giving them even bigger access at the DNC.\par \par \uc2 All of this is a strategy to counter Trump's Musk interview and his social media play the other day and brought the campaign.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well, that makes sense. I know this is what the Democratic Convention's TikTok site posted this week. It's a dance video. Well.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Yeah, well --\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: I actually learned how to do that over the weekend with my daughter's friends.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: I'm going to be -- I'm going to be looking for this, Laura, at the DNC.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: I know what that is.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: I expect you to recreate this.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Raymond, I'm not going to release the video. I did it this week. I did that dance. I, like --\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: All right.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: -- 9:30 at night on Saturday night.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Post it on \uc2 Instagram\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: All right. Check me out on \uc2 Instagram\uc2 . Raymond, thank you. Make sure to follow me on social media. Thanks for watching.\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2024 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2024 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document INGANG0020240815ek8e00001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 Media Fawns Over Harris-Waltz Ticket\b0\par\par\uc2 Sean Hannity, Sara Carter, Kevin Corke, Pete Hegseth \par \uc2 8,360 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 August 2024\par \uc2 Fox News: Hannity\par \uc2 SHAN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2024 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2024 ASC Services II Media, LLC.  All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 SEAN HANNITY\uc2 , FOX NEWS HOST: And welcome to "Hannity".\par \par \uc2 And tonight, the two most radical extreme well frankly dangerous far-left politicians ever nominated by a major party are hiding in plain sight in front of friendly crowds, of supporters, and they're cheering. Crowds aren't as big as they're letting you think.\par \par \uc2 Anyway, you got Harris and Walz reading their speeches from scripts, likely that other people wrote. They take zero questions. There are no interviews, no press conferences, no town halls, no impromptu gaggles, no television hits, no appearances, not even on friendly venues like MSDNC, which is pretty much most of the media.\par \par \uc2 Now, since her coronation, Kamala has only gone off script one time for a 30-second word salad about the return of American hostages. It was around 12:00, 1:00 in the morning. That's it.\par \par \uc2 Now, neither Kamala nor Tim have been asked about their radical positions, them in their own words. The alleged, subsequent flipping and flopping but we don't even know for sure if they flipped and flopped because we only heard that from their campaign and that was only after Harris was the presumptive Democratic nominee, that's called an election year conversion by every definition.\par \par \uc2 Now neither candidate has been asked about their radical past, radical statements or their votes, or their radical beliefs, or policy positions. These positions are not even on Kamala's website, which is pretty unprecedented. Neither candidate has been asked to explain their track record, they've not been asked to defend radical statements they've made.\par \par \uc2 The state-run media mob, they don't seem to mind. In fact, they actually seem to prefer it all this way. After all, the media created their own adoring fantasy about the Democratic ticket and they would hate for Kamala or Tim to get in the way of all that.\par \par \uc2 Remember in 2007, and I said, journalism in America is dead and buried. I had no idea how right I was. Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: This is America's dad, America's football coach, America --\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: She called him Coach Walz, yes.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Yes. She called him America's teacher.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Yeah.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: And the teacher that's cool enough without trying to be cool.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: She was John Wayne last night. She was a leader, a leader and she was clear that she was the boss.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Walz appears to fit the all-American definition of a man from middle America.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: He really has that perfect backstory. He also has those rural roots.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: I sort of thought in my head, you know, this guy, he really is kind of a rural American success story.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: A lot of people have noticed this sort of down to earth likable quality to him. A number of people that I have spoken to throughout this process, they have said that he is just a blast, that he is fun to be with.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: This ticket, the vice president and the coach, for those considering voting for the ticket, giving them the power to think that they're participating in something that will put a smile on your face.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Look, it's a non-stop love fest for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 . The biggest in-kind donation that any campaign would ever hope for and to think just a few months ago, Kamala was considered a political pariah with the lowest approval numbers ever for a vice president in American history. All of a sudden, she is now the second coming of Jesus. I'm sure tomorrow, the media is going to be dutifully reporting she could walk on water, cure cancer, perform miracles.\par \par \uc2 What changed? Did the border crisis get solved? I didn't see it. Did the economy get better? I didn't notice.\par \par \uc2 Did inflation go away? Is there peace in the Middle East, Ukraine and Russia, did that stop? Did anything get better? No, of course not.\par \par \uc2 And are any of you watching, here's the question you ought to be asking, the media ought be asking but they won't, are you better off than you were four years ago? How's that Harris-Biden economy, how's that working out for you? And what about your energy prices and electricity prices, how's that working out?\par \par \uc2 How about safety and security in your small town or big city wherever you happen to live? Is the world overall a safer place, war in Europe, war in the Middle East, and we're on pins of needles if Iran is about to bomb Israel.\par \par \uc2 Now, Kamala and Tim are getting the white glove treatment predictably from the state-run media mob simply because they are at the top of the Democratic ticket