s in my mouth.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: OK.\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 KENNEDY: I said she's a member of the loon wing of the Democratic Party. And there is a loon wing of the Democratic Party.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: Well, what's the difference between the loon wing and being a loon?\par \par \uc2 The only reason why I'm saying it is, if that is so, and you have a lot of American people who have now taken another look at her -- and maybe it's short-lived, to your point, Senator. She is running even with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . And I'm just wondering about the approach you're taking.\par \par \uc2 And it's very artful, don't get me wrong, and you raise a lot of substantive issues. It's going to come back to bite your heinies, isn't it? Aren't you concerned about that?\par \par \uc2 KENNEDY: I'm telling you what I think the American people think. It may not be what I think, and it may not be what you think. But this is Washington. You know...\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: Then what do you think of polls that shows that she's running even with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , regardless of what either you or I think?\par \par \uc2 KENNEDY: Well, the polls that I have seen, the most recent polls, you can't just look at the top lines, Neil. You have got to look at the crosstabs.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: All right.\par \par \uc2 KENNEDY: And if you look at the crosstabs and really drill down and see what people think, let me say it again, the polling that I have seen shows that many Americans think that the vice president is not a serious person, as I said, that she's a bit of a ding-dong, and, number two, that she is a member of the loon wing of the Democratic Party.\par \par \uc2 She's a San Francisco Democrat. She's a -- she's just like Congresswoman Ocasio-Cortez, except without the bartending experience. She is not mainstream.\par \par \uc2 And I -- the point I was trying to make was that, by making her first policy position known on abortion the idea that we should have a law that says you can have an abortion at any point, no questions asked, even up until the moment of birth, I think, for most Americans, is a loon wing position.\par \par \uc2 That's just my opinion. And -- but that's also what the polls says.\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: No, you're absolutely fair game to make it.\par \par \uc2 I'm just wondering how you think that will resonate with women, when she is called nasty and crazy and a ding-dong and all and disrespectful, between you and the president, what has been said about her.\par \par \uc2 I'm just wondering, do you worry how that comes across? And maybe you draw no distinction between a female candidate and a male one, and that's fair game, but that this could hurt you with female voters with these type of comments?\par \par \uc2 KENNEDY: Well, let me say it again.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: Sure.\par \par \uc2 KENNEDY: The vice president is a candidate for president of the United States. I don't care about her gender, Neil. Maybe you do, but I don't. I don't care about her race.\par \par \uc2 I care about her competence.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: Then why call her a ding-dong? Then why call her a ding-dong?\par \par \uc2 KENNEDY: And I'm telling you what the polling shows. I'm telling you what the polling shows.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: All right.\par \par \uc2 KENNEDY: And it does. And I will be glad to sit down with you and walk you through the polls.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: Yes, please do, because I never know when it's constructive to call people names, you know, Senator? I just -- on the left or the right. But we will see. We will see how it goes.\par \par \uc2 KENNEDY: Well, I'm sorry if it -- I'm sorry if it hurts your feelings, but let me say it again.\par \par \uc2 The polling...\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: Senator, you keep bringing it back to my feelings. My feelings matter little.\par \par \uc2 All I'm telling you is, if you think you can gain this November calling people names, I don't know how far that goes, left or right.\par \par \uc2 But we will see. It's still early, to your point.\par \par \uc2 KENNEDY: Your feelings seem to me like they matter to you a lot, Neil. And I'm trying to be objective here.\par \par \uc2 Let me say it again. The polling...\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: Are you really? Are you really being objective, Senator?\par \par \uc2 KENNEDY: I think so.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: I just think you have got a bash-a-thon of name-calling at her.\par \par \uc2 If you call that being objective, I don't know.\par \par \uc2 But, Senator, I do want to thank you for coming.\par \par \uc2 KENNEDY: I think you -- well, thank you for having me, Neil. I hope you have a better day.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: Yes, so do I. I hope you have a better day.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: We will have more after this.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: We could be just days away from \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  picking her running maid.\par \par \uc2 The list has dwindled down to a couple of very big bold-faced names, but not just two.\par \par \uc2 Bryan Llenas has more from Pennsylvania -- Bryan.\par \par \uc2 BRYAN LLENAS, FOX NEWS CORRESPONDENT: Neil, well, look, \uc2 Josh Shapiro\uc2  Pennsylvania's Governor \uc2 Josh Shapiro\uc2  is thought to be a top contender to be Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 's running mate.\par \par \uc2 He is set to take the stage here at a high school in Montgomery County,one of Philadelphia's critical blue suburbs, at any moment here. This is his third rally for the Harris campaign since she announced her campaign for president.\par \par \uc2 We're told to expect Shapiro to really go after the former President Trump on particularly this idea of him being a threat to real freedoms, including reproductive freedom for women and a threat to a free and fair election.\par \par \uc2 Shapiro has sharpened his attacks particularly after the Trump campaign says it won't commit to a debate until Harris is the nominee.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 GOV. JOSH SHAPIRO (D-PA): He's not just afraid to debate her because he knows she's going to kick his ass in the debate.\par \par \uc2 (CHEERING)\par \par \uc2 SHAPIRO: She is a skilled debater. But he's afraid to debate her because he's afraid of his record. He's afraid of having to defend a record that has been really dangerous and destructive.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 LLENAS: Michigan's Governor \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2  is also speaking alongside Shapiro here.\par \par \uc2 Earlier, she ended speculation that she could be Harris' V.P. pick saying she's not being vetted by the campaign. Other potential Harris V.P. picks include North Carolina Governor Roy Cooper, Arizona Senator \uc2 Mark Kelly\uc2 , Minnesota Governor \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , among others.\par \par \uc2 But a FOX News polls show Shapiro could make all the difference in what's seen as a must-win state here for Democrats. Shapiro, who campaigned as a moderate Democrat, has a 61 percent favorable rating in Pennsylvania. That's higher than Harris or Trump.\par \par \uc2 The poll also finds in a hypothetical matchup in Pennsylvania, Harris and Trump are tied. But the 51-year-old Shapiro beats Trump here in Pennsylvania by 10 points.\par \par \uc2 Now, Governor Shapiro happens to be Jewish and happens to be very pro- Israel. There are some that think that could hurt him with progressives. But I will say, Neil, speaking to voters here at this rally, they really appreciate Shapiro's blunt talk.\par \par \uc2 One guy was wearing a T-shirt that quoted Shapiro urging Trump to -- quote -- "stop bleep-talking" America, so a lot of folks here are excited to see how Shapiro is going to go after Trump. Trump is holding a rally in Harrisburg on Wednesday -- Neil.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: All right, thank you very much, Bryan Llenas.\par \par \uc2 Speaking of the former president, he does want to return to Butler, Pennsylvania, but some new revelations today on the ticktock about what went down a little more than two weeks ago might give him pause, certainly the Secret Service -- after this.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: Welcome back, everyone.\par \par \uc2 As you know, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  wants to return to Butler, Pennsylvania, where he darned near lost his life, and likes the idea of outdoor rallies.\par \par \uc2 The Secret Service is a little leery of that. And after hearing some of the details of what almost went down a couple of weeks ago, you can understand why.\par \par \uc2 Jeff Paul has more from Butler -- Jeff.\par \par \uc2 JEFF PAUL, FOX NEWS CORRESPONDENT: Well, yes, Neil.\par \par \uc2 So far, the \uc2 FBI\uc2  says they have conducted roughly 450 interviews as they try to figure out not only how this happened, but also why. They also said that Crooks, who they describe as a loner, is very intelligent and went to great lengths to try to conceal and hide what he was doing.\par \par \uc2 They also say, over the past year or so, he used aliases to purchase firearm supplies and materials to build explosive devices. We're also learning Crooks registered for the rally three days after it was announced and then searched how far Oswald was from JFK that same day.\par \par \uc2 They also say he surveilled the site and practice at a gun range using the same AR-15-style rifle. But on the day of the shooting, Crooks first visited Butler, bought ammo, and then went back home. He then returned to the rally side and flew his drone.\par \par \uc2 A short time later, local police identified him as a suspicious person. Texts between local law enforcement obtained by Senator \uc2 Chuck Grassley\uc2  appear to show a picture of Crooks with a local officer telling the group - - quote -- "If you want to notify Secret Service snipers to look out, I lost sight of him."\par \par \uc2 Local SWAT member Jason Woods telling ABC News they were supposed to have a face-to-face briefing with Secret Service, but that never happened.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JASON WOODS, BEAVER COUNTY, PENNSYLVANIA, SWAT TEAM: I think that was probably a pivotal point where I started thinking things were wrong, because that never happened. And we had no communication with the Secret Service.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 PAUL: The \uc2 FBI\uc2  also detailed Crooks climbed on the roof not using a ladder, but the HVAC system and piping. Investigators say he then moved across rooftops, concealing the rifle with a collapsible stock, before firing off eight shots and later being shot and killed.\par \par \uc2 No word on when the \uc2 FBI\uc2  is going to interview Trump. We know he has agreed to that standard victim interview that usually happens in situations like this. Also, Neil, no details so far on when Trump is going to come back here for that rally he has promised Butler, Pennsylvania -- Neil.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: Got it.\par \par \uc2 Jeff Paul, thank you very much.\par \par \uc2 I want to take you to Austin, Texas, right now to LBJ Presidential Library. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has arrived. He's going to announce a major revamp that he'd like to see at the Supreme Court. A lot easier said than done, and a lot of these are Herculean, some say overtly political, leaps on the part of the president, with the full backing of his vice president.\par \par \uc2 We're on it after this.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 QUESTION: Speaker Johnson says your Supreme Court reform is dead on arrival. What's your reaction, sir?\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 , PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: Who said that?\par \par \uc2 QUESTION: Speaker Johnson said it's dead on arrival.\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: I think that is what he is.\par \par \uc2 QUESTION: That he is?\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: That he is, dead on arrival.\par \par \uc2 QUESTION: How are you going to get this done?\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: You ask me that -- on everything I have ever passed, you ask me that. We're going to figure out a way.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: All right, so finally, some words to put together exactly what President Biden has said about this big speech he's going to be making at the LBJ museum, the library, a few minutes from now, a total revamp of the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  that we will call, for among other things, 18-year term limits, a binding code of conduct, a constitutional amendment saying presidents will not have criminal immunity.\par \par \uc2 Now, as you have heard, Speaker Mike Johnson has said it's at least dead on arrival in the House. We have heard as well from the minority leader of the \uc2 United States Senate\uc2  that it's going nowhere with him.\par \par \uc2 We have got Jonathan Turley back with us, the \uc2 George Washington University\uc2  law professor, and \uc2 Trey Gowdy\uc2 , the "Sunday Night in America" host, both of them to weigh in on that.\par \par \uc2 Gentleman, as I think you were both reminding me earlier, it is an uphill climb to get this done, and certainly to get a constitutional amendment passed to get this done. Spell out how difficult it is, Jonathan.\par \par \uc2 TURLEY: Well, first of all, in the constitutional amendment, it was a process designed to be extremely difficult. You need more than a simple majority, obviously, in the House. You need a very high number of the states, obviously, to pass it.\par \par \uc2 That's the reason there are few amendments relatively to our Constitution. In terms of legislation, you're going to have the same problems even with a majority, because a lot of members are going to privately say, look, this is wrong. If we start to take a hatchet to our main institutions, then there will be no end to this.\par \par \uc2 I mean, by the way, if Congress could do this with legislation, we will see if he's going to suggest that the limit has to be done by the amendment. But if they're suggesting they can do it by legislation, why not make it eight years, two years? How about one year? Then you could have a fresh new set of court, like it's a neighborhood farmer's market, a new justice every year.\par \par \uc2 The question is, where is the limiting principle here, and where does it stop? We have an abundance of rage. What we lack is reason. And I think that the president is really degraded, not just his legacy with this, but his office.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: You know, Trey, one thing that's missing here, and it used to be widely espoused by a number of Democrats, is adding more justices to the court. I think, in FDR's time, they called it packing the court, but that is not part of this.\par \par \uc2 What do you make of that?\par \par \uc2 GOWDY: Well, there's only one number in the Constitution, and that's one. And we have had almost every odd number between one and 13 since then, but we have been stuck on nine for a long time.\par \par \uc2 And there's a reason for that. People like it. I hope the reason for the delay, Neil, is so someone can actually read that \uc2 John Roberts\uc2  majority opinion to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , so he understands that there is no immunity for criminal activity for a president, and he better be careful what he wishes for.\par \par \uc2 I can't imagine that he wants \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  prosecuted for droning an American citizen overseas to death. And I guarantee you he doesn't want to be prosecuted under some theory of transferred intent because someone crossed the border on his watch and killed someone.\par \par \uc2 So he better be really careful what he has asked for. The Roberts opinion, as Jonathan said early -- earlier, is the middle ground. It rejected absolute immunity, and it rejected that you're just an average citizen.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: All right.\par \par \uc2 GOWDY: It's in the middle.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: Yes, I guess, specifically, Jonathan, distinguishing between official and unofficial acts.\par \par \uc2 But be that as it may, I mean, this is obviously a political clarion call, that Democrats don't like this conservative court. Then there's the conduct issue, and they're just fending the flames with this. So I'm just wondering how it resonates, but legally it's on very, very, very shaky ground, right?\par \par \uc2 TURLEY: It is.\par \par \uc2 And, first of all, it is a rallying cry, but it's a little sad because everyone has already left the field. I mean, he used this to try to rally people around his nomination, and it failed, and now the pledge will outlast his presidency.\par \par \uc2 But there are serious issues here about whether he can actually do this without a constitutional amendment. Is this better than packing the court? Yes, but he would still send at least three justices immediately packing in the form of Thomas, Roberts, Alito, would be across that line, which I think is the point of all of this.\par \par \uc2 And the question for the president is this really how you want your legacy to end? Is this where -- is this going to be the finer point, the final point of your presidency to yield to these demands after 50 years of resisting the demands as a senator, as vice president, and as a president?\par \par \uc2 I find it really quite sad to watch.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: All right, gentlemen, I want to thank you both very much.\par \par \uc2 For those of you waiting for this, he's running a little behind schedule. The president is going to outline all of this.\par \par \uc2 By the way, we will be talking about what's at stake for President Biden, letting the world know he is still president and still making some historic moves here. Chris Coons, the senator from Delaware, of course, was in charge of his campaign, on the significance of this and everything else tomorrow on this show.\par \par \uc2 All I can tell you, that, for the time being, the battle is on, and this itself has become a political, heated argument that itself becomes an issue in any debate, should there be any debate.\par \par \uc2 That will do it for us. We will be also focusing on day one of the Fed meeting that could be the game changer for a lot of things. That comes tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 "The Five" comes now.\par \par \uc2 THIS IS A RUSH TRANSCRIPT. THIS COPY MAY NOT BE IN ITS FINAL FORM AND MAY BE UPDATED.\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2024 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2024 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document CAVU000020240730ek7t00001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  Scolds Israel Critics In Address To Congress; Thousands Protest At \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2 's Washington Visit; President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  To Talk 2024 Decision And Remaining Priorities; \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  Shooter Searched JFK's Assassination; Video Shows Law Enforcement Response To \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  Shooting; First Trump Rally Since Biden Exit From 2024 Race; Trump Predicts Epic Landslide In North Carolina; Trump: Harris More Liberal Than \uc2 Bernie Sanders\uc2 ; Trump: "Fake News" Depicts Harris As Savior; \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  Holds Rally In North Carolina; \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  Attacks Presumptive Democratic Presidential Nominee \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  During Rally Speech As Too Liberal On Immigration, Energy, And Abortion; President Biden To Give Oval Office Speech About His Decision To Step Down As Democratic Party's 2024 Presidential Candidate.\b0\par\par\uc2 Bret Baier, Bryan Llenas, Aishah Hasnie, Peter Doocy, Chad  Pergram, Griff Jenkins, Juan Williams \par \uc2 10,358 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 July 2024\par \uc2 Fox News: Special Report with Brett Baier\par \uc2 FNSPBB\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2024 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2024 ASC Services II Media, LLC.  All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 KELLYANNE CONWAY, FOX NEWS CHANNEL CONTRIBUTOR: -- check out my brand new Fox Nation show. It's called "HERE'S THE DEAL WITH KELLYANNE". New episodes drop every Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Tomorrow, I'm joined by Charlie Hurt and Charlie Spiering. He wrote the book Kamala. Amateur Hour: Kamala in the White House. Check it out.\par \par \uc2 GREG GUTFELD, FOX NEWS CHANNEL HOST: Very interesting. Well, we're out of time. So, boo hoo. That's it for us. What's up Bret? Boo hoo.\par \par \uc2 BRET BAIER, FOX NEWS CHANNEL HOST: Hi, Greg. OK, thank you. Guess what? I'm at the White House.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Thank you.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Good evening. I'm Bret Baier.\par \par \uc2 Breaking tonight, we are coming to you live from the North Lawn of the White House, where in two hours, President Biden will address the nation. His fourth address to the nation from the Oval Office in his presidency, his first since announcing Sunday that he is dropping out of the presidential race.\par \par \uc2 President Biden will explain his reasoning behind the end of his reelection effort. He'll also outline what he intends to do during his final months in office.\par \par \uc2 Also tonight, we are waiting to hear from former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  at a campaign rally in North Carolina, his first rally there in five months. President Trump won that state narrowly in 2020.\par \par \uc2 Tonight, we're also learning new details about the attempted assassination of the Republican nominee hearing from the director of the \uc2 FBI\uc2 , and we will show you new body cam video from officers on the scene right after that shooting.\par \par \uc2 But leading off tonight, Israeli Prime Minister \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  says if the U.S. will give his nation tools to defeat \uc2 Hamas\uc2  faster, it will finish the job faster. But he said Israel is not ready to stop the fight against \uc2 Hamas\uc2  terrorists in Gaza yet.\par \par \uc2 Netanyahu addressing a joint meeting of Congress this afternoon. Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  was not in attendance. Neither were many progressive members. But dozens of anti-Israel protesters, hundreds of them, made their voices heard here in Washington. Netanyahu referring to those demonstrators and others as Iran's useful idiots.\par \par \uc2 Senior Congressional Correspondent Chad Pergram on Capitol Hill live tonight to lead us off. Good evening, Chad.\par \par \uc2 CHAD PERGRAM, FOX NEWS CHANNEL CONGRESSIONAL CORRESPONDENT: Bret, good evening.\par \par \uc2 Waves of anti-Netanyahu demonstrations outside the Capitol. Political tension inside. And even one silent but evocative protest from a controversial Democrat.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 PERGRAM (voice over): \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  had one message for lawmakers as they stare at a common enemy, Iran.\par \par \uc2 BENJAMIN NETANYAHU\uc2 , ISRAELI PRIME MINISTER: This is not a clash of civilizations. It's a clash between barbarism and civilization.\par \par \uc2 PERGRAM (voice over): Netanyahu defended Israel over how it's fighting \uc2 Hamas\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 NETANYAHU: The prosecutor of the \uc2 International Criminal Court\uc2  has shamefully accused Israel of deliberately starving the people of Gaza. This is utter, complete nonsense. It's a complete fabrication.\par \par \uc2 PERGRAM (voice over): While protest raged outside, a different form of demonstration boiled inside. Dozens of congressional Democrats skipped the speech in protest. The Senate's top Democrat attended grudgingly.\par \par \uc2 SEN. \uc2 CHUCK SCHUMER\uc2  (D-NY): I will attend the speech because the United States relationship with Israel remains ironclad and transcends any prime minister or president.\par \par \uc2 PERGRAM (voice over): Palestinian American and Michigan Democrat \uc2 Rashida Tlaib\uc2  wielded a sign reading war criminal on one side, guilty of genocide on the other.\par \par \uc2 Netanyahu had harsh words for protesters.\par \par \uc2 NETANYAHU: I have a message for these protesters. You have officially become Iran's useful idiots.\par \par \uc2 PERGRAM (voice over): Netanyahu praised President Biden.\par \par \uc2 NETANYAHU: I want to thank him for half a century of friendship to Israel and for being, as he says, a proud Zionist, actually he says, a proud Irish American Zionist.\par \par \uc2 PERGRAM (voice over): And expressed relief that former President Trump survived an assassination attempt.\par \par \uc2 NETANYAHU: I also want to thank President Trump for all the things he did for Israel, from recognizing Israel's sovereignty over the Golan Heights.\par \par \uc2 PERGRAM (voice over): One special guest of Netanyahu at the speech, \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 . Some Democrats were furious that Congress even awarded Netanyahu a record fourth speech to a joint meeting of Congress.\par \par \uc2 REP. PRAMILA JAYAPAL (D-WA): But I can speak to the unified belief that Netanyahu should never have been invited.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 PERGRAM (on camera): However, there was one bipartisan moment, Netanyahu praised frat brothers from the University of North Carolina. They guarded the American flag from anti-Israeli protesters. Members then chanted, USA, USA. Bret?\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Chad Pergram live on the Hill. Chad, thanks.\par \par \uc2 Let's go now to ground zero for those anti-Israel protests all day, simmering down a bit now.\par \par \uc2 Correspondent Griff Jenkins has been in the middle of it all pretty much all day. Good evening, Griff.\par \par \uc2 GRIFF JENKINS, FOX NEWS CHANNEL CORRESPONDENT: Good evening, Bret. And the message from the protesters, thousands of them, began with free Palestine and end USA to Israel.\par \par \uc2 But as you can see over my shoulder, the message turned into \uc2 Hamas\uc2  is coming, is what's written in graffiti and read over there.\par \par \uc2 And the sentiment, Bret, also turned anti-American. Take a look at this video here, just feet from me, outside of the Union Station, an American flag burned. It's flagpoles that carry three American flags pulled down by the protesters as police fought to maintain them. But at least one here we saw was burned.\par \par \uc2 Now what happened was the protestors flew the Palestinian flag instead on these polls. Take a look at this video. You can see on all three iconic polls in front of Washington's landmark Union Station, the Palestinian flag flying. Those have since been taken down.\par \par \uc2 But that wasn't the only violent clash, Bret. You can see here in some of the other video you shot -- that we shot this afternoon. In numerous places we saw the police clashing with the protesters. They were pepper sprayed by the police, and it was mostly isolated incidents of protesters taunting the police as they tried to maintain the security perimeter around that.\par \par \uc2 Among the arrests made, we know there was around a dozen or more. We don't yet have the final number, but there were violent episodes of the protesters being taken into custody, which, of course, fueled the fire.\par \par \uc2 Finally among the protesters, Bret, we did notice one woman carrying a \uc2 Hamas\uc2  flag with a Qassam Brigade's patch on her arm. We spoke to her. Here's a little bit of what she had to say to us. Listen.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 JENKINS: What message do you want to send today?\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: I don't have a message for