 they were like this. How about the guy right behind me in the black with the green hat? And he is looking like this.\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : That guy was -- I want to meet him. But they had a lot of guys like that back there. But did you see him? They have only played that clip about 5,000 times. They see it every day. It's over and over. But you see how brave. Normally when something like that happens, everybody but Richard will leave. Richard will stay. He's a tough cookie.\par \par \uc2 But, no, everybody scrambles, they run. Nobody ran. Same thing with the group out front. The group out front was the big group. Thousands and thousands of people. Nobody left. They just stood there watching because they saw that I was in trouble. Either I was in trouble or something was happening because I had a lot of blood on my hand. I checked that, I said oh, yikes, what's this?\par \par \uc2 But no, they saw that. And when I went down they saw that, and nobody left. It was like, the whole thing is like a big love fest. Let's face it. It's a whole big love fest.\par \par \uc2 (CHEERING)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : It's amazing. We love you. We love you. We love you.\par \par \uc2 (CHEERING)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : We love you. That was a horrible thing. That was a rough thing. And say what you want, the Secret Service, the ones on the dais, these guys right here, they're tough cookies. They ran --\par \par \uc2 (CHEERING)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : -- bullets were flying. Bullets were flying and they were running right at me. And it was a rough, horrible, horrible time. And they said sir, we have a stretcher for you. I said you are not putting me -- I'm not getting on a stretcher. They had a stretcher. I said that's not going to look very good if I get carried out on a stretcher. Hello, everybody. Thank you, everybody.\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: I said I'm not getting -- where are my shoes? My shoes got knocked off. They tackled me so damn hard.\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : But it was a terrible thing in so many ways. As you know we lost somebody who was fantastic. Corey, fantastic.\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: His family is fantastic. And two other great people. These are great people. I got to know their families a little bit. And, you know, the public has really been generous to them, too. They opened up their hearts. I won't even tell you, the numbers are so incredible. But they opened up their hearts to the three of them. And these two were hurt very badly, but they are both now in pretty good shape. They will soon be in very good shape. So --\par \par \uc2 (CHEERING)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : But -- but I just looked down here at front row Joes, and it just reminded me of that incident a week and a half ago. You were right there watching it. You saw it. And you guys, by the way, weren't moving either. I saw you, you didn't move. They were standing just like they're standing right now. They were standing. They're great. They're great.\par \par \uc2 And sad, such a distressed, sick world. But it could be caused when they call you a threat to democracy. You never know what causes it. I'm a threat? They're a threat to democracy. They are a threat to our country, period.\par \par \uc2 But that was some time we had. That was some rough time. But it was incredible. The people I got to know through that. I got to know some unbelievable, and really brave people. But the next time they show that clip, which will be as soon as you get home. They'll show it about 30 times. They show it every day over and over. But watch the people behind. They always stampede. If a bullet goes off or something happens at a soccer stadium or a stadium, and we had more people than most of those stadiums would have, everyone runs. Nobody ran. They stayed. And they -- and you have to look. The one guy, it just was so -- he just was so angry. He's looking. I got to meet him. There is something about brave people that I love. Right? People that love our country.\par \par \uc2 (CHEERING)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : He's up there. He's like up there, up there.\par \par \uc2 No. They are great, they are great people. And we had a great convention. We had a great convention. We had a convention that broke all television ratings.\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : How good was the Hulkster? Right, the Hulk? And Kid Rock called. He wanted to be a part. He was fantastic. But they are all fantastic. It was the greatest -- it was just a flawless convention. It was great. And the television ratings were record-setting ratings. Record. You all read that.\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : They were record-setting ratings. And it was just an honor. The stadium was beautiful. Milwaukee was beautiful. Wisconsin's had promised me they are all going to vote for me now because we put $250 million into their economy.\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : So we're going to win the great state of Wisconsin. But Milwaukee was great. They did a great job. The stadium is new. They built it for the basketball team, which is excellent. You know, the Greek. Right, the Greek. He is a good player. But they built it for the team, and it was like new. And it was one of the most -- I think it was the greatest -- I really believe it couldn't have been better. It was the greatest convention that anyone has seen thus far, Republican or Democrat.\par \par \uc2 (CHEERING)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : But getting back to a subject called Kamala. Who is the worst?\par \par \uc2 (BOOS)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : You know, I ask you this question because this has never happened before. So, Biden is running. I wouldn't say his debate performance was one of the best, right? Do you agree?\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : That's where it all started with the debate. The downfall started that night with the debate. The debate was like -- that was a rough debate. He said, I had a bad night. No, he had a bad night, he had a bad everything. He had a very bad night. But it started really with the debate. It was all, you know, the game was up. They say the jig was up. And it was indeed up. But it started with that. And then it only got worse.\par \par \uc2 And we were leading him 11, 12, 14, 15, points. And then he decides to get out because the bosses said we are not going to have you. He didn't want to get out, but they told him you're getting out. They said you're getting out. You're getting killed in the polls. You can't win. You saw that, you can't win. You're getting killed.\par \par \uc2 So now they bring in this one who is worse than him. She is worse than him, because he is a fake liberal. You know, he wasn't that liberal. He was fake. She is a real liberal. She really is a real liberal. She is much worse than him.\par \par \uc2 Now, if we start beating her in the polls by 10 or 15 points, are they going to bring in a third candidate? It's like, you know, Trump is killing this guy. All right, out. Let's bring in a new one. Out. Out. And then maybe at some point they get one right, but when will that stop?\par \par \uc2 (CHEERING)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : And you know, the guy had 14 million votes. So much for democracy. You know, they talk about democracy. He had 14 million votes, and they said we are going to give it to somebody with no votes. She had no votes. In addition to her horrendous record as vice president, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has also been caught red handed perpetrating the biggest scandal in American political history. For three-and-a-half years, Harris shamelessly lied to the public to cover up \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's mental unfitness, claiming that crooked Joe was at the absolute top of his game. I don't think so. I don't think so. I wish him well, but I don't like him. He's not a nice person. I mean, he's not a nice person. He's trying to put him in jail. Why would I like him, right? It's the first time, first time.\par \par \uc2 (BOOS)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : And she is the one behind it. And she has got a new line. You know, she is going I'm the prosecutor. She is one of the worst prosecutors in history. She destroyed San Francisco. I'm the prosecutor. And he is the convicted felon, or something. A radical left judge in an area where every one of these cases, every one of them is brought by them.\par \par \uc2 So, think of it. They get me to that position. And then the campaign says I'm the prosecutor, and he is the convicted felon. That's their campaign. I don't think people are going to buy it. And we won our big case. We won the case in Florida. That was a big one. We won that one.\par \par \uc2 (CHEERING)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : And I got out by beating their Justice Department, and he got out of the same case, except his was far different because he had 50 years of documents, right? He got out by being incompetent. The prosecutor said he had no memory. He basically said he's incompetent, so he shouldn't stand trial. Can you imagine? He can be president but he can't stand trial. What's that about?\par \par \uc2 (BOOS)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: No, but it was all headed up by her, because she is a prosecutor, a really bad one. If Kamala will lie to you so brazenly about \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's mental incapacity, then she will lie to you about anything. She can never ever be trusted. She can't be trusted.\par \par \uc2 (CHEERING)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : And just like crooked \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is unfit to lead. She is unfit to lead. She'll destroy our country. In a year this country will be destroyed. A vote for Kamala is a vote for four more years of dishonesty, incompetence, weakness, and failure.\par \par \uc2 (BOOS)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : Other than that, she is doing an excellent job.\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : A vote for Trump-Vance -- how do you like it? How do you like it?\par \par \uc2 (CHEERING)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : J.D. Vance, how do you like him? A vote for a Trump-Vance administration is a vote to restore leadership, competence, common sense, and strength back to the Oval Office, like we had it just three-and-a-half years ago.\par \par \uc2 (CHEERING)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: If \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  gets in, she would be the most radical far left extremist ever to occupy the White House times 10. There has never been a lunatic like this in the White House. And we have had some bad ones. But the worst one is Joe, actually. As a senator, Harris was ranked the number one most leftwing Democrat in the Senate. Think of that, she is ranked the number one. That's not what this country wants. She makes Bernie look like a moderate. You know, he looks like -- \uc2 Bernie Sanders\uc2 , he's actually quite moderate by comparison.\par \par \uc2 Here is just some of her crazy liberal record. \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , co-sponsored \uc2 Bernie Sanders\uc2  $32 trillion plan for a socialist takeover of the entire U.S. health system, which will be a disaster and will bankrupt Medicare and Social Security. They're gone. And remember, Social Security is going to be gone anywhere if we are not elected, because they are putting all these millions of people that are pouring into our country, they are putting them into Social Security, Medicare, schools, hospitals.\par \par \uc2 (BOOS)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : And we all have a big heart, but some of those people are tough, from prisons, from mental institutions, terrorists. When asked if her plan would outlaw private health insurance for 180 million Americans, Kamala replied, let's just eliminate all of it. That's all she said. We will eliminate all. That's nice. Thank you very much, Kamala.\par \par \uc2 She endorsed free taxpayer government funded healthcare for all illegal aliens, everybody that walks into our country that's illegal. This is why they come, when these stupid people, they are stupid low I.Q. people, when they say we're going to give you healthcare, we are going to give you everything, they come. You are not going to say we are going to give you all of these things. They are going to come, even if they are fine in their country. And people are being killed in the caravans, especially women. They are dying on the way up. It's horrible. It's horrible. You have to see the real numbers.\par \par \uc2 She co-sponsored the $100 trillion green new scam with a goal of completely abolishing the oil, coal, and natural gas industries, which would reduce the United States to a third world country.\par \par \uc2 (BOOS)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: No more oil, no more gasoline. Good luck with your electric car that goes for about 45 minutes before you have to get it. You know, some place like in the Midwest, did you see, they built eight chargers, sort of like the equivalent of a gas pump. They built eight chargers for $9 billion, and two of them, though, work. That's a big problem.\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : And if we were going to charge up the entire country for the electric car, if we were going to charge up, it would cost $5 trillion. That's more money than we would have. We would have to file for bankruptcy. And yet, they don't care. They say let's do it anyway.\par \par \uc2 She said that a 70 to 80 percent tax hike is, quote, a bold idea that should be discussed. She wants it 80 percent. You know, I gave you the largest tax cuts in history. She wants to take them away and increase your taxes. I don't think you are going to be too happy.\par \par \uc2 Kamala publicly boasted, quote, there's no question I'm in favor of banning fracking. She wants no fracking.\par \par \uc2 (BOOS)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: Now, that pertains to Pennsylvania, Texas, it pertains to Oklahoma. It pertains to a lot of other places, more so than you. But it pertains to you where your wallet, because you are going to be paying a lot of money. You are going to be paying so much. You are going to say bring back Trump, please, please, please, bring back Trump. We want Trump. We want some common sense. Please.\par \par \uc2 (CHEERING)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : She supports mandatory gun confiscation to rip firearms out of the hands of millions of law abiding gun owners.\par \par \uc2 (BOOS)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : She wants to take away your Second Amendment which we need. Lyin' Kamala is also a total radical on a word called -- you know this, right? A word called, what? Abortion. She is a radical, crazy person. When you compare my position on abortion to that of \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , my position is eight points higher in the polls, and that's because she is so radical. She wants abortions in the eighth and ninth month of pregnancy. That's fine with her. Right up until birth.\par \par \uc2 (BOOS)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : And even after birth, the execution of a baby, because that's not abortion. That's the execution of a baby. You remember the governor, you remember the former governor -- the current governor is excellent. The former governor of Virginia, he said yes, we may have the baby, and then we decide with the mother what to do with the baby. This is after the baby is born. No. She supports -- and she supports that.\par \par \uc2 She supports taxpayer funds to pay for abortion for any reason whatsoever. She even voted against legislation that would require medical providers to give care to babies born alive after an attempted abortion. Think of that one.\par \par \uc2 Whereas our position is that abortion is now back to the states. For 52 years, they have wanted to bring, it's Roe v. Wade. They wanted to bring it back to the states. It wasn't about how many weeks and how many -- everybody wanted it. Every legal scholar, every Democrat, every Republican, liberals, conservatives, they wanted it brought back to the states. And because we had a very brave six people on the \uc2 Supreme Court of the United States\uc2 , so they were very brave.\par \par \uc2 (CHEERING)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: After 52 years they allowed it. But everybody wanted it. And they were brave to do it. And now it's up to the will of the people in each state. And it's happening in Ohio. They voted and, frankly, it came out to be more of a liberal policy, but they voted. And it's getting back in Kansas. You saw what happened there. Somewhat of a liberal policy. Texas goes and Alabama goes and other states. But it's all being voted on by the states. It's back in the hands of the people. And the state returns the age-old question to where it belongs. And it belongs with the people, and it belongs over time.\par \par \uc2 And you see what's happening. And you see how it is working out, like \uc2 Ronald Reagan\uc2 . Very importantly, I support -- I happen to support. You have to go with your heart, but I happen to support the three exceptions rape, incest, and the life of the mother. I think that's the way.\par \par \uc2 (CHEERING)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : But follow your heart. But you also have to remember, you have to get elected. You have to remember, because we have elections, and elections are about a lot of other things, too, that are very important. But you have to get elected. But \uc2 Ronald Reagan\uc2  was for that, I was for that, the three exceptions. And as vice president, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  cast the tiebreaking vote to cut, as you know, Medicare by $273 billion. She cast a vote to cut Medicare. Nobody knows that she doesn't want people to know that.\par \par \uc2 Now what she is doing is running away from Israel. She refuses to go to \uc2 Bibi Netanyahu\uc2 , who is in Washington. She refuses to be there.\par \par \uc2 (BOOS)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : Even if you are against Israel or you are against the Jewish people, show up and listen to the concept. But she is totally against the Jewish people. And it amazes me how Jewish people will vote for the Democrats when they're being treated so disrespectfully and badly. It amazes me.\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : It's shocking. I don't get it. I don't get it.\par \par \uc2 Kamala even wants to pass laws to outlaw red meat to stop climate change and she is --\par \par \uc2 (BOOS)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : You know what that means. That means no more cows. This is serious. This means no more cows. I guess eventually she is going to mean no more people, right? No more people.\par \par \uc2 So if you want socialist healthcare, nation wrecking inflation, the death of American energy, and a lying, radical left liberal \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , San Francisco extremists as your commander in chief, then \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is your candidate. She is the one for you.\par \par \uc2 (BOOS)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : Just like she destroyed San Francisco, she will destroy our entire country. And, let me tell you, it's in pretty bad shape right now anyway. What they have done in three-and-a-half, especially, I mean, think of Afghanistan, the most embarrassing moment, day in the history of our country. We got out out of weakness. We were going to get out, but we were going to get out with strength and dignity. We were going to get out. They left, you know, $85 billion worth of brand new equipment, brand new beautiful military equipment. I rebuilt the military. They got equipment that I bought, and they left it in Afghanistan.\par \par \uc2 Did you know that Afghanistan, now the \uc2 Taliban\uc2  -- Afghanistan is the second or third largest seller of military equipment in the world. They are taking this gorgeous stuff, and they are selling it and they are making a fortune because they don't need, they don't need 700,000 rifles and guns. They don't need 77,000 trucks and cars. Many of them are built with all steel bottoms. They're all guarded up for the horrible bombs that he had they had to endure. They're all very expensive, these are very expensive things. And they are selling them now because they just need a tiny fraction of what they were left. We were going to take it all out. We were going to keep Bagram, the big air base. We had 13 soldiers killed. We had 47 soldiers horribly, horribly hurt. No legs, no arms. Nobody ever talks about them. They talk about the 13 dead. They never talk about the 47 that have been so horribly hurt. I mean, just it's so bad, it's so horrible to see. But 47 is an important number. Maybe there is something to it. You know, 47. That's an important number.\par \par \uc2 (CHEERING)\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in Charlotte, North Carolina, a packed house. Our Mark Meredith is on the ground there. He said people started showing up 8:00 a.m., thousands and thousands of people inside the Bojangles Arena. We are told that it is packed. They have a number of dignitaries, including the chairman of the Republican Party and some of the North Carolina delegation.\par \par \uc2 Obviously, changing his attack directly on Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , who is the presumptive Democratic nominee, and we're told has enough delegates to take that title in the first day of the vote in the Democratic convention in Chicago.\par \par \uc2 Let's bring in our panel to do some analysis, FOX News senior political analyst Juan Williams, Jason Riley, "Wall Street Journal" columnist and senior fellow at the Manhattan Institute, and Julia Manchester, national politics reporter for "The Hill."\par \par \uc2 Jason, he's sharpened his attacks. Obviously, he has changed the nominee that he is facing here, but clearly going after the liberal side of \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and really what she ran on as a candidate for president back in 2019.\par \par \uc2 JASON RILEY, COLUMNIST, "WALL STREET JOURNAL": Right. And I think he is smart to do that, Bret. That is what Democratic primary voters rejected four years ago. They thought that \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  was too liberal, and she is a coastal elite. She epitomizes that California liberal that conservatives like to parody and make fun of. And I think he is right to harp on those issues. This is a woman called for abolishing ICE, has called for healthcare for illegal immigrants. And he is going to hammer away at those points, and that's what you see him doing.\par \par \uc2 I think Republican, and Trump was caught a little bit aback by how quickly Democrats have corralled around her and supported her, and how positive the press coverage has been. You heard him talking about that in the speech. But they shouldn't be surprised by that. I think you are looking at a race now that's probably pre-debate stage, where we were back then. And so we're back at square one, and Trump is going to have to work at this.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: And it's a different opponent, Juan. And if you don't think that these efforts to go after liberal policies of the past are catching on, in swing state Senate races it's already the subject of ads. \uc2 Dave McCormick\uc2 , Republican running against Bob Casey, the incumbent Democrat in Pennsylvania, has an ad out. Here's a piece of it about \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 KAMALA HARRIS\uc2 , (D) VICE PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: There's no question I'm in favor of banning fracking.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Would you ban offshore drilling?\par \par \uc2 HARRIS: Yes.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: What is the solution for voters in the fossil fuel industry?\par \par \uc2 HARRIS: Giving the workers an ability to transition.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Banning fracking not too popular in Pennsylvania. Juan, as you look at the Real Clear Politics average overall right now, the average of recent polls, the former president has 47.6 to 45.9 percent. If you look at a five-way race with the other candidates, it's 43.4 to 40.6. But we've seen polls on both sides. Your thoughts?\par \par \uc2 JUAN WILLIAMS, FOX NEWS POLITICAL ANALYST: I think that's right. There was a lot of excitement among Democrats today when a poll came out that actually had Harris in the lead.\par \par \uc2 But I think as you can tell from the speech tonight, if he ever gets her name right, pronounces her name right, that will be news. But I think it's clear he is saying she is a San Francisco leftist. He said Biden was a fake liberal. This is the real liberal. And he said that he pushed Biden out of race. I didn't think that was very gracious the way he talked about Biden, but he basically said if Kamala is down by 10 maybe they will get somebody else.\par \par \uc2 He is back to himself. I remember at the Milwaukee convention there was a lot of talk maybe we're going to see a different \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . Well, tonight, he is back to himself. And he is really going -- he went after, as I said, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  at a moment when Biden is going to give his speech exiting. I guess that's why you are at the White House.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Yes, sir.\par \par \uc2 WILLIAMS: But he is going after her in a very, very strong way.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Yes, and this rally in Charlotte, Julia, is, we are told the security is very tight. Obviously, we are only days from this assassination attempt. It's hard to believe all of this has happened in this short of time.\par \par \uc2 We should point out, Bryan Llenas had this piece. We had a technical problem. We're going to post it on our website and on my \uc2 Instagram\uc2  page so people can see new body video camera evidence that's popping up in that investigation. I want to play this soundbite ahead of the speech here at the White House tonight.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Why did you drop out of the election? Was it a difficult decision to make?\par \par \uc2 KARINE JEAN-PIERRE\uc2 , WHITE HOUSE PRESS SECRETARY: Tonight, the president was discuss his historic decision to put the country above all else, and about the inflection point we face as a country in this moment.\par \par \uc2 REP. MIKE JOHNSON, (R-LA) HOUSE SPEAKER: If everyone acknowledges that he is incapable of running a campaign, then he's clearly incapable of running the country.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Just fourth Oval Office address, 8:00 p.m. tonight, will start at 7:55. But here's an excerpt we got from this address. "The great thing about America is here kings and dictators do not rule. The people do. History is in your hands. The power is in your hands. The idea of America lies in your hands."\par \par \uc2 Julia, there is a challenge to this president to explain exactly why he stepped down and why he should be here for the next five plus months.\par \par \uc2 JULIA MANCHESTER, NATIONAL POLITICS REPORTER, "THE HILL": Yes, certainly not a not a subtle dig at Trump without naming him. But look, this is an opportunity for Biden really to echo what a lot of Democrats have been saying over the past few days to talk about how this decision was a unifying decision. It was meant to bring the country together. It was a patriotic thing to do.\par \par \uc2 And he is going to sort of, I think, use this address really to position Harris as a forefront, to really publicly give his blessing to the vice president and sort of paint her as someone who is ready to take on the helm.\par \par \uc2 Remember, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will run on President Biden's legacy, on his platform. And we're going to see \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , even though he sort of explained -- said that Biden was the fake liberal here and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is the real liberal, I think you are going to see \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  sort of say that him and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  are united, that she is looking to essentially finish the job.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: I only have 30 seconds here, and I think that there is this effort that has to be made about what he says tonight to explain, right, to explain why he is stepping down?\par \par \uc2 WILLIAMS: I think it's a matter of -- it's a speech for the historians as much as it is for you and me, Bret. He is going to explain not only explain why he is stepping down, but say that he was a success in his first term and that he is acting. I mean, there is a certain wistfulness I think I feel about this moment. But he has to justify the idea that he now believes Harris can win.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Jason?\par \par \uc2 RILEY: I agree. Biden will want to talk about his accomplishments. But this is -- maybe he has some stuff he still wants to do with six months left. This is someone with 30 something percent approval rating though. He doesn't have a lot of political capital. And I think that's going to frustrate his efforts to get anything done in these remaining months.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: All right, panel, thanks so much.\par \par \uc2 Tomorrow on SPECIAL REPORT, we'll take a look at how Vice President Harris's name at the top of the ticket could affect down ballot races, especially in swing states.\par \par \uc2 Please join Martha MacCallum and me, 8:00 p.m. eastern for special coverage of President Biden's Oval Office address to the nation.\par \par \uc2 Laura Ingraham is up next. She is going to go back to that Trump rally. Thanks for inviting us into your home tonight from the White House, fair, balanced, and still unafraid. Here's Laura.\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2024 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2024 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document FNSPBB0020240725ek7o00001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  Makes Dramatic Early GOP Convention Appearance; Investigation Of The \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  Assassination Attempt Timeline; Some \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  Allies Push Nomination Before Convention; \uc2 Bob Menendez\uc2  Guilty On All Charges; Immigration Issue Resonates In Wisconsin; Wisconsin Produces More Than 3 Billion Pounds Yearly; \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  Picks Ohio Senator J.D. Vance As His Vice Presidential Running Mate; Sen. Steve Daines (R-MT) Interviewed On Republicans Chances Of Taking Control Of Senate In 2024 Elections; President Biden Condemns Political Violence In Wake Of Assassination Attempt On \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 ; Some Democrats Still Calling For President Biden To Step Down As Party's Presidential Candidate\b0\par\par\uc2 Bret Baier, Jacqui Heinrich, Aishah Hasnie, Eric Shawn, David  Spunt, Harold Ford Jr., Marc Thiessen, Mary Katharine Ham \par \uc2 7,983 \uc2 words\par \uc2 16 July 2024\par \uc2 Fox News: Special Report with Brett Baier\par \uc2 FNSPBB\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2024 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2024 ASC Services II Media, LLC.  All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 JESSE WATTERS, FOX NEWS CHANNEL HOST: We went on a roller coaster, didn't we just the other day?\par \par \uc2 JEANINE PIRRO, FOX NEWS CHANNEL LEGAL ANALYST: Yes.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: And we screamed like children.\par \par \uc2 GREG GUTFELD, FOX NEWS CHANNEL HOST: The problem would be, what do we do about your hair, Jesse?\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: No, you wear a helmet, it's fine. It won't come off if there's a helmet.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: No, just take it off.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Somebody else took jump for me, like I don't want to look and jump.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: OK, you want a body double. That's it for us. Have a great night, everybody.\par \par \uc2 BRET BAIER, FOX NEWS CHANNEL HOST: I'll go skydiving with you. I'll do it.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Yes.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: And do the hand over. Thanks, Jesse.\par \par \uc2 Good evening. I'm Bret Baier. This is day two of the Republican National Convention. We are coming to you live from the Fox forum in Milwaukee. The band's already kicked in.\par \par \uc2 This evening, session getting underway. Among the anticipated highlights tonight, former presidential candidate \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2 , former \uc2 U.N.\uc2  ambassador as well, who had been a fierce critic of former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  on the campaign trail.\par \par \uc2 Well, she'll try to convince undecided voters to come over to the GOP side. Today's theme here at the convention, Make America Safe Once Again. That sentiment has added meaning in the wake of Saturday's attempt to the assassination of the former president.\par \par \uc2 Congressional Correspondent Aishah Hasnie starts us off tonight live from the convention floor. good evening, Aishah. Bret, good evening to you.\par \par \uc2 AISHAH HASNIE, FOX NEWS CHANNEL CONGRESSIONAL CORRESPONDENT: We did see Senator J. D. Vance, a brand new V.P. pick on stage today, he was doing his run through ahead of his big speech tomorrow night. He did not speak to the press but he did speak with Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  on the phone today that we're talking about the upcoming debate. And that conversation was described to Fox as being brief and respectful.\par \par \uc2 Now, folks here I can tell you are fired up for day two, and it is poised to be just as dramatic as day one.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: \uc2 Donald J. Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 HASNIE (voice over): A surprise appearance.\par \par \uc2 BRENNA BIRD, IOWA'S ATTORNEY GENERAL: Senator J. D. Vance.\par \par \uc2 HASNIE (voice over): A surprise V.P. pick. And a promise to Fox that more surprises are coming.\par \par \uc2 Tonight, former presidential primary foes turned allies as \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  and \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  take the prime time stage at the \uc2 RNC\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Fox has told Haley who polls show is favored by Independents will address voters who are uncertain about voting for President Trump and make the case for why she is voting for him.\par \par \uc2 Tonight's theme, Make America Safe Again, a slew of GOP Senate candidates will stump on the big stage as they hope to flip the balance of power.\par \par \uc2 BERNIE MORENO\uc2  (R), SENATORIAL CANDIDATE OF OHIO: This is very different than a 2016 convention in which we had a very fractured Republican Party and we won that election. United we're going to absolutely sweep this election.\par \par \uc2 HASNIE (voice over): Expanding the map and expanding the base. Last night, the \uc2 RNC\uc2  paraded former Democrats turned conservatives to make Trump's case.\par \par \uc2 AMBER ROSE (MODEL AND T.V. PERSONALITY): The left told me to hate Trump.\par \par \uc2 HASNIE (voice over): And for the first time in \uc2 RNC\uc2  history that convention giving the prime time slot to \uc2 Teamsters Union\uc2  president Sean O'Brien who eviscerated corporate America, but did not outright endorse Trump.\par \par \uc2 SEAN O'BRIEN (GENERAL PRESIDENT, \uc2 INTERNATIONAL BROTHERHOOD OF TEAMSTERS\uc2 ): Never forget, American workers own this nation.\par \par \uc2 (CHEERING AND APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 O'BRIEN: We are not renters. We are not tenants, but the corporate elite treat us like squatters, and that is a crime. We have got to fix it.\par \par \uc2 HASNIE (voice over): The appearance alone though adding pressure on Democrats to secure those Rust Belt states like Michigan, Pennsylvania and Wisconsin.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 HASNIE (on camera): And Bret, that is where the presidential and vice presidential nominees for the Republican Party are headed right after this convention. President Trump and J. D. Vance will be headed to the state of Michigan for their first post-convention rally. And I have to mention to you that this one will be in an indoor venue.\par \par \uc2 Also Bret, tonight, Fox has told that Trump did make a phone call to the family of the fallen firefighter the man who was shot in that Pennsylvania rally. He called to express his deepest consult condolences, Bret.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Aishah Hasnie live on the convention floor just behind. Aishah, thanks.\par \par \uc2 We're getting new information tonight about the man who authorities say fired shots at former President Trump during last Saturday's campaign rally. We're also learning about a separate plot against former President Trump's life.\par \par \uc2 Correspondent David Spunt is at the Justice Department with both stories tonight. Good evening, David.\par \par \uc2 DAVID SPUNT, FOX NEWS CHANNEL CORRESPONDENT: Bret, good evening to you. Four federal sources tell Fox News. There was a plot that originated out of Iran to assassinate former president Don Oh Trump and in recent weeks, a confidential human source came forward. The Secret Service took it seriously and then gave Trump more security protection.\par \par \uc2 I want to reiterate that all four sources say there does not appear to be any nexus between the suspect in Pennsylvania and this Iranian alleged plot to kill former President Trump.\par \par \uc2 But the fact that Secret Service allegedly increased Trump's protection is being called into question given what happened in Pennsylvania on Saturday.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 SPUNT (voice over): \uc2 FBI\uc2  agents back at the scene of the crime today, looking inside and outside of this building were on the roof authority say 20 year old Thomas Crooks shot former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  also killing one and injuring two others in the crowd.\par \par \uc2 Fox News has learned before the shooting rally goers spotted a suspicious man with what appeared to be binoculars or a rangefinder, a device used to measure distances.\par \par \uc2 Various sources also said that same person later identified as Crooks was pacing around magnetometers in the security barrier before the event began. Police were called.\par \par \uc2 Fox has also told Crooks bought a ladder at a local hardware store. According to multiple different videos and witness interviews, it was at least 80 seconds from the time people alerted police to the time the shooting began.\par \par \uc2 A Butler township police officer was hoisted up by another officer onto the roof only to find Crooks pointing a gun at him. The officer dropped off the roof and called into threat.\par \par \uc2 Seconds later, the shooting began. \uc2 U.S. Secret Service\uc2  has confirmed local police were inside the building while the shooter was on the roof but maintained they're not passing blame.\par \par \uc2 In a statement, the Secret Service defended local police, writing, any news suggesting the Secret Service is blaming local law enforcement for Saturday's incident is simply not true.\par \par \uc2 Fox has told the Butler County Sheriff's Department is receiving threats from the public following the shooting. On Capitol Hill, lawmakers are growing frustrated after Secret Service Director Kimberly Cheatle cancelled a virtual briefing.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 SPUNT (on camera): And there was again no briefing today despite thought there would be some sort of communication from the Secret Service director. Bret, she'll testify in public on Monday. At least now she'll testify in public on Monday.\par \par \uc2 Tomorrow, all senators will be able to call in for a briefing with DOJ, the \uc2 FBI\uc2  and Secret Service to learn more until this investigation is making some progress. However, there's still one thing we don't know, motive, Bret.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: David Spunt at the Justice Department. David, thank you.\par \par \uc2 President Biden is back on the campaign trail following a brief pause in light of the attempted assassination of former President Trump.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, another prominent Democrat is warning of disaster if President Biden stays on the Democratic ticket. While some of the President's supporters are trying to fast track his nomination much earlier than scheduled.\par \par \uc2 Senior White House correspondent Jacqui Heinrich joins us tonight live from the North Lawn. Good evening, Jacqui.\par \par \uc2 JACQUI HEINRICH, FOX NEWS CHANNEL CORRESPONDENT: Good evening, Bret. In his first speech since the attempt on his opponent's life, President Biden criticized Trump for his response to the riots after George Floyd's murder and his response to the pandemic. At one point, he said that Trump wants to take American's freedoms away and rhetorically asked what the hell is wrong with this man, but he never said a word framing Trump or Republicans as a threat or a danger.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 , PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: We continue to pressure him and his family. It's time for an important conversation in this country. Our politics has gotten too heated.\par \par \uc2 I've said the oval office on Sunday night, as I made clear throughout my presidency, we all have responsibility to lower the temperature and condemn violence in any form.\par \par \uc2 HEINRICH (voice over): Biden's campaign denies any change to their messaging plan after the attempt on Trump's life.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: It hasn't changed. I would say that we've been focused on talking about the issues, reproductive freedom, worker's rights, Social Security, Medicare, the economy, a fair tax code.\par \par \uc2 HEINRICH (voice over): Last night Biden rejected criticism his rhetoric played a role in driving hostilities and struggled to articulate his view that Trump does pose a threat without pouring gas on the fire.\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: Look, I'm not the guy that said I want to be a dictator on day one. I'm not the guy that refused to accept the outcome of the election. That's the kind of language that is inflammatory.\par \par \uc2 HEINRICH (voice over): That left \uc2 Obama\uc2 's former speech writers scratching their heads.\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: How do you talk about the threat to democracy which is real when a president says things like he says?\par \par \uc2 HEINRICH (voice over): That left \uc2 Obama\uc2 's former speech writers scratching their heads.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: He manages to respond defensively to every question from Lester Holt, even where he shouldn't be in a way turning every question into a kind of gotcha question where he feels as though he is, I think reacting from a place of weakness.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Do you think he's stubborn? Like I can't figure -- this is what I can't figure out. It's like why can he not just get to the right message?\par \par \uc2 HEINRICH (voice over): Now, in private, Biden is still facing down calls to drop out, CNN reports that top aides are showing him memos from seasoned democratic pollster Stanley Greenberg saying he's on track to lose and take down ballot Democrats with him.\par \par \uc2 JON LOVETT\uc2 , FORMER BARACK OBAMA SPEECHWRITER: There's so much that the president just has to come to grips with here, the higher -- likelihood much higher is that he will lose by a landslide than that he will win 270 electoral votes, that is reality.\par \par \uc2 HEINRICH (voice over): To the \uc2 New York Times\uc2 , California Congressman Adam Schiff running for Senate told donors on Saturday, "I think if he's our nominee, I think we lose and we very, very well may lose the Senate and our chances to take back the house."\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 HEINRICH (on camera): Now, congressional Democrats are setting a change in Ohio law pushing back on a plan to formalize Biden's nomination with an early roll call vote.\par \par \uc2 But Biden is not going anywhere willingly. He said tonight, again, that he is in the race, and he's previously said it would take an act of God and also getting hit by a train along with convincing data to get him to change his mind, Bret.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Jacqui Heinrich live in the North Lawn. Jacqui, thanks.\par \par \uc2 New Jersey Democratic Senator \uc2 Bob Menendez\uc2  is facing multiple calls to resign tonight. Today he was convicted of all the charges he faced at his corruption trial, including taking bribes and acting as a foreign agent.\par \par \uc2 Senior Correspondent Eric Shawn outside the federal courthouse in Manhattan tonight with the latest. Good evening, Eric.\par \par \uc2 ERIC SHAWN, FOX NEWS CHANNEL CORRESPONDENT: Good evening, Bret. He will now forever be known by what some have called him. Gold Bar Bob, guilty on all charges for selling his Senate seat in exchange for cash and gold.\par \par \uc2 New Jersey senior Senator \uc2 Robert Menendez\uc2  convicted along with two of his co-defendants on every charge in the international bribery and extortion scheme.\par \par \uc2 The jury found Menendez accepted hundreds of thousands of dollars in payoffs and expensive gifts, all to interfere with U.S. foreign policy on behalf of Egypt, Qatar and three New Jersey businessmen. U.S. Attorney \uc2 Damian Williams\uc2  said the senator engaged what he called a shocking level of corruption.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 DAMIAN WILLIAMS\uc2 , U.S. ATTORNEY SOUTHERN DISTRICT OF NEW YORK: This wasn't politics as usual. This was politics for profit. And now that the jury has convicted \uc2 Bob Menendez\uc2 , his years of selling his office to the highest bidder have finally come to an end.\par \par \uc2 SHAWN (voice over): Prosecutors told the jury that the $480,000 in cash that was found throughout his house, some stash in his jacket pockets. And those 13 gold bars worth 100 grand were hidden in a bedroom closet, as well as a \uc2 Mercedes Benz\uc2  convertible and other lavish gifts were all payoffs for him to interfere with U.S. foreign policy.\par \par \uc2 But out of the verdict, Menendez said he was deeply disappointed and vows to appeal.\par \par \uc2 SEN. BOB MENENDEZ (D-NJ): I have never been anything but a patriot of my country. And for my country. I have never, ever been a foreign agent. And the decision rendered by the jury today would put at risk every member of the \uc2 United States Senate\uc2  in terms of what they think a foreign agent would be.\par \par \uc2 SHAWN (voice over): But prosecutors had claimed that Menendez funneled bribes through his wife Nadine, who was also charged, but her trial has been suspended indefinitely because she is undergoing treatment for breast cancer.\par \par \uc2 Senate Majority Leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  and fellow New Jersey Senator \uc2 Cory Booker\uc2  among the dozens of Democrats who are tonight saying Menendez needs to resign.\par \par \uc2 New Jersey Governor \uc2 Phil Murphy\uc2  also a Democrat said, "If he refuses to vacate his office, I call on the \uc2 U.S. Senate\uc2  to vote to expel him."\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 SHAWN (on camera): As Menendez left court here, he seemed defiant giving no indication that he has any desire to vacate his seat and step down. He will be sentenced in October. He could face up to 222 years in prison, Bret.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Eric Shawn in Manhattan. Eric, thanks.\par \par \uc2 The Dow had its best day in more than a year, check this out, surging 743 points to a new record close. The S&P 500 gained 36 to another record finish and the NASDAQ was up 37.\par \par \uc2 Up next, immigration and abortion two big issues for voters here in Wisconsin as we head to break here at the National the Republican National Convention.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Welcome back to Milwaukee. We expand our look at the issues important to voters here in Wisconsin. That's what elections are about, really. Issues, policy, a \uc2 Marquette University\uc2  poll shows the top issues here are the economy at 31 percent, immigration and border security at 19 percent, abortion at 15 percent, and Medicare and Social Security at 12 percent.\par \par \uc2 Tonight, we take a deeper look at two of those issues, immigration and abortion, and how their impacting the presidential race through the prism of Wisconsin.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 DONALD TRUMP\uc2  (R), FORMER U.S. PRESIDENT AND PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE: On day one, I will seal the border, stop the invasion, and send \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's illegal aliens, the hell back home.\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 , PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: Our offices secure the border, southern border is working.\par \par \uc2 BAIER (voice over): During President Biden's administration, \uc2 U.S. Customs and Border Protection\uc2  have recorded a record number of migrant encounters at the southwest border.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Biden help us.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Have you seen more and more people needing immigration help in legally?\par \par \uc2 EDWARD FALLONE, MARQUETTE UNIVERSITY LAW SCHOOL: Oh, absolutely. We have a few nonprofits that help with undocumented persons or persons with deportation or legal immigration issues. The demand far outstrips the supply.\par \par \uc2 BAIER (voice over): Edward Fallone is a law professor at \uc2 Marquette University\uc2 . He specializes in immigration law.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Immigration is the second most important issue for Wisconsin voters behind the economy.\par \par \uc2 FALLONE: Yes.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Why do you think, in a place like Wisconsin, this far from the border, immigration is this much of an issue?\par \par \uc2 FALLONE: Well, Immigration is always an emotional issue. In Wisconsin, in particular, we have a lot of industry that is dependent on immigration.\par \par \uc2 BAIER (voice over): Wisconsin brings in about 5,500 migrant workers each year for farm labor, but other estimates suggest the percentage of undocumented illegal workers on farms could be much higher.\par \par \uc2 FALLONE: We estimate about 70 percent or more of the labor force on Wisconsin dairy farms are undocumented, and this is a huge issue, as dairy farms are struggling to stay in existence, and that way of life is trying to survive.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: So, that's a big part of it. Is it difficult to find out how many illegal or undocumented workers are in Wisconsin?\par \par \uc2 FALLONE: Any statistic in immigration is really just a guess, sometimes an educated guess.\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: I'm not interested in playing politics with border or immigration. I'm interested in fixing it.\par \par \uc2 BAIER (voice over): President Biden has proposed a plan that would give the estimated 10.5 million undocumented immigrants already in the U.S. a pathway to citizenship.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : If the millions of Biden migrants became citizens, Medicare and social security will be gone. They'll be gone. They'll be gone.\par \par \uc2 BAIER (voice over): The former president's immigration platform includes strict vetting, merit-based immigration, and what the outline calls the largest deportation program in history.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Right now, on the issue of immigration, former President Trump is at 52 percent, and President Biden is at 28 percent.\par \par \uc2 FALLONE: Right.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: There is a big disparity there.\par \par \uc2 FALLONE: Yes, there is a big disparity. And I think that it's an issue that drives turnout. It's an issue to scare voters. And we have a situation now where both parties, their focus is not on making a positive message on what their policies are.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Do you think that it will be a driving issue for this election?\par \par \uc2 FALLONE: Oh, I think it will. Because, again, it's an emotional issue, and both parties are focusing on emotion. On the Democratic side, it's abortion, and on the Republican side it's immigration.\par \par \uc2 AMERICAN CROWD: (INAUDIBLE)\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Abortion, it is the third most important issue in Wisconsin. If you look at the polls, how do you see it playing out in the wake of Roe v. Wade, and how this issue has really changed as a political issue?\par \par \uc2 HEATHER WEININGER, EXECUTIVE DIRECTOR, WISCONSIN RIGHT TO LIFE: Absolutely. In Wisconsin, you know, we're the purple state, right? So, this, this really could come into play this election cycle. I think what we're seeing, though, is the Republicans clearly identifying where they are right now on abortion, something they haven't done in the past.\par \par \uc2 BAIER (voice over): Heather Weininger is the executive director of the pro- life advocacy group, Wisconsin Right to Life.\par \par \uc2 WEININGER: And now, we see President Trump, he came out and clearly told the public where he is on this issue, and I think that's really in part -- important for candidates, in particular, to help understand and not let the pro-abortion side define what it means to be a pro-life.\par \par \uc2 BAIER (voice over): President Trump has supported the Supreme Court's decision to end Roe v. Wade, leaving it to states to set their own abortion laws. He has faced criticism from those within his party for his stance on opposing only late term abortions.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: How much has the platform battle about, you know, saying against late term abortion, but not putting it in specifics overall? How much has that stirred the pot here?\par \par \uc2 WEININGER: You know, for us at Wisconsin Right to Life, we're not affiliated with a party, which is great for us, because we're just going to keep doing the work that we do.\par \par \uc2 We want to make sure we offer compassion to women who are in an unplanned pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 BAIER (voice over): Abortion is banned after 20 weeks of pregnancy in Wisconsin, state Republicans have tried to push for a more restrictive policy -- banning procedures after 14 weeks.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: You all fought for a long time to get Roe v. Wade overturned. It happened, but it has invigorated Democrats and pro-choice folks. Has it changed the dynamic?\par \par \uc2 WEININGER: I think the dynamic had always been there. They are just louder than ever before on this.\par \par \uc2 BAIER (voice over): President Biden says restrictive abortion laws have restricted access to fertility treatments. He's calling on Congress to restore the protections that Roe v. Wade put in place.\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: You should be accountable for states enacting extreme laws that put IVF treatments at risk for women desperately trying to have families.\par \par \uc2 BAIER (voice over): According to the \uc2 United Health Foundation\uc2 , almost 70 percent of voters in Wisconsin are women.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: How much do you think it will come up this week?\par \par \uc2 WEININGER: You know, I think in light of everything that has happened here over the weekend and the days to follow, I think we're going to have some really good conversations about how we can help families in America, and that's what I look forward to hearing.\par \par \uc2 BAIER (voice over): All right. Up next, we talk with the man leading the effort to try to flip the Senate to the Republican side.\par \par \uc2 But first, as we head to break, no trip to Milwaukee is complete without a visit to the Wisconsin cheese mart.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Wisconsin is also known for cheese. The Wisconsin cheese mart here in downtown Milwaukee, was founded in 1938, carries more than 150 different varieties of Wisconsin cheese, ships to all 50 states. It's been family- owned for more than 80 years.\par \par \uc2 Here's the traditional cheese curds. Get this stat, Wisconsin produces more than 3 billion pounds of cheese a year, more than Italy. That may get you stopped up, but that's a lot of cheese.\par \par \uc2 SPECIAL REPORT continues after this.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Welcome back to Milwaukee. Here are some other headlines, quickly. \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  says he's moving the headquarters of his \uc2 SpaceX\uc2  venture from California to Texas because of the golden state's new law banning school rules requiring parents to be notified of their child's pronoun change. Musk says it and other laws attack both families and companies.\par \par \uc2 Severe weather slammed Chicago Monday night as storms uprooting trees, ripping roofs off homes along a 500-mile stretch of the Midwest. Hurricane force gusts including 101 miles per hour gusts at Davis Junction, Illinois. An Indiana woman died when a tree crashed into her home.\par \par \uc2 Overseas, French President \uc2 Emmanuel Macron\uc2  accepting the prime minister's resignation Tuesday. Gabriel Attal will be kept on as the head of a caretaker government. This follows parliamentary elections this month that left the national assembly with no dominant political bloc in power in France for the first time in France's modern republic.\par \par \uc2 Independent presidential candidate \uc2 Robert F. Kennedy Jr.\uc2  is apologizing to former President Trump for the leak of details about their phone call. Kennedy says he was doing an interview at the time of the call and the videographer kept recording. Former President Trump on the phone can be heard recalling his conversation with President Biden about the attempt on his life.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 DONALD TRUMP\uc2 , FORMER U.S. PRESIDENT: He was very nice, actually. He called me. And he said, how did you choose to move to the right? I said I was just showing a chart. I didn't have to tell him the chart was on all the people pouring into our country, right? And something raps me. It sounded like a giant, like the world's largest mosquito.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BAIER: The former president also appears to pitch Kennedy on endorsing his campaign, something Kennedy so far has said he is not doing.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 SEN. \uc2 CHRIS MURPHY\uc2 , (D-CT): J.D. Vance is a believer in a national abortion ban, no exceptions. He is one of the Republican senators that routinely stops us from being able to approve appointees to the Department of Justice. He is being picked in part because he is going to help shape this transition away from democratic norms, this transition to a white patriarchal Christian dominated nation.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Democrats jumping on the V.P. choice of J.D. Vance. Today he had a brief phone call with Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 . It was said to be respectful, cordial, and they did talk about the possibility of a debate.\par \par \uc2 Let's bring in Montana Senator Steve Daines, chairman of the National Republican Senatorial Committee. It's his job to try flip the Senate to the GOP this November. Senator, thanks for being here.\par \par \uc2 SEN. STEVE DAINES, (R-MT): Glad to join you, Bret.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: First, let me ask you about the choice of J.D. Vance, what that means for some of your Senate races and how he factors in in a campaign scenario.\par \par \uc2 DAINES: Yes, I think it's a big help to appeal to what we call these lunch bucket Democrats, these Democrats looking for a home. J.D. Vance's story is unique. He definitely grew up on the other side of the railroad tracks, a native son of Ohio. Goes to Ohio State. Enlists in the \uc2 United States Marine Corps\uc2 . He will be the first U.S. Marine ever elected to vice president. He went to Yale. He's a very smart guy, but he appeals to voters in places like Pennsylvania, like Michigan. And he is going to help us in that Senate race in Ohio. I'm sure \uc2 Sherrod Brown\uc2  did not like hearing the news that J.D. Vance was Trump's V.P. pick.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Let me -- first of all, the balance of power is tight. You have a good-looking map, and you could flip the Senate depending, as you put up the balance of power, 47-49. And you look at the map of the 33 regularly scheduled elections this year, 10 seats held by Republicans, 19 seats held by Democrats, four seats are held by independents who caucus with Democrats. So you are in a good position. But some of these polls don't look good at this point, or at least so far. Let's go to your home state of Montana. It's pretty tight with the incumbent \uc2 Jon Tester\uc2  and the challenger Sheehy up just slightly. But that's a tight race.\par \par \uc2 DAINES: Well, it is. They spent $42 million, \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 's super PAC, attacking Tim Sheehy. That's like spending $500 million in a state like Pennsylvania because we only have a million people. Sheehy tied, maybe slightly up by one. When I ran for my reelect in 2021 against a very popular incumbent Democratic governor Steve Bullock, at this same time in July, it was a one-point race. We ended up winning by 10 points. I think the point is these voters tend to come home, they start to track more closely --\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Shift late.\par \par \uc2 DAINES: -- to the presidential ballot as it gets closer to election.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Let's go to Pennsylvania. That's a key state. You are saying Vance is going to help you in someplace like Pennsylvania. You have got McCormick trailing the incumbent Casey pretty significantly in the average of polls.\par \par \uc2 DAINES: Again, not surprised. These May through July polls, oftentimes you go back to prior Senate and presidential election, years like 2020, many of my colleagues, \uc2 Susan Collins\uc2 , \uc2 Joni Ernst\uc2 , they were well behind their opponents. They started to turn this thing back around Labor Day. And we have a massive resource gap as well, Bret. I think some understand the Democrats have a lot of money. We've got a website, Senate24.com. Really important to get folks to join us to help our candidates at the grassroots level.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Ohio, you've got the incumbent \uc2 Sherrod Brown\uc2  up on challenger Moreno. You think that something like this, the convention can give you a bump out of some of these Senate races?\par \par \uc2 DAINES: Yes, I do. And you look at the polling data with President Trump. Right now he is leading Biden by about 10 points in Ohio. Again, as we've looked at historical data, if you look at the 16 and 20 elections where there were 69 total Senate races in those two cycles with Trump on the ballot, the party that won the presidency in that state also won the Senate race in 68 of 69 of those races. The only exception was \uc2 Susan Collins\uc2  in Maine where she won Maine but Biden won Maine.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: OK, Maryland, you've got the former governor, \uc2 Larry Hogan\uc2 , trailing a Democrat Alsobrooks. Hogan was asked if he was going to endorse former President Trump. He said no. Does that hurt him there?\par \par \uc2 DAINES: Look, \uc2 Larry Hogan\uc2  is a Republican running in Maryland, not Mississippi. That's a state that Biden probably is going to win by 25 points. \uc2 Larry Hogan\uc2  has a very unique position. He's a maverick, not really emboldened to any particular party, any particular candidate. He runs as \uc2 Larry Hogan\uc2 . That's why he is a successful two-term elected Republican governor in a very Democrat state. We've had some other polling data that showed Larry hogan up six points here recently.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Michigan, it looks like Rogers is going to be the candidate, be the nominee. He's trailing Slotkin in Michigan in the matchup, potentially, should he get through all that, and it looks like he is going to. How do you see that race?\par \par \uc2 DAINES: The way I look at Michigan, it's an open seat. Senator Stabenow announced at the time that it's an open seat. Based on everything we've seen shows that race a toss-up tie. In fact, Cook just moved Michigan to toss-up. I think Trump has a good shot to win Michigan. Trump wins by two or three points in Michigan, \uc2 Mike Rogers\uc2  has a real good shot to win that state.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: And you look at someplace like West Virginia where you're going to pick up because \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2  retires, you are likely going to win that race going away.\par \par \uc2 DAINES: That race is all but over, Bret. I'm a conservative forecaster, but Trump is going to win West Virginia by 40 points. Both sides have virtually given up on that race. \uc2 Jim Justice\uc2  will be the next U.S. Senator. That's a pick up seat. That takes it to 50-50. The next most important seat will be Montana and Tim Sheehy. We win Montana, Tim Sheehy beats \uc2 Jon Tester\uc2 , we have the majority outright, and \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  is no longer the majority leader.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Where's the black race that you're saying, wait, there's a possibility we can pull this off?\par \par \uc2 DAINES: We've got another important race out west. We've got one in Nevada with Sam Brown. A West Point graduate, severely wounded by the \uc2 Taliban\uc2 . That race is also a toss-up by Cook. You go right next door in Arizona, Kari Lake, just down two points at the moment. A very important states. And in New Mexico, right now we've got Trump down just one point in New Mexico. We've got Nella Domenici down only three. That's a sleeper race right now we're keeping an eye on.\par \par \uc2 We like going down the states, so we would love to have you back and do this again as we go down closer to November.\par \par \uc2 Happy to do it, Bret, any time.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Senator, thank you.\par \par \uc2 DAINES: Thank you.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Up next, the panel on day two of the Republican Convention, plus the investigation into the attempted assassination of former President Trump, the fight over whether President Biden remains on the November ballot, and Menendez guilty verdict.\par \par \uc2 But as we head to break, a look at how people from Milwaukee way back when used to get their news.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BAIER: We're at Milwaukee City Hall not far from the convention site, the Fiserv Forum. This used to be the site in the 1850s for two German newspapers. There's a big history of German ancestry here in Milwaukee, and politics was as important back then for the new German immigrants as it is today. There were two different papers, "The Wisconsin Banner" and "Sentinel." They went opposite directions ideologically. "The Banner" tied with the Democrats, "The Sentinel" tied with the wigs. Eventually the papers came together and they published a weekly edition together in 1913. A lot of history here in downtown Milwaukee.\par \par \uc2 We'll be back after this.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 LESTER HOLT, NBC NEWS: Has this shooting changed the trajectory of this race?\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 , (D) PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: I don't know, and you don't know either.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Never have I seen a party coalesce the way it has, and it started before the shooting. But really after the shooting, it just really popped together.\par \par \uc2 SEN. \uc2 JOHN THUNE\uc2 , (R-SD) SENATE MINORITY WHIP: It's a great contrast, and we benefit from it. President Biden certainly does not. There is a lot of energy around the Republican Party, a sense of unity.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BAIER: There is this sense of galvanizing the Republican Party on this, the second night of the Republican National Convention. Meantime, there's a lot of chaos, if you will, on the political side in the Democratic Party. President Biden out today campaigning, calling for the temperature to be brought down.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 , (D) PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: If you're going to talk about standing against violence, you must stand against all violence. You must stand against violence perpetrated against presidential candidates in Pennsylvania. You must stand against all violence. The violence perpetrated against George Floyd in Minnesota --\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: -- against black veterans like police officers Eugene Goodman on January 6th.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BAIER: What about that? You've got Biden allies now calling to speed up the process here for -- the nomination process for President Biden. And is that going to happen? We don't know at this point. They are pushing to speed up the nomination amid the backlash among Democrats.\par \par \uc2 Let's bring in our panel, Harold Ford Jr., former Tennessee Congressman, co-host of THE FIVE, Mary Katharine Ham, columnist for "Outkick", and "\uc2 Washington Post\uc2 " columnist, \uc2 American Enterprise Institute\uc2  senior fellow Marc Thiessen.\par \par \uc2 All right, Harold, is President Biden going to be the Democrats' nominee by the time we get to Chicago?\par \par \uc2 HAROLD FORD JR., FOX NEWS CHANNEL CONTRIBUTOR: I'm not sure. And I think we all have to be honest with ourselves. I watched the interview with Lester Holt late last night, a replay of it. The grievances that the president had with the questions seemed curious to me. He had a poor debate performance. Language about politically charged language is something that's under question. I would have thought he would have just answered those questions forthrightly and said we all need to tone it down, and here's what I'm going to do going forward.\par \par \uc2 When asked would he debate, accept another debate between he and President Trump? I don't know how you don't say yes. The number one thing leading Democrats believe is he not fit to prosecute the Democrats case in the fall is the way he performed in that debate, people believing he is too old. You have to do these things. And for Democrats, some Democrats who are asking them not to speed this up process, they are right. There's too much at stake here.\par \par \uc2 When President Trump chose Senator Vance, and congratulations to him as his V.P., he sent Democrats a message that I'm going to serve four more years, and I'm putting a guy who is 39 years old who can serve an additional eight years. You think about the courts, you think about the economy, you think about taxes, education, that's what's at stake here. And Democrats have a big question to answer here in the next few days. And I think more and more of them are coming to the conclusion that maybe \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is not the right person to prosecute this case.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: So you are saying it might not be Biden by the time we get to Chicago? I'm just reading between the lines?\par \par \uc2 FORD: I'm absolutely saying it, if we want to win, and I think we do.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Mary Katharine it's a contrast to Senator Thune's point. This convention seems to be galvanizing. You have got \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  and \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  speaking tonight. And yet, on the Democratic side, there is this upheaval and people like Harold Ford saying it may change.\par \par \uc2 MARY KATHARINE HAM, FOX NEWS CONTRIBUTOR: Look, I think the assassination attempt obviously changed things in a huge way. You cannot write a better recipe, no matter how traumatic they come to it. And I'm so thankful that we didn't get anything worse out of that situation than that event. So people are feeling unity on this side.\par \par \uc2 On the other side, you couldn't write a better recipe for disunity. And the president managed to get the conversation back on the table when I thought there was no way he could do it this week by giving that interview to Lester Holt in which he did not perform well. And I think breaking up with this candidate is like canceling a wedding after the invitations have gone out. It is going to get more chaotic every single day from now until the wedding in late August. So if they want to do this, it's got to be unanimity of plan and purpose, but quick.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Originally the virtual nomination was August 7th because Ohio had this screwy law that Democrats wanted to virtually do it, lock it in. They changed it to move it to September 1st. But now the DNC wants to keep it on August 7th to try to speed up this process.\par \par \uc2 MARC THIESSEN, FOX NEWS CONTRIBUTOR: Yes. The Democrats have a structural problem that won't be solved by taking \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  off the ballot. It's not just that he's old. If the economy was strong, the world was at peace, the border was secure, no one would care how old \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is. No one would care if he could construct a sentence. The Democratic Party has presided over what the American people consider to be a disaster. And Biden's health and his cognitive ability is the icing on the cake.\par \par \uc2 And now what they've done is they've lost -- because of the assassination, they've lost the one argument they need to make which is the only one that gains traction with people, which is that Trump is going to be a dictator. Democracy is on the ballot. Your freedoms are literally at stake in this election. They can't say that after \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  went out and said we need to lower the temperature. We've got to stop this outrageous rhetoric, because every time either Biden or another Democrat starts making this case, they'll say this is the kind of language that got \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  shot. And they'll have a point.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: We're being told that former House Speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  is working the phones. And if you have got \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  working the phones against you, that's not a good thing. "\uc2 New York Times\uc2 ", Adam Schiff "warned of wipeout for Democrats if Biden remains in race. If Mr. Biden remained, not only would he lose to former President \uc2 Donald J. Trump\uc2 , he could be enough of a drag on other Democratic candidates that the party would most likely lose the Senate and miss an opportunity to win control of the House, Mr. Schiff said at a fundraiser in New York." You just heard Steve Daines, senator from Montana. There are races that Democrats are poised to potentially win, at least right now. But that could change if the top of the ticket --\par \par \uc2 FORD: I think that's the jeopardy, the down ballot pressure. Do we want to risk losing? And it's a gamble to change candidates. But the gamble, I think, is greater staying the course. I think a lot of Democrats believe losing the House, the Senate, and the presidency. We have a long tradition of forceful, passionate debate in politics. And we should continue to have it. We should not allow this shooter, and thank God President Trump is alive and the triumphant return he made last night. That was amongst many Americans who saluted that. But we have a strong tradition in our country of political disagreement. It shouldn't be violent. We should each lay out our visions and let the country decide. A beautiful vision is being laid out here. If Democrats don't counter that and have an effective person to do it, we will lose.\par \par \uc2 THIESSEN: But here's the thing, the script has been flipped, because \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  campaigned as uniter who is going to bring the country together, and now his only successful message is of division, that democracy is on the ballot, a dictatorship is in the offing. If \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  comes out on Thursday night and offers a message of unity and tries to bring the country together and reach out to disaffected Democrats and people, the whole script has been flipped. He can actually present himself as the guy who is going to fulfill \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's unfulfilled promise to unite the country. That would be a remarkable turnaround.\par \par \uc2 FORD: Which is why -- you are making my case, Marc -- which why \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  might not be the person to lead the prosecution for Democrats in the fall.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Yes. Meantime, Democrats have had a tough couple weeks. Since that debate, you have all of these things that have happened, and now today you've got Senator Menendez, majority leader Schumer calling on Menendez to resign following the guilty verdict. He says, "In light of this guilty verdict, Senator Menendez must now do what is right for his constituents, the Senate, and our country and resign." He didn't say that until today when the jury came back with the conviction.\par \par \uc2 HAM: I say bring back resigning. We have a giant public trust problem in this country, and it is because often leaders at the highest echelons do not pay a price, are not held accountable. In this case he's held accountable in a court of law and he should recognize in his job in the Senate as well. Of course, that's not great for Democrats. I would say the same for the head of the Secret Service who has presided over a gigantic failure that many layman could see was a vulnerability. And to say that the buck stops with me and also my behavior will not change and I'm not leaving, I think leads to just more and more erosion of public trust.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Which is insane, because the Congress right now, House Republicans are saying they are just not getting anything from Secret Service or DHS. They are going to have a briefing tomorrow, but they haven't had any interchange in communications.\par \par \uc2 HAM: Her conversation in an interview, her excuses were quite nonsensical. There hasn't been communication between her and Biden, which I find mind blowing. And I just think that in order to -- if anyone cares about public trust here, let's make a move to actually make someone pay the price for this, because someone should.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Yes. It's going -- this is a big investigation.\par \par \uc2 FORD: It turns out what you have just shared and what we have been hearing some things on the Internet, she should lose her job. But I'm going to let the report come out and we'll take action according to that.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: All right, panel, we've got a big night ahead here at the second night of the Republican Convention.\par \par \uc2 Up next, a very spooky sidebar to this convention here in Milwaukee, please join Martha MacCallum and me for our convention coverage special tonight, 10:00 p.m. eastern time right here on FOX News. We'll be back after a short break.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Welcome back. Here in downtown Milwaukee, the Pfister Hotel has played host to many presidents visiting this city. Former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is here now, but \uc2 Woodrow Wilson\uc2 , William McKinley, \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 . \uc2 John F. Kennedy\uc2  made this hotel his campaign headquarters in 1960. The hotel is also famous for hosting Major League Baseball teams. Many players actually on opposing teams have reported supernatural events here, from Bryce Harper to Mookie Betts. Two \uc2 St. Louis Cardinals\uc2  players even elected to room together after a ghost sighting here. Very few national teams have not reported a paranormal experience inside.\par \par \uc2 So now former President Trump and his team are staying here, and they are hoping for some good spirits before his big speech Thursday nights.\par \par \uc2 We have day two of the Republican National Convention tonight, 10:00 p.m. eastern time. Martha and I will be back to anchor that. Until then, that's it for this SPECIAL REPORT, fair, balanced and still unafraid.\par \par \uc2 THE INGRAHAM ANGLE starts right now.\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2024 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2024 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document FNSPBB0020240717ek7g00001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 Trump Arrives At \uc2 RNC\uc2  After Assassination Attempt\b0\par\par\uc2 Sean Hannity \par \uc2 11,282 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 July 2024\par \uc2 Fox News: Hannity\par \uc2 SHAN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2024 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2024 ASC Services II Media, LLC.  All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 SEAN HANNITY\uc2 , FOX NEWS HOST: Welcome to "Hannity."\par \par \uc2 And this is a FOX News Alert. We are broadcasting live. We're in beautiful Milwaukee. We are in Wisconsin, where the very first day of the 2024 Republican National Convention, it is off, it is running after a weekend that shook America and, frankly, the world to its core.\par \par \uc2 Make no mistake, Saturday's assassination attempt against President Trump, well, it put so much in perspective. And now it is official. The Republican ticket is now set. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has selected Ohio Senator J.D. Vance to be his running mate.\par \par \uc2 Senator Vance will enter a presidential race unlike any other in American history. How many times do I say we are at an inflection point? The world is at an inflection point. And he will join a ticket with tremendous momentum. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is now ahead in virtually every major poll. His lead is growing.\par \par \uc2 And breaking today, a federal judge -- and this is huge -- tossed out the DOJ's bogus document case against President Trump in Palm Beach. Now the Trump/Vance ticket can focus on what really matters, the American people, America's place in the world, immigration, the economy, law and order, energy, issues that matter to all of you.\par \par \uc2 So, without further ado, joining us now, marine, Senator, author of the massive big hit, both in a book form and movie, "Hillbilly Elegy," is the Republican vice presidential nominee, J.D. Vance.\par \par \uc2 Sir, how are you?\par \par \uc2 SEN. J.D. VANCE (R-OH): Good, man. How are you?\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Good to see you.\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Good to see you.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I'm sure you have had a very slow day today.\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Yes, that's right. Nothing happened. Pretty boring.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Nothing happened. Pretty boring day.\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Let's talk about the process.\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Sure.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: A lot of questions for you, obviously.\par \par \uc2 What was it like? Because the last couple of days, well, it's down to two, you and Senator Rubio. What was that like for you?\par \par \uc2 VANCE: You know, I just tried to enjoy the ride. What an honor to be considered. If it had been Senator Rubio, obviously, Marco is a good guy, he's a good friend. So I tried to just have a good attitude about it.\par \par \uc2 My family's very excited, obviously asking a lot of questions. I will say, Sean, I hope I'm not betraying too many confidences here, but when the president called me today to actually formally offer me to become the vice presidential nominee, which just sounds crazy, my son, my 7-year-old son was sort of making noise in the background.\par \par \uc2 I'm getting so embarrassed. It's like, oh, my God, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's asking me to be his vice president.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: So the phone rings, and he calls you and you're like, OK, this is the call or maybe not the call?\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Or maybe it's a bad call, right?\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Right.\par \par \uc2 VANCE: It's the call. Who knows whether it's good or bad.\par \par \uc2 But then he actually has me put my 7-year-old son on the phone. You think about this. Everything that's happened, the guy just got shot at a couple of days ago, and he takes the time to talk to my 7-year-old. It's a moment I will never forget.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. And what did he actually say?\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Yes, he just said, look, I think we have got to go save this country. I think you're the guy who can help me in the best way. You can help me govern. You can help me win. You can help me in some of these Midwestern states like Pennsylvania, Michigan and so forth.\par \par \uc2 And he said, rightfully, that we have been very, very close for a long time, "but especially since I endorsed you in 2022. And I would not have won that race without \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's endorsement. And the president's trust then and his partnership since then has been something I value a great deal.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Let me ask you. You know this happens all the time. You get announced, and incoming begins.\par \par \uc2 Let's go over some of it.\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Please.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And not questions you haven't heard before new would be asked. All of them are fairly predictable.\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Of course.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: But I think Americans want the answers.\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Sure.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Let me go back to, for example, after he announced this. The media immediately -- I'm starting to read every article, right?\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Yes.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And criticizing you that, here's a guy -- this was -- came out of Ohio -- "His support for a national abortion ban and his twisted belief that women should stay in violent marriages for the benefit of their children exemplifies his dangerous extreme extremism. He's not just wrong for Ohio. He's wrong for the country."\par \par \uc2 I actually saw those articles this weekend, and I said, why would I wait? I wanted to know the answer. I called you.\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Yes.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: How do you address that?\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Well, look, Sean, first of all, Democrats have completely twisted my words here.\par \par \uc2 And, as you know, both me and my mom actually were victims of domestic violence. When they say that Vance has supported women staying in violent marriages, I think it's shameful for them to take a guy with my history and my background and say that that's what I believe. It's not what I believe. It's not what I said.\par \par \uc2 And I think, Sean, it's evidence of the Democrats' complete inability to talk about the future. What are Republicans running on? Delivering the peace and prosperity that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  already delivered in his four years. What are Democrats running on? Lies and complete distortions of people's records.\par \par \uc2 That is something I think the American people want to reject. They're too smart for it.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I said on January 2, when the year started, I said, let me tell you what this year is going to be like. And I try to give a perspective to my audience. It's not my first rodeo, J.D.\par \par \uc2 VANCE: That's right.\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And I said, the Democrats are going to try to make this election about, quote, "democracy in peril." How often have we heard that? Meanwhile, they might want to disenfranchise every primary voter that they had. And they wanted to get \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  off the ticket in some states, another example.\par \par \uc2 It'd be about January 6. It would be about abortion and we hate \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Exactly right.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Can they run on the issue, is the country better off than it was four years ago?\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Of course they can't, Sean. They can't run on that at all.\par \par \uc2 And they can't run on the issue of, is the world more peaceful than it was four years ago? Remember, when \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  left office, you had real growing peace movements all over the world, the Abraham Accords that showed real promise of uniting the Israelis with some of the Sunni Arab states. There was no war in Europe.\par \par \uc2 Asia looked like it was under pretty good control. And three years later, it seems like we have a conflict in every corner of the world, and Americans are poorer, Sean.\par \par \uc2 You know a little about my background. I grew up in a poor family. I remember when my grandmother, who raised me, she used to negotiate with the Meals on Wheels people to give her additional food so that she could feed me.\par \par \uc2 How does a family like that deal with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's grocery price inflation? How does a family like that deal with gasoline and energy price inflation? It's gotten more expensive just to live a good life in this country.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and I want to make that better. And we have policies to make it better. Democrats have lies and distortions. And, again, I don't think the American people are going to reward that.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You know, I had an opportunity to talk to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . And I knew this question would come up probably, actually, for almost every person that was under consideration.\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Sure.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And that was past comments that you had made about him.\par \par \uc2 And when I -- I will tell you after what his response was.\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Sure.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: But you weren't -- didn't have the nicest things to say about him back in 2016 --\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Yes.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: -- which seems like a long time ago now.\par \par \uc2 You literally said -- you texted a friend that Trump is a cynical a-hole like Nixon, who wouldn't be that bad and might even prove useful, and that he's America's Hitler. And you compared him to a cultural heroin in The Atlantic Monthly.\par \par \uc2 And I will tell you Trump's response. But you said that then. What do you say to people that say, well, wait a minute, what did he mean?\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Well, Sean, I don't hide from that. I was certainly skeptical of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in 2016.\par \par \uc2 But President Trump was a great president, and he changed my mind. I think he changed the minds of a lot of Americans, because, again, he delivered that piece and prosperity. If you go back to what I thought in 2016, another thing that was going on, Sean, is, I bought into the media's lies and distortions.\par \par \uc2 I bought into this idea that somehow he was going to be so different, a terrible threat to democracy. It was a joke. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is the one who's trying to throw his political opposition in jail. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is the one who's trying to undermine American law and order.\par \par \uc2 President Trump did a really good job. And I actually think it's a good thing. When you see somebody, you were wrong about him, you ought to admit the mistake and admit that you were wrong.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: When I brought it up to him, he said --\par \par \uc2 VANCE: I can't wait for this.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: OK.\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: When I brought it up to him, he said, "Yes," he goes, "but he doesn't think that way now, does he?"\par \par \uc2 So he actually had a very good sense of humor about it. It also says a lot about him, and he understands. Were you as political back then?\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Not really, Sean. I mean, my book came out in 2016, "Hillbilly Elegy."\par \par \uc2 It's really sort of the story of growing up in poverty, achieving the American dream, starting out in business. And I really didn't care that much about politics. I certainly had views. I was a Republican, but I was not as nearly as involved, obviously, as I am today.\par \par \uc2 And, again, something that really changed for me, and I think for a lot of Americans, is, we saw the results of the Trump presidency compared to the obsessive, deranged media reaction in 2019 and 2020. Like, what's going on? What's so bad about this guy that he's delivered rising wages for American workers and peace in the world? Why is the media so obsessed with him?\par \par \uc2 I think a lot of Americans actually have had a similar awakening over the last few years, because you compare the results with the reaction, and, clearly, the people with the reaction to the problem, that's not President Trump's problem.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You know, a lot of people forget too, back in the first debate, I believe it was, and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  was on the stage with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  at the time, and she said, "I was that girl," if you remember that moment.\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Yes.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: It was a very hard-hitting moment.\par \par \uc2 And what she was referring to is the fact that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  had partnered with a former Klansman and tried to stop the integration of public schools. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's words, he didn't want those schools to become racial jungles and --\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Sean, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  basically said \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  wouldn't want a little black girl like me to live in her neighborhood. He also palled around with Klansmen.\par \par \uc2 She said this months before she joined his ticket, Sean. I said some bad things about \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  10 years ago, but I think it's actually important to be able, again, to admit that you're wrong, and I think I can make a good case to the American people, people who may have been skeptical of the president back in 2016. Who can be skeptical now that we have seen the results?\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right, let's talk about a little bit -- and I think these are important times and consequential times.\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Sure.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And we see what's happening with the border, for example. I think it's now become the number one national security threat.\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Oh, absolutely.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And we have nearly 11 million unvetted \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  illegal immigrants in this country. What should we do with them?\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Well, Sean, we have to deport people. We have to deport people who broke our laws, who came in here.\par \par \uc2 And I think we start with the violent criminals. And President Trump has been very, very effective at communicating on this, so to the point where now a majority of Americans believe that we need to deport a large number of people who have come here illegally. That's a major political victory for him.\par \par \uc2 And I think it's going to lead to a policy victory for the American people. But, Sean, we have to talk about the fentanyl problem, because this is something that I know extremely personally. And we have close to 100,000 Americans dying of drug overdoses every single year. Most of it is brought in by Mexican drug cartels, manufactured in China, then brought in by these cartels.\par \par \uc2 To get a little personal, my mom struggled with addiction for a big chunk of my early life. That's why my grandmother, who I call Mamaw, raised me.\par \par \uc2 But the coolest thing, maybe the greatest blessing of my life, is that my mom is about to celebrate 10 years sober. And she is able to celebrate 10 years sober, frankly, because the poison that's coming across the border now wasn't coming across in such large numbers 15 years ago.\par \par \uc2 We are depriving Americans of a second chance with their loved ones. You cannot keep on doing this. You're orphaning an entire generation of kids. Go to Pennsylvania, Michigan, Wisconsin, Sean, you have thousands of grandparents raising grandchildren that they weren't expecting to raise because of the poison. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  let it come across the border.\par \par \uc2 President Trump is the guy to stop this. And if we don't stop it, we're going to lose a generation of young kids.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You know, when I saw you in Atlanta, I said I felt a little embarrassed, because I was one of the few Americans -- because most people knew "Hillbilly Elegy." It was a massive bestseller that became a movie.\par \par \uc2 And I didn't -- I literally read at least a book a day researching radio and television.\par \par \uc2 VANCE: I know you do.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And so I decided, I will watch the movie. And when I saw you, I did ask you, is this really what your life was, Appalachia? And this is the history of your life.\par \par \uc2 Appalachia. You become a Marine. And, by the way, your mom was a drug addict and an alcoholic, your father not exactly the greatest father in the world. And you grew up poor. And you had an amazing grandmother that came out of your life too.\par \par \uc2 VANCE: That's right.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: But then you joined the Marines. You served in Iraq. You came out of school. You went to Ohio State. You went to Yale. You prospered at Yale.\par \par \uc2 Then you went on to be successful in business, which, by the way, Democrats are criticizing you for. They wish you failed, I guess, when they wrote that. Considering where you came from, it's the American dream.\par \par \uc2 And then you got into politics, and you did so successfully, a pretty amazing story. Give us some texture and context to that life, that -- I mean, that's a tough life you had.\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Yes, Sean, it was tough in a lot of ways, but blessed in a lot of ways.\par \par \uc2 And I think you have got to sort of accept the good with the bad. I wouldn't see the world the same way that I see it without that experience. And I really do see it as a blessing. The grandmother who raised me was such an amazing person. I mean, she was a woman of deep Christian faith.\par \par \uc2 She cursed like a sailor. I mean, she had a mouth that would really make a Marine Corps drill instructor blush, but she was so loving and so disciplined. And I really think that all the opportunities that I have had come directly from her.\par \par \uc2 She also believed in this country and recognized that most people in Washington do not care about people like her. And when I talk about generations of grandparents raising generations of grandchildren, that's exactly what I think about, because I remember my Mamaw, she couldn't afford her Medicaid payments.\par \par \uc2 She couldn't afford the prescription drugs that she needed. She sometimes couldn't even afford food for both me and her. Those are the people who suffer when we have the policies that we have had over the last 3.5 years.\par \par \uc2 And those are the people who stand to benefit the most from President Trump round two.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Let me go back to the scene, and you referred to it earlier, Meals on Wheels.\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Yes.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And she would negotiate an extra something, because you had nothing else? Nothing?\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Well, we -- sometimes, we struggled, but sometimes, Sean, we didn't have anything.\par \par \uc2 And she would negotiate to get a little bit of extra, so that she could share with me and also have enough for herself. Look, sometimes, tough work -- sometimes, times were hard, right? And -- but I look back on that and I think to myself, when I go and talk to people, when I serve people as a United States senator from the state of Ohio, I go and visit a food bank, I actually understand a little bit what people are going through.\par \par \uc2 And so, yes, it was tough when I was dealing with it, but now I really do think it's a blessing, because it's given me a perspective a lot of politicians don't have.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Let's talk about what you believe the role of a vice president should be.\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Sure.\par \par \uc2 Well, look, Sean, I think it's very simple. Number one, you need to support the president in enacting the agenda, whether it's going and meeting with foreign leaders, whether it's working with the Senate and the House to get legislation passed.\par \par \uc2 The president can't be everywhere. Even \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  can't be everywhere. So you have got to be a person he can trust, he can rely on to actually advance the agenda. That's the most important job.\par \par \uc2 Of course, if something, God forbid, happens, you got to be ready to step into that office. That's one of the most important roles of the vice president. But I think \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , very healthy, going to serve for four very good years, but we have got to have Republicans who are helping him with the agenda.\par \par \uc2 You remember this as well as anybody, Sean. As successful as he was politically, even after he was elected, certain Republicans didn't want to actually enact the America first agenda. You have got to have leaders in Washington who are supporting him, not fighting against him.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Let's talk about an occasion where you might disagree with them.\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Sure.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: How do you view your role in terms of handling that moment?\par \par \uc2 VANCE: That's very simple, Sean.\par \par \uc2 I think that you owe it to the president to be honest with him if you don't think that he's doing the right thing, if you disagree with him. But you do it in private. You offer your counsel in private, because a lot of the vultures in the press, they will blow up every public disagreement.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: So you have met my colleagues while you're here.\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Yes.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I call them state-run media.\par \par \uc2 VANCE: No, they absolutely are state-run media.\par \par \uc2 In fact, they're so state-run that, even after President Trump was shot, and he showed a remarkable amount of unity and defiance and calmness, they blamed him for the rhetoric, even though he was the victim of a near- assassination.\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 VANCE: It's crazy.\par \par \uc2 But I think it's really important that you don't have Republicans who blow up disagreements, so that they can win points with the media, who are never going to treat Republicans fairly. The job is to help enact the agenda. And why does that matter? Because that's what's going to make people's lives better.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Let's talk about, I'm sure, in the course of this process, it had to go through your head, God forbid, what if?\par \par \uc2 We saw this on Saturday, President Trump, a millimeter. If he didn't turn his head, we would be having a very different conversation tonight.\par \par \uc2 VANCE: It's an act of God, Sean. Yes, we would.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And I certainly believe in God and faith, and it's an important part of life.\par \par \uc2 VANCE: I know you do.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And -- but it was that close.\par \par \uc2 And you always hear about one heartbeat away from the presidency. And I'm sure Americans are watching you tonight. Are you ready at a moment's notice to step into that role? And what do you believe most qualifies you for that?\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Well, Sean, the answer is yes.\par \par \uc2 And I have to say, you have to have some humility about this. It's the biggest job in the world. But I served my country successfully in the \uc2 United States Marine Corps\uc2 . I had a successful business career. And I have the vision and the agenda aligned with President Trump to make the American worker better off, to bring peace to the world, and to actually advance an agenda that's good for American citizens.\par \par \uc2 I think the experience that maybe most Americans would care about, it's not that I spent two years in the Senate, and I think I have had a very successful two years in the Senate. It's that I came from nothing, became a United States Marine and succeeded in business. That's the experience that I think gives you a fresh perspective.\par \par \uc2 You combine that with the ability to get things done, and that's what you need to do. But, Sean, I got to say, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is as healthy as anybody I have ever met. I tell him all the time, he's got ridiculous genes. I plan to be a very good vice president for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for four years.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Let's talk about when the shooting occurred this weekend.\par \par \uc2 What was going through your head? And now we have some perspective. I thought the people around him on the stage, Secret Service -- I have gotten to know the Secret Service guys over the years --\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Sure.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: -- doing this job. And I have found them to be amazing people. They're willing to sacrifice their lives for you or for the president or for any elected official they may be assigned to.\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Sure.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: They were phenomenal. And then we found out, how is it possible, just a mere 130 yards away? They talk about a perimeter, it was outside the perimeter.\par \par \uc2 No, the perimeter would be shooting range for any assassin. And a guy was able to get on a roof unnoticed, apparently, except by people in the crowd trying to warn law enforcement. To me, a massive failure. What is your reaction to it?\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Well, look Sean, it's scary. I was actually playing mini-golf with my kids when people started to text me, and I realized that president had been shot. Of course, I didn't know what his condition was.\par \par \uc2 My first reaction was just to pray for him. I was terrified. If President Trump had been killed, of course, terrible, terrible, terrible, but the reverberations in the country, it would have been a world historic tragedy. Thank God he was OK.\par \par \uc2 I don't know enough about the security protocols, but I was a United States Marine, and 150 yards is not nearly enough of a security perimeter.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: That's a layup --\par \par \uc2 VANCE: It's a layup for --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: -- for anybody that has any skill at all.\par \par \uc2 VANCE: With any skill at shooting.\par \par \uc2 It's amazing Sean, frankly, that he wasn't hurt much, much worse. So I think there needs to be a full-scale investigation. We need to understand what happened, because, clearly, mistakes were made.\par \par \uc2 I mean, look, the Secret Service ran up there. They put their bodies over and they reacted quickly. That's not what worries me. What worries me is, why was there a shooter 150 yards from the President of the United States? It doesn't make an ounce of sense.\par \par \uc2 But we need to understand why, because, look, Sean, you know this. A lot of Americans are extremely worried about President Trump, rightfully so, and they're very skeptical of the official narrative on anything. The way to solve that is to get to the bottom of this, understand what happened, and fix it so it doesn't happen again.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right, let me go back.\par \par \uc2 Let's go through some issues and where you stand on positions and where the administration would stand --\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Sure.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: -- assuming that, in 115 days -- by the way, early voting starts in about 64 days --\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Right.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: -- in Pennsylvania, a state you know very well.\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Exactly right.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Let's start with immigration.\par \par \uc2 What do we do with the nearly 11 million unvetted illegal immigrants, and I might add, many coming from countries with terror ties like Syria and Iran and Afghanistan and people from Venezuela and Egypt and tens of thousands from China and Russia?\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Yes, absolutely.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: What do we -- what should happen? Is there an orderly way to say, if you didn't come in legally, we will escort you home?\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Yes, there is, Sean.\par \par \uc2 First of all, we have got to stop the flow to begin with. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has thrown open the southern border. President Trump had it under control. We have got to stop the flow to begin with. Now, what do you do with the 11 million people -- I actually think it's probably more than 11 million people who are here right now.\par \par \uc2 Number one, you start with the most violent people, the people who have criminal records, and you have got to be willing to deport them. Number two --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: How do we find them?\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Well, I think, a lot of them, we actually know where they are, Sean. That's what the crazy thing about the Biden administration is they let people in, they give them asylum, and we actually know that these people are sort of out there in our country.\par \par \uc2 Some will be hard to find, sure, but a lot of them, you actually can find just because -- just if you actually try to look, which is what the Biden administration hasn't done.\par \par \uc2 The second thing, Sean, is, we have got to make it hard for illegal aliens to work in our country. It undercuts the wages of American workers. It invites more people to come in illegally. And if you make it hard for people to work, a lot of them are going to go back anyway. And you do those two things, I think you can go a long way to solving a problem, but you have got to stop the flow. That's the most important thing.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Let me go to the issue of the economy.\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Sure.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Let's talk about maybe some Americans that you do know, people in Appalachia, poor people.\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Yes.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: There was a study that came out, 25 percent of Americans had to forego meals in the last year. Nearly two-thirds of Americans say that they're literally gasping for air and having a hard time making ends meet every month.\par \par \uc2 What is the best way to get America to economic prosperity quickly? How do you do it?\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Number one, you have got to unleash American energy. President Trump is so strong in this. We had energy independence. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has destroyed it.\par \par \uc2 We could have energy dominance. We could be the main source of energy in the world. Pennsylvania --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: For Europe --\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Absolutely.\par \par \uc2 And that would actually weaken Russia and Iran and some of these other regimes. But we're sitting on the Saudi Arabia of natural gas in Ohio and Pennsylvania. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  would rather buy the stuff from Iran than buy it from Pennsylvania workers. It doesn't make an ounce of sense, Sean.\par \par \uc2 The other thing is, you have got to reinvigorate the manufacturing economy. The biggest contrast the media doesn't talk about between \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and President Trump is, President Trump was right about every single disaster that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  was wrong about.\par \par \uc2 NAFTA\uc2  destroyed the manufacturing economy in Pennsylvania, Michigan. A real estate developer from New York, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , was actually right about that issue. Letting China into the \uc2 World Trade Organization\uc2 , \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  supported it. A real estate developer from Queens named \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  opposed it.\par \par \uc2 And now, of course, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is saying let's open up America's energy markets, and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is trying to destroy it. It's actually shocking. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's entire career has been about decimating the manufacturing economy of this country. President Trump's entire career has been about, how do we rebuild it and how do we correct the mistakes of our broken leadership class?\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Let's talk about foreign policy, and I won't call it the Vance doctrine, because it'll be the Trump doctrine.\par \par \uc2 VANCE: It'll be the Trump doctrine.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: OK, but let's go over some of the hot spots in the world. I, for the life of me, don't understand \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's policy towards Iran.\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Not at all.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I don't understand why he allows China to have spy balloons and hostile maneuverings against our Air Force in international airways and our Navy in international waterways, why Russia got a waiver for the \uc2 Nord Stream 2\uc2  pipeline, for example.\par \par \uc2 But we have got a lot of hot spots in the world.\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Yes.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You have been very outspoken on the issue of Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Yes.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Hundreds of billions of dollars, and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  -- and then I would argue that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  surrendered in the war on terrorism with \uc2 Hamas\uc2  by not supporting Israel further in their offensive moves after the worst terror attack in their history.\par \par \uc2 Let's get your overall view. Let's look at these hot spots, Ukraine, Iran, the war in the Middle East.\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Yes.\par \par \uc2 So, first of all, Sean, I served in the \uc2 United States Marine Corps\uc2  for four years, one of the things I'm proudest of. The most important part, I think, of the Trump doctrine in foreign policy is, you don't commit America's troops unless you really have to, but, when you do, you punch and you punch hard.\par \par \uc2 I think that's the way that you respect America's brave men and women who are serving. Now, let me say something about --\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: When you say that, does that -- like, for example, how President Trump beat the caliphate. It was overwhelming force and it was done pretty fast.\par \par \uc2 VANCE: How President Trump beat the caliphate, beat \uc2 ISIS\uc2 , which people said literally couldn't be done, and he did it in a matter of months, but also Iran, Sean.\par \par \uc2 A lot of people recognize that we need to do something with Iran, but not these weak little bombing runs. If you're going to punch the Iranians, you punch them hard. And that's what he did when he took out Soleimani.\par \par \uc2 By the way, that action, people said that it would lead to broader war. It actually brought peace. It actually checked the Iranians and slowed them down a little bit.\par \par \uc2 But let me just say something about this Iran issue, because maybe the most important diplomatic breakthrough of the Trump administration was the Abraham Accords. If you want to check Iran, the way to do it is to, one, withdraw their oil money, which, of course, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's been bad about. But you have also got to enable the Israelis and the Sunni Arab states to work together and actually provide a counterbalance to Iran.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has done nothing. You have the infrastructure there, sitting there to weaken Iran, to strengthen our ally Israel. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's done nothing with it. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  would reinvigorate it.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I think one of the more, I guess, achievements of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  that doesn't get talked about a lot, he created an alliance with the U.S., Israel, the Saudis, the Emirates, Jordan, the Egyptians that very few people knew about.\par \par \uc2 I think we can get back to that.\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Absolutely.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I didn't think I'd see that in my lifetime.\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Neither did I.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: OK. So let's stay in the Middle East. How do we deal with the situation there now? I think Israel should have the right to win their war on terror. And they're our greatest ally in the Middle East. And I don't think Israel had a better friend than \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 VANCE: No, they didn't have a better friend than \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 And here's the problem, Sean, is, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's made it harder and harder for Israel to win that war. You want two things to happen. Number one, you want Israel to get this war over, and as quickly as possible, because the longer it goes on, the harder their situation becomes.\par \par \uc2 But, second, after the war, you want to reinvigorate that peace process between Israel, Saudi Arabia, the Jordanians, and so forth. What Biden has done is the worst of all possible worlds. He's prolonged the war, Israel's war to actually take out \uc2 Hamas\uc2 , but, in the process, he's made it harder for us to really move towards a sustainable peace.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Let's talk about Ukraine. You have been a critic of President Biden's policies.\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Yes.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: What should the policy be?\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Well, very simple, Sean. We have to point this out. Russia would not have invaded Ukraine if \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  had been president. Everybody agrees with it. Even a lot of my Democratic colleagues privately agree with that.\par \par \uc2 But here's the issue, Sean, is, we have now spent $200 billion. What's the goal? What are we trying to accomplish? Is there a risk of escalation into nuclear war? Because there is when you have a buffoon running foreign policy, and we have got a lot of them right now in Washington, D.C.\par \par \uc2 I think what President Trump has promised to do is go in there, negotiate with the Russians and Ukrainians, bring this thing to a rapid close, so that America can focus on the real issue, which is China. That's the biggest threat to our country. And we're completely distracted from it.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I spent a lot of time on this program pointing out \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  being weak and frail and a cognitive mess.\par \par \uc2 And I have shown a lot of videotapes since before the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Yes.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I hope you watch the show.\par \par \uc2 VANCE: I do.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: If you do, you have seen a lot of the tapes.\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And so all of a sudden, the world noticed. A few weeks ago, they were claiming real videos unedited of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  were cheapfakes. oh, my gosh, he's a cognitive mess. We got to get rid of him.\par \par \uc2 What is your reaction to all of that? Because I find it disingenuous and, frankly, I believe they're outright lying and there's been a cover-up of Joe's cognitive state. Do you believe he will be the candidate? What do you think of the cover-up? Does \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  replace him? What are your thoughts on all of it?\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Well, literally, Sean, six months ago, what you were saying on your program, the media was calling a conspiracy, and now the media is just calling it obvious facts. So you're way ahead of your press colleagues.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I wish -- well, I was four years ahead of them.\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 VANCE: That's right.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I wish they would say, Hannity's right, and put it up on a lower third.\par \par \uc2 VANCE: That's right.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: That would be nice. By the way, hell will freeze over.\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Yes.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: But go ahead.\par \par \uc2 VANCE: But, look, first of all, the Democrats want to try to run from this, and they're saying that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has to step down or \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  can't run for president.\par \par \uc2 That's not public spiritedness. That's political cynicism, because they should have been saying it three years ago. \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has allowed America to be saddled with a president who clearly doesn't have the mental capacity to do the job. It is not public spiritedness to call for him to step down when he's about to lose an election.\par \par \uc2 They should have been doing it years ago. And it's not just \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 . It's \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 . The entire Democratic apparatus lied about this guy. And, look, being dishonest, that's a problem, in and of itself, but it was in the service of ensuring that America effectively had an empty vessel as president for three years.\par \par \uc2 My message to the American people, Sean, is, we can either reward or punish that behavior. And the only way to punish the Democrats for lying about \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's health and saddling us with an incapacitated president is to vote them out of office at every level come November.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Do you really believe -- regardless of who were to take \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's place, I believe the Democratic Party is basically a united -- they're a united front.\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Sure.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I don't think immigration policy would change, I don't think economic policy would change. I don't think foreign policy would change. I don't think energy policy would change. Would anything change?\par \par \uc2 VANCE: No, nothing would change.\par \par \uc2 Every single one of their policies is exactly the same. The one thing that might change is, you might at least have a foreign -- or a president who can engage with a foreign leader without falling asleep or forgetting where he is. But if the policies underlying that diplomacy and that conversation are bad, which they would be, you don't actually solve any problems.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Let me go back to the question when we started, because after reading a lot of -- the attacks have already begun on you.\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Of course.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You did anticipate them, correct?\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Sure, sure.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: OK. Let me go back to the issue of abortion.\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Please.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And there was this article that said, oh, J.D. Vance said it's inconvenient.\par \par \uc2 I want you to address that, and I want you to explain in great, as much detail as you are what your position is on the issue of abortion, especially in light of the Supreme Court ruling, which I would argue codified first-trimester abortion, which is mostly done with a pill. Availability would be nationwide.\par \par \uc2 But what's your position in detail?\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Yes, very simply, Sean, first of all, the Democrats have completely twisted my words.\par \par \uc2 What I did say is that we sometimes in this society see babies as inconveniences, and I absolutely want us to change that. I do want us to be a more pro-life.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: That's the word they focused on --\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Exactly.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: -- inconvenience.\par \par \uc2 VANCE: But we do see babies as inconveniences. And that's a mistake, Sean. And I want to change that because I do care about protecting people.\par \par \uc2 Now, here's the thing. Roe v. Wade is no more. And what \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has said very, very smartly is, California is going to want to have a different policy from Ohio. Ohio is going to want to have a different policy from Alabama. And it is reasonable to let voters in states make those decisions.\par \par \uc2 It doesn't mean we have to agree with it, but you have to have some respect for the political process. This is really important, Sean, that respect for the political process. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is running against a \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  president who wants taxpayer-funded abortions up until the moment of birth.\par \par \uc2 President Trump is trying to identify some reasonable compromises so we can tone this thing down, find some reasonable pro-life policy, like, for example, making it easier to have babies, bringing down the price of homes so that you can raise a family in a house if you choose to have babies.\par \par \uc2 These things are, I think, where the Republican Party is going and focused on. The Democrats want the most radical abortion policy funded by taxpayers. So the idea that they can run on this and attack us, when President Trump is the one trying to identify some reasonable compromise, and they're the ones who want pro-life Christians to pay for abortions at 39 weeks, it's insane.\par \par \uc2 And I don't think any American buys it.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: It's interesting. \uc2 Bill Clinton\uc2  famously said rare and legal. And I think where Republicans seem to be today is rare, legal and early, meaning maybe Dobbs, 15 weeks.\par \par \uc2 And I see this as the number one issue that they want to demagogue, for sure, which we can see in the statements that Democrats have made about you.\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Well, this is a big difference actually between Democrats of now and 30 years ago.\par \par \uc2 My Mamaw, the woman who raised me was a -- she was pro-choice. She used to say safe, legal and rare. And I remember that that was her understanding of what the Democratic Party view was. The Republicans were pro-life. The Democrats were safe, legal and rare.\par \par \uc2 Now the Democrats are saying taxpayer-funded up until the moment of birth unlimited? That's ridiculous. And for them to try to say that we're radicals on this, Sean, I don't think the American people buy it.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: So you completely agree, are in full, complete agreement with President Trump, and is the answer, for example, that he gave during the debate?\par \par \uc2 VANCE: My view is that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is the leader of the Republican Party and his views on abortion are going to be the views that dominate this party and drive this party forward.\par \par \uc2 And his views are very simple, Sean. It's, look, you got to follow your heart. You have to believe in reasonable exceptions, because that's where the American people are. And you have got to let individual states make this decision.\par \par \uc2 Alabama is going to make a different decision from California. That is a reasonable thing. And that's how I think we build some bridges and have some respect for one another.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Let me ask last question. I will combine two issues in one.\par \par \uc2 It always comes up, the issue of LGBTQ rights, now the issue of trans status and what's age-appropriate in schools for kids and the Second Amendment.\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Well, look, I mean, I think that we shouldn't be teaching kids sexually explicit anything, whether it's LGBTQ or anything else.\par \par \uc2 I want my kids to go and learn reading, writing and arithmetic. And one of the important things that we can do as a country, Sean, is cut out the federal funding for radical curricula. A lot of the craziest stuff that you see in our schools, the craziest books and so forth, it comes from federal funding.\par \par \uc2 And I think 90 percent of Democrats and Republicans, they just want their kids to get an education. They don't want them to be indoctrinated. They don't want fourth graders to read sexually explicit stuff. That's not a left/right issue. That's a commonsense, parents rights issue.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: So, if you look over your shoulder, there's a big stage down there, and you have a big speech coming up.\par \par \uc2 Has the world changed a little bit since Wednesday -- since Saturday? And you're speaking Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 VANCE: It's changed a little bit, Sean. Of course it has.\par \par \uc2 I mean, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has given me an incredible honor. And we get to go and make the case to the American people that President Trump's next four years can be as great as the first four years, maybe even better. And that's an incredible thing to do.\par \par \uc2 But, Sean, I'm still grounded, man. My faith. I got to spend a few hours with my wife and kids today. We have got a 7-year-old, a 4-year-old, and a 2-year-old. Things are crazy, and things are way different.\par \par \uc2 But I'm still a husband and a dad first, and that's going to make me a very happy guy over the next four months.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Well, we're going to look forward to seeing you. We will be out with you on the campaign trail.\par \par \uc2 First of all, congratulations.\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Thanks, Sean.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Congratulations to the great people of Ohio. I have a lot of friends there.\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Thanks, man.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: We wish you the best of luck in all of this.\par \par \uc2 J.D. Vance, for my colleagues in the mob and state-run media, they're not going to be your friend ever. Anyway --\par \par \uc2 VANCE: God bless you, Sean.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: God bless you. I appreciate you being with us.\par \par \uc2 All right. In case you missed it earlier today, this was the moment that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was officially nominated as the Republican candidate for president of the United States.\par \par \uc2 Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 ERIC TRUMP, SON OF FORMER PRESIDENT TRUMP: On behalf of our entire family and on behalf of the 125 delegates in the unbelievable state of Florida, we hereby nominate every single one of them for the greatest president that's ever lived and that's \uc2 Donald J. Trump\uc2 , hereby declaring him the Republican nominee for president of the United States of America.\par \par \uc2 REP. MIKE JOHNSON (R-LA), SPEAKER OF THE HOUSE: Pursuant to rule 40D of the rules of the Republican Party, I formally declare President \uc2 Donald J. Trump\uc2  and JD Vance as the Republican nominees for president and vice president of the United States.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. It was a long difficult road but \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is now one step closer to winning his second term.\par \par \uc2 Joining us now \uc2 RNC\uc2  co-chair \uc2 Lara Trump\uc2  is with us.\par \par \uc2 You're not working hard at all. You're not putting long hours.\par \par \uc2 LARA TRUMP, RNC CO-CHAIR: We don't have a lot going on.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: We don't have a lot going. It's your father-in-law. I have been around you and your father-in-law. You have a great relationship, very special relationship.\par \par \uc2 L. TRUMP: Yes.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I've been around -- and Eric obviously who you married to this is his father and I did have a conversation with you guys after I'd been on the air on Saturday night.\par \par \uc2 L. TRUMP: Yeah.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: What was that like for you watching that, seeing that, not knowing. I -- when did you first hear he was going to be okay?\par \par \uc2 L. TRUMP: I mean, it's something we'll never forget and it felt like an eternity. We were watching in real time with our kids actually at home and --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: They saw it.\par \par \uc2 L. TRUMP: They saw that something was happening and I had to turn him away and distract them and the time before he got up, you know, felt like forever and it did take us a little while to confirm. Of course, we all saw the fist pump and that that meant a lot.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: That's now iconic.\par \par \uc2 L. TRUMP: It's iconic and I think it's so much larger than that moment, than that crowd, than even the people watching. It is -- it's a moment in history but it's very representative of this country. And I think \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  really represents this country because we've been through a lot.\par \par \uc2 We may feel knocked down and in a bad place but you can always get back up and the fact that he got back up in that moment and rallied back was incredible. But I'll tell you it was a very, very upsetting time for all of us in the family.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: It's a millimeter away, and your husband happens to be quite a good marksman.\par \par \uc2 L. TRUMP: Yeah.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I know that for a fact and Don Jr. as well.\par \par \uc2 Let me -- let me go to the issue. We're 115 days away. You've taken on this position as co-chair of the \uc2 RNC\uc2 , big, big position.\par \par \uc2 And I know I've asked you this before, so forgive the redundancy. You know the question I'm going to ask you. But we're 115 days away from Election Day. Early voting starts in Pennsylvania in 65 days, and then every other state rolls out.\par \par \uc2 And I've asked you often about early voting, voting by mail and, of course, legal ballot harvesting. Now I see the president, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , has been out there on the stump, vote early, vote by mail. He had resisted that, a lot of conservatives, Republicans have resisted that.\par \par \uc2 Are they resisting still or do you see movement?\par \par \uc2 L. TRUMP: I think we're seeing movement and I think it's really important, Sean, and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  himself said voting early, voting by mail or voting on election day are all great ways to vote. And the reality is if we all wait until Election Day, life happens. We saw that Kari Lake lost an election in Arizona because there were problems on election day, in a very Republican area, with the machines at a very specific location.\par \par \uc2 You can't wait. We want you to get your vote banked and then we want you to spend every moment from that day, all the way to election day, taking people to go vote. If we do not play the game the same way, we will not win.\par \par \uc2 We want to swamp the vote. We want to make it too big to rig. We have a huge election integrity operation, unlike anything we've ever seen at the \uc2 RNC\uc2 , unlike anything you've ever seen in this country.\par \par \uc2 We are ensuring that every legal vote is counted and our message to anyone out there who would decide to cheat in an election is if you cheat, or you are a non-citizen who illegally votes, we will find you, we'll track you down and we'll prosecute you to the full extent of the law.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: We just had the bill in Congress, the SAVE Act, that was passed by Republicans. It won't pass in the Senate.\par \par \uc2 Why is it -- why do you think that Democrats don't want people to have proof of citizenship? Why they resist voting ID? Why they would resist integrity measures, signature verification, updated voter rolls, chain of custody controls, and partisan observers watching in every precinct in the country the voting all day the vote counting all night? Why would they -- why would they resist that?\par \par \uc2 L. TRUMP: I can't imagine anyone who would not want more safeguards and more transparency in our electoral process and anyone who would not want to make it harder to cheat and easier to vote not wanting anything but cheating in an election. I can't rationalize it.\par \par \uc2 But what I can tell you is that from the \uc2 RNC\uc2 , it is our number one focus. We realize that things have not gone smoothly in the past. We are rectifying it every single day. We are going to secretaries of state, making sure they clean their voter rolls.\par \par \uc2 We are making sure the rules of the road are set up so that the first day of early voting every American feels confident in their vote and every American should.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: When did you know JD would be the choice?\par \par \uc2 L. TRUMP: I knew today.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Like me.\par \par \uc2 L. TRUMP: I knew today.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I'm like -- I said to your father-in-law last time he was on, I said you could really break a lot of news, if you just tell me right now, I didn't really have that much luck with it.\par \par \uc2 When do you speak?\par \par \uc2 L. TRUMP: I speak tomorrow night. I'm the last speaker here.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. We'll be looking forward to it we'll be live probably up here at the time. \uc2 Lara Trump\uc2 , you always generous with your time. Great to see you. Thank you for being with us.\par \par \uc2 L. TRUMP: Thank you.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: We appreciate it.\par \par \uc2 All right. Coming up, night one of the 2024 Republican National Convention fully underway. There's a lot of noise behind me. We expect to see President Trump here apparently at any moment. When that happens, we'll bring it to you live as we continue. We're in Milwaukee. Hannity on the road, \uc2 RNC\uc2 , thank you for being with FOX.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. This is a FOX News alert: former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is now in the building as night one of the \uc2 RNC\uc2  is underway. We expect he's going to be on that stage any moment now.\par \par \uc2 And joining us now, the governor of North Dakota, \uc2 Doug Burgum\uc2 , and South Carolina Senator Tim Scott are with us. Both names certainly finalists to be vice president. I spent a lot of time tonight with JD Vance.\par \par \uc2 What's that -- we've known each other a lot longer. We've known each other but what was that like for you at any moment that call may come and you knew that you were under consideration for that?\par \par \uc2 SEN. TIM SCOTT (R-SC): What an honor to have an opportunity to be considered to be vice president of the United States. I mean, this is the most exciting time in American history in many ways. We have a chance to reclaim the high ground for the American people, and knowing that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has the right mission, the right passion and frankly, I believe he's called to do what he's doing.\par \par \uc2 But to be a part of that process was exciting. It was fun. I love this country, only in this nation is my story possible. So having a chance to share the gospel with this entire nation, to share hope, to be an ambassador for the good things that this nation brings to the entire world, what a blessing.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And you're getting married soon. Now, I did keep you -- I knew his girlfriend way, way, way early like, when he started dating her, and I wasn't allowed to talk about her because you're like, man, I keep my life private.\par \par \uc2 You know, I didn't really know you well, Governor, but I've gotten to know you a lot better. What was it like for you to be -- it's a -- I would imagine a great honor to be under consideration. When did you find out for example that it wasn't you? How close did you think you got? You certainly were a finalist.\par \par \uc2 GOV. \uc2 DOUG BURGUM\uc2  (R), NORTH DAKOTA: Well, it was absolutely a great honor, Sean, but I think like a lot of Americans today, we weren't thinking about ourself. I mean, it's only been 48 hours since we're 1 millimeter away from chaos and mourning in our country, and here we are today celebrating the endorsement of a fantastic ticket with the Trump-Vance, and the focus has got to be now on winning in November.\par \par \uc2 I mean, with -- there's a lot of good things, great lawsuit, victory this morning for President Trump, but we got some work to do between now and November.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: It certainly was an amazing ruling which by the way is something I believed in when -- the Mueller appointment. I didn't believe it was in any way constitutional. I was -- I thought it was the perfect right and the perfect and right ruling.\par \par \uc2 You know, we now have live in America where our Department of Justice has been weaponized. You see what has happened, and we also learned something else. I mean, the big shock and surprise after the debate over Joe's cognitive abilities, really? Has anybody -- have you ever seen my show? Because I've shown a lot of those videos for four years.\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: A hundred percent. The national media has been covering for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  for years, and finally, it came to light. The American people are frustrated with a media that is an extension of the Democrat Party. It is devastating to the average person in this country to wake up to the reality that for years they've been lied to.\par \par \uc2 And at the same time, the same media has been engaged in character assassination of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Well, you know what? They didn't care about the phony evaluation of Mar-a-Lago. They didn't care about a statute limitations issue with the misdemeanor in New York upgraded eight years later, a legal NDA done by a lawyer, labeled as a legal expense. They didn't care about 51 former intel officials lying to the people of this country before an election and they knew nothing about that laptop.\par \par \uc2 They didn't care about four FISA warrants based on a dirty Russian disinformation dossier of Hillary Clinton or the double standard. \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2 , \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  had top secret classified information.\par \par \uc2 Governor, they didn't go after and invade their homes the way they did \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 BURGUM: No, they certainly didn't and of course now we know that Vice President Harris was a co-conspirator and completely, completely complicit in this cover up of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , and I think \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's been a national security risk for our country for some time and he still is today. And I think that's the biggest -- the biggest cover up we've ever actually seen is where the media and the White House essentially lying to the American people.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You know, I think one thing that might come out of all of this the process that you guys have been through. And I'm -- I'm sure there probably bit of an emotional roller coaster for you both, is that America's gotten to know both of you and I've got to imagine, knowing President Trump pretty well, I've known him for 30 years, that you are both going to get phone calls, maybe to get other jobs.\par \par \uc2 I'm not so sure I want either one of you to leave your jobs because you're good at it. Would you do it though? Would you consider it?\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: You know, I've been saying the entire time, it's not the who, it's the what it's President Trump's agenda that matters, everything that we can do to make sure that the American people get four more years of, frankly, low unemployment, high enthusiasm, closing our southern border, whatever I can do to be a part of that process, sign me up.\par \par \uc2 BURGUM: And, Sean, as you know, I have 152 days left in the greatest job in the world being governor of the great state of North Dakota. So we're going to make sure we're focusing on that and getting President Trump elected. As I've said all along, I was never in this for a job, a cabinet position, the vice president role.\par \par \uc2 This was to support President Trump and because \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  was wrong on the economy, he's wrong on energy, and he's wrong on national security, including the border, and in a state like ours, we're affected by that every single day. And the policies that he's driving here, the united Republican Party, the Trump-Vance ticket, what these policies will lift every American, Democrat, independent, Republican are all going to get lifted up.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I'll say this, you two -- I don't think I would ever be considered to get the position of federal dog catcher.\par \par \uc2 Good to see you both.\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: Thank you.\par \par \uc2 BURGUM: Thank you, Sean.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Coming up, more live coverage from the \uc2 RNC\uc2 . We are expecting \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  himself at any moment. Jim Jordan is next as we continue from Milwaukee. Thanks for being with us.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. We continue with live coverage from night one of the \uc2 RNC\uc2  in Milwaukee, Wisconsin. So we expect President Trump, he will be making an appearance any moment. That happens, we'll bring it to you.\par \par \uc2 Joining us now, chairman of the all powerful House Judiciary Committee, good friend of the program, Congressman Jim Jordan.\par \par \uc2 Congressman, how are you?\par \par \uc2 REP. JIM JORDAN (R-OH): I'm just fine, brother. Good day for our team.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: -- texting me, it's hard to hear because all the noise in this building. It's pretty electric.\par \par \uc2 JD was on. We had a long interview.\par \par \uc2 JORDAN: Yeah.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I didn't know him as well.\par \par \uc2 JORDAN: No.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And then I finally said let me watch the movie.\par \par \uc2 JORDAN: Yeah.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: What a life.\par \par \uc2 JORDAN: Read the book. I mean, it's fascinating what he went through, his experience and he is so impressive with -- you know, never hurts to have smart people in charge and JD is one smart guy, great communicator.\par \par \uc2 I saw him on "Meet the Press" where the bad guys were coming after him a week ago, he knocked it out of the park. So, yeah, he's great pick. We're excited.\par \par \uc2 HANNTY: Think about this. Appalachia, poor.\par \par \uc2 JORDAN: Yeah.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Grows up, mother, alcoholic, drug addict, father in jail, then makes it to the Marine Corps. Then to Ohio state, right? Okay, and then to Yale. He thrives at Yale.\par \par \uc2 From Yale, he's a really successful businessman, senator.\par \par \uc2 JORDAN: Yeah.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And here he is.\par \par \uc2 JORDAN: It's -- it's a great country.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Can it happen anywhere else but America?\par \par \uc2 JORDAN: It's a great country where a young man from humble, humble surroundings like that can -- can be I think the next vice president of the greatest nation in history and it's again I think a testament to President Trump that he sees that, he sees what you saw in that interview, that 30- minute interview that went so well. He sees that and this is -- this is why this ticket and this place is so energized.\par \par \uc2 HANNTY: Yeah.\par \par \uc2 JORDAN: And you add that to what happened Saturday, where President Trump - - that that triple fist pump after this assassin tried to take out a great man, a great president, and the energy, the American people can feel it and they know change is coming back to the good days when President Trump was in office before.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: What really struck me once I got over the shock, that I first thought -- I thought they killed him. That was my first thought. And I've known him 30 years.\par \par \uc2 JORDAN: Yeah.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: We both have personal relationship, in a professional relationship and I thought they killed him. And then he got up and he threw that fist hard.\par \par \uc2 JORDAN: Yeah.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And he did it twice when he's getting in the car and what a comparison.\par \par \uc2 Here we go -- \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is making his way. You can see that he has from the shooting, his ear was pierced. He does have that right -- it was -- his ear pierced.\par \par \uc2 JORDAN: Yeah, I lost --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is in the building. You can't tell about the crowd noise though at all.\par \par \uc2 Wow, how iconic when we look back after the election, assuming if he wins, what will Saturday mean to this when he got up --\par \par \uc2 JORDAN: Yeah.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: What will that part mean?\par \par \uc2 JORDAN: Yeah. My -- my old -- my old college coach used to talk about moments of magnitude in your life, in your -- in the season. This is a moment magnitude Saturday for the whole country where he had that leadership literally under fire.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: He literally just pointed to his ear. He's got what looks like a mostly full gauze pad on the ear. You could see his daughter Tiffany with her husband, but this crowd just lit up big time. Every -- I'm just looking out right now and I see everybody in the reaction of the crowd.\par \par \uc2 My understanding is Speaker Mike Johnson is also with him or was just with him. So it's obviously going to get very, very interesting. I wish I could stay on the air for another five hours but I don't think I can.\par \par \uc2 Anyway, we're going to have to -- \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will be coming out any second. Stay with FOX News and our continuing coverage right here on the FOX News Channel.\par \par \uc2 Set your DVR. Never ever miss an episode. In the meantime, let not your heart be troubled. Bret and Martha, take it from here.\par \par \uc2 Bret, Martha, take it away.\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2024 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2024 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document SHAN000020240716ek7f00001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 Federal Judge Dismisses \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  Classified Documents Case; \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  Names Ohio Senator As Running Mate; Donald Trump-J. D. Vance Republican Ticket Solidified At Convention; Trump In Milwaukee After Assassination Attempt; Investigation Into Trump Assassination Attempt; Secret Service Faces Questions; Rooftop Access; Biden Resists Effort To Replace Him; Republican National Convention Underway In Milwaukee, Wisconsin; Media Coverage Of Presidential Race After Assassination Attempt On \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  Examined; Previously Republican Presidential Candidate Debate In Milwaukee Reviewed; President Biden Apologies For Some Rhetoric About \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  In Wake Of Assassination Attempt; Secret Service Director Kimberly Cheatle Says She Will Remain In Her Position Despite Assassination Attempt On \uc2 Donald Trump\b0\par\par\uc2 Bret Baier, Aishah Hasnie, Mark Meredith, Brit Hume, Trey Gowdy,  Katie Pavlich, Josh Kraushar, David Spunt, Jacqui Henrich, Howard Kurtz,  Josh Kraushaar \par \uc2 8,117 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 July 2024\par \uc2 Fox News: Special Report with Brett Baier\par \uc2 FNSPBB\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2024 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2024 ASC Services II Media, LLC.  All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 JESSICA TARLOV, FOX NEWS CHANNEL CONTRIBUTOR: So, that's all of us there and with my mom on Mother's Day, lots of estrogen happening at the house. Yes, but it's been great and --\par \par \uc2 DANA PERINO, FOX NEWS CHANNEL HOST: Congratulations. Wonderful.\par \par \uc2 JEANINE PIRRO, FOX NEWS CHANNEL LEGAL ANALYST: Yes, it's wonderful.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Jesse, do you have one quick comment?\par \par \uc2 JESSE WATTERS, FOX NEWS CHANNEL HOST: Sure. Tonight, Vivek, Jeanine Pirro and \uc2 Larry Kudlow\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 PERINO: All right, that's it for us. Have a great night, everyone.\par \par \uc2 BRET BAIER, FOX NEWS CHANNEL HOST: Congratulations, Jessica.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: Thank you so much.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: All right. Hi, Dana, thanks.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Have a good show.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Good evening. I'm Bret Baier. We are coming to you tonight from Milwaukee, Wisconsin inside of this week's Republican National Convention. We're covering several major stories at this hour.\par \par \uc2 Newly anointed Republican presidential nominee \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has selected Ohio Senator J. D. Vance as his running mate.\par \par \uc2 Meantime, a federal judge in Florida has dismissed the classified documents case against the former president. The judge ruling the appointment of Special Counsel Jack Smith was unconstitutional. Smith says he will appeal that according to the Justice Department.\par \par \uc2 The former president telling me today he's thrilled with the ruling and, "Is having a great week, blessed to be alive after the assassination attempts Saturday."\par \par \uc2 Those are some of his first public comments since the shooting in Pennsylvania, which resulted in a wound to the former president's ear, the death of one spectator and injuries to two others.\par \par \uc2 The shooter was killed by Secret Service snipers, and there has been a major development in the investigation today. We'll bring you that.\par \par \uc2 But first up, the opening hours of the 2024 \uc2 RNC\uc2  convention. Congressional Correspondent Aishah Hasnie starts us off live from the convention floor. Good evening, Aishah.\par \par \uc2 AISHAH HASNIE, FOX NEWS CHANNEL CONGRESSIONAL CORRESPONDENT: Bret, good evening to you. Trump's V.P. announcement really fired up the crowd here on the convention floor. I want to show you this as someone took some lipstick and wrote J. D. Vance's name right underneath Trump.\par \par \uc2 So, this actually might be the first signage of this ticket for the season. The freshman senator from Ohio beating out a slew of candidates with much more experience but in the end, he was the favorite of the former president.\par \par \uc2 Now, Vance brings in youth, he brings in blue collar appeal, thanks to his best-selling memoir, Hillbilly Elegy.\par \par \uc2 Now, supporters say he can help Trump with those Rust Belt states. But he lacks political experience which Don Jr., who was a big fan of Vance has told us earlier today is exactly the reason why this will be a winning ticket.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HASNIE: Not enough exe --\par \par \uc2 DON TRUMP JR\uc2 ., SON OF FORMER PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP: Zero political experience.\par \par \uc2 HASNIE: True.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP JR.: He wants peace deals in the Middle East. The greatest job economy in the world, incredible prosperity for everyone with no experience.\par \par \uc2 If experience is a marker for Washington, D.C. politics. It's a bad one. They're in positions of power because they've had tenure, not because they actually know anything about what they're sharing.\par \par \uc2 If experience in politics is anything, I don't think it's very important at all, frankly.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HASNIE: Now, Trump's good fortune continued beyond the convention stage today, a federal judge dismissing the special counsel prosecution over Trump's handling of classified documents. That's the Mar-a-Lago case, the judge ruled Jack Smith's appointment by Attorney General Garland was unconstitutional because his special counsel was never confirmed to the job by Congress. That's important.\par \par \uc2 Trump said that he is thrilled by the ruling but also blasted the separate election interference case, which may also now be dismissed.\par \par \uc2 A spokesman for special counsel Jack Smith's office said today to Fox, the dismissal of the case deviates from the uniform conclusion of all previous courts, to have considered the issue of the attorney general is statutorily authorized to appoint a special counsel. The Justice Department has authorized the special counsel to appeal the court's order.\par \par \uc2 Now, back here in Milwaukee, Bret, the president was officially nominated as the GOP nominee today, Florida's delegates and his families as being the delegates getting him across the finish line today. Now he is preparing for his big speech on Thursday, and as you know very well after talking to him, that he's completely changing the tone and the message focusing on uniting the party and uniting the country, Bret.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: That's what he says. Aishah, thanks.\par \par \uc2 Former President Trump has a new apprentice. He has selected Ohio Senator J. D. Vance as his running mate. The Marine Corps veteran, father of three has some pop culture value, he authored a best-selling book based on his life growing up poor that eventually became a movie and in an election featuring two men approaching over 80 years old, Vance is young. Hes a young addition at just 39 years old.\par \par \uc2 Correspondent Mark Meredith has a closer look at the winner of the Veepstakes.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 MARK MEREDITH, FOX NEWS CHANNEL CORRESPONDENT (voice over): An Ohio native whose life story became the best seller and movie Hillbilly Elegy Senator J. D. Vance has a new title vice presidential candidate.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: I am proud to announce that Senator J. D. Vance has the overwhelming support of this convention to be the next Vice President of the United States.\par \par \uc2 MEREDITH (voice over): Before politics and even college, Dan spent four years in the Marines serving in Iraq, later earning an undergrad degree from Ohio State and a law degree from Yale.\par \par \uc2 SEN. J.D. VANCE (R), U.S. VICE PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE: God bless you guys. And thank you.\par \par \uc2 MEREDITH (voice over): Vance, who turns 40 next month was once a critic of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  telling a journalist in 2016, "I'm a Never Trump guy."\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Do we love this guy?\par \par \uc2 MEREDITH (voice over): But after Trump's shocking win in 2016, Vance embrace the MAGA movement, even winning Trump's support for his own Senate bid in 2022.\par \par \uc2 VANCE: I'm excited about the ticket. And I'm excited about what this means for America in the years to come.\par \par \uc2 REP. KEVIN MCCARTHY (R-CA): After being a Marine, he also knows the challenges when it comes to drugs. He knows what it is to rural areas get wiped out from jobs, kind of the American first policy. So -- and he brings you to it at the same time.\par \par \uc2 BEN CARSON, FORMER HOUSING AND URBAN DEVELOPMENT SECRETARY: I think he'll be a very good pick. He's very articulate. He's very smart. He's young, he's energetic.\par \par \uc2 MEREDITH (voice over): Vance has a close relationship with \uc2 Donald Trump Jr.\uc2  But some believe remains a wildcard considering his short tenure in Congress.\par \par \uc2 But Trump's decision now catapults fans to a new era of GOP politics, and depending on November's results, also to the White House.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 MEREDITH (on camera): Fox has learned that Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has reached out by phone to Senator Vance to congratulate him on this post. We're also waiting to see whether or not the two of them may to get together for a televised debate, that has still been up in the air.\par \par \uc2 And while of course, the spotlight is on Vance tonight. He's also going to be on his wife and his three kids. And there is a very closely watched Senate race in Ohio already. It's not Vance's seat. Instead, you got Democrat \uc2 Sherrod Brown\uc2  fighting for his political life this fall. And we could see whether or not there's a new turnout because of Vance being on the ticket in that state, which could have an impact on the balance of power in Washington, Bret.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Mark, thank you. Fox News, by the way, offered to a V.P. debate that the former president accepted on behalf of his nominee. We'll see what go - - where that goes from here.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Could you imagine yourself behind the resolute desk as president?\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Well, look, Bret, I think that's ultimately, that's \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's choice.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Are you ready to be president on day one?\par \par \uc2 VANCE: If Trump picks up the phone and calls you, the first sort of thought you have to have with yourself is not just could I be vice president, but could I stand ultimately in the big chair?\par \par \uc2 And look, if he asked me, I'll think about it, but I think the answer is yes.\par \par \uc2 I know Trump very well. I like him. He's in very good health. And so, I think whoever he selects as vice president is going to have a real opportunity to be very good vice president for the country for the next four years.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Senator J. D. Vance, now the vice presidential nominee and former President Trump talking to Harris Faulkner, this is just hours before he leaves from Butler, Pennsylvania. He said this about his choice.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 DONALD TRUMP\uc2  (R), U.S. PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE: I don't want to belittle it, because it's very important position, especially if something bad should happen. But it's just -- that's the most important if something bad should happen.\par \par \uc2 There was one time as students of this you and I are. Lyndon Johnson helped a lot with Illinois, but that was a different kind of a help. He was a -- he was a wheeler dealer.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Again, just hours before the assassination attempt in Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 Let's bring in our panel, Fox News Chief Political Analyst Brit Hume, \uc2 Trey Gowdy\uc2 , former congressman from South Carolina, Katie Pavlich News editor at Townhall.com and Josh Kraushar our Fox News radio political analyst.\par \par \uc2 Brit, let me start with you digesting this J. D. Vance choice and what it means for the campaign, what it means for the former president.\par \par \uc2 BRIT HUME, FOX NEWS SENIOR POLITICAL ANALYST: Well, you can kind of see why Trump made the choice he did. young, dynamic guy, very bright, dazzlingly articulate, he can -- I'm sure he pictured him in a debate with \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and having no trouble with the competition.\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, you know, if you're looking at this as someone who might be reluctant to vote for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , and we're looking for reassurance that everything would be OK if this old -- you know, saying after this old man, which we learned over the weekend, it certainly can.\par \par \uc2 And we're learning that -- and we learned about, you know, what kind of shape a president can be in after a few years in office when we saw \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's condition.\par \par \uc2 I'm not sure this is that reassuring a choice. I mean, he's 39 years old. Yes, he's very smart, but his inexperience is real.\par \par \uc2 Don Jr. is wrong when he says that experience is not a -- is not important. It's very important. And he has very little of it. And it makes -- and people looking at him and saying, is this guy a plausible president? You can argue that he is but I think you could also very well argue that he's not.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: He may, Katie, be the pit bull that former President Trump wants in order to make maybe a pivot on the stage behind this Thursday night towards the unifying message, we'll see.\par \par \uc2 KATIE PAVLICH, FOX NEWS CHANNEL CONTRIBUTOR: Well, the argument up into this point for Vance has been that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  wanted someone who could carry the MAGA legacy on through '28, hoping to continue the evolving nature of the Republican Party, that certainly does this.\par \par \uc2 I will disagree slightly on the issue of people being skeptical of voting for president Trump as a result of not picking someone outside the MAGA movement per se. That is true that he needs independence and people who maybe would have voted for the Trump ticket given a certain V.P. pick, but the Trump team is still picking off people in coalitions that Biden and Democrats have typically been able to lock down earlier.\par \par \uc2 Those people are still up for grabs and J. D. Vance can go into Pennsylvania, Michigan, Wisconsin, and he can be a wrecking ball in those blue states given this is his national natural language given his own personal story.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Yes, rustbelt Josh, also, you know, he's a Marine, a Catholic, a father of four. The Democrats, however seem like they're happy with this choice. This is the Biden-Harris campaign chair.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  picked J. D. Vance as his running mate, because Vance will do what \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  wouldn't do on January 6th, bend over backwards to enable Trump and his extreme MAGA agenda, even if it means breaking the law. And no matter the harm to the American people.\par \par \uc2 JOSH KRAUSHAAR, FOX NEWS RADIO POLITICAL ANALYST: This is the pick you make when you're feeling confident about your chances