out the massive security breach, you know, it's shocking.\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 HUME: Yes, yes. And what do they mean by independent investigation? Independent of whom? Who's going to carry out this independent investigation? The \uc2 FBI\uc2 , part of the executive branch under \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , presided over by an attorney general who is a Cabinet mate of Alejandro Mayorkas?\par \par \uc2 I mean, what it is -- it's a good thing Congress is investigating, because I think we'd have to be skeptical of a -- of a -- of a -- investigation carried out by the executive branch.\par \par \uc2 PAVLICH: Well, Mayorkas said today, he has 100 percent confidence in the Secret Service head. So, we'll see if they fire anyone.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: We will see. We have some new developments on that. David Spunt on that in a second. Panel, thanks. We'll see you in a bit.\par \par \uc2 Stocks were up today. The Dow surging. 211 for a new record close. The S&P 500 gained 16. The NASDAQ jumped 74. As Federal Reserve Chair \uc2 Jerome Powell\uc2 , says the Fed will not wait until inflation falls to two percent before cutting interest rates. The markets loved that.\par \par \uc2 Up next, a major development in the investigation, as we said, into the assassination attempt on former President Trump. And later, we go live to the White House, where President Biden has just recorded another network interview as he tries to salvage his endangered candidacy.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 BAIER: \uc2 FBI\uc2  technicians are learning new information tonight about the man identified as the shooter during the Trump assassination attempt, Saturday. We are still waiting for investigators to give us a motive behind the actions of 20-year-old Thomas Matthew Crooks.\par \par \uc2 Correspondent David Spunt is following the story from the justice department tonight. Good evening, David.\par \par \uc2 DAVID SPUNT, FOX NEWS CHANNEL CORRESPONDENT: Hi, Bret. Good eveni