dn't just send it to the states only. It's not a states only issue. It's a moral issue.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: That debate is still playing out as the Republican committee released its platform which states that the party, quote, "will oppose late term abortion." Conservatives like former vice president \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  called the stance a profound disappointment.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : The abortion issue is much simplified right now because I brought it out by getting rid of Roe v. Wade.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: The platform also lacks details over the future of aid for Ukraine, an issue Republicans have been debates for the past year.\par \par \uc2 You would not support an increase of funding to Ukraine?\par \par \uc2 VIVEK RAMASWAMY\uc2 , (R) FORMER PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE: I would not. I think that we have to put the interests of Americans first.\par \par \uc2 HALEY: First of all, the American president needs to have moral clarity. When you look at the situation with Russia and Ukraine, here you have a pro-American country that was invaded by a thug. So when you want to talk about what has been given to you Ukraine, less than three-and-a-half percent of our defense budget has been given to Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: If fiscal year 2023, the \uc2 Congressional Research Service\uc2  estimated about $27 billion in security assistance went to Ukraine. For fiscal year 24 Congress has allotted about $9.7 billion so far, making up 1.1 percent of the defense budget.\par \par \uc2 HALEY: Sending weapons to Ukraine and Israel isn't foreign aid. It's an investment in the world.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : Every time that Zelenskyy comes to this country, he walks away with $60 billion. He is the greatest salesman ever.\par \par \uc2 The European nations together have spent $100 billion or maybe more than that, less than us. Why doesn't he call them and say you got to put up your money?\par \par \uc2 BAIER: The party remains united on one thing heading into this November's election rematch.\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: Best thing \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  can do for America on the global stage, stay off of it.\par \par \uc2 HALEY: Biden has been a catastrophe.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : He is the worst, he is the most corrupt, the most incompetent president in the history of our country. And we have to take it back from that party, that's an evil party.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO TAPE)\par \par \uc2 BAIER: And now that party here, gathered in the convention floor, seems galvanized behind the former president as they wait to see the ticket together on the stage. Trump-Vance is the ticket.\par \par \uc2 Up next, the panel measures the GOP ticket versus the Democrats. But, first, Milwaukee and beer, well, that goes back a long way.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Wisconsin is known for a few things. One of them is beer. The \uc2 Miller Brewing Company\uc2  here in Milwaukee, they started to making that famous beer with a unique yeast in 1855. And the abundant farmland here in Wisconsin for the barley and hops, the ample water supply made Wisconsin a big beer state. Now the former president doesn't drink, but there will be a lot of beer consumed at the \uc2 RNC\uc2  this week.\par \par \uc2 SPECIAL REPORT continues after this.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 LESTER HOLT, JOURNALIST: Have you taken a step back and done a little soul- searching on things you may have said that could incite people who are not balanced?\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 , (D) PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: Well, I don't think -- look, how do you talk about the threat to democracy, which is real, when a president says things like he says? Do you just not say anything because it may incite somebody? Look, I -- I have not engaged in that rhetoric.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BAIER: But, pressed in this interview by Lester Holt about the use of putting Trump in a bullseye, the president then stepped back from that and said that was a mistake.\par \par \uc2 Also, in this interview, he said he still hasn't watched the entire debate. He says he has seen pieces of it. He also said that inflation was nine percent when he took office. It actually was 1.4 percent.\par \par \uc2 More from this interview. We're back with our panel, Josh, Trey, Katie, and Brit. Brit, these interviews don't seem to be helping President Biden.\par \par \uc2 HUME: I don't think they really had much of a chance to help him because I think the impression left by that debate and countless other incidents that preceded it that the public noticed but the media seemed not to, or much of the media seemed not to, I think it's indelible. And look, the reason why the guy makes these mistakes he can't help making them. So that's where he is. This is a real Biden. So, you see these blunders. He says things that are false, repeats them, blunders, says the wrong word and so on. This, alas, is who he is.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: We should point out the band is back. We've got some good tunes going in behind us as they get ready to restart the convention here in the evening. Josh, there is still a really precarious point here for the Democrats.\par \par \uc2 KRAUSHAAR: Look, I thought it was notable that he apologized. He said he made a mistake by using the rhetoric of putting Trump in a bullseye, because, look, a lot of Democrats don't know how to attack Trump right now. They know that some of their overheated rhetoric about the end of democracy, fascism, they can't use that playbook anymore. They realize that they went too far, and that's not politically tenable right now.\par \par \uc2 And I thought the fact that Biden is stepping back is a good sign for the country for the health of our democracy, but it's also a limit to their political playbook. Biden is running as the head of the anti-Trump coalition. And if you don't have the glue that holds that together, it's a political problem for the White House.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Trey, it's a step back now, but he's back on the campaign trail. This is a go-to line, the threat to democracy, all that stuff is going to be back in the repertoire.\par \par \uc2 GOWDY: Yes, well, it's that. Do you remember the press conference he had in what looked like Satan's house? It was a red background where he was talking about threats to democracy, that he might not leave office if Trump wins again, the mischaracterization of the Georgia voting law. I mean, I'm glad he apologized, but he should apologize for more than just that one comment. He has been doing it for three years.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Katie, is there a chance that now still Democrats are trying to find a way to get him off the ballot?\par \par \uc2 PAVLICH: There is always a chance. But their time is very limited. And you have a number of Democrats saying that the effort to get him off the ballot is dead for now, anyway, because of what happened over the weekend.\par \par \uc2 But, for a long time the Biden campaign has really been trying to reach for different things then can throw against the Trump campaign. Now after the weekend you have President Biden trying to coalesce around this unity message when it's not just that je's gone after \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and said he's a threat to democracy, fascism, he's an existential threat to the country. It's also called anybody who voted for him a MAGA extremist. So it's very difficult for people, I think, to accept his record of this and then to just try and turn around while he's flailing and trying to save his candidacy and his first term in office to say all of a sudden that he is the unity candidate against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Some of these ads are writing themselves, Brit. This Trump-Vance ticket could use the \uc2 George Clooney\uc2  letter saying why he should not be the nominee as an ad.\par \par \uc2 HUME: Yes, I think that's right. The question is, at this stage, how many voters who were not already yesterday to give up on Biden because of this senility will be swayed by ads about that? Obviously, you populate some of your ads with Trump showing who and what is he now. The Democrats are going to depend, as I think Trey has suggested and you have, as well, Bret, that this threat to democracy line which they've been peddling now since January 6th, 2021, is going to be a big part of the campaign.\par \par \uc2 I think it is almost complete B.S. I really do. I think it's a reprehensible message. I think it is the kind of thing that would inspire somebody to be violent because if it was really true, it would be something very much for people to worry about. I don't think it is. We keep hearing democracy is on the ballot. Baloney. Democracy is the ballot. And that is the method that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is choosing now to try to return to power. It doesn't sound like a threat to democracy to me. It sounds like participation in democracy.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: All right, more with the panel after a quick break.\par \par \uc2 But first, as we head to break, a look at piece of world history that's made its way right here to Milwaukee.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BAIER: We're on the campus of \uc2 Marquette University\uc2 , and this is the St. Joan of Arc Chapel. It was built in France in 1420 and was visited by St. Joan of Arc. This building was moved to New York in the 1900s and then finally here to Marquette in the 1960s. A lot of history in this building. The \uc2 RNC\uc2  is trying to make history in Milwaukee this week.\par \par \uc2 SPECIAL REPORT continues after this.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 KIMBERLY CHEATLE, SECRET SERVICE DIRECTOR: What I would say is the Secret Service responsible for the protection of the former president.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: So the buck stops with you?\par \par \uc2 CHEATLE: The buck stops with me. I am the director of the Secret Service. It was unacceptable, and it's something that shouldn't happen again.\par \par \uc2 We are going to continue to be transparent and communicate with people.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Do you plan to stay on, absolutely?\par \par \uc2 CHEATLE: I do plan to stay on.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Secret Service Director Kimberly Cheatle talking about the shooting, the attempted assassination of former President Trump, saying she will stay on, or at least she says she will.\par \par \uc2 We're back with the panel. Trey, I don't know, if the buck stops with her, this was horrible, horrible effort at protecting the former president.\par \par \uc2 GOWDY: Bret, I'm not a security expert, but I would think a rooftop would be one of the first places you looked if you were trying to protect a speaker. I don't see how she survives this.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Josh, we talked about it earlier. There is this video out there with people shouting, there's gay on the roof. And you see him actually shimmying up with a rifle on that spot.\par \par \uc2 KRAUSHAAR: It's remarkable that there was over a minute where there were attendees pointing to the shooter, and took that long for anyone to spot him. Look, Capitol Hill is going to be conducting an investigation. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  does not like to fire cabinet officials, but this would be in his political benefit to send a message to the country.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Brit?\par \par \uc2 HUME: It seems to me that we live in a society now where people don't take full responsibility for what's happened. I take responsibility, the buck stops with me, but I'm staying in my job. After a failure that catastrophic, could nearly have been even worse, I don't see how she survives. I don't know why she would try. And I don't know how Alejandro Mayorkas, with the legion of failures that occurred with him with immigration, what he is still doing there, either.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Katie?\par \par \uc2 PAVLICH: Another example in a long list of things, of catastrophic failures that the Biden administration, President Biden in particular, could fire her. And there's no accountability for a number of these things. And so it really begs the question whether there will be real accountability for this at all. I was talking to a security guard, one of our wonderful security guards. He said any time your principle gets shot in the face, it's a big f for anyone. And the fact that she is saying she's staying on board, she should resign.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: All right, panel, thanks. Thanks for getting through the band. Some good tunes, but tough to hear sometimes.\par \par \uc2 Tomorrow on SPECIAL REPORT, day two of the Republican convention. President Biden resumes his campaigning following his pause due do the Trump assassination attempt.\par \par \uc2 Tonight J.D. Vance talks with \uc2 Sean Hannity\uc2 , 9:00 p.m. eastern time for that exclusive.\par \par \uc2 Thanks for inviting us into your home tonight. That's it for this SPECIAL REPORT, fair, balanced, and unafraid. Special coverage of the convention tonight at 10:00 p.m. THE INGRAHAM ANGLE is now.\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2024 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2024 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document FNSPBB0020240716ek7f00001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 J. D. Vance Accepts \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  V.P. Nomination; \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  Wins GOP Nomination, J. D. Vance Named V.P. Pick; Violent Rhetoric: Media Keeps Bias On Full Display After Trump Shooting; Biden: Mistake To Say Bullseye To Discuss Trump: Secret Service Failure: Agency Slammed After Attempted Trump Assassination; Democrats Back Off Biden After Trump Shooting\b0\par\par\uc2 Dana Perino, Jessica Tarlov, Greg Gutfeld, Jesse Watters, Jeanine  Pirro \par \uc2 8,691 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 July 2024\par \uc2 Fox News: The Five\par \uc2 FOXFIV\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2024 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2024 ASC Services II Media, LLC.  All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 LT. GOV. JON HUSTED (R-OH): He must share the values and principles of our presidential nominee and be trusted to faithfully implement the will of the people. J. D. Vance is such a man.\par \par \uc2 DANA PERINO, FOX NEWS CHANNEL HOST: And welcome into THE FIVE. We are about to see J. D. Vance nominated to be the vice presidential candidate, we want to listen in here.\par \par \uc2 HUSTED: A man who loves America and will represent our people with moral courage, strength and honor. J. D. is a living embodiment of the American dream. He came from humble beginnings and even as his life took him to places he might have never imagined. He never forgot where he came from, Ohio values are in his blood.\par \par \uc2 He served our nation in the \uc2 United States Marine Corps\uc2 . He is a graduate of the \uc2 Ohio State University\uc2 . He graduated summa cum laude from Yale Law School and is the author of the best-selling book Hillbilly Elegy. And he is a crusader for the people of the Ohio in the \uc2 United States Senate\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 He has never forgotten the working people of our country, and he never will. He fought to bring investment to middle America as a businessman and has fought to defend them every single day in the Senate.\par \par \uc2 In this I know -- this I know, he will faithfully stand by President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's side as they win this election and change the course of our nation.\par \par \uc2 They will change the course of our nation to the benefit of all American citizens and truly make our country great again.\par \par \uc2 It is therefore my honor to nominate Ohio Senator J. D. Vance for the office of Vice President of the United States of America.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Delegates and alternates pursuant to rule 40A, a motion to nominate by acclamation is now in order. The chair now recognizes delegate \uc2 Bernie Moreno\uc2  Senate candidate from Ohio for the purpose of making a motion.\par \par \uc2 BERNIE MORENO\uc2  (R), SENATORIAL CANDIDATE OF OHIO: Thank you, Madam Chair. My name is Bernie Marino. I'm honored to be the Republican nominee for the \uc2 U.S. Senate\uc2  from the great state of Ohio.\par \par \uc2 I know firsthand that my dear friend J. D. is a selfless and brilliant fighter. He is a patriot who loves America. He loves Ohio. He loves his family. He's a great father. He's a great man. And that's what we need in this nation today.\par \par \uc2 The J. D. Vance America First is not just a slogan. It's his North Star. He has followed in every moment of his life and career. He knows what it's like to live in poverty, forgotten by Washington politicians. He is dedicated to ensure that no American is ever forgotten again.\par \par \uc2 Madam Chair, it is a great honor to move that J. D. Vance be nominated by acclamation by this Republican National Convention as its candidate for the office of Vice President of the United States of America.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Without objection, the previous question is order. The question is on the motion that Senator J. D. Vance be nominated by acclamation. All those in favor signify by saying aye. All those opposed signify by saying no.\par \par \uc2 In the opinion of the Chair, the ayes have it and the motion is adopted, without objection, the motion to reconsider is laid upon the table.\par \par \uc2 Delegates and alternates. Ladies and gentleman, I am proud to announce that Senator J. D. Vance has the overwhelming support of this convention to be the next Vice President of the United States.\par \par \uc2 The chair is pleased to make the following appointments to the escort committee for Senator J. D. Vance, his vice presidential nominee Usha Vance, thank you and God bless America.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Listen, gentlemen, please welcome back speaker Johnson.\par \par \uc2 REP. MIKE JOHNSON (R-LA): What a great night. Pursuant to rule 40D of the rules of the Republican Party, I formally declare President \uc2 Donald J. Trump\uc2  and J. D. Vance as the Republican nominees for President and Vice President of the United States.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Ladies and gentlemen, please welcome back \uc2 RNC\uc2  Chairman Michael Whatley.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL WHATLEY, RNC CHAIRMAN: What a great afternoon for the Republican Party and what a great afternoon for America.\par \par \uc2 It is now time to take the official convention photograph, if all of the delegates would please stand and turn to the center camera directly opposite the stage, we will take the official photograph.\par \par \uc2 Thank you delegates.\par \par \uc2 At this time, please welcome Leora Levy, delegate and National Committeewoman from Connecticut who will lead us in a benediction.\par \par \uc2 LEORA LEVY, DELEGATE AND NATIONAL COMMITTEE WOMAN FROM CONNECTICUT: Let us pray. That means be quiet. Bow your heads.\par \par \uc2 Heavenly Father, we thank you for the life and the strength of President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and pray that you continue to protect his family. We pray for Corey Comperatore and his family. May his memory always be a blessing. We pray for the two patriotic Americans who were wounded and for their speedy, complete recovery.\par \par \uc2 King of the universe, who knows all, sees all. Please watch over us as we embark on the work for which we have gathered here today. We are here to elect President \uc2 Donald J. Trump\uc2 , a leader with wisdom, strength, courage and the experience to repair what has been badly broken.\par \par \uc2 Lord, please bless the leaders of our great Republican Party. Bless President Trump. Vice President J. D. Vance, \uc2 RNC\uc2  Chairman Michael Whatley, co-Chairman \uc2 Lara Trump\uc2 , the delegates, alternates and guests gathered here today, as we work to make America Great Again.\par \par \uc2 May we remember your word in Deuteronomy 31:6, be strong and courageous. Do not be afraid because of them for the Lord your God goes with you. He will never leave nor forsake you.\par \par \uc2 Our Father in heaven, bless our exceptional country, the United States of America and all who stand vigilant to protect us, the members of our armed forces, police and first responders.\par \par \uc2 Oh Lord, our God, we pray for the peace of Jerusalem, your eternal city, and for all the children of Abraham. We remember and pray for freedom for the hostages kidnapped and held so cruelly against their will. Lord, please keep them in your sight and hasten the day of their freedom.\par \par \uc2 Lord, we have gathered here from different communities, cities, states and territories. Let us pray together united for our nation, the United States of America. May our prayers unite the American people to work together for the betterment of our nation and of the entire world.\par \par \uc2 May America be a light unto the nations and an emissary of clarity and leadership for the world.\par \par \uc2 Grant peace, goodness, blessing, Grace, loving kindness and mercy to us. Bless us, our father, all of us as one with the light of your face, amen.\par \par \uc2 WHATLEY: In a moment, we will recess until this evening session. This evening session will reconvene at approximately 5:45.\par \par \uc2 However, I will instruct delegates to please return to the hall at 5:30 p.m. in order to be in your seats by 5:45 p.m. I thank you for consideration.\par \par \uc2 The Chair declares that the 2024 Republican National Convention is in recess subject to the call of the chair.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: You have it, the \uc2 RNC\uc2  convention is underway. That was the Chairman Michael Whatley and we're excited to be here in Milwaukee. You got your whole five here.\par \par \uc2 Judge Jeanine Pirro, Jessica Tarlov back from her wonderful maternity leave, and we're so glad that you're here. And then there's Jesse Watters. Just kidding. Jesse Watters and Greg Gutfeld. So great to be here.\par \par \uc2 J. D. Vance announced as the vice presidential pick, not a huge surprise, since that had been out there for a while. We do expect him to speak at some point, we will keep you updated on as to when that will be.\par \par \uc2 So, four of us at this table, I've had a chance to tell you our thoughts about the \uc2 RNC\uc2  kickoff, the failed assassination attempt of President Trump and the V.P. pick but Greg Gutfeld has yet to give you a bit of his wisdom and his wit, so I turn it over to you sir, for the -- give me the floor here in Milwaukee.\par \par \uc2 GREG GUTFELD, FOX NEWS CHANNEL HOST: Well, I missed the whole thing. You know, so many things, this has probably been the last few days, probably the most unbelievable surreal moment in political history. I don't think there's any way to oversell it.\par \par \uc2 I do find it funny, watching people who call Trump a threat to democracy now wishing for his speedy recovery.\par \par \uc2 I mean, did people who fought Hitler wish him a speedy recovery after they attempted to kill him? No. Or could it be that they never really meant it to begin with and it was just words, stuff you say to when.\par \par \uc2 I almost respect the dogs not barking to \uc2 Joy Reid\uc2 , Madonna, Cher. Hollywood for once is biting its collective lip. Maybe they realize they went too far to walk it back with a hallmark greeting card.\par \par \uc2 But I think the Dems never understood the statistical possibility of demonic messaging, right? Say this stuff repetitively to 300 million people, there's going to be a few nutcases that act on it.\par \par \uc2 My feeling is the left doesn't know it goes too far until they go too far, it's always been about abolishing boundaries, from borders, to gender, to the nature of crime, to rhetoric, without any normal stopgap of moderate Democrats, they just keep going and keep going until you see what happens on Saturday.\par \par \uc2 The fact that \uc2 Joy Reid\uc2  protected her tweets, going underground, morning breath taken off the air to the mission that the boundaries were crossed. And even they realized that they themselves cannot be trusted. This is the drunk who actually hands over their own car keys.\par \par \uc2 And I think what we're seeing is what happens when you conflate boundaries with losing. It's not losing to surrender to limits, it's being a conscious human saying, you know, maybe we went too far. I'm looking for something that -- I'm just going to say. There was something you said, I don't know when it was a couple of days ago, Jesse said, like, why can't you just not win this one? Why can't -- why do you have to win everything?\par \par \uc2 And I go back to that thought, because it's like for Republicans, politics on the list of things that matter are below family, you know, work, religion, NASCAR, hunting, fishing, but for a lot of Democrats, it's personal, it's their life.\par \par \uc2 And so, they don't have any boundaries when it comes to the things that they say.\par \par \uc2 You know, I'm not saying that they caused this thing. What I'm saying is that it's assassination by amplification. You can't -- you don't call somebody Hitler in the hopes that they don't get killed, right? You don't demonize somebody hoping that they get flowers sent to them. You do this because you have a desire to win it at all costs.\par \par \uc2 And now you've seen what happens. And now you have people saying, you know what, maybe we should dial it back a bit, dial it back a bit. I think it was on "The View." They said we need to lower the temperature. And they are nothing more than arsonists who aren't aware of the actual work they've done. They've raised the temperature every day. They are a threat to democracy, a threat to democracy.\par \par \uc2 I don't know what's worse, believing that Trump was a threat to democracy, or saying he was and knowing you were lying, and not understanding what you did.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Right.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: So, that's my thought.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Can I just follow up with one thing, and we're going to get everybody at the table in here. I just -- I was wanting to ask you about MSNBC's decision to pull "Morning Joe." I mean, this is the president's show that he watches every morning.\par \par \uc2 So, he has a big primetime address. And then the next morning, his big show isn't on because it's presumably because somebody told CNN they felt like that either the panel couldn't be trusted.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: It's an admission of guilt. That's what it is. If they take -- like, let's say something take anything like January 6th, for example. Nobody was taken off of Fox, because we aren't guilty. We are here to talk about what happened. They understood that they have people like \uc2 Joy Reid\uc2 , why did she lock her tweets down? Is she cleaning up her -- all her media footprint?\par \par \uc2 MSNBC must understand that where they are in this game, that they lead it here. And I mean, to me, it's like, either you double down on Trump as Hitler or you go quiet. Either way, you're guilty.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: And then, also, you can just go quiet for a week.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Yes.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: All right, so we did have big news today, President Trump announced his V.P. pick. Jesse, it is the senator from Ohio, the junior Senator J. D. Vance. He won in 2022. So, he's been a senator just for a couple of years, kind of reminds me of \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 JESSE WATTERS, FOX NEWS CHANNEL HOST: Yes, exactly like \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 As soon as I said it, Jesse was like, oh yes. Two years.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Well, first of all, Jessica, it's good to have you back around the table.\par \par \uc2 JESSICA TARLOV, FOX NEWS CHANNEL CONTRIBUTOR: Thank you.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: You were so missed and you just happened to be pregnant at the perfect time and deliver this baby when you missed the Trump trial and Biden's meltdown, the debate and the attempted assassination.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: We have good fertility Mojo.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Great timing, Jessica. All right, so Vance is good. I like him. They like him because he's great on television. He is composed and he'll be calm when he prosecutes Kamala, we call her laffin' L-A-F-F-I-N', and he's great on these mainstream media shows, he's just very moderate and then hit you in the face eloquently.\par \par \uc2 But his biography is stunning. His biography, he's a poor kid from a steel town in Ohio. His dad wasn't there. His mom was an addict, raised by his grandmother in one of these towns that was hollowed out by these dumb trade deals. He's kind of has the biography of populism.\par \par \uc2 And he goes and joins the Marines. And then he comes back goes to the Ohio State, and then Yale, which was my safety school, and then becomes this brilliant author, and also a venture capitalist, but he's not a corporate Republican. He's for the American worker. And that really distinguishes him from a lot of the older Republicans, and then his age obviously distinguishes him, I think he's younger than Jessica. She pointed that out in the green room, she's not upset about it.\par \par \uc2 But ideologically he's America First, Jeanine touched on it last week, he doesn't want to get entangled with these alliances. He's for strong borders, strong tariffs, and just has a very nice family structure.\par \par \uc2 And he will be a great future leader in the party, but he's not being anointed, he's not going to be, you know, Trump's not saying you're going to take the MAGA torch and run with it, he's going to have to work for the nomination in '28 and he probably will do a good job.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Judge, can you give us a sense of President Trump's frame of mind, we're 48 hours since the assassination attempt, he is here in Milwaukee. I don't know exactly when we're going to hear from him. But we do know that he gave a pretty remarkable interview. And that was ran in the New York Post, in which he said, I have been given a chance to unite. What do you think?\par \par \uc2 JEANINE PIRRO, FOX NEWS CHANNEL LEGAL ANALYST: Well, I've spoken to him a couple of times in those 48 hours. And you know, it's amazing. It's just been 48 hours since he was knocked down by a shot in that iconic moment, where his fist is up, he's down with the American flag in the background. And it shows that -- and I believe that will be a statue one day. I mean, I don't think there's -- it's so iconic. It's just so telling of the moment.\par \par \uc2 But the fact that he made a decision to get up, he even said he wanted to continue the speech. And he talked about being defiant in the face of wickedness. And then he would continue to go forward, continue with the Republican National Convention, announce the vice presidential candidate.\par \par \uc2 You know, he feels -- he feels that there was a hand of God involved. He does believe that there was divine intervention here. And I think that in picking J. D. Vance, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is feeling bullish. I think that you know, there was those who said, you know, you have to pick a woman, you have to pick a minority, you have to pick someone from a swing state.\par \par \uc2 Well, you know, J. D. Vance is from Ohio. I think Trump is 10 points up in Ohio. But J. D. Vance's story is a story of America. I mean, Jesse made it clear. I mean, he came from next to nothing with a mother who had a lot of problems. And he went to Yale, and he went into the Marines after 9/11. He's got three young kids. He's married to a woman who's an attorney, and it tells me it's MAGA now, and MAGA in the future, and that's what \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is interested in.\par \par \uc2 He loves this country. He believes that J. D. Vance's policies are now aligned with his and so he's comfortable with it. He's comfortable with a former Iraq veteran. And I think that this is a great pick for him. And I can't wait to see the Vance-Kamala debate.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Oh, yes. Popcorn and Milk Duds. We are going to be there for that. Jessica, Jake Tapper --\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Racist.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Axios yesterday, not Jake Tapper, he tweeted it, but Axios said that a senior House Democrat tells them we've all resigned ourselves to a second Trump presidency, \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2  said if you're a senior Democrat, it feels that way, you should absolutely retire and make space for true leadership. Where do you sit? Your thoughts on all that?\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: Well, I sit with AOC on that. And I don't think that reporting is accurate. And you know that there was a big piece in Politico today about \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  working the phones. She is out there. She thinks what's best is that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  doesn't stay on the top of the ticket, if this reporting is correct. And she wants to make sure that they move ahead with that. And she doesn't want to lose the House. That's her legacy there too, and \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2  who she's worked side by side with, and we want to hold on to the Senate as well, we think with just a three seat margin that we could take back the House realistically.\par \par \uc2 So, I don't know. Axios has had a lot of really good reporting on the back and forth on all of this, but that doesn't ring true to me. I haven't spoken to one Democrat who doesn't think that we've got to do everything we possibly can to save the top of the ticket and all the way down.\par \par \uc2 In terms of the J. D. Vance pick. This is what Democrats wanted for him to pick J. D. Vance. J. D. Vance is, you know, a security blanket with a beard for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . And I know the beard was a big point of contention and I'm glad that he is willing to give the facial hair a chance there.\par \par \uc2 He has exactly the same base as \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . It doesn't expand the map. He was going to win Ohio anyway. His policies are the same, protectionist, America First, anti-\uc2 NATO\uc2 , throw Ukraine to the wolves. He's got a great backstory for sure. I read Hillbilly Elegy like every good liberal and really enjoyed it, the movie was not as good as the book.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Never is?\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: No -- yes, probably never. What the election was going to be about, it's still about and when I saw \uc2 Glenn Youngkin\uc2  come out today. And the reception was so booming to him, I thought, oh, is this happening? Like that would be really bad, not necessarily just about putting Virginia in play, and I know it's close there. But just looking forward, you know, \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  is going to be here. So did Trump. Really have a moment with God or come to Jesus over the weekend where he said, it'll be -- it should be \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  or \uc2 Glenn Youngkin\uc2  or someone who gets me those never Trumpers.\par \par \uc2 But he didn't do that. He went with instinct, and he went with the pitfall and I said this earlier, I was talking to Martha about it. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  wants to strike this uniting tone. He talks about that in his interview, J. D. Vance was the first person to blame \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and the Democrats for what happened to him.\par \par \uc2 So, maybe they'll just do this as a, you know, a twofer, right? \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  goes this way. And then J. D. Vance zags that way and says the thing that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is really thinking, but he thinks isn't presidential enough.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Well, I will just add one comment here is that I don't think President Trump needed a vice presidential pick that would help expand the map because Trump himself is expanding the map, because now we're looking at new Hampshire, Minnesota, Virginia states that the Democrats had won before.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: I forgot to add, and it's my favorite topic, right? Abortion.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: We were waiting for that.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: So, I just -- you know, I'm a new mom, so I don't want to bring it up right away. But really bad for J. D. Vance and what's going on in Ohio, you're going to hear a lot about that story again, about that 10-year-old who was raped and had to go to Indiana to get health care. And he -- when he talks about who's on meet the press recently, it was a little bit more reasonable personally, but policy is the policy and he's from a state that is insanely restrictive.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: OK, welcome back, Jessica.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: Thank you.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: All right. Coming up. President Biden just reacting to the attempt on Trump's life in a brand new interview. We'll have it for you.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Fox News Alert. NBC News has just released a clip from Lester Holt's interview with President Biden. Let's listen to that.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 LESTER HOLT, ANCHOR, NBC NEWS: Let's talk about the conversation this has started, and it's really about language, what we say out loud and the consequences of those. You called your opponent an existential threat. On a call a week ago, you said it's time to put Trump in the bullseye. There's some dispute about the context but I think you appreciate the word --\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 , PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: I see crosshairs. That's what I'm going focus on. Look, the truth of the matter was what I guess I was talking about at the time was there's very little focus on Trump's agenda.\par \par \uc2 HOLT: Yes, the term is bullseye.\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: Was it -- it was a mistake to use the word. I didn't -- I didn't say crosshairs -- I mean, bullseye. I mean the focus on it.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: But will the media and Democrats listen to the president when he calls to lower the temperature. While the former President was still bleeding from a bullet wound to his head, some in the press were quickly trying to blame Trump for getting shot.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS, ANCHOR, ABC NEWS: Of course, President Trump and his supporters have contributed to this violent rhetoric as well.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Well, absolutely, George. We were just looking back this morning at some of the things that former President Trump has said. It's going to be a bloodbath for the country. That will be the least of it. He said he was partly joking and that that was taken out of context. But those are indeed his words.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: He is recovering from these injuries now. This was a traumatic event no doubt for him. But I did notice there was no call for lowering the temperature, condemning all political violence, and really trying to signal to his supporters as well not to retaliate or to have any kind of escalation here.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Jesse, I'll go to you first. You know, it's interesting, I just pulled up the quote. The quote by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  within days before the shooting is we're done talking about the debate, it's time to put Trump in a bullseye. Can he really lower his own tone and temperature?\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: He won't because that's all the Democrats have. They have this demonization strategy that animates their base, that gets them fired up, they get ratings from it. They make money, fundraising from it. So, if you take that, that's basically the cornerstone of the Democrat's turnout operation which is Trump is a threat. And without the Democrats being against Trump, they don't even know what they're for. So, we'll see if they're able to table that. I doubt it. I think they just need to go into a corner and sit down and think about what they've been saying.\par \par \uc2 Now, we don't know if Crooks was watching Morning Joe all day and watching Politico report the bullseye comment. We don't know if he had help. We don't know if he's one of these cooks like the Reagan assassin that was trying to impress Jodie Foster. We don't know. But we do know the stories that they've been telling about this man have been toxic and the language has been way too hot.\par \par \uc2 It's the same thing the CIA does with foreign governments that they want to overthrow. They controversialize the leader, they deplatform, they drum up stupid investigations, and then they whip up this hurricane of hostility which makes the public so crazy they think they're in imminent danger if the leader stays around. It's damaging. It should never be done inside this country.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: You know, Dana, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has indicated that before the Republican National Convention, he had "a humdinger of his speech." And he said that after the shooting, he made a decision to give a whole different speech, suggesting that that speech is going to be talking about unity. And this is an opportunity for President Trump to be one of the greatest president.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: And he says in that interview, I was given a chance to help unite the country and even the world. That might not be the exact quote, but it's along -- it's along those lines. And last night in Biden's speech afterward, I said -- I felt like it fell short of hitting the mark. And the reason I did is because he didn't say something like including me.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Right, right.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: In fact, last week I said -- which mean the bullseye. Now, that's a metaphor. Lots of us use metaphors, but I could see how that could be taken today. And so, follow me. Follow -- I will lead. I'm going to be the one who does it. Because he didn't do that, Lester Holt is able to say what about what you said? So, they could have taken the sting out of it, but they decided not to do that.\par \par \uc2 And just remember, you know, it was \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  who said that Romney was going to put Black Americans back in chains. It was the Jim Crow 2.0. Even last night, \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2  tweets that we have to protect the country from the fascist. So, I'm not sure that the message is getting through on the left.\par \par \uc2 I don't know what the end of this week will look like on that front, but yes, there is an opportunity. And I also believe that all of us use metaphors, so we can give each other a little bit of grace on that front and just say OK, going forward let's be a little bit more thoughtful about the language. I don't know how long that lasts. But I do appreciate the spirit of the moment.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Yes. And we'll see. And Jessica, I didn't say before, I missed arguing with you. I really did. And I'm so glad to have you back. But you know, Jens Psaki was demanding -- this is after the attempted assassination, that Republicans change their rhetoric, their tone. And that she said she's incredibly scared. Rachel Maddow, of course, has always talked about being taken off the air and being put in a camp. I mean, that's the kind of language that I'm really surprised in this moment that \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  is sticking to.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: I think that everyone is concerned about what's to come next. And I've spoken to a number of Republicans obviously around the convention who are worried that there something else may happen, right? That if it's possible that that shooter could get that close to him, that we could see something else. And it could happen to anyone of any political stripe. And I think that's where Jens Psaki's concern is coming from.\par \par \uc2 I happen to think that you don't need to change the program. You could watch your words. Whatever you're going to say and there are going to be a lot of fiery speakers. Some of them are coming during the day. Obviously, the prime time speeches are going to be big. But I'm not in the business of telling Republicans what they can do with their convention. We'll lead by example of what we think our convention should look like. And the themes of the convention are the basis for the campaign.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: But Jen was demanding that the Republican --\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: I know. I'm saying I don't agree with that.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: You don't. OK.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: I think that they -- I think that they should be sensible and responsible about the moment and it's a huge moment to do that. But I wanted clarity from President Biden on the bullseye comment. We'll watch the Lester Holt interview with interest. But nobody who's being an honest broker can possibly believe that the Democratic rhetoric is the problem here.\par \par \uc2 So, if the issue is that we're saying all the time that he's like Hitler and he's a threat to democracy -- and by the way J.D. Vance has also said that he's like Hitler and I guess he's redeemed now. But \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  sent a fundraising email just last week that said \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is a threat to democracy. And only one of these candidates has inspired people who sent pipe bombs to leading Democrats across the country who has inspired mass shooters.\par \par \uc2 Talk about firing up the base, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has been doing that since 2016. Remember, when he said the Second Amendment people could take care of it? Remember when he was talking about \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  abolishing the Second Amendment and she'll get to appoint judges. He talked about -- remember that congressman from Montana who body-slammed a reporter and he said he's my type? He retruthed (ph) or whatever it was a video of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  hog-tied just --\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Oh, come on. That was hilarious.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: Oh, that's hilarious.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Your differences are so tiny.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: No, they're not.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: We're talking about an attempted assassination that left a man dead. A shooter groomed and incentivized by a drum beat of demonization --\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: You have no idea what happened --\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: You can call people -- no, no, you can call people Hitler all you want but you have to ask yourself why would you? You have a right to say whatever you want. You can say I'm a Nazi, I'm Hitler, but the question is why would you?\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: I would never.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: You cannot pretend that you did not know where it would lead. Trump laughs about a picture of a hog-tied \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  on the back of a pickup truck. That is not demonization. That is a meme.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: And saying to Second Amendment people you could take care of it about \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2 . What is that, Greg? That was his opponent. That was his political opponent.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: You know, the day before the attempted -- the attempted assassination of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  said he's even more dangerous than I've said before. He's unhinged. He's snapped and I guess he really didn't watch the debate when he was asked if he had seen it. He's a threat to this nation. He'll win over my dead body.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: You know, but you know what? I'm sure when he called Trump, he said no hard feelings. You know, that's how it works in politics. I say you're evil.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: I think just said it rather than the lies.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: No, but you have to understand, it's scary to think that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  would lie like that but he has or it's scary that he would believe this stuff. The real challenge for the party is what do you do next. You can't do the Trump as Hitler narrative anymore because you'll be thoroughly reviled by the public, you know. You're going to need more than demonization but you got nothing else planned, so you're going to pivot to abortion, good luck with that.\par \par \uc2 The -- when it comes to Trump as Hitler, you -- the dog caught the car and you realized you can't drive it. I think you know -- and you can sit here and you can say throw all the rhetoric at Trump that you want. Everybody understands Trump. Everybody understands. He makes jokes. Your side wasn't making jokes. When you call somebody Hitler, and we say no we're not, those two aren't the same thing.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: The guy who sent pipe bombs understood the jokes?\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: I don't know who that is.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Yes.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: Oh.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: There were pipe bombs -- there were pipe bombs that were --\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Why doesn't anybody talk about Steve Scalise? I mean, come on.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: I'm happy to talk about it. And Bernie Sanders came out right away and said --\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: OK, Jesse.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: All right, well, I just think you should prepare for a beautiful dictatorship, Jessica. It's going to be a four-year dictatorship, and we're going to get everything --\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: From day one.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: From day one.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: Well, he'll probably get the Supreme Court to give him a second term. They' do that.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: All right, if --\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: Third term.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: If we could only hope.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: Yes.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: The Secret Service scrambling to explain their most stunning screw up in decades. The woman who heads the agency says that changes are coming to Trump's security detail but she accepts no fault for the attempt that left a would-be assassin being able to get within 130 yards of the former President. Biden's DHS Chief, Mayorkas was also outs spinning over who's at fault for the deadly security breach. Watch.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 ALEJANDRO MAYORKAS, SECRETARY, DEPARTMENT OF HOMELAND SECURITY: A direct line of sight like that um to the former president should not occur. That is precisely why President Biden directed that an independent review of the incident occur. We are going to really study the event independently and make recommendations to the Secret Service into me so that we can assure the safety and security of our protectees, which is one of our most vital missions in the Secret Service, the \uc2 Department of Homeland Security\uc2  and across the government.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: That as we get new details on what went wrong. The building that the gunman was on was the staging area for the local police tactical team doing overwatch of the crowd. That's according to ABC. And the gunman gained roof access without a ladder. The \uc2 FBI\uc2  says they have gained access to the gunman's cell phone but have not yet determined a potential motive.\par \par \uc2 Biden caught up with reporters today who pressed him on his confidence in the Secret Service.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Do you feel safe with your Secret Service detail?\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: Yes, I do.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Do you still have faith in the Secret Service, Mr. President?\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: Yes, I do.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: The fact that he hasn't fired her already, Judge Jeanine -- but the fact that she hasn't offered her resignation is stunning to me.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: You know, ordinary Americans with no experience in security, law enforcement, know that you can call it an outside perimeter, you can call it an inside perimeter, you could call it mars, but it was 150 yards from the place where a former president was speaking and within a direct line of sight. And the truth is that if you -- the Secret Service wants to blame the local police and you've got the local police acting like they did in Uvalde, apparently went up and then he came down, we've got some issues.\par \par \uc2 But you can't just say local police had that. You've got to do your own advanced work. And as the local D.A., I have people who did advanced work. How dangerous is it? How many people do we have to bring? And you know that there have been problems with the Secret Service. I mean, there -- Kamala's detail, there were two of them who had a problem. We covered it a few months ago where a woman was hired who had problems in the Dallas Police Department. You know, then the problem with prostitutes in other countries.\par \par \uc2 I mean, there's a culture there that has to be addressed. And they need a leader who's going to take no prisoners. And they need someone unlike this woman. The night that there was an attempted assassination of a former President of the United States, she doesn't speak. The next day she shows up, Cheatle, the head of the Secret Service, she says I'm not going to talk about it. Well, you need to talk about it.\par \par \uc2 You deserve -- we deserve answers. You owe us an answer. And in the end, how can we possibly believe that she is in a position with her agency to protect the President going forward when they failed on the last one and aren't even willing to address it? And Mayorkas say who is her boss says, well, I don't know if anyone will be fired. That's because nobody gets fired on the left. They just keep going.\par \par \uc2 And I want to talk about the guys on the -- on the state -- on this area where the President was -- the President popped up. He popped up too many times. If there was a second shooter they would have had him. You know, there's a lot to talk about. But I want to talk about finally the Trump crowd. They were as resilient as \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . They didn't run. They didn't scatter. They didn't stampede. They started yelling USA, USA. They learned this from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: So, now we're hearing this guy didn't gain access to the roof, Dana, with a ladder. That means he must have gotten inside the building somehow and gotten to the roof --\par \par \uc2 PERINO: He just walk up the stairs and open the hatch --\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: So, how is he having access to that building if that's supposedly a tactical site for the locals?\par \par \uc2 PERINO: There are so many questions to be answered. And there's going to be a hearing next Monday starting that -- on the Congressional side of things. I do wonder about Biden not at least calling her in to say, you in my office right now. And at least even to say I want to know what happened, tell me more, but they don't do that. And I think that Mayorkas, because he has been saying for three years the border is secure, no -- it's like, I don't actually hear what he says when he talks.\par \par \uc2 So, the last thing I would say is most presidents will always defend the Secret Service. They have to have complete trust with the Secret Service. But Biden could have done that for Trump.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Right.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: And for future presidents that he should have.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Greg Gutfeld.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Yes, I think that agents, they're doing the best they can. You know, it's up to the investigators to decide whether the people up top really screwed them -- screwed it up and screwed them over. You know, if Trump was short-staffed or given the B or C squad creating vulnerabilities. I don't have any idea. And I don't think it's a going to social media to finding those answers is a good thing.\par \par \uc2 I think there might be some opportunity costs as you see in every industry when it comes to DEI when -- you know, I don't mind DEI at \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  or DMV, but at Secret Service, DEI, DIE.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Right.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: You know, it's -- but having said that, that is not a testament. That's not a criticism of the agents. You can -- you can have the bravest, most passionate agent fulfill this dream to protect the President. It's no comment on their bravery, but you know, it's -- Tyrus once said to me, I can be your bodyguard but you can't be mine. You know, there's no way I could block a shot to Tyrus' head, chest, or even belt buckle. So, there's some things that you kind of have to like look at. And it's way above my pay grade. I think the Secret Service, they're brave. It's not about them. It's about what's above them.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Jessica?\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: So, I was particularly taken with that interview that the BBC got. The incredible blind journalist who was interviewing the rallygoer wearing the great visor that has orange hair attached to it who said I saw him and I was yelling about it. And the reporting that's come out since then is that they knew that that particular building was a vulnerability. And I don't understand how you go forward with a rally knowing that something within sniper range is a vulnerability.\par \par \uc2 On the DEI front, I mean, she's a 27-year veteran of the Secret Service. We need to hear from her. We need to really understand what happened there. But the snipe -- the Secret Service sniper who didn't shoot him at first but then did end up shooting him was a man. And the local cop who climbed up and then didn't do anything was also a man. So, I'm not sure -- oh --\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: You did -- that guy didn't do anything.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: Well --\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: He ducked because he was going to get shot and he rushed they guy.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: But you are supposed to shoot -- if you -- if you see somebody holding a rifle pointed at the former President of the United State --\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Pointed at him, he ducked. But his presence probably caused the shooter to rush, causing him to shoot early. Who knows?\par \par \uc2 PERINO: And maybe --\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: I don't know. I wasn't there.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: That also might have saved the President.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Yes.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: But unfortunately, another person was killed.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Yes, Mr. Comperatore.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: Yes.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Yes, and we're praying for them and their family.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Yes.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Coming up, President Biden gets a break from Democrats trying to boot him after the attempts on Trump's life.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  getting a political lifeline after the attempt on Trump's life. Democrats are calling off the dogs, for now, on their effort to kick him off the ticket. It seems, Jessica, there's no point in replacing him now. That's like trying to put a new engine in a Pinto that's just blown up, right? Just tow it to the lot, sell it for parts.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: I'm not a car gal so I can't really comment on that.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Pinto was a car that blew up a lot.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Yes.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Just to --\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: I knew enough. I just didn't want to play your game. So, I already mentioned this big story about \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  starting to go to work and \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  rarely fails at what she's trying to do. So, we'll see how that bears out. But it is important to note and we'll see of course what the impact of Saturday will be on the polls, but we still have a static race, right?\par \par \uc2 So, there were huge polls that came out in the last couple of days, Fox, \uc2 CBS\uc2 , NBC, everyone. Trump one to two points ahead. The RealClearPolitics average 2.7 points. We've been there before and talked about that. And Marist even had him up too. So, it seems like Biden's polling has largely recovered, swing state polls as well for \uc2 CBS\uc2  but within the margin of the error. So, that all benefits \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in his argument that he can stay on the ticket.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Dana?\par \par \uc2 PERINO: You know, when you're having a bad day and then you're trying to rush, and then you keep having a bad day, and the day keeps getting worse because then you drop your keys and then your heel breaks and then your car broke breaks down and you get arrested. Like, all those bad things were happening to Biden for like two weeks and all of a sudden he got a boom, failed assassination attempt and he could reset.\par \par \uc2 I'm in a rare camp. I think that this accelerates the likelihood that Biden is not on the ticket.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Judge, agree to disagree?\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: I think it's going to be very hard at this point. I really do. And I respect, Dana, what you're saying but it seems to me that they're almost frozen right now that, you know, let's just try not to look guilty. We got to make sure whatever we're doing doesn't make us look guilty, like we're responsible. We're just going to stay with Joe.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Jesse?\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Yes, they're frozen mid coup and that's the worst time to freeze. He's already was in decline. He was losing going into the debate. He's got a 37 percent approval. And then he just had this terrible debate. And then there was the just absolute cannibalism that took place for two weeks within his own party and within the media. And then Trump dodges an assassination, and now he's basically like a certified American political hero, and gets this Florida papers case dismissed.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: We didn't talk about that.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: And so, Joe's like about that barely hanging on and I'm just here as an observer.\