s?\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CLAIRE MCCASKILL (D), FORMER MISSOURI SENATOR: He had one thing he had to accomplish, and that was reassure America that he was up to the job at his age. And he failed at that tonight.\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 , PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: I don't walk as easy as I used to. I don't speak as smoothly as I used to. I don't debate as well as I used to. But I know what I do know. I know how to tell the truth.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BREAM: Well, that was Missouri Senator Claire McCaskill after President Biden's rough debate showing Thursday. And Then the president addressing his rocky performance at a fired-up campaign rally the next day.\par \par \uc2 Let's talk about it with our group, Fox News contributor and "Outkick" columnist Mary Katharine Ham, Heritage President \uc2 Kevin Roberts\uc2 , "Axios" political reporter Stef Kight, and Fox News contributor and "Forbes" contributing writer, Richard Fowler.\par \par \uc2 Welcome everybody.\par \par \uc2 Well, we have something to discuss. OK, let's start here.\par \par \uc2 So, we know that the president had some follow-up fundraisers. They've given us numbers this morning. They say since the debate $33 million have come in. He was at some big Hampton's fundraisers this weekend. But, Mary Katherine, they said he was using a prompter.\par \par \uc2 MARY KATHARINE HAM, FOX NEWS CONTRIBUTOR: Right.\par \par \uc2 BREAM: The donors didn't feel like they really could talk to him about the access in a way that would reassure them.\par \par \uc2 HAM: Yes. Look, I think they - I agree with Senator McCaskill. The problem for the Democratic Party as we move through this in these 72 hours is they need two things. They need \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  to decide to step aside, which seems unlikely, and then they need unanimity of plan and purpose moving forward very quickly. And I think that that is even less likely. And the problem 