hat the Biden campaign can successfully talk about. And this is a place where they can say, listen, under \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's leadership, even though he might be old, even though you might question his competency, here's what he's been able to do. And that's just one example.\par \par \uc2 You have \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2 , another example of this. There's tons of governors and congressmen who are working with the Biden administration to get things done for the American people. And this is - this is an opportunity that is not open for the Biden campaign to talk about.\par \par \uc2 BREAM: OK.\par \par \uc2 HAM: Isn't it a bit like a quarterback controversy though? Like, you're not sure you want to be talking about that?\par \par \uc2 FOWLER: But, no. But I think that - but, let's remember, elections are team sports, right? You want everybody to win. And you want to regain the House. That's what Democrats need to do.\par \par \uc2 BREAM: Well, I do think it's - I think it was - exactly. And there are down-ballot worries now for Democrats who are worried about what they saw the other night. And they're - interesting to me that a fundraising email went out from the Biden-Harris campaign this weekend and it showed polling with a bunch of these other people. It mentioned \uc2 Pete Buttigieg\uc2  and \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2 , Amy Klobuchar. It mentioned all these other people, which kind of seemed a little odd. If you want to quiet that conversation, don't put their names in your email.\par \par \uc2 KEVIN ROBERTS\uc2 , PRESIDENT, THE HERITAGE: It's a terrible situation. And, look, the political dilemma is legitimate. We ought to be talking about it. But I say the following, and I put politics off to the side. If, in fact, we're asking the question whether President Biden is up to the campaign, we have to ask the question, is he up to serve as president of the United States?\par \par \uc2 I'll lament the fact, my political differences with him aside, that it seems a