eper and more cavernous and she actually ends up endorsing Trump. This -- I -- is like a national --\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: \uc2 Michelle Obama\uc2  you're talking about.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Yes. This is like a National Enquirer story. I don't know if it's true but I want to believe it.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Yes. Well, don't -- wouldn't you be weirded out if you said --\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: The whole country is weirded out but the whole country won't say anything because it's the President's family. Finally, someone came out and said this is ridiculous. You're sleeping with your dead brother's widow, and then you got her hooked on crack.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Well --\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: I mean, come on, America.\par \par \uc2 FORD JR.: Let me be very clear. We've never had that happen in my family. It's nothing like that.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: But you know, apparently, Dana, they were close \uc2 Michelle Obama\uc2  and Kathleen Buhle, Hunter's ex-wife. And they used to go to Soul Cycle together, and then they apparently have drinks in the White House afterwards. But the Bidens are upset with Kathleen Buhle because she started talking about the fact that Hunter was having affairs, affairs plural, and his drug problem.\par \par \uc2 And it's -- you get an insight into the Biden family being more concerned about the reputation of the family than the individual members of the family.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: So, Axios got the scoop and good on them. And they included this little detail that \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  was leaving a Biden family event and described their family dynamics as some weird S-word.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Yes.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: OK, so that just encapsulates it. I also think that \uc2 Michelle Obama\uc2 , she really doesn't like politics.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Yes.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: She doesn't like partisan politics which is why I can't stress enough that she is not going to be the Democratic nominee.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: I agree. I agree.\par \