tial frontrunner \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 MCENANY: So, Victor, Jake Tapper compares Trump to Hitler and the campaign press secretary just can't bring it up, is that where we are?\par \par \uc2 VICTOR DAVIS HANSON, SENIOR FELLOW, \uc2 HOOVER INSTITUTION\uc2 : Yes, I think they're going back to the 2020 formula, Kayleigh. They think it worked then and what was that formula, it was to sequester \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  away from the crowds, not having campaign have it out. So, his talking points outsourced to a whole array of subordinate lackeys and then count on the media to demonize Trump and then count and this is what's scary is on that Election Day is a mere construct and 70 percent of the people would be voting early or in mail in ballot.\par \par \uc2 And I think they're going to xerox that 2020 formula all over again, you're not going to see him on the campaign trail, they're going to try to raise a lot of money from bicoastal elite. Some they will, and they're going to outsource it to the media and then these subordinates will be attack dog and we know what the -- what the message is going to be, January 6th, democracy dies, abortion, abortion, abortion, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is Hitler. I don't think it's going to work the second time.\par \par \uc2 MCENANY: I wonder if Biden is xeroxing the same debate strategy? Victor, there are some new reporting out about two and a half hours ago. I want to pull it up from \uc2 The New York Times\uc2 . This is \uc2 Katie Rogers\uc2 . She got an overview of what Biden is doing sequestered at Camp David, it's pretty interesting.\par \par \uc2 At Camp David, a movie theater, and an airplane hangar had been outfitted with lights and production equipment to create a mock debate stage, at least 16 and current former aides summoned from Washington and Wilmington whizz back and forth on golf carts, to join President Biden and strategy sessions.\par \par \uc2 Victor, this seems like a movie set. Is he preparing all these people around him on a movie set? Is that going to work or is Trump's strategy of being in and amidst the people the better one?\par \par \uc2 HANSON: Well, it's the same idea. They're replicating what they think were, we saw in the first debate and the second debate in 2020. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  was sequestered again. He was not really out anywhere. He rested, rested, rested, he changed his time clock. There were rumors that he got maybe some stimulatory help. And then he came out and he kind of growled, and he yelled, and he did the same thing in the State of the Union. He did it in the infamous Phantom of the Opera, ultra MAGA semi fascist.\par \par \uc2 So, I think \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  should expect that he hasn't been on work for four or five days. He's been resting. He's been prepped on everything, and he's going to come out. I don't think he's going to come out cognitively sharp, but he's going to become animated, angry, like the State of the Union.\par \par \uc2 I think \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , if he stays cool, and that doesn't mean he can't be sharp in the questioning, just be calm and polite. And one of the questions he should have said to him, I think he could, Joe, you know, the last time -- one of the last times we debated you -- you look me in the eye and said I was incorrect or lying about the laptop and you told the American people that it was the work of Russian disinformation and 51. And now do you want to apologize and say that your campaign operative to \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2  set that all up?\par \par \uc2 He can do things like that if he does it calmly and politely and but mostly, he needs to talk about his past record, his current agenda and what he will do for us and contrast that with the utter disaster of the last three and a half years.\par \par \uc2 MCENANY: I think that's exactly right. And I think that disaster, I am just going to guess. I at least believe he will have a \uc2 Red Bull\uc2 , but we will see. Victor, thank you.\par \par \uc2 HANSON: Yes.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: Communities have suffered more under the Biden regime than Philadelphia. Under Crooked Joe, the City of Brotherly Love is being ravaged by bloodshed and crime. This November, the people of Pennsylvania are going to tell Crooked \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , you're fired. Get out, get out. You're fired.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 MCENANY: Another massive rally in a traditionally deep blue city, Philadelphia at this time. Trump is fearlessly going into once great cities tragically ruined by decades of Democrat incompetence and corruption and the people they're loving it.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : I want to leave a tip for you guys. I'm going to give you $500, you guys all split it up. Is that, OK?\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Thank you.\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: No tax on tips.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 MCENANY: Can you imagine Biden doing that, anything like that in a Republican city? We highly doubt it. Trump's 50 state strategy is in full swing with a clear message, the Democrat monopoly on our cities is over.\par \par \uc2 Joining us now is Florida Congressman Byron Donalds. Congressman Donalds, welcome. Great to have you here. I am fascinated. I read a piece every word of it just before coming here and it is with the Biden Campaign Chair Jen Dillon O'Malley, it was with Puck News. And here's what she says, despite all the polling, despite the energy we've shown you, she says this. The first thing I'll say is that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is going to win. Period. And I'm not saying that because I wish it to be so, I'm saying that because I know it will be so by who he is as a leader, and what we are building as a campaign. why she's so confident?\par \par \uc2 REP. BYRON DONALDS (R-FL): Kayleigh, it's good to be with you. I think the reason why she's confident is because that's what you're supposed to say when you're running a campaign. The truth is, everybody else is looking at \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and saying, you can't have four more years because you destroyed the border, you've destroyed the purchasing power of every American citizen.\par \par \uc2 The world is on fire under your watch. We don't even know if he can mentally do the job for another four years, let alone another four weeks. The American people have serious questions. That is why when \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  goes to the Bronx, goes to Detroit, goes to Philadelphia, the reception has been warm. More and more voters are looking at him because they remember his presidency. They remember that he was the mantle of leadership, not just here in America, but across the globe.\par \par \uc2 Americans were better off, the world was better off. She can say whatever she wants, but that is false, fake hope from a dying campaign that's not going to win this November.\par \par \uc2 MCENANY: Yes, she did admit that they're not playing for Florida, Florida is just long gone. So that's some good news. But a CNN political commentator, he's name is Jamal Simmons, he was \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 ' communications director, he had some advice for Biden. Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JAMAL SIMMONS, CNN POLITICAL COMMENTATOR: He's kind of got resting old face. He needs to smile. And when he smiles, it goes away a little bit, he smiles, his face comes to life, I would just say if they're practicing this, practice smiling.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: You basically just said smile more.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 MCENANY: Is a smile all America needs to make this all go away for Joe.\par \par \uc2 DONALDS: No, and this is where the radical left is left to, smile, makes everybody feel better, to feel better. The country is in a terrible spot. There has been crises after crises brought to us by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 . And quite fran