)\par \par \uc2 (GUNSHOT)\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 MCENANY: Well, you just watched a former California sheriff's deputy who left the force after being brutally attacked by a suspect. She's now giving future law enforcement a chilling warning saying that being a cop is not worth it.\par \par \uc2 Meagan McCarthy joins me now. Meagan, that is chilling footage. You were beaten. You were shot at. You are a mother. I cannot imagine what you went through before ultimately leaving the force.\par \par \uc2 And we wanted to bring you on today because the Biden administration chose to elevate someone from department of interior up to the communications office in the West Wing.\par \par \uc2 This individual named Tyler Cherry compared police officers to slave patrols, called for the abolishment of ICE, and he's attempting to downplay it. He apologized by saying past social media posts from when I was younger, do not reflect my current views, period. And he goes on as you can see there.\par \par \uc2 But I've got to wonder, I mean, you know what the cost of serving is, you know, how tough this is for police officers. What do you think when you hear that?\par \par \uc2 MEAGAN MCCARTHY, FORMER SAN BERNARDINO COUNTY, CALIFORNIA, DEPUTY: Well, I think that's exactly our issue these days is these elected officials, our leaders have no idea what it's like to be a police officer. You know, less than 1 percent of our entire population even takes the oath to become a law enforcement officer.\par \par \uc2 And then you have our elected officials dehumanizing, villainizing the exact profession. That is the only stand between good and evil. I mean, look at what's happening at our Southern border. We're having an explosion in crime because of these instances.\par \par \uc2 And then you have these individuals who will further propel this idea that cops are all bad. We're all discriminatory. We all have this horrible narrative. Yet, we're human beings. We have families. We