 all around. ABC is reporting that Biden is now hunkered down working on his punchier, more pointed remarks to attack Trump, he's working hard in Camp David. Now, in what universe did they think that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  at any age was capable of sounding punchy, witty, and more pointed?\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: Trump is trying to make the country forget just how dark and unsettling things were when he was president. We'll never forget lying around and I said, him lying around, actually.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Whatever. Can I buy a vowel? Now even if Biden managed to remain relatively coherent through the debate and doesn't do one of those. Well, it still doesn't solve his biggest problem. He cannot run on his agenda. He can't tell people their life is better than it was four years ago, because it's not and their plan to make this campaign about character, well, it's a total loser. That new Fox poll that so many people are talking about shows that the candidate's ability to handle the issues is what this campaign is mostly about beating out the candidate's character and fitness by 30 points. Whoops.\par \par \uc2 And a second point, I think there are plenty of voters out there who are questioning Biden's character. And think about it this way, how could a good man do what this man has done to the country these past three and a half years? How can a man of integrity blatantly lie about inflation, blatantly, or about what he knew about his son's foreign businesses?\par \par \uc2 So given where things stand today, you bet, you bet they're pushing the panic button. Joining me now Glenn Greenwald, Pulitzer Prize winning independent journalist. Glenn, it's so wonderful to see you. You know, when I know that the press has spent an enormous amount of whatever's left of its credibility and capital on this Trump's a dictator storyline. And maybe that explains a little bit of the erosion you've seen in some of these state-wide polls. But how do you see this line of attack playing out over the next four or five months for Biden?\par \par \uc2 GLENN GREENWALD, INDEPENDENT JOURNALIST: I think the whole issue here is the media issue and its relationship to our politics. We know, of course, that the key dynamic shaping our politics is that most people have come to hate major institutions of authority, the media being the most hated of all. And the reason is, is because they've seen the media lie on purpose for partisan ends in 2016, when they concocted the Russia gate collusion theory and based around the country, and that it turned out to be false.\par \par \uc2 2020, they proved they would lie for the Hunter Biden laptop which they called Russian disinformation, that was false. So, I think in these two areas, Laura, one, how people are managing and faring in the United States, and the other is how capable is Biden really, people don't need the media to tell them what to think, they're able to see that much better for themselves.\par \par \uc2 How do they feel their family is doing, not well? How do they think Biden is performing, extremely poorly. And the media cannot convince them that what they're seeing is false.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: And Glenn, this line, that -- it's kind of in tandem with Trump's a dictator, is that Trump is out for revenge, and it will be nothing but a bloodbath of political revenge, if he wins. And I'm hearing them say this, I think you are literally trying to put him in jail in multiple court cases, and Trump's out for revenge. That's rich.\par \par \uc2 GREENWALD: Well, yes, I mean, first of all, again, I think they have a huge uphill battle, it'd be one thing if there was some new personality that very few people understood politically, and they wanted to say, oh, this is some kind of Hitler figure. And they tried that with Trump in 2016 and people went through the next four years, we didn't see concentration camps being built, or AOC and Rachel Maddow, and Joy Behar being thrown into them.\par \par \uc2 So, this idea that he's going to be a real Hitler figure this time, people remember Trump for four years and didn't see any of that. And, of course, the real irony is what you said, Laura, they're basically saying explicitly, we must keep Trump out of the office by imprisoning him before the election, because if we don't, and he wins, he will then weaponize the Justice Department in order to try and imprison his political enemies.\par \par \uc2 And it's not just Trump, but a huge number of people who are associated with Trump who are either in prison facing charges and that has been the case since 2018. They have been weaponizing the system against their political opponents in a way we've never seen before. And so, to try and convince Americans, he's the real danger to do that. I think, even for the media, if I were them would be a bridge too far.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Yes. And their disinformation ploy is also just revealing once again that they're all kind of collaborating with each other. They want less free speech, not more free speech. And so, they call everything disinformation, if it actually, you know, is in any way critical of their worldview. Glenn, you've been all over it. Thank you so much. Wonderful to see you.\par \par \uc2 All right, Trump's outreach to democratic strongholds may be bearing fruit. Multiple polls now show that Biden support among black voters dipping between 15 and 20 percentage points since 2020. Politico today warning that Biden has that problem with black voters in Milwaukee, as I mentioned, and that in 2016, Hillary Clinton's underperformance in Milwaukee, Philly and Detroit hurt her immensely. Congressman \uc2 Jim Clyburn\uc2  is now saying, it's all disinformation.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 REP. JIM CLYBURN (D-SC): This man says he's delivered for African Americans. I asked him to show me one single substantive thing that he has done that would make black Americans proud to be a part of his effort. We have to be very careful because this is all about out miscommunication, disinformation, the media repeating these things rather than recording what has actually happened. That is what's causing the problem.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Yes, higher incomes under Trump were misinformation. Nice try, Jim. All right, Trump continues his blue city tour this weekend in Philly. Now that's a city we know has been rocked by skyrocketing drug use, homelessness and retail theft. And the scenes from neighborhoods in Philly. I know we've seen them on social media and they're in every major city, but in Philadelphia, the birthplace of freedom. It's heartbreaking. And \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  thinks that Philadelphia's minority community is getting a raw deal here. And that message may resonate.\par \par \uc2 Joining us now are two Pennsylvania voters, Israel Cruz and Antoine Gist. Antoine, let's start with you. Congressman Clyburn says that Biden is not losing support with black voters. Do you agree with that?\par \par \uc2 ANTOINE GIST, PENNSYLVANIA VOTER: Thank you, Laura, for having me on. Biden is losing the streets, as they would say, in Philly, all the internet is talking about it. You know, they have to actually drum up support to actually protest against Trump coming here tomorrow. But I met President Trump last week in Detroit, a very warm, you know, comforting man. And I really believe that people are waking up, the scales are coming off of their eyes.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Israel, why did you shift to Republican, identify yourself as a Republican, after you voted mostly Democrat during your lifetime?\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL CRUZ, PENNSYLVANIA VOTER: Yes, I mean, I grew up in New York and Philadelphia. And that's all we -- that's all we were told is, you know, vote Democrat, vote Democrat, vote Democrat. And so, you don't understand why. But once you start seeing what the media says, and where you're living at, and there's no correlation going on there, like the media is lying. So, what else do I -- do I not trust, and that's the problem. I started not trusting them. I started not trusting the Democrats. And then I started looking into things myself.\par \par \uc2 And I saw that when they spoke, they were lying. And when I saw the -- the Republican Party is supposed to be for the rich and the Democrats are for the poor. Why do I want to be for the poor? I wanted to move my family forward. I wanted to propel myself. And that's all they wanted us to do is take that, you know, take that little meal ticket, welfare checks, whatever --\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Yes, scraps.\par \par \uc2 CRUZ: -- and we said, no, we're not going to do that in my family.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: I liked that analysis. So, the most of the billionaires are still supporting Biden, most of them not all, but most of them because they like to keep wages low in the United States. Antoine, I know you voted for Hillary back in 2016. You started looking at Trump's politics more closely. You shifted to him in 2020. And a lot of people don't know this, but in Philadelphia, although of course, Hillary won handily. Trump picked up more voters, and he picked up a third ward in northeast Philly. I think it was the 58th ward.\par \par \uc2 So, there's obviously a lot of room to grow for Trump. But people are citing the way he's been treated by the legal system as yet another reason for African American voters to take interest in his campaign. Do you see that as a possible plus for him?\par \par \uc2 GIST: I do see that because Trump is being looked at as the underdog, he's being looked at as the person who's being persecuted. And you know, Philadelphia, we're a home of Rocky, you know, the Vince Papale story, so we're always rooting for the underdog. So that's why Trump is really resonating with a lot of Philadelphians.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Israel, do you think this visit by Trump is going to matter in the end, every trip to a blue city by Republican, it's not been done in a long, long time. But what does it say to the voters on the ground?\par \par \uc2 CRUZ: It says exactly what I wanted, what I would do myself, if you want the people to know that you care about them, you show up. That's what family does. That's what friends do. When you show up you, you're telling them, I'm here for you. And when you don't, you're telling them exactly, who cares, who cares about you.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Amazing.\par \par \uc2 CRUZ: So, I guess it will --\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Israel, Antoine, we could talk all night. Thank you so much. I'm fascinated by what's happening in Philadelphia and in Pennsylvania. And up next, woke Manhattan D.A. Bragg rewarding his friends, punishing his enemies. We're going to explain it next.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 ALVIN BRAGG\uc2 , DISTRICT ATTORNEY, MANHATTAN: While this defendant may be unlike any other in American history, we arrived at this trial and ultimately today at this verdict in the same manner as every other case that comes to the courtroom doors, by following the facts and the law and doing so without fear or favor.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Alvin without fear or favor. Bragg using that novel legal theory to convict the political opponent of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in New York last month. And his office is now dropping nearly all cases against those racist \uc2 Columbia University\uc2  anti-Israel protesters. Now as a reminder here's what these lovely people were like.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CROWD: Free, free Palestine.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Free, free, free Palestine.\par \par \uc2 CROWD: Free, free, free Palestine.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: There is only revolution.\par \par \uc2 CROWD: There is only one revolution.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Intifada revolution.\par \par \uc2 CROWD: Intifada revolution.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: We are \uc2 Hamas\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: You're \uc2 Hamas\uc2 . Wow. That's good one. You're what? You're \uc2 Hamas\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Yes, we're all \uc2 Hamas\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: She's arrested just for banging that thing against the -- well, it took over Hamilton Hall, it was a complete nightmare, but rewarding your friends, punishing your enemies isn't just a New York philosophy. In D.C., liberal pro-\uc2 Hamas\uc2  protesters who defaced statues and rioted outside the White House were rewarded with zero arrest. Remember that police officer also got pelted with water bottles.\par \par \uc2 In California, the Marin County D.A. reduced charges after a Catholic Junipero Serra statue was vandalized. And remember this visual of migrants storming the border. Well, you think, something, something would have happened to them. Nope. All charges dismissed.\par \par \uc2 Former Justice Scalia and Justice Thomas law clerk, former U.S. ambassador to Mexico and attorney extraordinaire, Chris Landau joins me now. Chris, great to see you tonight. This is really quite something. This group of \uc2 Hamas\uc2  protesters takes over, they commandeer that Hamilton Hall at Columbia throw the whole campus into chaos. And I think to myself, Chris, imagine if these were a bunch of MAGA supporting students if there are any at Columbia. And imagine if they had taken over kind of the Muslim students center or any Center at Columbia, what do you think \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2  would have done to them?\par \par \uc2 CHRIS LANDAU, FORMER SCALIA AND THOMAS LAW CLERK: Laura, this is a real problem. And these Soros D.A.'s like \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2  are really undermining the rule of law in this country. I mean, the rule of law depends on having certain laws that people can understand that can conform their conduct to the law, and that those laws are enforced even handedly.\par \par \uc2 What we're seeing right now is a massive under enforcement of the law. I mean, these people are obviously breaking the law by trespassing, by doing all kinds of other things that are clearly illegal and unlawful and the D.A.s aren't prosecuting. I mean, that's the way our system works. The legislators make the laws, but the executive branch has the obligation to enforce them. And now we're seeing that that's not happening.\par \par \uc2 And so, what's happening now, is that we're seeing the selective enforcement of the law, will that come up -- as you just said, with his novel theory to go after President Trump, while at the same time, they're ignoring all of this lawlessness that's taking over the streets of our country.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: And we wonder why the West Coast is suffering from a major exodus in most major cities there. I mean, if people want to live in safety, people want laws evenly applied and it's obvious that criminals know they can get away with it. So, they go into a LEGO store and take out $2,000 with a merchandise or any store, they know they're going to be able to get away with it and ANTIFA for the most part knows it's going to be able to get away with what they do. And so, they keep doing it. It's not that complicated.\par \par \uc2 LANDAU: Laura, it's really sad. I mean, I'm an ambassador, I'm a lawyer, I'm used to be ambassador, as you said to Mexico, one of the great things about our country that we can be so proud of. And the reason people would want to come here is that we traditionally have been a country of the law, where you didn't see this kind of brazen disregard for the law, go completely unpunished.\par \par \uc2 In fact, we're rewarded in some of these circumstances. It's very disturbing. And, you know, I hope the American people are starting to see with their own eyes what's going on here, because I have to say --\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Chris, it also seems -- excuse me that that the \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2 's office doesn't want \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to really discuss his case at the debate. I don't even think he should spend a lot of time on his case. I think he should talk about the American public and issues that people care about, but -- he's pushing for an extension of this gag order. Now, he's already been sentenced, Chris, what is this?\par \par \uc2 LANDAU: It makes no sense, Laura. I mean, the whole justification for the gag order was not to influence the jury or witnesses or anything like that. At this point, this is just naked election interference. What does \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2  have with this unprecedented gag order? I mean, this is really spinning out of control. And I just think it's undermining respect for the rule of law.\par \par \uc2 I have to say, I think the courts have to start taking these selective prosecution cases very seriously now, because traditionally it's been very hard to show that you're a victim of selective prosecution, but I think what we're seeing with our own eyes and ears that the courts are going to have to start addressing that in saying, no, no, you can't do this.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: That is a great point. They need to feel the pain on the legal side. Chris, excellent point. Of course. I wish I thought of it. Chris Landau, always great to see you. All right. And what can we really expect from the Trump-Biden debate? And why is Raymond making a wish for \uc2 Michelle Obama\uc2 , Friday Follies with Raymond Arroyo is next.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 KEVIN CORKE, FOX NEWS HOST: Hi, everybody, I'm Kevin Corke. This is a Fox News update. A trip to the grocery store turns deadly for shoppers in a small Arkansas town. Three people are dead after a gunman opened fire outside of a store in Fordyce.\par \par \uc2 Police say at least 13 others are injured, two law enforcement officers among those hurt. Their injuries not considered to be life-threatening. Suspect was taken into custody following a shootout with state police. No word yet on a potential motive.\par \par \uc2 No relief yet for millions of people suffering from the sweltering heat. Heat domes sending temperatures soaring into the 90s in the Northeast. It's expected to last, by the way, through the weekend. Maybe a bit of relief at the start of next week.\par \par \uc2 Meantime, there are heat warnings and advisories in effect for the Northeast, Mid-Atlantic and some states out west. Heat being blamed for at least two deaths in Idaho. I'm Kevin Corke in Washington. Now back to the Ingraham Angle.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Yeah, it's Friday. That means it's time for Friday Follies. Oh, my voice just croaked. For that we turn to Fox News contributor Raymond Arroyo. All right, Raymond, this early CNN presidential debate. OK, this is shaping up, I guess, to be one of the major moments of the election. And Biden is taking seven days to prepare.\par \par \uc2 RAYMOND ARROYO, FOX NEWS CONTRIBUTOR: Laura, prize fighters don't go off the grid this long before a bout. But what intrigues me is the expectations narrative coming out of the White House.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: This is going to be a robust preparation led by his former chief of staff, \uc2 Ron Klain\uc2 . I'm also told that we should expect some surprises as well, because this is such a critical performance for President Biden, not only on the content, but on his physical performance as well.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Surprise.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: What?\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: It is a surprise in his physical performance, Laura? Now, look, look at the shuffle this poor man has at Camp David on his way the other day. He looks like Tim Conway as a little old man. And -- but they're promising some physical feat, Laura. He can barely lift his feet or himself into an SUV at this point. I mean, come on.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well, I think \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's got to be careful here, because if Biden has a