ORTAGUS, FORMER STATE DEPARTMENT SPOKESPERSON: Yes. When I saw the first lady saying that about her husband, I just thought, well, bless her heart. And those of you who are watching from the south know that that was not a compliment when I said that.\par \par \uc2 When I say that, I mean, listen, there is no convincing people. People are able to see things like him freezing up at the ceremony, the pictures that you showed. I'm less worried about these gaffes. I mean, sure, it's weird to see him wandering off during the \uc2 G7\uc2  meeting and it's weird to see these gaffes. But I'm much more concerned about whether he has the strong control and authority that we need in a president.\par \par \uc2 And I can tell you, as I look around the world at the national security threats, at wars erupting in almost every theater, of America losing its ability to influence -- listen, we can't even get five Americans home. Eight months later, they have been held captive by a terrorist organization in Gaza. It's been eight months, and we can't get five Americans home. That is endemic to me of what going on around the world and how President Biden -- listen, he may wander off during these events. He may look frozen, all of that stuff, does it matter? Sure. What matters a lot more is that he is not in control of this country or on the world stage. And it's evident to everybody.\par \par \uc2 GALLAGHER: It's interesting to me, Byron York, because you look at the media this week and everybody is kind of on the same page, all talking about Trump's age. Maybe because it's birthday week. But I find it kind of funny where you have the Biden-Harris campaign putting out this picture of the former president wishing him a happy 78th birthday. One, the picture could not be any worse. It just couldn't be any worse. And then they go and take a few swipes at him at the same time. What do you think?\par \par \uc2 BYRON YORK, FOX NEWS CONTRIBUTOR: I think they don't really mean it. They are actually close in age. I mean, Trump has just turned 78 and Biden is 81. And both men, by the way, would tell you that the number, their numerical age is not the big deal. And certainly, in the campaign, the word "age" has been taken by everybody as shorthand for whether a candidate has the physical and the mental ability and stamina to handle the job until 2029. And I think most voters, if you look at the polls, most voters say Trump has a lot more physical and mental stamina than Biden does. That's just all there is to it.\par \par \uc2 And this is something, the big thing is, this is something that people see for themselves. They don't have to read a secret report about it. They can see it right in front of them.\par \par \uc2 GALLAGHER: Right. But you look at this, Francesca, and for weeks and weeks you have seen the Democrats kind of avoid the whole age thing and not talk about it, and suddenly it's all they talk about, only they are talking about it from the other candidates' position.\par \par \uc2 FRANCESCA CHAMBERS, "\uc2 USA TODAY\uc2 ": And President Biden has actually made a number of jokes about his own age on the campaign trail. But former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has said when he has attacked \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  that it's been competence, and that's what he thinks is the problem, because, as Byron was just noting, he is 78, and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is 81 years old. And so there is not a large age gap at this point in between the two. And so he has chosen to focus on other issues.\par \par \uc2 GALLAGHER: Yes, we talk a lot about the economy. We talk about the border, Morgan Ortagus. Clearly, abortion is a top issue in a lot of aspects. The Gallup poll says this, and you put this up on the screen here, it talks about only vote for the candidate who shares your abortion views, and right now you have record numbers of people saying that, OK, 32 percent will do just that. What do you think?\par \par \uc2 ORTAGUS: Listen, the poll speaks for itself. I think you are going to see President Biden and the Democrats running hard on this issue going into November. They also have to lean into this issue because they don't have a winning record to talk about. As I just said, there is chaos and war in every theater. We know that, listen, even if inflation does come down, there's still the residual effect. People still, the price of bananas, the prices of peanut butter, the price of milk, that's still incredibly high for a lot of people, as is gas prices.\par \par \uc2 So I think you have to run on abortion when you really don't have a record of accomplishment or a feeling from the American people that you are in charge and that you are in control.\par \par \uc2 GALLAGHER: We talked about President Biden having an audience with the Pope today, Byron York. But two years ago, Pope Francis took a swipe at \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's abortion views. Quoting here, Pope Francis said the president should check his conscience and consult his bishop or his parish week. And of course, it comes the same week when a CNN analyst says that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is the most Christian president in her lifetime.\par \par \uc2 YORK: Abortion turned out to be an issue at the \uc2 G7\uc2 , kind of a collision between American politics and Italian politics. There was a final statement from the 2023 \uc2 G7\uc2  that supported access to abortion. And Biden just wanted that the to be repeated in this statement, and the new leader of Italy did not. And they took the word "abortion" out. Biden had threatened, actually, not sign it if they did that. But they essentially reaffirmed their commitment to last year's statement, so they found a diplomatic way out of it. But it was really interesting to see how powerful this issue is domestically for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  that he takes it to the \uc2 G7\uc2  as well.\par \par \uc2 GALLAGHER: Meantime, tomorrow is the big Hollywood fundraiser for Biden. "Politico" writes the following, "Next up, a star studded June 15th fundraiser in Los Angeles where late night TV host \uc2 Jimmy Kimmel\uc2  with interview \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and his predecessor \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  along with special guests \uc2 George Clooney\uc2 , Julia Roberts. It's the latest indication that Hollywood, long a significant part of the Democratic coalition, is beginning to focus its attention on an election where Biden has consistently trailed in the polls." Trump also pulled a bunch of money out of California, Francesca.\par \par \uc2 CHAMBERS: And President Biden had been ahead in fundraising so far in the election. But now that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is the presumptive Republican nominee and he has been able to work more closely with the \uc2 Republican National Committee\uc2 , he has been able to boost his fundraising for the general election campaign. And so President Biden is now going to California to pick up this money. I expect that we'll see some other major glitzy fundraisers in the new future as well for him to try and to get that boost back up again.\par \par \uc2 GALLAGHER: Interesting, \uc2 Kayleigh McEnany\uc2  was talking about in comparing \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and the fundraiser with \uc2 George Clooney\uc2 , and then you have the former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in California, the fundraiser with Logan Paul. Watch this.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 KAYLEIGH MCENANY\uc2 , FORMER WHITE HOUSE PRESS SECRETARY: The Clooneys represent kind of an old Hollywood. Logan and these podcasters, this is the new fame that Gen Z is appealing to, that Gen Z is tuning into. And that's where Trump is. He's meeting voters where they are and bringing a fun message, and he's out on TikTok, which is a great thing.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 GALLAGHER: Very quickly, Morgan, we've got Winners and Losers to get to.\par \par \uc2 ORTAGUS: Yes, listen, I would just say Kayleigh is right. I had to \uc2 Google\uc2  Logan Paul, or Paul Logan, whatever his name is.\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 ORTAGUS: It's a new demographic for sure. But what's important about this is that he is reaching these young people, and that's not something the Biden campaign can do.\par \par \uc2 GALLAGHER: So apparently we're not getting winners. Byron York, give us your thoughts on this Logan Paul and \uc2 George Clooney\uc2  comparison.\par \par \uc2 YORK: Well, look, Democrats have owned Hollywood forever and ever. When \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  was inaugurated in 2009, the entire entertainment industry came to Washington to celebrate. So, I mean this is absolutely nothing new.\par \par \uc2 What is interesting is that there is a large class of new influencers, people who really can reach large audiences, mostly of younger people, and Trump is working on that. Sometimes that's a little bit smarter, especially when Hollywood doesn't support you to begin with.\par \par \uc2 GALLAGHER: Yes. Byron, Francesca, Morgan, thank you.\par \par \uc2 It is Friday. It is time for "Notable Quotables."\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 , (D) PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: I wish you guys would play by the rules a little bit.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: He is thumbing his nose at us.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  has been found guilty.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: This case was about the illegal choices the defendant made while in the throes of addiction.\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: I will not pardon him.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: What they got \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  on was lying on a gun form. It would be like getting Jeffrey Dahmer for littering.\par \par \uc2 DONALD TRUMP\uc2 , FORMER U.S. PRESIDENT: Do I stay on top of the boat and get executed, or do I jump over by the shark and not get electrocuted.\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: She knows -- so long -- denied.\par \par \uc2 KAMALA HARRIS\uc2 , (D) VICE PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: Get yours if that's what you want, right?\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is the best insurance policy for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  because she is maybe be the only person who would be even worse at it than he is.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Eight nationals of Tajikistan with suspected ties to \uc2 ISIS\uc2  were all arrested.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: It's frightening, and we're headed for another 9/11.\par \par \uc2 SEN. \uc2 MITCH MCCONNELL\uc2 , (R-KY) SENATE MINORITY LEADER: Unhinged throngs of \uc2 Hamas\uc2  apologists occupied Lafayette Square.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: These idiots call my name as fanny.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: I call her Fani Wade.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: All these cars are abandoned.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: No bueno, right?\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: No, no, no.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Price of gas, food, it's just hard.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : We're going to drill, baby, drill.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Cheers to lowering energy costs.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: The Senate stands adjourned until 3:00 p.m. on Monday, bang gavel.\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 GALLAGHER: Monday on SPECIAL REPORT, our space series examines the James Webb telescope and how it has contributed to technology advancements here on earth.\par \par \uc2 Please join Shannon Bream for FOX NEWS SUNDAY. Her guests include North Dakota Governor and perspective vice presidential nominee \uc2 Doug Burgum\uc2  along with House Intel Committee Ranking Member \uc2 Jim Himes\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 And remember, if you cannot catch us live, set your DVR, 6:00 p.m. eastern, 3:00 p.m. on the west coast.\par \par \uc2 Thank you for watching SPECIAL REPORT. I'm Trace Gallagher in Los Angeles. Please join me tonight, FOX NEWS AT NIGHT, 11:00 p.m. in the east, 8:00 on the west. We will take a much closer look at \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 's claim that he is sending National Guard troops to the border.\par \par \uc2 Meantime, THE INGRAHAM ANGLE is next. Have a great weekend.\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2024 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2024 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document FNSPBB0020240615ek6e00001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 Americans Embarrasses America On The World Stage\b0\par\par\uc2 Sean Hannity, Tomi Lahren \par \uc2 7,841 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 June 2024\par \uc2 Fox News: Hannity\par \uc2 SHAN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2024 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2024 ASC Services II Media, LLC.  All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 SEAN HANNITY\uc2 , FOX NEWS HOST: Welcome to "Hannity".\par \par \uc2 And tonight, the left's egregious lawfare against President Trump, it is now falling apart under even a minimal amount of scrutiny. Coming up, we're going to show you a bizarre moment from disgraced former Trump prosecutor Nathan Wade during a bizarre interview on fake news CNN.\par \par \uc2 Also, outrage as Biden blocks a pay raise for the troops after handing out billions to you know the those overeducated social science major people at Ivy League institutions with their massive student loan bailouts and few real world skills.\par \par \uc2 But we begin tonight in Europe where Joe spent the day humiliating himself and us on behalf of America on the world stage yet again. He's in Italy for the 50th G7 Summit, not going particularly well. Joe started the summit by awkwardly kissing Italy's Prime Minister Georgia Meloni on the head, sniffing her hair at one moment seemingly. Then he saluted Meloni before shuffling away.\par \par \uc2 Then during a parachute demonstration, Biden got dazed and confused, how shocking, and started to just you know wander off like that, as other \uc2 G7\uc2  leaders looked on in agony, desperate for somebody to bring Joe back into the fold. Luckily, Italy's Prime Minister very graciously helped Biden get back to the group.\par \par \uc2 And during the summit, Biden also somehow mustered the energy for a speech, but unfortunately, he got distracted by a plane flying overhead. Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 , PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: They include key parts of Russia's financial sector. I'll wait until it goes over. As well as individual and entities that supply Russian with item critical to its defense production, like micro econ -- like micro electronics, machine tools and industrial materials.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. That was part of a joint speech with Ukrainian Prime Minister Zelenskyy. And after those remarks, Biden allowed questions from four reporters, two from the U.S., two from Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Of course, reporters were selected ahead of time, let's start with -- so and so from the "AP". And then the questions appeared to be pre-scripted as per usual, and then something pretty remarkable happened. One reporter from "\uc2 Bloomberg\uc2 " actually dared to go off script, causing Biden to become very, very annoyed. It's not supposed to work like this.\par \par \uc2 Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 REPORTER: Thank you, Mr. President. I have a question for Mr. President Zelenskyy shortly on the announcements but if you don't mind I'd like to ask you about your discussions on the situation in Gaza here at the summit. You were asked just a short time ago about it after the skydiving demonstration. Can you give us your assessment of \uc2 Hamas\uc2 's response? And do you believe that they are trying to work towards a deal or is this response working against a deal? And what is your message to allies including those here at the \uc2 G7\uc2  about what more if anything the U.S. can do to drive towards a peace agreement? Thank you.\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: I wish you guys would a little play by the -- by the rules in a little bit. I'm here to talk about a critical situation in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: The way you treat Israel versus the way you treat Ukraine, the rhetoric you use about Ukraine versus the rhetoric you use about Israel -- yeah, that would be a relevant question. How dare this reporter though not ask the question that is preapproved by the Biden White House?\par \par \uc2 Of course, the compliant media mob that's supposed to stick to the script and, of course, Joe doesn't want you talking about Israel and in order to turn out his radical base, he seems to feel the need to trash America strongest ally in the Middle East after the worst terror attack in their history and do what? Put restrictions on Israel's war for its very survival against terrorists that, oh, let's see, have in their charter the destruction of the entire state of Israel and they want to force them out of the Middle East? And by the way, eight Americans, Joe, they're still being held hostage in Gaza.\par \par \uc2 But Joe would rather talk about his little proxy war with Russia. According to Biden, that is far more pressing. After years and years of fighting, Joe now wants to give Ukraine pretty much whatever they want so they can fight their war against Putin. Meanwhile, it's really America versus Putin, while he put hand -- he's putting handcuffs on Israel. He's barely lifting a finger to get any of our hostages home.\par \par \uc2 So far, the U.S. has committed $174 billion taxpayer to Ukraine in their war against Russia while allocating am measly $12.6 billion to Israel after the October 7th terrorist attack by the Islamic terrorist group \uc2 Hamas\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Now, for Biden, this is all political, as per usual. His radical base, they call the shots. He's merely an empty vessel comp -- you know, that complies with their demands. The radicals run that party. Ultimately, nothing will satisfy their blood lust against Israel and capitalism.\par \par \uc2 They want modern civilization basically to cease to exist as we know it. They want it replaced with radical Marxism, socialism, and they frankly don't like the principles on which this country was created. They hate our system. They hate our way of life.\par \par \uc2 And \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is desperately needing their vote. The Democratic party as it once was no longer exists. They're a party of radicals they're in shambles we see chaos everywhere, success pretty much nowhere.\par \par \uc2 There are far left protests every day. At nearly every single event, including last night's congressional baseball game. There are also prominent Democrats now trashing \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and his mental decline. They're doing it behind the scenes and if they get a little too loud, they get brought in and lectured.\par \par \uc2 Biden is even losing thousands of votes in the uncontested Democratic primary to uncommitted, hundreds of thousands of votes he's lost.\par \par \uc2 This is what happens when the person at the top is barely able to walk and talk, much less lead his party and adapts the most radical policies in the history of the country, to give into the radical base of his party.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, it is a very different story over the GOP. Today, former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was warmly greeted on Capitol Hill during what was a joint meeting with Congress. The Republican Party is now rallying around President Trump and his plan to fix the border to end the weaponization of justice, to end lawfare, to restore fairness to our justice system, to fight violent crime, to lower inflation, lowering the cost of energy, reduce taxes, increase energy production, spur yet another American boom like never before.\par \par \uc2 Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 DONALD TRUMP\uc2 , FORMER U.S. PRESIDENT & 2024 PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE: Well, thank you very much. This was a great meeting. There's tremendous unity in the Republican Party.\par \par \uc2 We want to see borders. We want to see strong military. We want to see money not wasted all over the world. We don't want to see Russian ships right off the coast of Florida which is what they are right now, that's unthinkable.\par \par \uc2 We want to see just success for our country. And we don't have success right now. We have inflation that's killing everybody. We have levels of inflation that nobody seen for they say 42 years, they say 53 years and they say 75 years. I would say probably all of them are wrong, probably we've never seen levels like this before.\par \par \uc2 And we're going to end that, we're going to bring back our jobs we're going to bring back common sense to government we're going to have strong borders and we're going to have people come into our country but they're going to come illegally. They're not going to pour in from prisons all over South America, and all over the world, and it's not just south America, by the way. It's all over the world.\par \par \uc2 And we're not going to have them pour in from mental institutions which is where they're coming from, large numbers and large numbers are terrorists, and we're not going to have this. So what's happening to our country is of great concern to the group of people standing alongside of me, and I just wanted to say that we have great unity. We have great common.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Joining us now, someone who was inside that closed door meeting on Capitol Hill. He's the speaker of the House, Mike Johnson is with us.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Speaker, welcome back. Great to have you.\par \par \uc2 Can we just settle one thing once and for all here? Did President Trump -- it's been attributed to him that he took a shot at Milwaukee. Did you hear that?\par \par \uc2 REP. MIKE JOHNSON (R-LA), SPEAKER OF THE HOUSE: No. I didn't hear it and I was sitting right next to him. I introduced him this morning at breakfast where he started the day.\par \par \uc2 He spoke for an hour without notes, Sean. He can stand up there and hold court as long he wants. As you know, President Trump is on his A-game.\par \par \uc2 And I'm telling you, in the room this morning, there was energy, enthusiasm, excitement. We had colleagues in there, Sean, who were commenting after his visit was this morning, the House Republicans, that -- that they haven't been this excited about the future of our country in 40 years. That's what one of my colleagues told me.\par \par \uc2 Look, there's a palpable energy. In his words, something said this morning, he said: Something is happening in America and we see it. There's a demographic shift going on and all these different segments of the population.\par \par \uc2 We're headed for a great November. We have to run like we're ten points behind, but I'm convinced \uc2 Donald J. Trump\uc2  is going to get a second term as president. We're going to retake the Republican majority in the Senate and we're going to grow the House majority in the House, and that's going to be a good day for America.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: If you go issue by issue, if you go to law and order, you go to the economy, if you go to immigration, if you go to America's rule on the world stage, I don't see where the Democrats run on any policy of success.\par \par \uc2 Let's start at the border. Let's start at the fact that we've