pe -- and eventually I pray to God I'm wrong, if a terror attack happens by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's unvetted illegal immigrants and his open border policies now on 11 million unvetted in this country, he's got blood on his hands.\par \par \uc2 What did President Trump specifically say he will do on the border? I'm assuming he probably said just to go back to the policies that were working when he left office.\par \par \uc2 JOHNSON: Yeah, that's the whole thing.\par \par \uc2 See, President Trump is a bold leader and he understood. He ran on the border. He reminded us back in 2015 -- border, border, border, because he saw this disaster coming.\par \par \uc2 And he got control of it, because he used his authority. He used executive orders for the right policies. They -- he instituted "remain in Mexico" where people had to stay on the other side of the border to adjudicate their claims for asylum. That's a no-brainer.\par \par \uc2 The Border Patrol agents have told us and the leaders of that agency said if President Biden would just issue that executive order "remain in Mexico" again, we can reduce the flow by 70 percent at the border.\par \par \uc2 But he will not do it, Sean. You know why? You and I know why, because they want the open border, because they want to turn these people into voters. And we're working hard to prevent that from happening as well. So many problems.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. So -- what did the -- what did the president say he'd do on the economy? What did he say he'd do with Israel, with Ukraine? What did the president say that he would do to get energy prices down and get -- you know, get the American people, get money back in their pocket?\par \par \uc2 JOHNSON: Well, a lot, on all those fronts.\par \par \uc2 With regard to the economy, we've got to revive the American economy again and we know how to do it because you and I both know, after the first couple of years of the Trump administration, we had the greatest economy in the history of the world, not just the U.S.\par \par \uc2 Why? Because we implemented policies that we've all always believed in. We reduced the regulatory burden on job creators, innovators, entrepreneurs, to allow the economy to thrive, and we reduced taxes on job creators as well, and the hard-working families.\par \par \uc2 We've got to make those tax cuts permanent because they're going to expire soon and that will be the largest tax increase in U.S. history if we don't fix it next year. And we've got to get to -- getting the regulatory state under control.\par \par \uc2 Under \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , they've weaponized agencies and smothered American business and the free market.\par \par \uc2 We can reverse that. President Trump is ready to do it.\par \par \uc2 He's got so many plans, we can spend all night talking about it. We're excited to implement those things and I think we're going to get a chance.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Ninety-five days, Congressman, early voting starts in Pennsylvania, 95 days from tonight.\par \par \uc2 Speaker Johnson, thank you.\par \par \uc2 All right. Joining us now is South Carolina Senator \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Senator, an awful lot of money has been spent in Ukraine. It seems in many ways that that has devolved into a proxy war between \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  versus Putin or the U.S. versus Russia.\par \par \uc2 American people are pretty angry about it. They're angry that Europe has not stepped up financially to protect their own continent enough, and then you got what $12 billion, that's it, that goes to Israel. But even worse than that, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will not allow Israel to fight the war they need to win against radical Islamic terrorists that slaughtered them on October 7th, took their own citizens hostage, Americans hostage, and he's lecturing \uc2 Bibi Netanyahu\uc2  the entire time. He's not helping at all.\par \par \uc2 And the worst part is, he says the U.S. won't help in terms of offensively helping to win 