resident has identified every problem that he could when he was running in 2020, and his solution spend more money. Now that it comes time for us to share with those young men and women who are willing to put their lives on the line, this president suddenly doesn't want to spend. You can't be this wrong by accident.\par \par \uc2 Now, with regard to these other concerns, many Black Americans are complaining that this president's priorities have everything to do with the cocktail hour in the professor's lounge and absolutely nothing to do with their real lives. It is a amazing how many Hispanics are saying they're no longer willing to support this president and his party.\par \par \uc2 We're looking at an election where it is possible that a Republican may win the Hispanic vote for the first time. You're seeing the young vote, you're seeing the women's vote, you're seeing so many areas where this president's poor stewardship of the economy, prioritizing all of the progressive agenda over the needs of mainstream America, and it's no surprise that you're seeing Americans complain across the board.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Why is -- why is it okay for China to have a spy balloon or China to -- you know, be saber rattling, you know, hostile maneuvers against our fighter jets and international airspace, hostile maneuvers against our navy in international waterways. Now, we've got uh Russia with a sub nuclear arm we believe, with hypersonic missiles.\par \par \uc2 Why isn't that a bigger deal, Congressman?\par \par \uc2 WALTZ: Well, because at the end of the day, you have a -- you have an administration that has a concessions based approach, and you've got -- you've had \uc2 John Kerry\uc2  leading the delegation over to China the last three years begging them to do more on climate which they know they could take advantage of and then continue their nuclear buildup, their space buildup, their military buildup. I mean, this crew is asleep at the switch, Sean, and it's going t