 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BREAM: What do you make of the back and forth, Tammy?\par \par \uc2 BRUCE: Look, I mean, Trump has said, even before about Hillary, when asked specifically about the, you know, put her in jail line, is that that would be too divisive. This has been a consistent position of his for - for years now. At no point has he made an - create an action or - or made a point of saying, I'm going to be a dictator or I'm going to throw everyone in jail. It's been the opposite.\par \par \uc2 And then, of course, you've got the left using media to try to gaslight people. The fact of the matter is, Biden has joked about defying the Supreme Court on the student loan decision. He's joked about that. Only President Trump is the one who's been in - you know, on trial and faces being put in prison, which many, including I, think that they will, in fact, try to incarcerate him in some fashion.\par \par \uc2 So, it seems a little bit like projection, considering the nature of what's been going on. And I - I think it's a shame. But I - the American people can see the difference. And Trump has been vocal about this consistently, what they're saying is simply not true.\par \par \uc2 BREAM: OK, before we go, we only have a couple of seconds, does \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  testify next week? I don't think he does. Do you? Anybody?\par \par \uc2 BRUCE: No.\par \par \uc2 ZELDIN: Well, I think he should.\par \par \uc2 BREAM: You do? OK, but, no?\par \par \uc2 BRUCE: Well, he's the second greatest liar of all time. So, no.\par \par \uc2 BREAM: Oh, boy. OK.\par \par \uc2 FORD: He might.\par \par \uc2 BREAM: We'll see what the jury thinks about that. And, you know, his - his father saying this week he is not planning to pardon him.\par \par \uc2 OK, panel, thank you very much.\par \par \uc2 Coming up, I'm going to introduce you to an Israeli man who survived the October 7th attacks. He was huddled with his family in a safe room as friends and family members were murdered and kidnapped. Hear about his mission to get all the remaining hostages home from Gaza now.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 BREAM: The stunning good news this weekend about the four hostages rescued in Gaza once again highlighting the fact that \uc2 Hamas\uc2  is still holding more than 100 people taken on October 7th.\par \par \uc2 I talked with Naor Pakciarz this week, a survivor of the October 7th \uc2 Hamas\uc2  attacks, who lost his father-in-law and many friends and is now fighting to get the remaining hostages home, including several from his own community.\par \par \uc2 We spoke before the news of this weekend's courageous rescue. It's this week's "Sunday Special."\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 BREAM: How are you doing? Several months out, but still very fresh.\par \par \uc2 NAOR PAKCIARZ, OCTOBER 7TH SURVIVOR: First - first of all, thanks for - for letting me speak here.\par \par \uc2 And difficult times. I think we live in difficult times. And for the last eight months I live in a hotel. It's not so easy. In a very small room with my four kids and my wife and actually with my dog. But it doesn't matter because we think only about our 125 people from Israel that are still in Gaza kidnapped, and 11 of them are our community, our family.\par \par \uc2 So, these are - this is the hardest event, this is the hardest thing to do.\par \par \uc2 BREAM: And not knowing for sure.\par \par \uc2 PAKCIARZ: Not knowing.\par \par \uc2 BREAM: So, I want to ask about too about both your ribbon and - and the necklace that you have that we, in the U.S., would call it a dog tag, but I think it's very similar in Israeli culture what it is.\par \par \uc2 PAKCIARZ: Yes, so in Israel we call this - this (INAUDIBLE). When you serve the army, you get one with your number, with your personal number in the army. And now we hear in English it says, "bring them home now." And in Hebrew which - it says (Speaking in Foreign Language), which means, our heart is kidnapped to Gaza. The yellow ribbon is a symbol, again, to be with the kidnapped people and their families and their friends as a symbol of empathize with them and so they will know that we're thinking about them all day long, all the time.\par \par \uc2 BREAM: It's incredible difficult. And people who were taken, some of those have not survived, as we know, that we continue to find out there are hostages who have not survived their captivity with \uc2 Hamas\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 What is your message here in the U.S. as you visit?\par \par \uc2 PAKCIARZ: We need to get help from everyone we can. First of all - first of all, to bring everybody home.\par \par \uc2 BREAM: What do you make of the conversations that are ongoing, because there have been some releases. Can Israel negotiate with \uc2 Hamas\uc2  over these things? Are they a reliable actor in these negotiations?\par \par \uc2 PAKCIARZ: I think that one of the problem that we have is that we have some targets, not one. And when you have some targets, it's very difficult to know what you do first. So I think that the Israeli government thinks that we need first to win the war. I don't know what it is. I think we lost the war on the 7th of October. We lost that fight. We lost the battle. But to win the war, it's, first of all, bring the citizens back. It's not soldiers, it's citizens, civilians, they were taken from their homes. So, to win the war, first bring them back. Then we'll deal with Gaza.\par \par \uc2 BREAM: Can you envision a future - you - you grew up there.\par \par \uc2 PAKCIARZ: Yes.\par \par \uc2 BREAM: I mean right there on the board with Gaza your entire life. Can you envision a future post-war in which you can live peacefully and feel safe on that border?\par \par \uc2 PAKCIARZ: I hope so because - I'm an optimistic, OK? So, we need to change something. I still don't know what. But I know that we can go and live the same way we live.\par \par \uc2 Now when my kids hear a siren, for example, they think that the terrorists are going to come. We are refugees in our own country. I don't know when I'm going to go back. It will take time physically and mentally. But when we are going to go back, and we want to go back, OK, we're lot leaving. This is our land. This is our home.\par \par \uc2 BREAM: Do you feel - do the Israeli people feel supported by the Americans?\par \par \uc2 PAKCIARZ: I want to think, yes. I think, yes. The majority thinks that the United States, you help us very much. I met with many, many people these last few days, from the Congress, the Senate. And I feel the love and I feel that - that we're together in this occasion, because it's not justified a fight between Israel and \uc2 Hamas\uc2 . It between - it's between good and bad. Good and evil.\par \par \uc2 BREAM: Thank you for sharing your story with us. We appreciate it.\par \par \uc2 PAKCIARZ: Thank you.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 BREAM: Since we sat down with Naor, we, of course, learned of the amazing rescue of those four hostages in Gaza. So, he sent us a statement. He says, "we're very happy that four of our captives were rescued by the \uc2 IDF\uc2 , yet we must remember that the job is not done. We're still missing 120 hostages that we need to bring back home fast. We continue to call upon the international community for help until all our families are back home."\par \par \uc2 We thank him for his time.\par \par \uc2 Just a quick note. My podcast is out, "Livin' the Bream," this morning. It drops - it's - I sat down with Tonya Prewett. She wanted to give hope to some students on the Auburn campus, where her husband's a basketball coach. It led to a gathering that has sparked revival on numerous college campuses across the south. How it happened and where they're going next, "Livin' the Bream," anywhere you like to get your podcasts. You'll get the story.\par \par \uc2 That's it for today. Thanks for joining us. I'm Shannon Bream. Have a wonderful week. We'll see you next FOX NEWS SUNDAY.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2024 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2024 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document FOXN000020240609ek6900001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 Peace With Trump, War With Biden; The Left's Deflection Game; Biden Will Not Pardon Hunter If He's Convicted; Prosecutors Say Gilgo Beach Murder Suspect Kept Notes; Trump Team Actively Vetting VP Contenders; How Will Biden Defend His Disastrous Record; Laura's Debate Advise For Trump; Report Says CNN To Run Commercials During Debate; Why More Money For A Woke Military; Military Is Focusing On DEI Instead Of Fighting\b0\par\par\uc2 Laura Ingraham, Bill Melugin, Kevin Corke, Lisa Boothe, Newt  Gingrich, Pete Hegseth \par \uc2 7,715 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 June 2024\par \uc2 Fox News: The Ingraham Angle\par \uc2 INGANG\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2024 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2024 ASC Services II Media, LLC. All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2  (D), PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: Every generation must preserve it, defend it and fight for it.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: American World War II Veterans. You stand relieved. We have the...\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 LAURA INGRAHAM, FOX NEWS HOST: I'm Laura Ingraham. This is The Ingraham Angle from Washington tonight. Thanks so much for joining us. Biden on the cliff. That's the focus of tonight's Angle.\par \par \uc2 It was a beautiful somber setting in France to commemorate the 80th anniversary of D-Day today. The few remaining World War II vets on their final mission. The Biden team hoped that the President's remarks would resonate with voters back home, showcasing him as a Reagan-esque figure who would unite Americans and the rest of the world behind his vision.\par \par \uc2 But the speech they wrote for him merely demonstrated how muddled, unserious and unrealistic their thinking is. First, the Biden folks seem to think that they can convince us that Russia in Ukraine poses the same existential threat to the West, as Germany did in 1944.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: We will not walk away, if we do, Ukraine will be subjugated and will not end there. Ukraine's neighbors will be threatened, all Europe will be threatened. The hour of trial, the allied forces of D-Day did their duty. Now the question for us is and our hour of trial, will we do ours?\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: But this is simply ridiculous. European nations themselves are so unconcerned about the Russian threat that to this day, many of them are not meeting their own targets. Remember that was decided upon back in what 2014 to spend 2 percent of their GDP on defense.\par \par \uc2 Now, under these circumstances, Biden speech comes across as just irresponsibly fear-mongering that could actually end up without getting into a nuclear war with the former Soviet Union, especially the fact that now Biden has authorized that Ukraine can use American weapons to fire into Russia.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Are American weapons being used right now inside Russia?\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: They're authorized to be used in production at the border. we not authorized to these strikes 200 miles into Russia, we did not authorized strikes on Moscow, on the Kremlin.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Oh, thanks. Remember, the 200 mile rule now. That's no problem at all. It's cavalier attitude, given where this can lead, which Putin responded forcefully to yesterday?\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR PUTIN\uc2 , PRESIDENT, RUSSIA (VIA TRANSLATOR): We are thinking that if they consider it possible to deliver such weapons to the combat zone to launch strikes on our territory, and create problems for us, why don't we have the right to supply weapons of the same type to some regions of the world where they can be used to launch strikes on sensitive facilities of the countries that do it to Russia? The answer may be asymmetric.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: This is not good. And the bloodlust in Biden's remarks today is not going to help calm tensions.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: They suffered tremendous losses Russia; the numbers are staggering. 350,000 Russian troops dead or wounded. nearly 1 million people have left Russia, because they can no longer see a future in Russia.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Now contrast that celebration of the bloodshed in this conflict to Trump's call for peace five years ago at Normandy.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: What do you pray for when you pray for this country?\par \par \uc2 DONALD TRUMP\uc2  (R), FORMER U.S. PRESIDENT AND 2024 PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE: Peace, really peace. And we built up our military. we built up our wealth, we built up everything, our country is in such great shape right now. Iran is in a much different position than they were two and a half years ago. Two and a half years ago, Iran was a disaster for us. Now they're -- they've got problems. Let's put it that way. They're not the same country.\par \par \uc2 North Korea, no nuclear tests, have a good will. And we'll see what happens. And we're going to see what happens. China wants to make a deal. Everybody wants to make a deal. We're the best, we're the strongest, there's nobody even close.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Wow. What had changed to, today. Another big problem with Biden's remarks his comments on democracy,\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: Living at a time when democracy is more risk across the world than a point since the end of World War II. Now we have to ask ourselves, will we stand against tyranny, against evil, against crushing brutality of the Iron Fist. we stand for freedom. We defend democracy. We stand together. My answer is yes only can be yes.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: This is nonsense. If we were truly worried about the fate of democracy. Well, Biden himself would be laser focused on the rise of China, which is the only existential threat to democracy around the globe today with the power of China.\par \par \uc2 Instead, his DOJ and his party are focused on putting their political opponents in jail. That's democracy while his cabinet members and big donors fly to Beijing to kiss President Xi's ring. Yes, even future Democrat contenders are in on the China flattery competition.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Expectation, as you suggest of turning the page of renewing our friendship, reengaging foundational and fundamental issues that will determine our collective faith and future.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: For several years now, the Angle has warned the White House that their problems are not communications issues that can be solved with a new speech or a new slogan. We need better policies. And we need to put the Ukraine situation in the right perspective.\par \par \uc2 Putin is a horrible dictator, but he isn't a supreme threat to the United States of America. We need a president who sees our domestic policy that it should be geared toward restoring U.S. manufacturing, and then decoupling us from the communist regime in China, and then reestablishing our ability to once again serve as the arsenal of democracy. That is the peace through strength that President Reagan spoke about.\par \par \uc2 The entire Biden apparatus has it backwards. For them, it will be war through weakness. Divide the country at home, turn Americans against their constitution, their history, spend us into a possible debt levels, leave our southern border open, then ask Americans to sign up to defend Finland and Sweden against Russia.\par \par \uc2 I'm not sure they're going to like the answer, our young people give them about fighting to serve that mission. By trying to draw parallels to Reagan, Biden staff only underscores the extent to which the United States has declined over the past 40 years since Reagan's Pointe du Hoc moment.\par \par \uc2 You can ask yourself, is America stronger now than she was in 1984? No one believes this. It was moronic for them to ever make this comparison. Reagan won 49 states and 525 electoral votes in 1984. We think Biden's going to hit that mark too. These are moments from today that our press will not show you. Biden confused upon arriving at the event.\par \par \uc2 (VIDEO PLAYING)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Biden making sure he follows directions\par \par \uc2 (VIDEO PLAYING)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: You're not supposed to tell people that. Biden gets pulled back by Dr. Jill as Macron greets D-Day vets.\par \par \uc2 (VIDEO PLAYING)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: This is our Commander-in-Chief. If in a Biden's second term, there is a realistic chance that American troops are going to be fighting Russian troops, then President Biden and the White House and the Pentagon, they need to be honest about this now. Listen closely to today's speech and to Blinken's aggressive remarks lately. And you can hear the war drums beating in the background.\par \par \uc2 Biden was on the cliff today. But if he's going to push us over the cliff of war, we should all take that into account come Election Day. And that's the Angle.\par \par \uc2 Joining us now is Victor Davis Hanson, Senior Fellow at the \uc2 Hoover Institution\uc2 . Reagan -- Reagan comparison, Victor, I think we should delve more into that. Here's Reagan in 1984.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 RONALD REAGAN\uc2  (R) 40TH U.S. PRESIDENT: We in America have learned bitter lessons from two world wars. We've learned that isolationism never was and never will be an acceptable response to tyrannical governments within expansionist intent.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: And then Biden today.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: Isolation was not the answer eight years ago. And is not the answer today. We know the dark forces that these heroes fought against 80 years ago. They never fade.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Oh, Victor, Reagan was against isolationism, Biden's against isolationism. So, is the parallel real?\par \par \uc2 VICTOR DAVIS HANSON, SENIOR FELLOW, HOOVER INSTITUTION: No, Reagan spoke from confidence. He knows how quiet he was and determined. He wasn't screaming or yelling. He was a member of that generation. And he was since close to D-Day as he is to Biden. It's a different world. And \uc2 Ronald Reagan\uc2  in that speech actually said to the Russians that we didn't want to war with them, but what he was doing was speaking softly and carrying a big stick.\par \par \uc2 He was ushering in 7 percent economic growth in 1984. He had rebuilt the military, and he was essentially saying to the world, we're very strong, but we're not going to brag about it. We don't want war with you. But it would be a very stupid thing to challenge the United States. Biden, in contrast, is the baby boomer. So, he's