rsal for public transit advocates who had championed the tolls as a way of raising billions of dollars for New York's beleaguered subway and commuter rail systems while reducing traffic in the city streets.\par \par \uc2 WDRB in Louisville as the National Weather Service confirmed seven tornadoes touched down in southern Kentucky last week causing damage more than 255 miles in a 58 County area. That's a record for the state.\par \par \uc2 Five people were killed in the Memorial Day weekend storms and thousands were left without power.\par \par \uc2 And this is a live look at Chicago from our affiliate Fox 32. One of the big stories there tonight, Illinois lottery officials say a Mega Millions ticket worth an estimated $560 million was sold in the state, one ticket. No details have been released on who bought that ticket or at which store. At least not yet.\par \par \uc2 That's tonight's live look outside the Beltway from SPECIAL REPORT. Congratulations. We'll be right back.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 BAIER: There are new warnings tonight about alleged Chinese attempts to recruit top Western military officials. The U.S. Director of National Intelligence along with Australia, Canada, Great Britain, and New Zealand, The Five Eyes, says China is increasingly aggressive in its efforts that potential recruits would be used to train China's military.\par \par \uc2 A Western official tells the Associated Press, Ukraine has used U.S. weapons to strike inside Russia in recent days. The weapons were used under recently approved guidance from President Biden, allowing American arms to be used to strike inside Russia for the limited purpose of defending Kharkiv, Ukraine's second largest city. And does not change U.S. policy that directs Ukraine not to use American provided weapons to strike offensively inside Russia.\par \par \uc2 Speaking of Russia, Russian President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 , says nothing will change in terms of Russia-U.S. relations, regard