at they said would have made it better. And the Border Patrol Council and the agents said they would have taken that deal to try to at least incrementally get better border security. They are akin to taking a piece of what you want. You don't get everything you want, but you get it passed. For example, you had negotiations on police reform --\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: I did.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: -- in September of 2021. You had this statement, saying "After months of making progress, I'm deeply disappointed that Democrats have once again squandered a crucial opportunity to implement meaningful reform. I offered to introduce a bill that included our areas of compromise. Once again, the left let their misguided idea of perfect be the enemy of good, impactful legislation." They would argue, Senator, that that's the same thing happening with this bipartisan piece of legislation that was being negotiated on the border.\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: Well, Bret, let me say in December when that issue was on the table, I think in the month of December we had 300,000 illegal immigrants cross our borders, and the legislation that was being proposed would allow about 5,000 per day. Half of a number is still about 1.6 million illegal immigrants crossing our border. That is not a solution. And, frankly, the number of exempted categories, like unaccompanied minors being exempted, over 500,000 unaccompanied minors have made their way into our country.\par \par \uc2 So you can't take their top number that you see. You have to add back in the categories of illegal immigrants that are allowed to come in without any vetting, without being a part of that number. That's why the number continues to grow even higher when you understand that what they are selling from the sticker, so to speak, is not exactly what's in the details. The details makes that number significantly higher. And it frustrates the American people to have \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  come to a microphone and to pretend to sell a closing of 