All the Senate Democrats have voted, not talked about, but voted for abortion up until the day of birth. The former Virginia governor, Democrat pediatrician, has suggested even infanticide. I'm not making this up, Bret. These are votes taken in our chamber.\par \par \uc2 That tells me very clearly, they are doing every single thing they can to hide from their own voting record. This is an issue we should continue to push because this is an issue where the American people say, wait, abortion up until the day of birth? That's wrong. Infanticide, allowing a child to be born and then letting it die? That's un-American. And so when you hear what \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  suggested --\par \par \uc2 BAIER: You think most Democrats are in that space? Why does he do that vote today on contraception?\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: The polls are clear that they are losing this November election. The day of reckoning is November 5th of this year. They are doing anything they can to try to demonize the Republicans as if we're going to do something as ridiculous as he suggests. He is just wrong. He knows it. The American people can see through it. And we'll continue to push the issues that the American people are focused on and give wide access to everything that today is already available.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Have you talked to the former president about a possible V.P. choice?\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: The only thing I'm talking to the President Trump about is how to make sure he gets four more years. So we have talked a lot about how we continue to reduce inflation so interest rates come down. We have talked a lot about making sure that the unemployment rates for Asians and African- Americans and Hispanics and for women continue to reverberate as they did during his time in office, talking about the majority of the population having a 3.5 percent unemployment rate. We continue to talk about bringing more resources into the poorest communities through our joint work on opportunity zones.\par \par \uc2 I talk a lot with President Trump and his campaign, but we keep the focus not on me, frankly not even on him, but on the American people where it belongs.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Senator Scott, we appreciate the time today. You're welcome back any time.\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: Thank you, Bret.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Up next, the successful launch for a new spaceship. And later, the panel on the Hunter Biden trial, new questions about his father's ability to fulfill his duties as president.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 BAIER: You're looking at a live image of earth from the International Space Station. Two American astronauts are on their way there right now after the long awaited first crewed launch of the new Starliner spacecraft went off without a problem this morning. Correspondent Jonathan Serrie watched the launch from Kennedy Space Center in Florida.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO TAPE)\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN SERRIE, FOX NEWS CORRESPONDENT: After months of delays and two scrubbed launch attempts, \uc2 Boeing\uc2 's Starliner lifted off from Florida's space coast with astronauts Butch Wilmore and Suni Williams on board.\par \par \uc2 BILL NELSON, NASA ADMINISTRATOR: Now Butch and Suni do what they do best. They're test pilots. And they are going to test this thing from izzard to gizzard.\par \par \uc2 SERRIE: \uc2 NASA\uc2 , which depends on \uc2 SpaceX\uc2  to shuttle astronauts to and from the International Space Station has been keen on adding a second type of commercial spacecraft. That way if a safety concern grounds one fleet, they can go to the other. As the Boeing Starliner left earth, \uc2 SpaceX\uc2  CEO \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  posted on social media, "Congratulations on a successful launch."\par \par \uc2 MARK NAPPI, BOEING VICE PRESIDENT: We don't see it as a competition. We have got two providers that are going up to the International Space Station, and \uc2 SpaceX\uc2  is up there and we're up there now as well.\par \par \uc2 SERRIE: Before today, Starliner faced many hurdles. Engineers had to fix a weakness in the parachute system and remove about a mile of insulation tape that posed a fire hazard. A malfunctioning relief valve on the Atlas Five rocket scrubbed Starliner's first launch attempt in May only to be followed by a second scrub on June 1st because of a faulty power unit on backup ground computer. Just minutes before today's launch, the astronauts praised the unity and purpose of everyone involved with the mission.\par \par \uc2 BUTCH WILMORE, MISSION COMMANDER: Each of you just flying what this nation's forefathers envisioned, a people committed to God, family, and country, a people who use their gifts and talents for the common good and are passionate and tough.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO TAPE)\par \par \uc2 SERRIE (on camera): Starliner is scheduled to dock with the International Space Station just after noon tomorrow. Bret?\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Jonathan Serrie at the Kennedy Space Center. Jonathan, thanks.\par \par \uc2 Up next, the panel on the Hunter Biden trial and new concerns over President Biden's mental fitness.\par \par \uc2 First, Beyond our Borders tonight.\par \par \uc2 An Italian court reconvicts Amanda Knox of slander. The verdict quashes her hope of removing a legal stain against her that has persisted after exoneration in the brutal 2007 murder of her British roommate while the two were exchange students in Italy. It's the sixth time that an Italian court ruled Knox had wrongly blamed the killing on an innocent plan, the Congolese owner of the bar where she worked part time.\par \par \uc2 And this is a live look at Seoul, South Korea, courtesy of Earth Cam. One of the big stories there tonight, the U.S. flies a long-range B1B bomber over the Korean peninsula. It was part of its first precision guided bombing drill with South Korea in seven years. The exercise comes as tensions are rising over the north's recent launches of rubbish carrying balloons towards South Korea and other provocations.\par \par \uc2 Just some of the other stories Beyond our Borders tonight. We'll be right back.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 HUNTER BIDEN\uc2 , PRESIDENT BIDEN'S SON: Crack takes you into the darkest recesses of your soul, as well as the darkest corners of every community.\par \par \uc2 ANDY MCCARTHY, "NATIONAL REVIEW": What this case is going to come down to is how do you analogize drug addiction, which we don't have a long history in the United States of regulating?\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Americans in many ways are very sympathetic to the Bidens because so many of them have also had struggles with addiction. They don't think this would be much of a political issue for the campaign. But they are worried about the human toll on this president going forward.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BAIER: The Hunter Biden trial underway in Delaware today. \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 's ex-wife testifies she learned of drug use after finding a crack pipe on the porch. "\uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 's ex-wife Kathleen Buhle said during Wednesday's testimony she discovered \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  was using drugs when they were married. Buhle she found a broken pipe, white powder, and white crystals in his car. She said from 2015 to 2019 she would search his car for drugs when he would lend his care to her daughters because she wanted to make sure they weren't driving with the drugs."\par \par \uc2 What about this trial? Let's bring in our panel, FOX News chief political analyst Brit Hume, Morgan Ortagus, host of "The Morgan Ortagus Show" on \uc2 Sirius XM\uc2 , founder of Polaris National Security, and "Axios" political reporter Stef Kight.\par \par \uc2 What about that soundbite, Brit, about the political implications of this trial as we look at it now?\par \par \uc2 BRIT HUME, FOX NEWS SENIOR POLITICAL ANALYST: It sounds like the defense had a bad day today. But I think that even if there's a conviction, as there well may be, I don't think it politically is going to be that serious of problem for this reason -- countless American families have had wayward kids. And you know the story of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and his family. When he was in the Senate, he used to take the train home from Washington to Delaware virtually every night to be with those boys when they were growing up. And so I think people will look upon this with some sympathy.\par \par \uc2 Now, obviously, it's embarrassing and painful for young \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  and for his family. But politically, I don't think it's -- I don't think it's a big -- it's going to be damaging to President Trump -- I mean President Biden, if it hurts him at all.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Stef, you agree? Obviously, the president has come out and been very empathetic to his son, talking about his love for his son. And there are a lot of people, including \uc2 Trey Gowdy\uc2 , who say that the tax case is much stronger than this one.\par \par \uc2 STEF KIGHT, POLITICAL REPORTER, "AXIOS": Yes. I mean, look, this is going to be a messy trial. And we know that President Biden cares a lot about his family. He cares a lot about Hunter, and he is very emotionally invested in this trial and others. And so one of the questions here is how much of a distraction this becomes to the president. We know that we're going to ultimately see this being Biden family talking both for the defense and for the prosecution, as my colleague Alex Thompson has reported, who is there in the courtroom for all of this.\par \par \uc2 And this is -- this is still going to be a very emotional trial, very trying for the family, very trying for Biden as he is trying to put up a solid few months of campaigning, as he is trying to go after former President Trump, and as he continues to struggle in the polls. So, whether or not this particular case will impact Biden directly politically is still a question. It may not have much effect, but it is certainly going to have a toll on Biden and his family emotionally.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Yes, morgan, there are elements of this though that have definitely played into politics in the past and could in the future. The laptop, the infamous laptop was shown to the jury yesterday. And they confirmed, the \uc2 FBI\uc2  agent confirmed that was, in fact, the laptop -- \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 's laptop. And of course, we remember that infamous exchange in that debate. Take a listen.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 , (D) PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: There are 50 former national intelligence folks who said that what he is accusing me of is a Russian plant. They have said that this has all the -- four -- five former heads of the CIA, both parties, say what he is saying is a bunch of garbage. Nobody believes it except his and his good friend \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 DONALD TRUMP\uc2 , FORMER U.S. PRESIDENT: You mean the laptop is now another Russia, Russia, Russia hoax? You got to be kidding. Is this where you are going?\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: That's exactly what --\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : This is where he is going.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Think about that in context now, and you look back to "\uc2 The New York Times\uc2 " cover. This is in March of 2022, "Spies Who Lie," that listed all of the folks who signed that letter. And now the prosecution, the \uc2 U.S. government\uc2 , is saying this was not only legitimate, but it wasn't tampered with.\par \par \uc2 MORGAN ORTAGUS, FORMER STATE DEPARTMENT SPOKESPERSON: Yes, every single person, every single national security official and former CIA directors, et cetera, who signed that letter, they owe an apology to the American people. There is so much damage that has been done to the intelligence community by these former Obama and Biden appointees politicizing this case before an election.\par \par \uc2 This is why people, if you are the head of the CIA, if you're the head of the DNI, you probably shouldn't be commenting on the record, signing things about things that you don't have any active information on. Not only was it wrong, listen, it was an untruth. Maybe it was a lie. Maybe the president didn't realize he was lying to the American people. But ultimately, that is what happened in that debate. The president and every single person who signed that letter not only owe an apology to the American people, but there needs to be a reckoning for what they have done to undermine the intelligence community, the \uc2 FBI\uc2 , the CIA, to the American people.\par \par \uc2 When you want to know why the American people don't have faith in institutions, it's because of leaders -- gutless leaders who get involved politically and do the things that they did. It's infuriating to me as somebody who spent almost 20 years in national security to see them do this, to see them undermine the profession.\par \par \uc2 And listen, I think when it goes to the bigger trial writ large, what I am more concerned about, and I think that this will bring the conversation into the general election as it should, we'll see what happens with this jury trial, Bret. What I'm more concerned about is we still don't have a full accounting of the business dealings between \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  and China, members of the Chinese Communist Party, Ukraine, and if the president was involved at all. Those are serious things that still need to be examined in my mind.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: To that point, House Republicans have criminal referrals now issued today against James, the president's brother, and \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  about alleging false testimony. They want the DOJ to investigate that and move forward on that.\par \par \uc2 Brit, I want to turn to the reaction to "The Wall Street Journal" report that has kicked up all kinds of reaction on all sides about the president's mental fitness. Here's a couple of them.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: I want to congratulate "The Wall Street Journal" for cracking the cold case that Biden is old. I mean, breaking news.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: I am sort of actually embarrassed for "The Wall Street Journal" with this piece. This piece is so tilted, so off the mark. Is he 81-years-old? Yes. Is he a bit slower in terms of his reactions to some things? Probably.\par \par \uc2 NIA-MALIKA HENDERSON, OPINION COLUMNIST, "BLOOMBERG": My response to the piece when I read it was now do \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 MIKE POMPEO\uc2 , FORMER U.S. SECRETARY OF STATE: The requirement is not about age. It's about the capacity, the energy, the mental focus, the energy that is required to deliver. And our adversaries are sensing this as well. And I think that's why you see \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  testing us. You see \uc2 Hamas\uc2  now continuing to hold onto hostages in the face of America trying to restrain Israel.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Brit, this was an article that they said was based on 45 people over several months, interviews with them, that essentially said the president is slipping.\par \par \uc2 HUME: Yes, Bret, I think this age issue and the lack of mental sharpness that has become so evident to people is as close to an insoluble political problem as I can think of. I mean, all this argument stemming from this article about whether he is sharp or not behind the scenes comes down to whether you believe your eyes or your ears. You can see it when he is public. It's pretty hard for people to believe that in private he turns into Superman. I just don't think that people will buy that. He is too old and people know it.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: We'll continue to follow this. Panel, thank you, as always.\par \par \uc2 Finally tonight, a SPECIAL REPORT salute. Commemorations for the 80th anniversary of D-Day continued Tuesday evening. Powerful scene in Normandy at the Commonwealth War Cemetery, tombstones of more than 2,100 personnel illuminated with candles as onlookers listened to a performance of Amazing Grace. The ceremony featuring music from the Pegasus Memorial Band and group of volunteer musicians from England. Full coverage tomorrow here on FOX.\par \par \uc2 And we have a special delivery to tell you about as well. Georgia (ph) Lapointe (ph) Meredith came into the world this afternoon just before 2:00 p.m. eastern time. She is the daughter of correspondent Mark Meredith and wife Lauren. Their son Tripp (ph) is promoted to big brother. Everybody is doing great. Congratulations. One viewer at a time. The demo is improving. There you go.\par \par \uc2 Tomorrow on SPECIAL REPORT, fellow West Point graduates Congressman John James and Pat Ryan talk about veterans' issues and D-Day, the anniversary, in our "Common Ground" segment.\par \par \uc2 Thanks for inviting us into your home tonight. That's it for this SPECIAL REPORT, fair, balanced, and still unafraid. THE INGRAHAM ANGLE starts now.\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2024 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2024 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document FNSPBB0020240606ek6500001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; International\par \b \uc2 Interview with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , Fmr. President of the United States (R) and Current U.S. Presidential Candidate (R)\b0\par\par\uc2 Sean Hannity \par \uc2 8,623 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 June 2024\par \uc2 Fox News: Hannity\par \uc2 SHAN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2024 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2024 ASC Services II Media, LLC.  All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 SEAN HANNITY\uc2 , FOX NEWS ANCHOR: And welcome to "Hannity."\par \par \uc2 And, in just a moment, we are going to hear from the Republican candidate for president, \uc2 Donald J. Trump\uc2 , for the hour during our exclusive sit-down interview. Now, we just had it a short time ago at Mar-a-Lago.\par \par \uc2 We're only 152 days away from an election like never before. The candidates might be the same, but guess what? The country has changed drastically, not in a good way. For the first time in history, the left is using lawfare against a presidential candidate, but it's not going according to plan.\par \par \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2 's absurd case in New York will soon be headed for appeals. Meanwhile, breaking news tonight. The case in Fulton County, Georgia, is now officially on hold pending an appeal over DA Fani Willis and her possible disqualification.\par \par \uc2 And in the state of Florida, the DOJ's document case against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has now been postponed due to significant issues surrounding the evidence and, by the way, the legitimacy of the appointment of the special counsel.\par \par \uc2 And while Biden's lawfare seems to be collapsing, his presidency is even worse, the border shambles. It keeps getting worse and worse. Violent crime remains high. Inflation continues to spike. Housing is totally unaffordable. We have two wars that are raging overseas with no end in sight, and now even Democrats are questioning Biden's mental acuity.\par \par \uc2 It is no surprise the vast majority of Americans believe that our country is on the wrong track. And so how will former President Trump cut through the lawfare and dirty political tricks to reach these Americans and demonstrate a better future?\par \par \uc2 Anyway, moments ago, I sat down with the former president. Here's part one of that interview.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: We just have breaking news, as I mentioned in my open tonight, and I want to get your reaction to the fact that the appeals court has now stopped your Georgia case, election case, while appeal on Willis' disqualification is pending.\par \par \uc2 This is on the heels of Florida Judge Aileen Cannon looking into whether or not the prosecutor, Jack Smith, the special prosecutor, was appointed in an inappropriate way, which would render the case and the indictments out completely. That is going to take place in fairly short order.\par \par \uc2 A lot can change in a couple of days, with only 152 days out of the election.\par \par \uc2 DONALD TRUMP\uc2 , FORMER PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES (R) AND CURRENT U.S. PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE (R): And what -- we call him deranged Jack Smith, because you look at his career, he's been overturned by the Supreme Court unanimously, so many other things. He goes too far.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Let me ask you this.\par \par \uc2 You had said something during the trial in New York. Mother Teresa beat these charges is one thing that you said.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : Yes.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And you turned out to be right.\par \par \uc2 And, secondly, you were asked about the possibility that Judge Merchan might send you to jail. You said something that really kind of got my attention. What did you say, that it didn't faze you, in the sense that if that's what it takes.\par \par \uc2 You don't have to be doing this. You could be playing golf every day and you probably wouldn't be charged with anything.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: Well, I think I say it about almost all of these cases that are brought against me. They are doing it for the purposes of hurting a political opponent of Biden and trying to get him to win. And he's the worst president in the history of our country.\par \par \uc2 But in the case that you're talking about, I said very strongly that I'm very proud to fight for our Constitution. And that's what it takes. Everybody said, this is such a minor thing. You don't go to jail for this, all of them.\par \par \uc2 But you don't understand what we're dealing against, Sean. We're dealing against these -- a system that is so corrupt. Nobody's ever seen anything like it. I did nothing wrong in any of these things. I did nothing wrong. We did nothing wrong at all.\par \par \uc2 And when you look at the analysts, whether it's Gregg Jarrett, or Andy McCarthy, or Jonathan Turley, or your friend, the great one, Mark Levin, Dershowitz, all of them, they said...\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Judge Jeanine, yes.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: ... there's no case here.\par \par \uc2 Judge Jeanine was so incredible two weeks ago. She was unbelievable. Angry. She was angry. And you know why they are angry? Because I love our country, and they see what's happening. It's totally unconstitutional what they have done.\par \par \uc2 And if you look at the statements made by the people I just mentioned -- and I'm not friends with any. I mean, they -- I think they respect what I have done. They might respect me. They might not respect me. But they said there's no case. It shouldn't have been brought.\par \par \uc2 And the way the judge charged the jury, told the jury, gave jury instructions, nobody's ever heard anything like that.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: It was basically, when you break it down, a records-keeping issue on a misdemeanor whose statute of limitations had run out that they upcharged into a felony on a federal election.\par \par \uc2 And that raises another issue of appeal. What will be your appeal?\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : And, by the way, when you say records-keeping, you know what the record-keeping was? They charged an election, if you look, a lawyer's fee, a legal fee.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Yes.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : And you call it a legal expense. It's known. You call it a legal fee, a legal expense.\par \par \uc2 The bookkeeper, who I never spoke to, correctly wrote a legal expense for a lawyer that was paid.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: We have a similar case. \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  funneled money to a law firm, and that law firm hired an op research firm. And that op research firm hired a guy by \uc2 Christopher Steele\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 That became the basis of what I described as the dirty Russian misinformation dossier. That became the basis of not one, but four FISA applications, and it all turned out not to be true. So, in that case, well, nobody was charged. Nobody was charged with top secret classified information. Her home wasn't raided on her server, deleted subpoenaed e- mails, 30,000 of them.\par \par \uc2 We didn't hear of BleachBit. Then you have all the people that signed off on those warrants. Nothing happens to them. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , four locations, top secret documents, nobody raided his house. That, I guess, we have come -- we have added a new word to our lexicon, and that is lawfare...\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : Yes.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: ... or weaponization of justice.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : That's right.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: My question to you is -- and people are saying, actually because of an interview we did together.\par \par \uc2 You said, "I would be dictator for the day," and just to secure the border and drill for oil. I thought it was tongue in cheek. I was sitting there with you.\par \par \uc2 However, my question is a very serious one. People are claiming you want retribution. People are claiming you want what has happened to you done to Democrats. Would you do that ever?\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: Look, what's happened to me has never happened in this country before, and it has to stop, because...\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Wait a minute. I want to hear that again. It has to stop.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: Well, it does have to stop, because we're not going to have a country anymore.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And if you're elected, what does that mean? Define that.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: Look, what I have gone through, nobody's ever gone through. I'm a very legitimate person.\par \par \uc2 I built a great business. Everything's been -- I have been under siege. Nobody's ever seen anything like this in this country. Now, in other countries, in other Third World countries, or banana republics, as they say, a banana republic -- we have become a banana republic. At the border, we become a banana republic.\par \par \uc2 With so many other elements of our country, we become a banana republic. You take a look at what's happening with inflation. That's a banana republic inflation, what we have. I think it could be as high as 50 percent if you add everything in. When you start adding energy prices in, when you start adding interest rates, which have gone from 2 percent to 9 percent and 10 percent.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I'm going to get to all of that.\par \par \uc2 But focus on those that want people to believe that you want retribution, that you will use the system of justice to go after your political enemies.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : So, number one, they're wrong. It has to stop, because, otherwise, we're not going to have a country.\par \par \uc2 Look, when this election is over, based on what they have done, I would have every right to go after them. And it's easy, because it's \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , and you see all the criminality, all of the money that's going into the family and him, all of this money from China, from Russia, from Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 During one of the interviews, I said, what about the $3.5 million paid to the Biden family from the mayor of Moscow's wife? What about that?\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Russian oligarch.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : And Chris Wallace defended him, said, you can't ask that question.\par \par \uc2 Well, then it turned out to be a big deal long after that debate. That was one of the debates. And it turned out to be a big deal. And Chris Wallace said, we can't go there because we don't know that it's true.\par \par \uc2 Turned out to be true, millions and millions of dollars. Now, if we're going to do that...\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: He -- by the way, he had dinner with her at the Cafe Milano.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: Right.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And he said to America he never once talked to his son, brother, or anybody about their foreign business deal.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: Well, he said it, and then you found out it was absolutely untrue. Everything he says is untrue.\par \par \uc2 There's never been a president like this. Look, he's a horrible president. He's destroying our country at the border. He's allowing millions of people to come in from prisons and jails, from mental institutions and insane asylums, which is a step above, a big step above a mental institution.\par \par \uc2 He's allowing terrorists to flood into our country. And the numbers are probably 16, 17, or 18 million people. You're going to have over 20 million people, I think, I believe, and a lot of other people do too, by the time he hopefully gets out.\par \par \uc2 November 5, Election Day, will be the most -- and, by the way, it starts on September 22. It starts earlier because of very voting. But November 5 will go down as the most important election in the history of our country. It's going to be the most important day and period in the history of our country.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Will you pledge to restore equal justice, equal application of our laws, end this practice of weaponization? Is that a promise you're going to make?\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: Well, you have to do it. But it's awful.\par \par \uc2 Look, I know you want me to say something so nice.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: No, I don't want you to say. I'm asking.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : But I don't want to look naive.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I don't want to...\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : What they have done to the Republican Party, they want to arrest on no crime. They want to arrest the person that won the nomination in a landslide. There was nobody even close, in a landslide, the person that got millions of votes, more votes than any other sitting president in history in the last election, the person that won an election that he wasn't expected to win against \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  in 2016.\par \par \uc2 They want to arrest that person on no crime. They want to arrest. There was no crime. There was no criminality. There was no crime. And you can go back to all of these legal scholars. They can't believe what's happening. Some of them don't even like me. And they're saying, this is a very, very dangerous thing that's happening.\par \par \uc2 No, we can't let this happen. And I will do everything in my power not to let -- but there's tremendous criminality here. What they're doing to me, if it's going to continue, we're really not going to have much of a country left. It's really -- it is weaponization. You call it lawfare. You call it -- some people call it just warfare.\par \par \uc2 But it is weaponization of the election. And we're talking about, I think, the most important election in the history of our country. This will go down, I believe, as the most important election in the history of our country. We can't have this stuff go on, because you know what?\par \par \uc2 When Biden goes out, everyone says, bye-bye, and then he gets indicted two days later, and they go after him? The country doesn't want that. And you know what? They didn't want it with \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  either. I thought it was terrible. I'd make a speech, everyone would say, "Lock her up, lock her up, lock her up."\par \par \uc2 And I was at a UFC fight the other night with Dana White, who is a fantastic...\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You got a terrible reception.\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : Yes.\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I did -- well, I'm kidding.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : You better tell them...\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I'm kidding. I'm not telling Dana that.\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : People don't understand, sometimes, sarcasm.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Yes. No, it was -- we played it. It was pretty overwhelming.\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : It was 25,000 people, whatever they had going, absolute -- there wasn't...\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Right after your conviction.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : But you know what?\par \par \uc2 What I watched, and it was very -- some of the fighters, two, in particular, hated their opponent. And this went on for months. The fight was broadcast out.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: \uc2 Sure\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : And they announced the fight. And the hatred was real. It was the real deal. These people have -- they have a lot of hatred. And they hated.\par \par \uc2 And then the fight ended, and they're hugging and kissing in the ring. They're down, sitting on the -- they're hugging and kissing. It's like nothing happened. It happened on two fights. There was tremendous animosity between the two fighters and the other two fighters. And, at the end, that's what happened.\par \par \uc2 And, in a certain way, after we won against Hillary, people would say, "Lock her up, lock her up." And I said, wouldn't it be terrible if I locked up the wife of the president of the United States, former, and locked up the former secretary of state? It's a terrible thing.\par \par \uc2 You're starting off, you want to bring the country together. I want to bring the country together. And success does bring the country together, because we had the most successful economy in the history of our country just prior to COVID. And, even at the end, I got it back. It was an amazing thing.\par \par \uc2 But we had the most successful economy in history. And I was getting calls from radical left people wanting to meet. And I'm telling you, success, African American, Asian American, Hispanic American, women, men, people with diplomas, people without diplomas, people that went to MIT, Harvard, and Wharton, people that didn't get out of high school, the most successful economy we have ever had.\par \par \uc2 And people that I would say you call them on the radical left -- call it whatever you want, liberal people, progressive people. They were all calling. And they were saying, let's get together. This is amazing.\par \par \uc2 Nobody, no -- every single group, nobody has ever done better than during that period of time, in my administration, during that period. And they wanted to get together. And it would have happened. We would have happened. It was really something.\par \par \uc2 I'm not sure I would have been able to say to you that there was a way to unify. Success will unify. And I think we're going to have a tremendous success. We have to bring it back fast, because this country is -- we're a failing nation. We are really a failing nation right now.\par \par \uc2 We're being laughed at all over the world.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right, a lot of ground to cover.\par \par \uc2 Part two of my exclusive interview with former President Trump is up next. We will ask the president about \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 's gun trial straight ahead and about the issue of addiction, as "Hannity" continues tonight, beautiful Palm Beach, Florida, straight ahead.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And here is part two of my interview from just a few hours earlier with former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Let me ask you, are you following at all the Hunter Biden trial?\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: I am.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: OK.\par \par \uc2 Let me ask you about two aspects of it. There's the legal aspect of it.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : Yes.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: OK, the case seems pretty overwhelming on the gun charge in this case, in my opinion.\par \par \uc2 He has -- he does not quite have as hostile a venue in Delaware as you had in New York.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: No, he's got a very friendly venue.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Right.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : I had -- I had the most hostile venue you could have. We asked for a venue change.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Yes.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : And we asked for a judge change.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Yes, none of which happened.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : And they wouldn't do it.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: OK.\par \par \uc2 So, however, there's another aspect of it. And it's something that, if you look at like, for example, the fentanyl flowing into this country that is killing our children...\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : Yes.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: ... in massive numbers...\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : Yes.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: ... and opioids killing our children in massive numbers, there is this issue that is very real.\par \par \uc2 And I guarantee you there's not a person that's watching this show that doesn't know somebody, family member, friend, neighbor, that hasn't had to deal with addiction. You have had to deal with it in your life. You don't drink.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: No.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Never have.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: No. Never had a drink.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: No.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: I had a brother who suffered tremendously from alcoholism and alcohol.\par \par \uc2 And it was a terrible thing to watch. He was an incredible guy with the best personality. He was the best-looking person you have ever seen. Everything was perfect. But he had an addiction. And so I understand addiction, because I -- I was very close. He was very close to me. He was an incredible guy.\par \par \uc2 But he suffered a -- and I have had many friends. But my brother suffered tremendously from this addiction. In fact, he was older than me, and he'd go out and say, never drink, never, ever drink. Now, in those days, drugs were not prevalent.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Right.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : You didn't have that.\par \par \uc2 But he'd say, never, ever drink. He knew exactly what he was saying. I used to say, why does he always say it? But I never had a drink. I was -- I'm not bragging about it.\par \par \uc2 I know one thing about addiction, because a lot of people say, what do you tell children? I say, if you don't have a drink, you're never going to have a problem. If you do have a drink, you have a good chance that you will be addicted, or drugs, because now its drugs are probably equal to or greater.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Terrible. They're dying.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: I mean, that's what's so bad.\par \par \uc2 And they're dying from the -- from a drug the size of a pinhead. A little bit of fentanyl, literally what could fit on the end of a pin, can kill 10 people. It's crazy and so dangerous out there. And so many are dying where they think they're getting something and going to have a little fun on a Friday night, and all of a sudden they're dead because of the power of what's happening.\par \par \uc2 And the sad thing is that I had an agreement with President Xi of China. I said, listen, you're killing our people. It's going through Mexico, and Mexico is paying a big price also from me. It's going through Mexico, coming through. Most of it is 95 percent coming through the southern border. I built 571 miles of wall.\par \par \uc2 What we -- and I had the Mexican army protecting us. I said, you're either going to protect us or I'm going to charge you big tariffs, and got along very well with the president of Mexico. They gave us tremendous protection during the time.\par \par \uc2 We had the best level of numbers. Nobody's ever had numbers, like the best we have ever had, in terms of illegal immigration. In fact, my last week in office, we had less people coming into our country than at any time before.\par \par \uc2 But, importantly, we also had -- drugs were down 19 percent, 20 percent. And that's not enough. And, by the way, you will never really solve the drug problem unless you do what other countries do.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: So, have the sympathy...\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : And that's the death penalty for drug dealers.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: But the...\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : If you have the death -- a drug dealer, on average, will kill during that person's life 500 people, unless you have a death penalty, unless there's a -- something that they're -- right now, they don't even get charged with anything.\par \par \uc2 If you don't institute the death penalty for drug dealers, you will never solve that problem. You will get it down to a number that -- like, I got it down -- actually, at one point, it was 22 percent down. That was a good thing.\par \par \uc2 But you will never solve the problem. We set up committees. We set up all of this. The cartels are run by very smart, very vicious people. They're pouring drugs into our country. Now, the number coming in now compared to four years ago is 12 times higher, drugs. So it's not only people. It's not only human trafficking. It's drugs.\par \par \uc2 The drugs are pouring into our country totally unchecked.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Back to Hunter.\par \par \uc2 So, you have sympathy for addiction. OK, I think most Americans do. OK. That's not what the trial is about. And I think there are bigger issues involving the Biden family. We discussed -- we touched on it earlier. And that is, OK, how does somebody with no experience get paid millions of dollars?\par \par \uc2 Goes on "Good Morning America," no experience, oil, energy, gas, Ukraine, millions of dollars. Then, of course, Vice President at the time \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  leverages a billion tax dollars...\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: Right.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: ... to get a prosecutor investigating the company he's in business with, his son is in business with fired within six hours using a billion of our dollars.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : Yes. And you have a statute of limitations.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: There are other legal -- there are real legal issues.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: Excuse me.\par \par \uc2 The really big stuff and their trial -- look, I feel very badly for them in terms of the addiction part of what they have right now.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Right.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : Because I understand the addiction world. And I have also -- not only a brother. I have lost a lot of friends to addiction, drugs, alcohol. And there are other addictions also, frankly. It would be nice if people would do certain things and live certain ways.\par \par \uc2 But you're not able to -- they're just not able to break it. I have had -- I have had friends that are so strong. My brother was a strong person. I have had friends that were so strong, so powerful, they couldn't stay away from a glass of alcohol. They couldn't stay away from a drug. They had to have a drug.\par \par \uc2 But you know the way that you solve the problem? Don't have them. If you don't have a taste for alcohol -- I remember, when I was going to school, college, I had a friend, he hated the taste of Scotch, hated it. It was like...\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Yes.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : But he wanted to develop it because, socially, he thought it was a good thing. He would sit down with the bankers and all the -- at the Wharton School of Finance, they want to have dinners with bankers, right? That's a big thing.\par \par \uc2 And they want to -- he developed the taste for Scotch. And by the time he finished, he ended up being a very bad alcoholic.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Yes.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: He's -- I mean, 20, 25 years later, he ended up being an alcoholic. And he couldn't stay away.\par \par \uc2 I say the way you stay away, just don't drink. Just don't have it. If you don't have drugs, if you don't experience early on, you're not going to have a need for it. You're not going to have an addiction. If you don't drink alcohol, you're not going to have an addiction. You're not going to have this insatiable urge to have a drink.\par \par \uc2 And I say that to people with your children. They ask me, what do you think and, children, what do you tell them? I say, no drugs, no alcohol. I also say, no cigarettes. Don't have the cigarettes. Don't have cigarettes. Don't have them. I have friends that can't stop smoking. If they never had a cigarette before, they'd have no problem.\par \par \uc2 When I look at a friend that can't stop smoking, I don't understand why it's hard to stop. There's smoke all over the place. The fact is, if you never had a cigarette -- I never had a cigarette. I have no urge to smoke. But if you are, you get addicted. It has something, and you just can't stop.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right, a ton of ground to cover.\par \par \uc2 I asked President Trump about the Democrats' plan to use fear, hysteria to win in November.\par \par \uc2 Stay with us.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Let's get right to part three of my interview with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: There's two issues we're going to talk about. One is what I think the Democrats are going to run on, and one I think are what -- the issues you will be running on.\par \par \uc2 Democrats -- democracy in peril, January 6th, abortion, abortion, abortion, all of these issues.\par \par \uc2 And then, of course, we have this -- with 153 days out of the election, yesterday, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , who'd been telling America that the border's closed and the border secure for over three years, and his vice president said it, and his spokespeople had said it, and his \uc2 Department of Homeland Security\uc2  secretary said it -- then, all of a sudden, they wanted to blame Republicans. I don't have the power.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, they did undo all of your policies with the stroke of a pen.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: Yeah.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Now, finally, yesterday, he implemented a new policy. However...\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : It's meaningless.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: ... two million illegals a year.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : Millions of people are allowed to come in.\par \par \uc2 It's meaningless. It's a joke. Everybody knows it. It has nothing to do with border security.\par \par \uc2 And he didn't need anything from Congress. All he has to do is shut the border. You say, shut the border, sign an order, and the border will close.\par \par \uc2 I did it. We had the best border, the safest border in history.\par \par \uc2 But your question is a large question because you're asking about a lot of things.\par \par \uc2 Take abortion. For 52 years, people wanted to get rid of Roe v. Wade. And the people that wanted to do it were legal scholars, lawyers, polit -- everybody wanted it to go back into the state system, not the federal system.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Let the states decide.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : Let the states decide. The people decide. Let the states decide.\par \par \uc2 For 52 years, they fought it. I was able to get it done with the appointment of great justices, three great justices, plus others that joined them as you know. And we don't have to go into all the names, but they're great.\par \par \uc2 And they were -- they had the courage to end Roe v. Wade, which really meant from a legal standpoint, it now goes back to the states. And now, the states are deciding.\par \par \uc2 And, by the way, in many cases, like Ohio, it became -- if you want to use the word "liberal" or "progressive", it was more liberal or progressive than people would have thought, but the people of Ohio decided. The people of Kansas decided.\par \par \uc2 The people are now deciding, and it's taken it off the shoulders of the federal government. Always, they wanted it to be decided by the states, and Roe v. Wade didn't do that. It put it into the federal government.\par \par \uc2 So, now, states are voting on it and in many cases, it's more progressive, or I like the term liberal. You know, they want to get away from the word liberal I guess, but it's -- it's more liberal in many cases, not in all cases. In some cases, they're going the other direction.\par \par \uc2 But the people are deciding, and in many ways, it's a beautiful thing to watch.\par \par \uc2 So they wanted to -- for 52 years, move it back to the states. That's why they wanted to fight Roe v. Wade.\par \par \uc2 Then about 10 or 12 years ago, it started getting more complex. They were talking about lots of different things.\par \par \uc2 But remember this, the radicals in many ways are the Democrats of this issue because they want to have abortion be OK in the eighth month and the ninth month and even after birth.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You're talking about -- by the way, when you say that, you're talking about former Governor Northam.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: Yeah.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Who said the baby will be born and the -- in that case, the baby will be born, the baby will be made comfortable, then the doctor and the baby will talk about it.\par \par \uc2 I had \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  debating \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  on this very show.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: Yeah. Right, I watched.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And it took a long time to get Gavin to answer, will you support any restrictions in months seventh, eighth, or ninth? And he, at one point, got annoyed because I kept going in for an answer.\par \par \uc2 And the answer came back. He goes, that is a decision between a doctor and a patient, and their conscience. That's it. That means to me no restrictions.\par \par \uc2 I think the country probably is around where Dobbs is, but the states will decide it as you point out, because I do think it hurt the Republicans in '22.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : It did. But I think the Republicans didn't know how to talk about the issue. And when it came to things having to do with abortion, instead of saying the states will decide -- the states will decide, it really -- it really hurt the Republicans. They didn't know how to talk about the issue.\par \par \uc2 And now, I think they're learning how to talk about it and all they're going to do is say, and they campaign one way the other within the state. The states are all deciding right now, and I think it's working the way that people wanted it to work.\par \par \uc2 And it's going to bring the country together on an issue that was very, very bad.\par \par \uc2 But you mentioned when you -- about Gavin, I call him Gavin Newscum because he's done a terrible job as...\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: A friend of yours?\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: Yeah, another (ph) name.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: By the way, $70 billion budget deficit.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: No, no, he's done a terrible job in California. One of the most beautiful places, environmentally, from a weather standpoint, the ocean, the whole thing. I have things in California. It's so beautiful.\par \par \uc2 But the regulation in California is just incredible, what they've done to that state. I mean, it's just horrible. And now, people are moving out as opposed to moving in. That never happened there.\par \par \uc2 But, you know, when you talk about the abortion -- because it's an important thing to talk about and a lot of people are afraid to talk about it, and a lot of politicians are destroyed talking about it, but -- like the exceptions. I like the three exceptions, and you have the three exceptions.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Rape, incest, mother's life.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: Correct, and you have the three exceptions.\par \par \uc2 And I think people, they have to follow their heart, they have to, you know, do what's right, and what's right before their God, if they're religious people, but they have to follow their heart.\par \par \uc2 And I happen to believe like \uc2 Ronald Reagan\uc2 . \uc2 Ronald Reagan\uc2  was very strong on the three exceptions. And I think you should do that, at the same time, you have to follow your heart.\par \par \uc2 But what's happening is everybody agrees pretty much that in the eighth, ninth and beyond -- I mean beyond is really an execution. We're not even talking about the word abortion. We're talking about an execution.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Infanticide.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : And the former governor, not the current governor who's doing a very good job, by the way, he's doing a very -- Youngkin...\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Yeah.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: ... doing a very good job.\par \par \uc2 But the former governor before him said, you lay the baby down and you decide with the mother what to do. The baby's born. That's an execution.\par \par \uc2 I think everybody knows that in the eighth month and the ninth month and beyond that, I mean, hard to believe, they have -- some states passing legislation where you can execute the baby after birth. It's crazy.\par \par \uc2 It's like so many other things -- open borders, crazy. Men playing in women's sports, crazy.\par \par \uc2 So I think the Republican Party has done an amazing job in certain ways, but they've never understood how to talk about, and I agree with you, it's hurt the Republican Party. It's hurt some people.\par \par \uc2 Exceptions is very important, I believe that. But what we did is we took Roe v. Wade out of the federal government, put in the states and now the people are deciding.\par \par \uc2 And in some cases, not everybody's happy. But the people are deciding. And I say, let the states decide.\par \par \uc2 This is -- every legal scholar wanted this to be where abortion should be. And you know, I've been following the issue very closely, but over the years, I've followed it less closely. But I always noticed that they always wanted to move it back to the states, everybody, and I was able to do that. And it's all happening and it's happening correctly.\par \par \uc2 And I wish that Republicans could talk about it correctly. And if they would, you'd see it's a very different issue.\par \par \uc2 And remember, they're not really the radical one. The radical ones are the ones that eighth month...\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: No restrictions.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: ... ninth month, after birth, you can execute the baby. Those are the radicals and those are the liberals and the progressives. And nobody wants to see that.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Up next -- next, I asked President Trump about Biden's obvious cognitive decline, straight ahead.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And here is part four of my interview with former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Let me ask you this. "Wall Street Journal", big article, Democrats are worried. You keep reading, Democrats are in a state of panic. Democrats are in a state of panic.\par \par \uc2 And now, it's something that we have covered at length on this program, and that is \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's cognitive decline. Now, Democrats are saying it and they're saying it out loud.\par \par \uc2 And let me play you a clip of Joe and get your reaction to it, and then I'm going to butt it together with a different Joe. I called them the night after State of the Union Address, jacked-up Joe. Maybe he had a lot of \uc2 Red Bull\uc2  or Monster Energy drink.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : Or something.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Or something.\par \par \uc2 Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 , PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: I've been a senator since I was 29 years old, never left government.\par \par \uc2 In the fall, he had tied -- that fall, he decided to -- look, I shouldn't get into this probably.\par \par \uc2 Never forget America is the strongest when we lead, not only by our example of our power but by the power of our example. You can clap for that.\par \par \uc2 As President Lincoln said...\par \par \uc2 We'll never forget -- lying around -- us -- him -- him, lying around actually.\par \par \uc2 They're trying to erase Black history. We're going to write Black history because it's American history.\par \par \uc2 On Memorial Day, I proudly stood with a Black man.\par \par \uc2 Just checking if it's afternoon. Good afternoon.\par \par \uc2 Will not bring Israel in -- will not bring down -- bog down -- will only bog down Israel and Gaza.\par \par \uc2 REPORTER: What's your response to that, sir?\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 : Is Steny here? \uc2 Steny Hoyer\uc2 ? \uc2 Steny Hoyer\uc2 ?\par \par \uc2 JILL BIDEN, FIRST LADY OF THE UNITED STATES: I hear him in the back. He's drinking the -- he's over by the beer.\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 : Well, \uc2 Steny Hoyer\uc2  lives in the western shore of Delaware -- in Maryland. The thing about -- I'm just -- let me put it this way. I remember when I was vice president and things weren't going too well.\par \par \uc2 I inherited an economy that was on the brink. Now our economy is literally the envy of the world.\par \par \uc2 Too many corporations raised prices to pad their profits, charging more and more for less and less. That's why we're cracking down on corporations that engage in price gouging and deceptive pricing.\par \par \uc2 Wall Street didn't build America. They're not bad guys. They didn't build it though. The middle class built the country and unions built the middle class.\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 Wages keep going up. Inflation keeps coming down. Inflation has dropped from 9 percent to 3 percent, the lowest in the world and tending lower.\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: So most days, you see Joe struggling. Now Democrats are saying it. But State of the Union, we saw a very different -- in my view -- Joe, maybe -- maybe just \uc2 Red Bull\uc2 . I don't know.\par \par \uc2 I'm not going to make any allegations, but it certainly was not the normal Biden. How significant an issue is this?\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: Look we are...\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Because I don't think he could sit here and have this conversation.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: Right. We're at the most dangerous point in the history of our country because of the power of weaponry, nuclear weapons in particular. Weapons that are so powerful that -- and I've seen the effects.\par \par \uc2 And I had an uncle, a great professor at MIT for many years, we used to talk about nuclear a lot. He understood nuclear very well. And even then, that was many years ago.\par \par \uc2 My father's brother. Dr. John Trump, and I think it was a longest-serving Professor in the history of MIT, I think 41 years -- very smart. We used to talk about nuclear and he used to talk about the power of nuclear.\par \par \uc2 And I'd say, Uncle John, you're done. We're -- a briefcase the size of a regular briefcase would -- would do damage that I don't even want to discuss. And we're a long way from that in terms of the advancement of that technology. And it's very bad, very scary.\par \par \uc2 And I will tell you, we have a chance of going into World War III because of our leader. So I don't want to get into what state he's in, you know. It's -- it's -- in one way, it's not something for me to talk about.\par \par \uc2 I can tell you this. President Xi of China, Putin, Kim Jong-un, all of these leaders are at the top of their game mentally. They're at the top of their game.\par \par \uc2 And they're dealing with somebody that's not at the top of their game -- his game. And honestly, he never was. He was never the brightest bulb. And everybody understands that. Everybody knows that.\par \par \uc2 You look at his foreign policy over the years. It was always wrong. You look at all of the things, you look at his crime bill in the 1990s. How -- how horrible that was to certain groups of people. He was never great at what he did. He did it because he was hale and hearty and well met.\par \par \uc2 And I have a real problem. I love this country. I don't want to see this country get into a nuclear war and be so badly damaged, what we say won't matter. This won't matter, this place won't matter, nothing will matter because practically nothing's going to be here anymore.\par \par \uc2 The level of power -- the level of power with the weapons and weaponry -- that's real weaponry. That's worse than the weaponry that we were talking about a little while ago. This is the ultimate -- this is obliteration, maybe world obliteration. And we have a man that is not capable of even discussing it.\par \par \uc2 He talked the other night about -- that nuclear doesn't matter so much. What matters is, think of this, global warming. The only global warming that matters to me is nuclear global warming because that's the real deal.\par \par \uc2 He said, it's an existential threat. He loves the words existential threat. That global warming is an existential threat. And he doesn't know why. What is it? It's weather.\par \par \uc2 And I'm all for that. You know what? I'm in a certain way, in a very powerful way, I'm an environmentalist. I'm -- I want clean air. I want clean water.\par \par \uc2 But this is not the existential threat. Tomorrow, we could have a war that will be so devastating that you can never recover from it, nobody can. The whole world won't be able to recover from it. And he's talking about something, in 400 years from now, the -- the oceans will rise by an eighth of an inch.\par \par \uc2 Look, we have a man that shouldn't be doing this job. He's not qualified. He's not mentally sharp enough, and I don't believe he was 20 years ago either. You know, they can show me clips. Take a look at the clips of he -- how he did 20 years ago.\par \par \uc2 His level of hatred for me is incredible. But all I'm trying to do is lay out the facts, lay out the facts. We have to have somebody that's sharp and strong. And \uc2 Viktor Orban\uc2 , who's a very strong kind of a guy, I guess -- they call him a strongman. Oh, Trump likes -- I don't like strongmen or hate strongmen.\par \par \uc2 He's leading a country. He's a strong leader. He's the Prime Minister of Hungary. He said the only way we're going to solve the problems of the world, you got to bring Trump back.\par \par \uc2 China was afraid of him. Russia was afraid of him.\par \par \uc2 Look, I ended the Russian pipeline \uc2 Nord Stream 2\uc2 . Before I came in -- even you, nobody ever heard of \uc2 Nord Stream 2\uc2 . I said, they're building \uc2 Nord Stream 2\uc2 . Everyone said, what is that?\par \par \uc2 It's the biggest pipeline in the world, going to Germany. So we're protecting Germany and Germany's paying billions of dollars a month to Russia for energy.\par \par \uc2 And I also said it's bad for Germany because if they ever do end up with a war, which they have many times, they'll turn off the juice and Germany doesn't have a chance. That's when I gave \uc2 Angela Merkel\uc2  a white flag. Do you remember? I sent over a white flag at a table. She said, what is it?\par \par \uc2 That's the flag of surrender.\par \par \uc2 So we need a president that's sharp and that's respected. And we're closer to World War III.\par \par \uc2 Now, you take a look at what's happened in the last few days. Putin is now talking about nuclear weapons for the first time, right? I mean, he's talking about him all the time because Ukraine is now talking about hitting Russia. And Biden doesn't know what the hell to say. But all of these things, they're going to end up leading to World War III.\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : I'll get the Ukrainian situation settled and I'll get it settled fast. It would have never happened.\par \par \uc2 The other thing that would have never happened is the October 7th attack of Israel, would have never happened. And you know what else? I'll add something else that won't -- wouldn't have happened, inflation. We have the worst inflation maybe in the history of our country, far worse than they report.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: It was 1.4 percent when you left.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : Because when you add interest rates and when you add energy prices -- look at the energy. By the way, gasoline prices are going way up again. When you add all of this in -- I think it's the worst inflation we've ever had. And our country...\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Let me stay focus on...\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : Our country has become, Sean, a failing nation.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You say declining nation.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : I say declining or failing.\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: So let me go back to the foreign policy...\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : I say a lot of things about it. But it's -- whatever I say about it, it's real bad.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I want to talk more about that.\par \par \uc2 But let me stay focused for just a second, if I may, on the issue of the war in Europe, we have war in the Middle East. And we have the Iranians, according to reports, even the \uc2 IAEA\uc2  may be very close to nuclear weapons...\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : Very close.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: That should scare everybody...\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : Yes.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: ... because they're crazy enough that I think they would -- they would use them. And a precarious situation, more dangerous, I think, than at any point.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : The most dangerous time in the history of our country.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I would agree.\par \par \uc2 And so, my question to you is, you -- if you are elected and you are the next president, the 47th president, how do you begin the process of restoring world order?\par \par \uc2 Now, one other thing. I never thought in my lifetime, I would listen to a president of our country, the leader of the free world, you know, literally tell a country that was attacked by radical Islamic terrorists that we'll support your defense, but we won't support you fighting back after the Iranians fired weapons into their country.\par \par \uc2 To me, that was a surrender in the war on terror. We're trying to lecture Israel. You know, you can't go to Rafah, you can't do this. OK, excuse me, well, how would we act if we lost what would be, by population extrapolated out, 40,000 Americans in a day?\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : So number one, they have to finish the job. Israel has to finish that job. They have to finish it quickly, strongly and they have to get back to life again. Because it's taking too long. They have to finish the job.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You're saying go in, win and finish?\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : Got to win, got to win. The attack on October 7th -- and it's getting more and more demeaned. They're demeaning it. I have people now telling me they don't think the attack ever happened.\par \par \uc2 And take a look. You watch the news reports, where people that are protesting...\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I have the 50 minutes of video...\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: \uc2 Sure\uc2 , I know you do. And so do I. But here's the thing, you watch these people on television and then -- just like you have Holocaust deniers also, they say, the Holocaust never took -- it's the exact same people. They're saying it never happened.\par \par \uc2 AOC plus three, you know? Israel was the most powerful lobby in the country 15 years ago. Today, between Tlaib and AOC and all of these people, what they're doing, Israel, they don't have the backing that they once had.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You'll give it to them?\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: Yeah, I have -- I'm good. I'm good. But they don't have the backing. Even Schumer, he's become like a Palestinian. \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , Jewish, always strong for Israel. He's become like a Palestinian.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: He called for elections in the middle of a war.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: Yeah, it's a -- it's a