s they should.\par \par \uc2 Hispanic Americans who are here illegally are just as traumatized, by the way as other Americans.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: In El Paso, it's become a huge problem to where we've had break-ins. I've been here for 30 years, my whole life, I've lived here, and you know, this is not something that we've really had to like, worry about, you know, like, hey, we got to make sure everything's locked up. Or hey, make sure like when you're walking around, if you're in the dark, like be careful, like because you just don't know anymore. It's scary.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: You bet, it's scary, but voters are also angry. And they blame the guy who opened the spigots for dozens of countries. The guy who gave corrupt foreign leaders a gift, easy way to export their problems here by just emptying their prisons, and insane asylums. That this endangered Americans are somehow overwhelmed our system, our schools, our health care, that didn't matter to Biden and his open borders, America hating fanatics who work for him, because their sole goal was to fundamentally change this country.\par \par \uc2 Remember the country that they consider systemically racist and wicked. So, they flooded America with what they hope will be future Democrat voters in order to create a permanent majority. And what will that do? Well, that's going to render your vote meaningless.\par \par \uc2 And yes, Democrats, every single one of them who's honest, they want illegals to vote as soon as possible. Oh, yes, that's coming. That's the plan. Thus, nothing that Biden said today about the border matters. It's all smoke and mirrors. It's an election year. Biden has no intention of limiting the number of people coming here, let alone stopping asylees from gaming the system. But you've got to give his speech writers some credit. They're trying to turn the tables on Republicans. It's hilarious.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VID