rld, and lastly, he's abandoned our allies and the world is watching. I think the damage now is incalculable.\par \par \uc2 CHAFFETZ: Yeah. He's all about appeasement. He didn't know how to get our troops safely out of Afghanistan. He's never stood up to Iran. He just keeps taking it, putting our troops in harm's way. And here at home, no, no, don't want to stand up to somebody don't want to actually say I'm going to fight for this principal, I'm going to go ahead and let them spew their hate and perform a form of terrorism to scare the living daylights of good honest people who are just wanting to be good Americans.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Yeah, and, Elizabeth, now, it may result in what -- they have such a fear of their own base, the voters that they're courting and capitulating to that maybe we won't have a regular convention, maybe we'll do most of it online, this way, we won't show the entire country who really supports us. Your reaction to that?\par \par \uc2 PIPKO: I mean, honestly, at this point, can you blame them, right? I mean, they're trying to tell us these are anti-Israel protests which are bad enough, as it is. But they're not anti-Israel protests as you said. At this point, they're antisemitic protests, many are anti-American protests.\par \par \uc2 We're hearing chants of "death to America" happen on college campuses. That is a serious problem for Democrats and even for Republicans who have allowed this to happen in this country. We have a duty to this country to make sure this doesn't happen especially in younger generations.\par \par \uc2 And this administration which flip-flops back and forth between saying they support Israel unconditionally, and then withholding weapons from Israel, our ally, who was fighting for its own survival against a terrorist group that slaughtered 1,200 people in the single worst day for Jews since the Holocaust, a terrorist group that wants to do the exact same thing to Americans as they did in Israel on October 7th, and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  doesn't know where he stands. It's inexcusable.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Jason, last question, the whole Ukrainian impeachment of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was over \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  requesting that they not waste and pillage our money away, and throw it down the drain and not have corruption rule the day as has happened in the past. That was deemed a quid pro quo. Is \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  withholding funding from Israel in exchange for them not going into Rafah, is that a quid pro quo? Because articles of impeachment being drawn up as we speak.\par \par \uc2 CHAFFETZ: Hey, if you listen to Senator Cotton, you listen to Senator Hawley, it's Democrats that set that standard. And why aren't the Democrats rushing to do this? Why is it that Senator Schumer is just so quiet on all of this?\par \par \uc2 Come on. You set the standard Democrats, live by that principle but they won't do it.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Jason, thank you. Elizabeth, thank you.\par \par \uc2 All right. Straight ahead tonight, another embarrassing Biden blunder.\par \par \uc2 Plus, why New York is looking to ban individually wrapped slices of cheese, you know, like \uc2 Kraft\uc2  singles. Jimmy Failla, next.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Biden had another embarrassing blunder yesterday while hosting the \uc2 WNBA\uc2  champions, the Vegas Aces, at the White House. Now, the star player Candace Parker, announced her retirement at the end of the season and did not make it to the White House yesterday. But Biden still gave her a shout-out -- well, at least he tried. Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 , PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: While she couldn't be here I want to acknowledge someone who will be considered one of the greatest all- time coaches, Candace Parker. She played 16 seasonal leagues.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: She's not a coach, Joe. She's never been a coach, Joe.\par \par \uc2 Here with reaction, the host of the hit show FOX News -- you know, just seeing your face makes me laugh, I don't know why -- "FOX News Saturday Night" host Jimmy Failla.\par \par \uc2 You know, we got the giggling vice president, we got a president that can't talk, he surrendered in the war on terror, stabbed our ally Israel in the back, what a week it's been for Joe, and he can't even -- you know, he doesn't even know what position this player was playing.\par \par \uc2 JIMMY FAILLA, HOST OF "FOX NEWS SATURDAY NIGHT": Well, you make a good point, Sean, confusing a player for a coach is not as bad as confusing \uc2 Hamas\uc2  for an ally, okay? It's been a really sloppy week for this guy.\par \par \uc2 But the bar is low. I mean, technically speaking, this represents progress because at least he was talking to a living person. But I mean, what an embarrassment, although the only thing I would add, Sean, is this isn't as bad as the golf mistake. Remember that time he confused our border policy for the U.S. Open? Bad.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Yeah. I think my favorite is, is Uncle Bosie eaten by cannibals. I really do. That might be my all-time favorite. Poor Uncle Bosie. Although none of it happened, just like pretty other tall tale he told.\par \par \uc2 FAILLA: None of it happened.\par \par \uc2 Sean, let me make one point, one point, okay? Because you -- the part about it not happening, okay? But the White House tries to clarify this, like when this press release comes out and he accidentally called the player a coach, they walk it back. They go, what he meant is she traveled on a coach bus or she had a coach bag, like we all see through it, man. It's so ridiculous.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. All right, and the liberal lunacy is getting really bad.\par \par \uc2 All right. So in your state of New York where you used to be a cab driver, well, your state assembly is now advancing a bill aimed at reducing plastic packaging. So they're opposed -- they put out this bill and apparently that means individually wrapped cheese slices, for example, you buy \uc2 Kraft\uc2  and you get the cheese slices, and you know you take the plastic off and it's fresh and you put it on your sandwich or whatever.\par \par \uc2 Yeah, they want to get rid of all that, ban that, and it's going to cost these companies a fortune to complete with this regulation, which means more Biden inflation, if you want to buy cheese.\par \par \uc2 FAILLA: Yeah. Imagine that. Okay, the plastic is there to keep the food fresh and safe so the food will become less safe, but you know what won't improve? The environment. Nobody can explain how getting rid of plastic wrappers on cheese slices is going to do anything for the weather. It's like if you really want to help New York, I don't know, maybe stop throwing people in front of the subway, maybe put criminals to jail.\par \par \uc2 But the idea that we got to lock up the Velveeta guy, it just seems like a misappropriation of resources here.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Yeah, it does. And you know, think about this, they used to give away free government cheese, that were being really generous back in the day. Now, you don't get free government cheese.\par \par \uc2 Now, now, you're going to have to pay more for your \uc2 Kraft\uc2  singles if you like \uc2 Kraft\uc2  cheese which I happen to, just like I like \uc2 Kraft\uc2  macaroni and cheese. I like the deluxe brand, I like the gooey orange, I don't like the powder but that's way too many details.\par \par \uc2 All right. Two crazy -- two crazy plane incidents this week. The first, a brawl that broke out between two men on a Spirit flight as soon as the plane landed. Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (VIDEO CLIP PLAYS)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And it gets worse on a Southwest flight. This video was posted on TikTok. You're going to love this, a woman lounging in an overhead bin, allegedly taking a nap.\par \par \uc2 All right. What's going on up in the air these days, Jim?\par \par \uc2 FAILLA: I, first of all, I love the woman in the overhead bin. That hits home for me because I'm not a big star on this channel. FOX fly -- FOX flies me stow away. I'd be -- I'd be happy to have the bin.\par \par \uc2 But the -- but the \uc2 Spirit Airlines\uc2  thing, I'll tell you why this happens. Everyone's in a bad mood on Spirit because they charge you for everything on discount airlines. When you fly Spirit, Sean, during the pre-flight announcements, they're like in the event of a changing cabin pressure, swipe your \uc2 MasterCard\uc2  or \uc2 Visa\uc2  and pull down on the oxygen mask. Everybody's mad because they nickel and dime -- if they nickel and dime them to death, I'd be fighting too.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Jimmy Failla, we're going to be watching this weekend. You're the only guy that got me to work on a Saturday night. You and Kilmeade.\par \par \uc2 All right. Thank you, Jimmy Failla.\par \par \uc2 When we come back, a sneak peek, brand new FOX Nation special "Outlaws and Lawmen," hoping you can watch this weekend on FOX Nation, straight ahead.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Before we go, a quick programming note. The first episode my new special "Outlaws and Lawmen," it is out right now. It -- you can get it on FOX Nation. Hopefully, you can watch this weekend. Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: We ain't going anywhere. We wait you out all night if we have to.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: When their food runs out, Billy and his friends realize that any chance of survival, that means surrender.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: All right, fellas. It's over.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: After years of corruption and ineptitude in the Lincoln County sheriff's office, Garrett shows he's cut from better material .\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Hope you can watch it this weekend. New episodes will drop every Wednesday. I think you're going to like it.\par \par \uc2 All right. That's all the time we have left this evening. Please set your DVR so you never, ever, ever miss an episode of "Hannity." As always, thank you for being with us.\par \par \uc2 In the meantime, let not your heart be troubled. Greg Gutfeld is standing by to put a smile on your face. Have a great weekend.\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2024 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2024 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document SHAN000020240511ek5a00001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 Biden Abandons Israel And Turns His Back On Americans Held Hostage In Gaza\b0\par\par\uc2 Sean Hannity, Jonathan Turley, David Asman, Joe Concha, Mark  Levin \par \uc2 7,731 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 May 2024\par \uc2 Fox News: Hannity\par \uc2 SHAN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2024 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2024 ASC Services II Media, LLC.  All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 SEAN HANNITY\uc2 , FOX NEWS HOST: And welcome to "Hannity."\par \par \uc2 And tonight, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , your president, caught in the act here is your president lying through his teeth in 2019.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 , PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: The idea that we would cut off military aid to an ally, our only true, true ally in the entire region is absolutely preposterous.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Preposterous, really?\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's words -- they mean nothing. He turned his back on America's top ally in the Middle East he abandoned American hostages in Gaza. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is a nothing but a spineless coward, no moral compass, who can never be trusted.\par \par \uc2 Our allies don't trust them and guess what? Our enemies are emboldened, and much more than that. We'll have a lot more on Joe's betrayal straight ahead.\par \par \uc2 Plus, new shocking revelations from Robert Kennedy Jr. Watch this.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 ROBERT KENNEDY, JR. (I), 2024 PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE: I believe this, we should leave it to the woman. We shouldn't have government involved.\par \par \uc2 INTERVIEWER: Even if it's full term?\par \par \uc2 KENNEDY: Even if it's full term.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Wow. Full-term abortions. Make no mistake, RFK Jr. is somehow running to the left to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . We've got the vetting that nobody else seems to want to do, a full report coming up.\par \par \uc2 But we begin with Juan Merchan's well, kangaroo court in New York City. There's nothing but bogus politically motivated trial against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has gone totally completely off the rails, and we still have not heard from the prosecution's star witness, you know, the convicted felon, notorious liar, \uc2 Michael Cohen\uc2 . We'll have more on that in a moment.\par \par \uc2 Now, this week, as a prelude to Cohen, well, the Biden loving prosecutors called the career porn actress to the stand whose testimony apparently serves no other purpose than to smear, besmirch and slander \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, she horrified jurors with her, quote, so-called inappro -- so- called jokes. They were inappropriate, graphic stories, erotic physical gestures, totally unrelated to the case. And all of her testimony has been irrelevant and immaterial despite being prepped by the prosecution. Wasn't that nice of them to prepare her?\par \par \uc2 And today, during cross examination, well, things got even more strange and maybe a little bit spooky. Even fake news CNN, they couldn't believe what they were hearing. Take a listen.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Necheles asked if Daniels has claimed she can speak with dead people and that her house in New Orleans is haunted. I believe Stormy Daniels was involved with some sort of paranormal show at some point.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: You have actually reached the limits of my knowledge of this case. I am not familiar with her paranormal --\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: I read --\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Remember the first question I cannot answer.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: I mean, literally, we are now in the toilet in the realm of paranormal activity. It was a lot of interesting and unexplained activity, a lot of the activity was completely debunked as a giant possum he says with a laugh.\par \par \uc2 Time to go back to D.C. and Jim Acosta. Jim, back to you.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Gee, thanks, Anderson.\par \par \uc2 I don't know if we're watching CNN or \uc2 QVC\uc2 . That's the question I have right now. I mean --\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: There were comments about candles and paranormal ghost hunting shows, and so on. I feel like we're losing the narrative here.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Salacious material and talking to the dead. This is not a serious trial in any way, shape, manner or form. But it wasn't all ghosts and spirits during cross examination.\par \par \uc2 Now, President Trump's attorney caught Stormy Daniels and what looked like to be a lie. Remember, Daniels said she felt pressured to sign the NDA with Trump because she feared for her safety but during a phone call recorded -- a recording that was played in court today, Daniels lawyer can be heard, well, telling \uc2 Michael Cohen\uc2 , Stormy wanted money more than anything, and was worried that she would lose leverage after the election.\par \par \uc2 The trial is a disgrace. The Biden donating judge Juan Merchan should be ashamed for enabling this kangaroo court. He should have recused himself, any guilty verdict should be easily overturned on appeal. But here's the problem, will that happen after the election? That would be a travesty of justice.\par \par \uc2 Merchan has already denied two motions for a mistrial, continues to muzzle \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  with an unprecedented gag order, all while the prosecution and their witnesses, they get to say, any and everything they want, and even ask for gifts for their commentary.\par \par \uc2 So you got a porn star who hates \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , coached by prosecutors, who has already been ordered to pay him hundreds of thousands of dollars, that she said she's never going to pay him, after a failed defamation lawsuit, she can say whatever she wants about Trump, as everybody else can about ghosts and spirits and graphic sexual encounters that have nothing to do with the bookkeeping case. But \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  can't say anything to defend himself against wild accusations from a person that seems to have a lot of problems.\par \par \uc2 But this case is about to get even worse. \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2 's star witness, \uc2 Michael Cohen\uc2 , not particularly reputable, is he? 2018, Cohen pled guilty to eight serious charges including tax evasion, lying to a bank, lying to the Federal Elections Commission. He was also convicted of making a false statement of Congress for lying on Capitol Hill. Also, Cohen was recently referred to the DOJ yet again for prosecution. Over six other lies to Congress. So, even more charges may very well be in his future