0 presidential campaign, as protests also raged across the country, Biden pledged to bring people together.\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: I'm going to bring all these interests together, peaceful protesters, police chiefs, police officers.\par \par \uc2 TOMLINSON: Five blocks from the White House at \uc2 George Washington University\uc2 , the statue of the first president remains defaced.\par \par \uc2 After a giant American flag was unfurled, protesters superimposed this image with the words "genocide Joe".\par \par \uc2 (CHANTING)\par \par \uc2 TOMLINSON: Biden's former Press Secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  will give the commencement address in two weeks.\par \par \uc2 Republican lawmakers visited GW including Byron Donalds.\par \par \uc2 REP. BYRON DONALDS (R-FL): Everybody believes in peaceful protests, but this is trespassing now.\par \par \uc2 TOMLINSON: Critics say the protests have cost Biden support among young voters.\par \par \uc2 REPORTER: Mr. President, have the protests forced you to reconsider any of the policies with regard to the region?\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: No, thank you.\par \par \uc2 REPORTER: Mr. President --\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 TOMLINSON (on camera): Right now, President Biden's CIA Director \uc2 Bill Burns\uc2  is in Cairo as hostage and ceasefire negotiations continue -- Shannon.\par \par \uc2 BREAM: All right. Lucas Tomlinson at the White House for -- Lucas, thank you.\par \par \uc2 We turn now to FOX News correspondent Jeff Paul in Tel Aviv.\par \par \uc2 Hello, Jeff.\par \par \uc2 JEFF PAUL, FOX NEWS CORRESPONDENT: Oh, yeah, Shannon. \uc2 Hamas\uc2  leader \uc2 Ismail Haniyeh\uc2  reportedly said today that he wants to see not only a full withdrawal of Israeli troops but a comprehensive ceasefire.\par \par \uc2 Israeli Prime Minister \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  saying that they can't accept that, and if they did, the next October 7th would be only a matter of time.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 PAUL (voice-ove