rst fired a ballistic missile at one of its satellites to demonstrate this new capability and threat.\par \par \uc2 House Intelligence Committee chairman, \uc2 Mike Turner\uc2 , raised alarm bells two months ago, after seeing classified intelligence that suggested Russia plan to launch a nuclear anti-satellite weapon in space.\par \par \uc2 REP. \uc2 MIKE TURNER\uc2  (R-OH): I believe that this is the Cuban Missile Crisis in space and this administration is sleepwalking itself into an international crisis.\par \par \uc2 GRIFFIN (voice over): Last week, Russia vetoed a U.S. and Japan sponsored \uc2 U.N.\uc2  resolution reaffirming the 1967 Outer Space Treaty, calling for nations to prevent a nuclear arms race in space.\par \par \uc2 China abstained.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 GRIFFIN (on camera): National Security Adviser Jake Sullivan called out Russian President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 , who has said publicly Russia has no intention of deploying nuclear weapons in space. If so, he asked, why did Russia veto the resolution? Bret?\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Jennifer Griffin at the Pentagon. Jennifer, Thank you.\par \par \uc2 Up next, former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  returns to the campaign trail. We'll have a live report from Michigan. As you look live there in Freeland, Michigan.\par \par \uc2 First, beyond our borders tonight. Police used tear gas to disperse protesters during the May Day March in Paris. Thousands of people marched through the French capitol seeking better pay and working conditions.\par \par \uc2 Tourists are evacuated by air from a national reserve in Kenya amid flooding and heavy rains there more than a dozen hotels lodges and camps are flooded.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Kenyan Red Cross\uc2  says it rescued 36 people by air, 25 by land. More than 170 people have died across Kenya since mid-March when the rainy season started.\par \par \uc2 And this is a live look at Cape Town. One of the big stories there tonight. An aquarium in South Africa is trying to help more than 500 baby sea turtles washed up on beaches by a rare and powerful storm.\par \par \uc2 These little turtles are mostly endangered loggerheads, they should be cruising the ocean most of them. Instead, will spend their first few months of their lives in the newly built plastic tanks in an aquarium in Cape Town.\par \par \uc2 Just some of the other stories, "BEYOND OUR BORDERS" -- way "BEYOND OUR BORDERS" tonight. We'll be right back.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 BAIER: The Arizona State Senate has approved a bill to repeal an abortion ban dating back to the 19th century. Two Republicans sided with Democrats in Arizona to pass the House bill. The legislation comes after the state Supreme Court decided an abortion law from 1864 could be reinstated. The bill now goes to Democratic governor \uc2 Katie Hobbs\uc2  who is expected to sign it.\par \par \uc2 Former President Trump is back on the campaign trail during a short bake break in his New York criminal trial. He is trying to flip Michigan and Wisconsin back into his column after winning them in 2016 and losing them in 2020.\par \par \uc2 Correspondent Garrett Tenney reports tonight from Freeland, Michigan.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 DONALD TRUMP\uc2  (R), FORMER U.S. PRESIDENT AND PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE: Hello, Wisconsin. How are you this evening?\par \par \uc2 GARRETT TENNEY, FOX NEWS CHANNEL CORRESPONDENT (voice over): Former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  back on the campaign trail today holding rallies in Wisconsin and Michigan.\par \par \uc2 Those states and Pennsylvania make up Democrats blue wall strategy, since winning those states which flipped for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in 2020, after going for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and 2016 would nearly secure Biden a second term.\par \par \uc2 But right now, the race is a virtual tie in all three states. One of the top issues for voters is the economy.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : We had the greatest,