ion, I -- are not as high as they should be. The other thing that should be made is a very clear message to Tehran that these attacks are being that we would hold them as to account and continue to support and go after the IRGC.\par \par \uc2 Again, the odds of that are also very low. But, again, the timing for the resumption of these attacks just after the prime minister from Iraq returned from a weeklong visit in the United States shouldn't go unnoticed, and also with the timing of Israel's response to Iran's attack just over a week ago.\par \par \uc2 SMITH: So, to your point about what we should do and how we will respond, based on your response, what message does that send to the world our lack of response?\par \par \uc2 SADLER: Well, if we don't respond, and the most likely is the performance of the past continues into the future, is that we will have more of these attacks, and they will spread.\par \par \uc2 SMITH: Hmm.\par \par \uc2 SADLER: Again, we had 171 since October, as your earlier slide showed.\par \par \uc2 But, again, there was a lull for the last month-and-a-half to two months. We're probably going to go back to those high levels.\par \par \uc2 SMITH: Yes.\par \par \uc2 SADLER: And we're probably going to see increased activity against U.S. forces, not just in Syria and Iraq, but also in Yemen.\par \par \uc2 SMITH: Got it. Really appreciate, Brent, you joining us today. We have got some breaking news. Thanks for your time, sir.\par \par \uc2 And we want to head back to those anti-Israel protests. They are growing and rocking college campuses, now at \uc2 NYU\uc2 . Across the U.S., we are seeing this happen. Across the city, we're seeing this happen.\par \par \uc2 Alexis McAdams has been at Columbia.\par \par \uc2 What a split screen this is. I know you're getting some new information, Alexis, on that \uc2 NYU\uc2  demonstration. What are we -- what exactly are we learning?\par \par \uc2 OK.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 SMITH: FOX 