near that campus and they're all protesting. It's happened over there near that park as well, where they kind of all overtake in that area and then try to get onto the campus.\par \par \uc2 But because it's private property, the \uc2 NYU\uc2  says they have to be given the green light by the university before they can go on. So that hasn't happened just yet. We did ask if they have been in communication, the \uc2 NYPD\uc2 , with \uc2 Columbia University\uc2 , like they were the other day. They said they had not heard from the president so far today.\par \par \uc2 Nobody called them and said, hey, come on and help it out here. We do know that these protests are supposed to wrap around 6:00 today. So maybe, if they don't wrap by 6:00, Sandra, they will end up asking the police to come in and help. But a lot of these pro-Palestinian supporters here were livid that the \uc2 NYPD\uc2  had come in the other day.\par \par \uc2 They said the \uc2 NYPD\uc2  was violent. The \uc2 NYPD\uc2  told FOX News and several other outlets they had no issues with getting these people in and out, there were no problems. So it kind of depends on who you talk to.\par \par \uc2 I have tried to talk to all these protesters here who are blocking us now with their umbrellas. They're not interested in saying why they're out here to support the Palestinian people, but we will keep trying to check in with them, Sandra.\par \par \uc2 SMITH: So, Alexis, as this is Columbia, obviously, and the tents that have been set up there, they were asked to leave. They did not. Clearly, nothing's being done to ask them or remove them.\par \par \uc2 But to those live pictures outside of \uc2 NYU\uc2 , Alexis -- and we had the aerials there as well, but outside of \uc2 NYU\uc2 , you can see someone carrying the Israeli flag. As often happens, you have the counterprotesters that do show up as well.\par \par \uc2 The mayor of New York City was just asked about this in a new interview, calling some of the language,