r \uc2 That's close to unprecedented.\par \par \uc2 PERGRAM: And that's problem that Mike Johnson has.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: Yes.\par \par \uc2 PERGRAM: Yes. That's the problem that Mike Johnson has. The question is, does he call the shots?\par \par \uc2 I mean, I talked to one Democrat today, \uc2 Jason Crow\uc2  of Colorado, about Ukraine. And, supposedly, that's next in the queue. The speaker did not say that today. He said, we will move on to other things. He did not necessarily hand-signal if they were going to do Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 But \uc2 Jason Crow\uc2  said, look -- he said that's a bad sign for Ukraine if he's down there talking with the former president in Florida.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: So the fact that Speaker Johnson is down there, they're on the same page. They're getting along. I mean, it wouldn't be a nasty event when it starts, right?\par \par \uc2 PERGRAM: Well, we don't know.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: Yes.\par \par \uc2 PERGRAM: That's always the issue. You just don't know the level of tension. We think they're on good terms, but it's hard to divine these things.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: Yes.\par \par \uc2 PERGRAM: I mean, obviously, the president and the speaker were not on the same page earlier this week. I mean, Mike Johnson was confident that bill was going to move earlier this week, and he sent out the tweet -- or -- I'm sorry -- the post on TRUTH Social on Wednesday morning.\par \par \uc2 They were in a Republican Conference meeting at that point. And by the end of the meeting, it was clear that they did not have the votes on that test vote that morning. That indicates, that underscores the presence of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  looming over Capitol Hill.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: Absolutely. That's an understatement.\par \par \uc2 Chad, thank you very much.\par \par \uc2 Chad Pergram following all of that.\par \par \uc2 Want to go to Bob Cusack right now, The Hill editor in chief.\par \par \uc2 And, Bob, I don't want to belabor this point. And maybe 