cremental way. We have to -- Roe -- end of Roe was not the end of the fight; it was the beginning. We have to convince Americans over time of the sanctity of unborn life. And that's going to take incremental progress at the state level, and not --\par \par \uc2 If you do it the opposite way, they are going to elect pro-choice -- pro- choice Democrats and it will set back the pro-life cause even more.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: Yes, in some ways, a lot of the same people who were fighting to overturn Roe v. Wade, and say this is a state issue. It has to be decided by people closer to the issue in their own states.\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 THIESSEN: Yes, exactly.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: Some states will be very conservative on it, some states will be more liberal, and they claimed that, that was exactly what they felt should happen. Now that they got what they wanted, they want to go back to some sort of blanket federal decision on all of this. So, we'll see where it goes.\par \par \uc2 Marc, thank you very much. Good to see you as always.\par \par \uc2 THIESSEN: Take care. Thank you.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: All right. Here is a story that is popping on social media, getting a ton of attention. A chair flew off a rooftop bar. One of the many rooftop bars along Broadway in Nashville in the chaotic moments leading to country star Morgan Wallen's arrest.\par \par \uc2 We're now going to show you the arrest video and what happened on the rooftop later this hour.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: He is a rock star. He is trying to be a rock star. Why not?\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Like, I'm a huge Morgan Wallen fan -- like huge.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Yes.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: And it's just very, very upsetting like what the heck? You know?\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 AMERICAN CROWD: (INAUDIBLE).\par \par \uc2 