ar. The island administrator says the ferry was overcrowded and that there were 130 people on board. He says many who drowned were children.\par \par \uc2 And this is a live look at London. One of the big stories there tonight. French troops join their British counterparts in the famous changing of the guard ceremony outside Buckingham Palace for the first time. The personnel marched together in a display of solidarity between Britain and France, amid the war in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Just some of the other stories, "BEYOND OUR BORDERS" tonight. We'll be right back.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Secretary of State \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2  says Ukraine will become a member of the \uc2 NATO\uc2  alliance. This comes amid continued pressure on Congress to get a major aid package to the president's desk soon.\par \par \uc2 State Department correspondent Gillian Turner has the store tonight.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 ANTONY BLINKEN\uc2 , UNITED STATES SECRETARY OF STATE: Ukraine's future is in \uc2 NATO\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 GILLIAN TURNER, FOX NEWS CHANNEL CORRESPONDENT: The Biden administration is going full steam ahead on \uc2 NATO\uc2  membership for Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Well, sort of. First, the State Department says the war against Russia must end.\par \par \uc2 MATTHEW MILLER\uc2 , SPOKESMAN, UNITED STATES STATE DEPARTMENT: Ultimately that's a process that moves forward at the end of this conflict.\par \par \uc2 Then, Ukraine needs to meet certain conditions to qualify.\par \par \uc2 BLINKEN: Ukraine is attracting more and more private investment. And it is valiantly holding ground on the battlefield in the face of an ongoing Russian onslaught.\par \par \uc2 TURNER: President Zelenskyy, though, says his military desperately needs more weapons and funding now or Putin will win.\par \par \uc2 VOLODYMYR ZELENSKYY, PRESIDENT OF UKRAINE (through translator): That will be a tragedy for all of us, not only for Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 TURNER: But the White House says it's Congress's fault.\par \par \uc2 KARINE JEAN-PIERRE\uc2 , WHITE HOUSE PRESS SECRETARY: Ukraine is losing ground in the battlefield, and that's because of congressional inaction.\par \par \uc2 TURNER (voice over): Speaker Mike Johnson faces pressure to get an aid package done this week. The sticking point, Republicans in both chambers.\par \par \uc2 SEN. J.D. VANCE (R-OH): That he brings up a foreign aid package sending billions of dollars to Ukraine without doing anything on the southern border, it will be a disgrace.\par \par \uc2 TURNER (voice over): But rather than vote on the Senate to $95 billion bill, Johnson is pushing the Repo Act.\par \par \uc2 REP. MIKE JOHNSON (R-LA): If we can use to seized assets of Russian oligarchs to allow the Ukrainians to fight them, that's just pure poetry.\par \par \uc2 TURNER: Most House Republicans acknowledge the stakes are high.\par \par \uc2 REP. MIKE LAWLER (R-NY): If Ukraine falls, other former Soviet satellite countries like Moldova will fall with it. And that would be an apoplectic crisis across the globe.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO TAPE)\par \par \uc2 TURNER: Well, the timeline for both Ukraine's \uc2 NATO\uc2  membership as well as this aid package going forward are uncertain tonight, as is Speaker Mike Johnson's leadership spot. Representative \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  has been threatening to vacate the speakership if Ukraine goes forward in its current form, meaning it could just take one member of Congress to cast him out of the speakership, Bret.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: That could happen this week. Gillian Turner live at the State Department. Gillian, thanks.\par \par \uc2 We're getting new information tonight about Israel's battle plan against \uc2 Hamas\uc2 . This comes amid speculation about the true meaning of recent Israeli troop movements inside Gaza. Correspondent Trey Yingst reports tonight from Tel Aviv.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO TAPE)\par \par \uc2 BENJAMIN NE