ival and they're doing it.\par \par \uc2 The DOJ then dutifully is doing their job. In November, you -- you have the opportunity to elect somebody that would be far more authentic with a much better track record who is clearly a fighter for this country that will reestablish America's strength on the world stage, that understands the needs to control our borders, bring back law and order and safety and security, and by the way, ran a much better economy than \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  ever dreamed of. And that's -- that's going to be the difference in just 215 days.\par \par \uc2 Now, by the way, or you can treat it like a retirement house like Joe does, the White House, in between trips to Delaware.\par \par \uc2 All right. Let's look deeper into these polls. Joining us now, pollster Matt Towery. He's with Insider Advantage. Along with the founder of the Trafalgar Group, Robert Cahaly, and former senior adviser to the Clintons, pollster -- well, that's \uc2 Mark Penn\uc2  is with us.\par \par \uc2 All right. Let's start with you Matt Towery.\par \par \uc2 Look, the polls are consistent. Your polls have shown the same. Robert's polls have shown the same. Mark, I don't see you polling as much, but you're -- you're an interesting voice here. Matt, it's 215 days out, you can't count on polls at this point, but they're -- they do mean something. What do they mean?\par \par \uc2 MATT TOWERY, "POLLING PLUS PODCAST" CO-HOST: Well, they mean a couple of things. I look at them more right now from a strategic standpoint. For example, we now see the effect of these third party candidates. They do drain from Biden. That's a serious issue that Biden has to deal with, but I also realize that we're still going to have this setup of the way the Democrats are able to gather votes and get votes in.\par \par \uc2 Every one of these battleground states is going to be nip tuck race in the very end. We all know it you, know that as well, Sean. It's going to be a real battle.\par \par \uc2 But I will say one other thing, I look at the Biden campaign and they seem -- I think their strategy is a P and A campaign. In other words, they want to see Trump go to prison or be found guilty in New York, and they're -- they're hanging their hopes partially on that. And they're also hanging their hopes on abortion, because they now believe, particularly now in Florida, now that that's an issue on the ballot in November, that they -- they can broaden the field and they can make things more competitive and bring more female voters out who were brought out in 2022.\par \par \uc2 So that's their strategy and also to deflect, which is what they do basically every day to try to rope a do this thing through like they did in -- in the last election.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And, Robert, it's good -- we know what the -- the playbook is. They will demagogue on abortion. Republicans, they better have a good answer and they also need to understand where the country is. If people were to ask me my personal views, okay, I'm pretty pro-life. If you're asking me politically where a politician needs to be, I would say the Dobbs decision of 15 weeks, that's where the country is.\par \par \uc2 And if Republican politicians don't understand that, then -- and they run on that, they're going to get their asses kicked and they're going to lose. You agree or not?\par \par \uc2 ROBERT CAHALY, TRAFALGAR GROUP FOUNDER: Absolutely, and it's also the way that you talk about it. When the -- when the word of ban is being thrown around, Republicans are losing. When you start talking about simple limitations, reasonable limitations and talk about the extreme being third trimester abortion and partial birth, Republicans are winning.\par \par \uc2 So they have to want to fight that fight and state their position and make it clear as the bill where they stand and where the extremists on abortion really are and who they are.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Yeah, and \uc2 Mark Penn\uc2 , just on this one issue before I ask you about the Democratic Party, the Democrats will demagogue this there were more ads run in New York in the congressional -- my former congressional district, in the -- in the last runoff campaign to fill the Santos seat, than any other topic. They are banking on abortion and lying to women about abortion. Dobbs allowed the states to decide. That's all that changed.\par \par \uc2 And California, New York, they'll have very liberal laws. Other states will have more conservative laws with some restrictions, but there will be legal abortion in America in perpetuity it seems based on public sentiment today. Do you agree?\par \par \uc2 MARK PENN\uc2 , FOX NEWS CONTRIBUTOR: Well, yes, I mean when you look at our polls, the Harris poll, really Trump's by winning about by two points, which means he's winning by two to five in a lot of the swing votes -- swing states, and I think that's exactly what you see.\par \par \uc2 I think the key swing voters are going to be these suburban women voters and they are going to be cross pressured between the economy that they don't see as good and what they see is a fundamental right to abortion. And in Florida now, given that DeSantis put in a six-week bill, there's now going to be on the ballot of 23-week bill.\par \par \uc2 So the choice isn't going to be 15 weeks or not, it's going to be six or 23, and this could bring a lot of Democrats out in Florida. So this is a good issue for the Democrats in this current political environment in a close race where Trump is leading.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Why? Why is Biden bleeding over 20 points, African-Americans, Hispanic Americans and young people?\par \par \uc2 PENN: Well, look, I -- the polls are showing that, but will that really be true on Election Day? We've seen that several times where during the election period before the bases really come together, that that votes begin to sag or drift --\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: We have, but never this big, Mark. I agree with you. We've seen signs that it might be real and it doesn't materialize and in the end, people go back home.\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 CAHALY: It's grown on Trump. It's grown on Trump.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: What's that?\par \par \uc2 CAHALY: Trump has grown those -- Trump grew those numbers from `20 from `16, the votes he got in the Black community, and even more in `20. So it's always been on an upswing and if the Republicans get 25 percent of the Black vote and 45 percent of the minority vote, I mean, of the Hispanic vote you spend all the time -- you won't worry about suburban women, they're not going to matter.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Quick response, Mark.\par \par \uc2 PENN: Yeah, I just don't think that's how it's going to come down in the final days. In the final days, I think the Black community will come back to Biden and the Democrats and the suburban women will be the critical voters and that will be a choice between the economy and immigration and maybe crime, and abortion and climate change on the other hand.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Matt, you get the last word. You agree or disagree?\par \par \uc2 TOWERY: Well, I don't think this suburban voter issue is not as big to me because you're going to get what you're going to get. The bigger issue is how big is the intensity going to be for the turnout for Trump that he maintains and how much can these independent candidates and how many get on the ballot can they siphon away? That's going to decide this election this time.\par \par \uc2 And I will say one other thing, the Republicans need to get going right now because you win elections in April and May, not in November.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Matt, Robert, Mark, thank you all. We appreciate it.\par \par \uc2 Now, according to "The Wall Street Journal", Trump's swing state lead is likely bolstered by voters who trust Trump more than Biden on the economy, inflation, immigration. Immigration again and again shows up as the number one issue on people's minds.\par \par \uc2 Anyway, here with reaction, Texas Senator Ted Cruz.\par \par \uc2 One thing I keep reading is not only is -- are the Biden people signaling that they're going to target Florida, I think their odds are very low. That's my take, but also your state of Texas. This is -- this has been a dream of the Democratic Party for a long time, knowing if they flip Texas, it's probably game, set, match, it's over for a long time.\par \par \uc2 SEN. TED CRUZ (R-TX): Yeah. Look, Sean, that's exactly right. We've got a battle nationally. The polling numbers we're seeing nationally are encouraging, but it's close. It's going to be a battle to see who shows up and who votes.\par \par \uc2 And when it comes to Texas, \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  has been explicit. He's coming after Texas. I am his number one target in the entire country. I'm on the ballot. I'm running for re-election and the Democrats are coming after me. They are going to spend more than $100 million this year. \uc2 George Soros\uc2  is already spending millions of dollars in the state of Texas.\par \par \uc2 My opponent, a liberal Democrat named \uc2 Colin Allred\uc2  is out-raising \uc2 Beto O'Rourke\uc2 , my last opponent, three to one. They are flooding millions of dollars into Texas and the reason is simple, you remember my last reelect, it was a three-point race. I won by 2.6 percent. And so, \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , his view is he floods millions into Texas, he gains three points and that's how they win.\par \par \uc2 And I'll tell you how we're fighting back against it. You've got the Democrat fat cats, you've got big tech, you got celebrities writing checks to my opponent.\par \par \uc2 We're supported by millions of Americans, millions of conservatives all across this country that go to our website. It's tedcruz.org. They go to tedcruz.org. They give 25 bucks or 50 bucks or 100 bucks.\par \par \uc2 That's how we stand up to the \uc2 George Soros\uc2 's and the \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  and the \uc2 Mark Zuckerberg\uc2 's is the 25 and 50 bucks at tedcruz.org because we got a fight to defend Texas. If we lose Texas, we lose the whole country.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And, by the way, I was there. I was on the ground. I was covering your race at the time. I remember it was that close and I remember many a conversation we had at the time. It's amazing how fast six years go by.\par \par \uc2 But I don't think they're going to succeed, and I'll tell you why, because Texas, more than any other state, has had to deal with Biden's disaster at the border. You have been in the forefront. Governor Abbott has been in the forefront of fighting.\par \par \uc2 I don't know how you felt -- when I read that now they're flying people direct, you don't have to pass go, collect 200 bucks, you don't have to make the difficult trip to our border, now they're just flying people indirectly with American taxpayer money from whatever country they're coming from, you know, to whatever state they want to go to, but they're targeting Florida and Texas and dropping and dumping 90 percent of these illegal immigrants in your state and now my state.\par \par \uc2 CRUZ: Yeah. I mean, let's be clear, the 10.4 million illegal immigrants that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and the Democrats have let in, have deliberately let in, they're letting them in because they view them as future Democrat voters. They hope as many of them as possible will vote illegally right now. They want them to stay in Texas. They want them to be in Florida because they want to flip our states.\par \par \uc2 Look, if they bring a million illegal immigrants into Texas and they vote Democrat, Texas is in real trouble, and that's what the Democrats are aiming at. It's why they're flooding our state.\par \par \uc2 And I got to say, you know, the point you just made, you're right. It's not just the invasion every day at the southern border of thousands upon thousands of people coming, the Biden administration is literally flying people in from Venezuela, from Cuba, from Haiti. Last year, 320,000 people the Biden administration flew from their countries to America. They flew them to over 40 different airports in America. They won't tell us which ones, but you want to know the consequences.\par \par \uc2 We saw just two weeks ago, a tragic story about a Haitian that the Biden administration flew in from Haiti. They flew him to Boston, Massachusetts, and just two weeks ago, he was arrested for brutally raping a 15-year-old girl who's severely disabled. This is what the Biden administration is doing, is literally bring bringing criminals to our communities and it's Texas, it's Florida, and it's every other state in the Union.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You know. I've -- I've said this before, Senator. I said this is a tipping point. This is an inflection point.\par \par \uc2 CRUZ: Yes.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I've never been more concerned about our country, borders, the economy, law and order, America's place in the world, war in Europe, war in the Middle East, things heating up even more every day, a new axis of evil. These are consequential times. This will be a consequential election and we will live with the government we vote for.\par \par \uc2 CRUZ: Well, and you know what makes that perfectly clear? The Democrat Party abandoning Israel. \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  demanding the elected leader of Israel to step down. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  orchestrating the United Nations to effectively condemn Israel.\par \par \uc2 That's never happened before. It's how radical they're getting. If you want Israel to stand and stand with America's support, we got a win in November. That means \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  needs to win.\par \par \uc2 It also means I need your support in Texas. So please come to tedcruz.org and let's fight to pull this country back.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You know, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and his administration stabbing Israel in the back has been repulsive. It has been -- to watch the reason why to cater to the radicals that have now taken over the Democratic Party, it is beyond my comprehension, it really is.\par \par \uc2 Senator Cruz, thank you.\par \par \uc2 When we come back, all right, all these leftist policies, they're getting more ridiculous by the day. They actually are going to be shocked, and they're all going to have dire consequences for you and your family and your wallet. \uc2 Larry Kudlow\uc2  examines that, straight ahead.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Just when you thought things couldn't get worse -- well, liberal policies, they're growing more asinine and idiotic by the day. Now, despite push back from the American people, consumers people that actually spend real money -- well, pot hole Pete, your transportation secretary, he continues to try to push electric vehicles whether you want it or not, all in an attempt to appease the green new deal climate alarmist religious cult.\par \par \uc2 Earlier today, he actually made this ridiculous comparison. You decide.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 PETE BUTTIGIEG, TRANSPORTATION SECRETARY: Let's be clear that the automotive sector is moving toward EVs and we can't pretend otherwise. Sometimes when these debates happen, I feel like it's the early 2000s and I'm talking to some people who think that we can just have landline phones forever.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: No, just the opposite is true. After Ford lost $4.5 billion last year, yeah, they decided to cut back on the EV line because nobody was buying the cars. And I say that as somebody I hope a company like \uc2 Tesla\uc2  is successful because it'll create jobs right here in this country. And if people want the choice of an electric car, they should have it. I'm all for it.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Cal -- but if you want a gas powered car, you should have the freedom to get that, too. Meanwhile, California's fast food minimum wag